E["item:bernice-s-necklace"] = {t="item",n="Bernice's Necklace",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest, Bernice keeps her late husband's necklace close.",h="At Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest, Bernice keeps her late husband's necklace close.",sec={{t="A Soldier's Lost Charm",b="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's necklace once belonged to her late husband, a veteran of Stormwind's military campaigns. He carried it into battle as a charm for good fortune. Bernice says tragedy came only during his final campaign, the one expedition when he forgot to bring it. Since his death, the keepsake has remained among her most cherished possessions at Stonefield Farm.",sp=0},{t="Stolen by Scavengers",b="Young Billy Maclure was exploring near the Fargodeep Mine when he dropped the shiny necklace. Goldtooth, a prominent kobold inside the mine, spotted it and carried it away. Like other kobolds, he was drawn to bright, valuable trinkets, and he kept the necklace among his scavenged treasures.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Whose necklace was this originally?",a="The necklace belonged to Auntie Bernice Stonefield's late husband, who wore it as a good-luck charm during Stormwind's military campaigns.",al={"who owned the necklace","bernice necklace owner","husband necklace"},it="identity"},{q="How did the necklace end up with the kobolds?",a="Billy Maclure saw a large kobold with gold teeth pick up the necklace near the Fargodeep Mine and carry it away. Auntie Bernice hopes it can be recovered.",al={"how was it lost","why does goldtooth have it","who took the necklace"}},{q="Why is the necklace so important to Auntie Bernice?",a="The necklace is a cherished memory of Bernice's late husband. He believed it protected him in battle, and the only time he fell in war was the day he left it behind.",al={"why does bernice want it","bernice husband story","is the necklace magic"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is a prominent kobold scavenger who makes his lair inside the Fargodeep Mine in Elwynn Forest. He collects shiny baubles and took the necklace after it was dropped nearby.",al={"what is goldtooth","goldtooth lore","who has the necklace"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance farm families in Elwynn Forest, the necklace recalls the toll Stormwind's long military campaigns take on everyday lives."},kw={"auntie bernice","bernice's necklace","billy maclure","fargodeep mine","goldtooth","lucky charm","stonefield"},rel={"npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:87","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:stonefield-farm","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","quest:62"},src={"Bernice's Necklace","Goldtooth (quest)"}}
E["item:bloodstone-choker"] = {t="item",n="Bloodstone Choker",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, the Bloodstone Choker binds a warlock’s ritual to the void. Gakin the Darkbinder once held the bloodstone talisman, until an apprentice stole it and fled to the Defias Brotherhood.",h="In Stormwind, the Bloodstone Choker binds a warlock’s ritual to the void.",sec={{t="A Stolen Conduit",b="The Bloodstone Choker once belonged to Gakin the Darkbinder, a warlock mentor in the chambers beneath Stormwind’s Slaughtered Lamb. His apprentice, Surena Caledon, betrayed him and stole the choker. She fled into Elwynn’s forests and joined the Defias Brotherhood, carrying the enchanted talisman with her. She is at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, where the choker must be reclaimed before the bandits can use its power.",sp=1},{t="Taming the Void",b="Carved from bloodstone, the choker can bridge the mortal world and the twisting shadows of the Twisting Nether. Gakin puts it to use in the crypts beneath the tavern, channeling its magic at the summoning circle to draw a hostile Voidwalker from the void. A warlock must subdue the furious creature in direct combat while wielding the talisman to prove the will to command such a guardian.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Bloodstone Choker?",a="The Bloodstone Choker is an enchanted bloodstone necklace that warlocks use as a ritual conduit. Its magic can tear through reality and summon an unruly Voidwalker from the Nether.",al={"bloodstone choker","what is the choker","what does the choker do"},it="identity"},{q="Who originally owned the choker?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder originally owned the choker. He trains warlocks in the covert basement beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter.",al={"who owns the choker","gakin choker","where did the choker come from"}},{q="Why was the choker stolen?",a="Surena Caledon stole the choker from her mentor, Gakin, then fled to join the Defias Brotherhood. She sought power among the bandits hiding in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who stole it","why did surena steal it","surena caledon choker"},it="motive"},{q="How is the choker used in warlock training?",a="A warlock activates the recovered choker over the summoning circle in the crypts beneath The Slaughtered Lamb. It draws out a Voidwalker, which the aspiring warlock must defeat and subdue to command the demon.",al={"how to use choker","voidwalker ritual choker","the binding choker"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Bloodstone Choker wanted?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder values the Bloodstone Choker as a potent magical catalyst required to summon and bind a voidwalker. After his former apprentice Surena Caledon stole it to aid the Defias Brotherhood, Gakin seeks its return to restore his arcane authority and test new warlocks in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",al={"why do they want bloodstone choker","who wants the bloodstone choker","why does gakin want the choker"},it="why_wanted",add="9d3659ea"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, recovering the Bloodstone Choker marks a rite of passage from basic spellcraft to command of formidable demonic minions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Surena Caledon’s flight to the Defias Brotherhood shows that outlaws in Elwynn seek dangerous occult relics to strengthen their rebellion against Stormwind."},kw={"bloodstone choker","defias","gakin the darkbinder","surena caledon","the binding","the slaughtered lamb","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"quest:1471","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1688","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","topic:warlock","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn"},src={"Bloodstone Choker","The Binding (Voidwalker, Stormwind)"}}
E["item:brass-collar"] = {t="item",n="Brass Collar",z="elwynn",s="At the Brackwell pumpkin patch, Princess wears a brass collar that Ma Stonefield wants as proof the sow is gone.",h="At the Brackwell pumpkin patch, Princess wears a brass collar that Ma Stonefield wants as proof the sow is...",sec={{t="A Trophy of Farmyard Rivalry",b="Princess is a huge, prize-winning sow owned by the Brackwell family. She roams their pumpkin patch east of the Maclure homestead, and her appetite leads her into the Stonefield Farm’s crops. After losing valuable vegetables to the sow, Ma Stonefield seeks someone willing to slay her. Princess wears a brass band around her neck, and the collar proves she will not raid the Stonefield fields again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Brass Collar come from?",a="Princess wears the collar at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, past the Maclure farm.",al={"brass collar source","who drops brass collar","where to get brass collar"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ma Stonefield want the collar?",a="Princess eats Ma Stonefield’s prize vegetables. The collar proves to Ma Stonefield that the sow has been put down before ruining more of her harvest.",al={"why stonefield wants collar","ma stonefield collar purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who owns Princess?",a="Princess belongs to the Brackwell family and roams their pumpkin patch with her smaller boar companions.",al={"princess owner","who owns the pig"}},{q="Can anyone other than Princess drop this item?",a="Only Princess can yield the collar. It is fashioned to fit the Brackwells’ enormous prized sow.",al={"other collar drops","where else find brass collar"},gp=true},{q="What is the Brass Collar?",a="The Brass Collar is the distinctive neckband worn by Princess, a prize-winning sow owned by the Brackwell family. Due to Princess's enormous size and habit of raiding neighboring crops, the collar serves as undeniable proof that the destructive beast has finally been put down.",al={"what is brass collar","brass collar lore","who wears brass collar"},it="identity",add="92e34b72"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer helping Elwynn’s rural folk, taking Princess’s collar helps settle a feud between neighboring farms."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","brass collar","elwynn forest","ma stonefield","princess","princess must die","stonefield farm"},rel={"quest:88","npc:ma-stonefield","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:stonefield-farm","zone:elwynn"},src={"Brass Collar","Princess Must Die! (Classic)"}}
E["item:bundle-of-wood"] = {t="item",n="Bundle of Wood",z="elwynn",s="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Bundle of Wood waits in the trees for an urgent shipment west.",h="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Bundle of Wood waits in the trees for an urgent shipment west.",sec={{t="Abandoned Timber",b="Freshly chopped timber from Eastvale Logging Camp helps supply the Kingdom of Stormwind. The camp sends wood west for town buildings and other construction. Bears and wolves have pushed into the groves northwest of camp, and terrified loggers fled, leaving their freshly gathered Bundles of Wood among the trees. With delivery deadlines close, overseer Raelen needs travelers to pass the predators and recover the timber before the lumber contracts are breached.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why were these bundles of wood abandoned in the woods?",a="Wolves and bears ambushed the loggers harvesting timber northwest of Eastvale Logging Camp and drove them off. Their freshly chopped Bundles of Wood were left scattered on the forest floor.",al={"why is wood on ground","why abandon wood","abandoned lumber elwynn"},it="origin"},{q="Who needs this wood collected?",a="Raelen, an overseer at Eastvale Logging Camp, urgently needs the wood gathered to meet an impending lumber shipment deadline.",al={"who wants the wood","raelen lumber","wood turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these bundles found?",a="The bundles lie on the ground directly northwest of Eastvale Logging Camp, among the trees where Elwynn's bears and wolves prowl.",al={"bundle of wood location","where is the wood","eastvale wood spots"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't the town guards clear out the beasts?",a="Raelen asked Deputy Rainer for help with the beasts, but Elwynn's marshals and guards are stretched thin across the region. The lumber workers need outside help to recover the logs quickly.",al={"why no guards","deputy rainer wood","guards at eastvale"},it="threat"},{q="What is a Bundle of Wood?",a="These are stacks of freshly harvested timber cut and gathered by the laborers of the Eastvale Logging Camp. Prepared for transport and processing, they represent the camp's ongoing lumber operations in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"what is bundle of wood","bundle of wood elwynn","what are these wood bundles"},it="identity",add="e892b12c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, gathering the bundles helps Stormwind's rebuilding efforts and gets vital timber shipments to settlements across Elwynn and Westfall on time."},kw={"bundle of wood","eastvale","elwynn","logging camp","lumber","raelen","timber"},rel={"quest:5545","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison"},src={"Bundle of Wood","A Bundle of Trouble"}}
E["item:crate-of-horseshoes"] = {t="item",n="Crate of Horseshoes",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn, fifty iron horseshoes are bound for Lakeshire.",h="In Elwynn, fifty iron horseshoes are bound for Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Delivery to Lakeshire",b="Smith Argus forged fifty fresh horseshoes in Goldshire, then packed the crate and hammered it shut. Verner Osgood commissioned them for Lakeshire, where constant pressure from gnolls and orcs leaves local craftsmen reliant on Elwynn for essential metal goods. The delivery answers Verner's desperate need for equipment, and Argus includes a stern bill of sale so the Redridge craftsman knows frontier survival comes at a steep price.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="The crate holds fifty iron horseshoes forged by Smith Argus in Goldshire. An attached bill demands payment from the buyer.",al={"contents of crate","what is in the crate","horseshoe crate contents"},it="item"},{q="Who ordered this crate?",a="Verner Osgood commissioned the horseshoes. He is a tradesman and craftsman in Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, and needs them to keep his work and local draft animals running.",al={"who wants the horseshoes","verner horseshoes","crate recipient"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who crafted these horseshoes?",a="Smith Argus, Goldshire's blacksmith in Elwynn Forest, forged the horseshoes, packed the crate, and prepared it for delivery.",al={"who made the horseshoes","blacksmith in goldshire","smith argus"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Verner need horseshoes from Elwynn?",a="Hostile Blackrock orcs and gnolls besiege Lakeshire, leaving the frontier settlement isolated and short of raw materials and trade goods. Local workers must bring basic supplies from safer settlements such as Goldshire.",al={"why redridge needs shoes","why import horseshoes","lakeshire supply problem"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="The Crate of Horseshoes is a heavy wooden delivery box containing fifty newly forged horseshoes, packed alongside an invoice note. Smith Argus prepared the shipment in Goldshire to fulfill an order placed by Verner Osgood, who desperately needs fresh iron to keep draft animals and mounts shod in nearby Lakeshire.",al={"what is crate of horseshoes","crate of horseshoes lore","what are the horseshoes for"},it="identity",add="50a21bee"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The delivery shows the steady demand for basic smithing goods along frontier roads that connect the towns. Lakeshire depends on Goldshire's anvil to keep its draft animals working.",["faction:Alliance"]="Couriers carrying goods between Elwynn and Redridge keep the kingdom's fragile trade routes open and outlying garrisons equipped, even as Stormwind withholds military reinforcement."},kw={"crate of horseshoes","elwynn forest","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","verner osgood"},rel={"quest:119","quest:118","npc:verner-osgood","zone:elwynn","quest:124","quest:126","quest:122","topic:gnoll"},src={"Crate of Horseshoes","Return to Verner"}}
E["item:crystal-kelp-frond"] = {t="item",n="Crystal Kelp Frond",z="elwynn",s="Murlocs carry Crystal Kelp Fronds from the ocean to Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest. William Pestle in Goldshire seeks them for an invisibility liquor.",h="Murlocs carry Crystal Kelp Fronds from the ocean to Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Rare Aquatic Reagent",b="Crystal Kelp Fronds come from saltwater oceans, so their presence in Elwynn Forest’s fresh water is unusual. Murloc tribes along Crystal Lake’s shores gather and keep the fronds for reasons of their own. Alchemists value their strange power to distort sight. William Pestle in Goldshire uses them as the chief ingredient in an invisibility liquor, meant to help sweethearts slip past watchful family eyes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does crystal kelp naturally grow?",a="Crystal kelp grows in saltwater oceans. It is not native to freshwater lakes, though murlocs gather the cuttings and carry them to places such as Crystal Lake.",al={"where does crystal kelp grow","crystal kelp origin","kelp habitat"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the murlocs at Crystal Lake have ocean kelp?",a="The entry gives no reason the murlocs at Crystal Lake have ocean kelp. It says they gather and keep the fronds for reasons of their own.",al={"why do murlocs have kelp","murloc kelp reason"}},{q="Who wants Crystal Kelp Fronds in Goldshire?",a="William Pestle, an apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, wants Crystal Kelp Fronds. He uses them to brew invisibility liquor for Maybell Maclure, so she can slip away from her family vineyard to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who needs crystal kelp","william pestle kelp"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What properties does crystal kelp possess?",a="Alchemists value crystal kelp fronds for their ability to distort sight. William Pestle uses them in an invisibility liquor meant to help sweethearts pass unseen.",al={"kelp effects","what does crystal kelp do"},it="power"},{q="What is a Crystal Kelp Frond?",a="A Crystal Kelp Frond is a cutting from crystal kelp, a rare aquatic plant native to the ocean. Although primarily marine vegetation, these fronds are sometimes gathered and kept by murlocs around freshwater bodies such as Crystal Lake. Alchemists value the fronds for their potent, translucent properties, which can be harnessed to brew specialized draughts such as invisibility liquor.",al={"what is crystal kelp frond","crystal kelp info","what is crystal kelp"},it="identity",add="e295764f"},{q="Why does anyone want Crystal Kelp Fronds?",a="William Pestle, the alchemist in Goldshire, requires crystal kelp fronds to brew a potent invisibility liquor. He intends to use the concoction to aid young Maybell Maclure, allowing her to slip away from her family's watchful vineyard undetected to secretly meet her forbidden beau, Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who needs crystal kelp","why gather crystal kelp fronds","use for crystal kelp"},it="why_wanted",add="8bde59b0"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Crystal Kelp Fronds are aquatic, unlike herbs rooted in soil, and do not grow in standard herb nodes across Elwynn. Herbalists and gatherers must pry them from local murlocs, who keep the fronds."},kw={"crystal kelp","crystal kelp frond","crystal lake","goldshire","invisibility liquor","murloc","william pestle"},rel={"quest:112","subzone:crystal-lake","npc:william-pestle","item:invisibility-liquor","topic:murloc","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","subzone:maclure-vineyards"},src={"Crystal Kelp Frond","Collecting Kelp"}}
E["item:garrick-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Garrick's Head",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire's vineyards, Garrick Padfoot's severed head proves the cutthroat is dead. The authorities at Northshire Abbey require it to pay the bounty.",h="At Northshire's vineyards, Garrick Padfoot's severed head proves the cutthroat is dead.",sec={{t="A Bandit's End",b="Garrick Padfoot and his gang harassed Northshire Valley's farmers and merchants for weeks. With Stormwind's defenses stretched thin, Garrick made his hideout in a shack near the vineyards and raided passing trade. Local guards were occupied by kobolds and Defias bandits, so Deputy Willem offered a bounty for the outlaw's death. He sought someone willing to kill Garrick and bring back proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Garrick Padfoot?",a="Garrick Padfoot was a cutthroat who terrorized Northshire Valley's farmers, vineyard workers, and traveling merchants. He set up an outpost with his gang east of Northshire Abbey, across the river.",al={"who is garrick","garrick padfoot lore","who was padfoot"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a severed head needed to collect the bounty?",a="Deputy Willem and the Northshire authorities require proof of Garrick's death before paying the bounty.",al={"why his head","proof of death","why take garricks head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was Garrick Padfoot hiding?",a="Padfoot hid in a small wooden shack east of Northshire Abbey, across the river bridge near the Northshire vineyards.",al={"where is garrick","garrick shack location","where to find garrick padfoot"},it="place"},{q="Who pays the bounty for Garrick's head?",a="Deputy Willem posted the bounty and pays it when he receives Garrick's head. He is stationed just outside Northshire Abbey's entrance.",al={"who wants garricks head","turn in garricks head","who turned in garrick head"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Garrick's Head?",a="This severed head is the gruesome proof of the demise of Garrick Padfoot, a notorious cutthroat who has terrorized local farmers and merchants across Northshire Valley. Bringing this trophy back to the Abbey confirms his band of brigands has lost its ringleader.",al={"what is garricks head","garrick head item","who does this head belong to"},it="identity",add="cb1a40d1"},{q="Where does Garrick's Head come from?",a="It is claimed directly from Garrick Padfoot himself. The rogue made his camp at a small shack nestled near the Northshire vineyards, across the river to the east, surrounded by loyal thugs protecting his plunder.",al={"where do you get garricks head","who drops garricks head","garricks head source"},it="origin",add="79b2de99"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, taking Padfoot's head is an early blow against the lawlessness spreading through Elwynn Forest.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, eliminating Padfoot shows local ruffians that banditry will meet deadly, professional blades."},kw={"bounty","deputy willem","elwynn forest","garrick padfoot","garrick's head","northshire abbey","northshire valley"},rel={"quest:6","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Garrick's Head","Bounty on Garrick Padfoot"}}
E["item:glyph-of-azora"] = {t="item",n="Glyph of Azora",z="elwynn",s="From the Tower of Azora, Theocritus uses Glyphs of Azora to watch distant threats. The inscribed stones extend the Eye of Azora's reach, letting him read enemies' thoughts and plans.",h="From the Tower of Azora, Theocritus uses Glyphs of Azora to watch distant threats.",sec={{t="Eyes Across the Border",b="Theocritus watches hostile powers from his tower in Elwynn Forest. His crystal relic, the Eye of Azora, lets him see across great distances, but cannot reach into the minds or plans of his adversaries. He places small focuses called Glyphs of Azora on surfaces far away to carry his magic farther. Each glyph anchors his power, letting him read enemy intentions and project his voice across miles to speak with field agents.",sp=0},{t="Espionage in Redridge",b="In the Redridge Mountains, Theocritus places glyphs in hostile territory. He fixes the first to an ancient lion statue overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar, where his rogue rival, the dark wizard Morganth, holds his stronghold. Through the glyph, Theocritus enters Morganth's mind and finds a dispute between the renegade mage and the Blackrock orcs at nearby Stonewatch Keep. To learn the cause, he sends a second glyph into the heights of the keep's intact watchtower, concealed in a discarded liquor jar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus uses a Glyph of Azora to extend the Eye of Azora's reach. Set in a distant place, it anchors his magic so he can read his adversaries' thoughts and plans and speak with field agents across miles.",al={"what does glyph of azora do","why use glyph of azora","glyph of azora purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus created the Glyph of Azora. He lives in the Tower of Azora along Elwynn Forest's eastern border.",al={"who made the glyph","glyph of azora creator","theocritus glyph"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the Glyphs of Azora placed?",a="One glyph is fixed to an ancient lion statue overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar. A second is hidden in a discarded liquor jar in the intact watchtower at Stonewatch Keep.",al={"where do i put the glyph","glyph placement locations","where does glyph go"},it="target"},{q="Why is Theocritus spying on the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is Morganth's stronghold. The rogue dark wizard is Theocritus's rival, and the glyph lets Theocritus read his thoughts and plans.",al={"why spy on morganth","theocritus ilgalar","morganth feud"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the glyph allow Theocritus to speak to people?",a="Once fixed to a distant surface, the glyph anchors Theocritus's magic and lets him project his voice across miles to speak with field agents.",al={"talking glyph","theocritus voice in glyph","can the glyph talk"},it="power"},{q="What is the Glyph of Azora?",a="The Glyph of Azora is an enchanted arcane marker crafted by the wizard Theocritus at the Tower of Azora. Working in tandem with his scrying focus, the Eye of Azora, these inscribed stones serve as remote listening posts. Once affixed to a surface near an area of interest, a glyph allows Theocritus to delve into the minds and thoughts of his targets from across great distances, as well as project his voice to whoever stands beside it.",al={"what is glyph of azora","glyph of azora item","tell me about glyph of azora"},it="identity",add="16152ed3"},{q="Why does Theocritus want you to plant the Glyph of Azora?",a="Theocritus relies on these glyphs to conduct deep espionage against dangerous adversaries in Redridge. While the Eye of Azora lets him view places from afar, it cannot pierce minds without a conduit nearby. Placing a glyph near the Tower of Ilgalar lets him probe the thoughts and future plans of his rival, the renegade mage Morganth, while planting another near Stonewatch Keep helps him unravel Morganth's contention with the Blackrock orcs.",al={"why plant glyph of azora","why does theocritus want the glyph placed","glyph of azora purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="7c5a9e02"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can use arcane divination to extend crystal scrying into targeted telepathy and remote sensory relays.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can use the glyphs to gather intelligence on Morganth and the Blackrock orcs at Stonewatch Keep."},kw={"glyph of azora","morganth","redridge","scrying","stonewatch keep","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"npc:theocritus","quest:94","quest:248","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:249","subzone:stonewatch-keep","topic:mage","zone:elwynn"},src={"Glyph of Azora","A Watchful Eye","Looking Further"}}
E["item:glyphic-letter"] = {t="item",n="Glyphic Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Glyphic Letter calls promising novitiates to arcane study. After early service to the garrison, they are summoned upstairs to Khelden Bremen, the resident mage trainer.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Glyphic Letter calls promising novitiates to arcane study.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Arcane",b="Khelden Bremen seals the Glyphic Letter with his personal insignia. Apprentice spellcasters receive it after proving their discipline in Northshire Valley. The summons calls them away from basic field duties and into dedicated magical instruction within the abbey. Bremen tests each student's resolve before they take up the arcane, with its dangerous forces, unyielding scrutiny, and burdens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen writes and seals the Glyphic Letter as a summons to instruction. It directs aspiring human mages to find him in Northshire Abbey's upper chambers for formal arcane schooling.",al={"what is this letter","glyphic letter item","khelden letter"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen, the mage trainer at Northshire Abbey, seals the letter with his insignia. Garrison command hands it over after an apprentice proves their mettle against nearby vermin.",al={"who wrote it","who gave me glyphic letter","letter sender"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I take the Glyphic Letter?",a="Take the letter inside Northshire Abbey. Enter behind Marshal McBride, follow the left corridor, climb the stairs, and look toward the back room where Khelden Bremen teaches the arcane.",al={"where to go","where is khelden bremen","khelden location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Khelden send for young mages?",a="Khelden wants to test your determination. He warns that pursuing the arcane invites both fear and respect, and means challenging potent forces. He needs to know you have the will to endure that fate.",al={"why does khelden want me","mage trainer reason","what does khelden want"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Khelden Bremen want the Glyphic Letter delivered to you?",a="The letter serves as an official summons and a trial of resolve for fledgling mages. Sealed with his personal insignia, Khelden Bremen's note lays out the perilous and daunting path of the arcane, warning you of the fear and challenges that accompany the pursuit of forbidden knowledge. Handing it to you ensures you are willing to face that fate before he undertakes your formal training.",al={"why glyphic letter","why was i given the glyphic letter","purpose of glyphic letter"},it="why_wanted",add="4321b6bd"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, this marked dispatch calls you upstairs to begin formal study of the Alliance's arcane traditions under Khelden Bremen.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin your service to Stormwind's magical disciplines with this summons. Northshire Abbey has sheltered students of the arcane throughout the kingdom's history."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage trainer","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey"},rel={"quest:3104","npc:khelden-bremen","subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:mage","zone:elwynn"},src={"Glyphic Letter","Glyphic Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:gold-dust"] = {t="item",n="Gold Dust",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, kobolds gather and hoard flecks of gold in the mines. Local buyers pay for the dust, while miners seek whole veins of ore.",h="In Elwynn Forest, kobolds gather and hoard flecks of gold in the mines.",sec={{t="A Pouch Full of Scraps",b="Kobolds dig through the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines beneath Elwynn Forest. They keep the gold dust they find in pockets and pouches instead of refining it. Local peddlers and fences want these scraps, hoping to profit without paying official smelting tariffs.",sp=0},{t="Goldshire's Black Market",b="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" asks travelers to bring him recovered gold dust. He says he offers the best price in town, trading coin and suspicious tokens for raw dust on behalf of unnamed associates. Travelers retrieve the gold from kobolds, while the brokers secure wealth beneath the noses of the Stormwind guards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Gold Dust come from?",a="Kobolds throughout Elwynn Forest carry Gold Dust. Miners, tunnelers, geomancers, and their leader Goldtooth gather and hoard it as they dig through the hills.",al={"how to get gold dust","gold dust drop","where find gold dust"},it="origin"},{q="Which mines hold the most kobolds carrying Gold Dust?",a="Kobolds carrying dust overrun both Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire, and Jasperlode Mine, to the northeast.",al={"where are the mines","best mine for gold dust","mine locations"},gp=true},{q="Who buys Gold Dust in Elwynn Forest?",a="Remy \"Two Times,\" a shady dealer outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, buys collected pouches of Gold Dust for money and tokens from his associates.",al={"who wants gold dust","remy two times gold dust","turn in gold dust"},gp=true},{q="Why do kobolds carry dust instead of ingots?",a="Kobolds lack the discipline and infrastructure to smelt ore properly. As they dig through the rock with crude pickaxes, loose gold dust gathers on their belongings and in small pouches they carry as shiny trinkets.",al={"why do kobolds have dust","kobold gold"}},{q="What is Gold Dust?",a="Gold Dust consists of fine, raw flecks of precious gold mined by the kobold infestations lurking beneath Elwynn Forest. Rather than refined currency or poured bullion, it is the raw residue kobolds chip directly out of rich veins in places like the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines.",al={"what is gold dust","gold dust item","about gold dust"},it="identity",add="38570104"},{q="Why does Remy Two Times want Gold Dust?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire buys up raw gold dust for his own trade and shadowy associates. Kobolds possess little sense for smelting ingots, leaving plenty of untracked mineral wealth on their bodies for anyone bold enough to take it from them and sell it off.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","why want gold dust","remy two times gold dust why"},it="why_wanted",add="4a74ebdb"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners seek solid veins of copper and tin with pick and pan. Kobold dust suggests Elwynn's underground passages hold richer lodes than standard surveys reveal.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can learn how the underworld moves unrefined, untracked dust through shady dealers like Remy \"Two Times,\" hiding raw wealth from Stormwind's magistrates."},kw={"elwynn","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","goldtooth","jasperlode","kobold","remy two times"},rel={"quest:47","npc:remy-two-times","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:87"},src={"Gold Dust","Gold Dust Exchange"}}
E["item:grape-manifest"] = {t="item",n="Grape Manifest",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, the Grape Manifest records grapes recovered from Milly Osworth's vineyard after brigands seized the harvest. The fruit is bound for the abbey's cellars.",h="At Northshire Abbey, the Grape Manifest records grapes recovered from Milly Osworth's vineyard after brigands...",sec={{t="A Record of the Harvest",b="Milly Osworth tends a vineyard in Northshire Valley, where local farms help feed Northshire Abbey. Defias bandits seized the harvest, putting the abbey's supply of fresh fruit and fermentable grapes at risk. The Grape Manifest records the grapes reclaimed from the fields and their quantity, so the abbey's quartermasters can account for their stores and prepare barrels for fermentation.",sp=0},{t="The Abbey's Cellarer",b="Brother Neals oversees Northshire Abbey's food and drink, and he enjoys sampling its wine in the quiet of the bell tower. The manifest tells him the grapes are coming, helping ensure monks and visiting recruits have drink. For the abbey's brothers, each saved bushel is a victory for their stores and a blessing from the Holy Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grape Manifest?",a="The Grape Manifest is an inventory written by Milly Osworth that records the harvest recovered from her overrun vineyard. It tracks the fresh grapes being delivered to Northshire Abbey.",al={"what is grape manifest","grape manifest item"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives the manifest?",a="Brother Neals receives the manifest. He oversees the abbey's food and wine stores and often samples vintages in Northshire Abbey's bell tower.",al={"who gets grape manifest","who do i give grape manifest to","where does grape manifest go"},it="target"},{q="Why were the grapes in danger?",a="Defias brigands descended on Northshire Valley and drove Milly Osworth from her vineyard, putting the harvest at risk and cutting off the abbey's fresh fruit until recruits intervened.",al={"why did grapes need saving","vineyard brigands","what happened to milly harvest"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Brother Neals do with the grapes?",a="Brother Neals uses the grapes to replenish the abbey's food stores and ferment fresh Northshire wine for the resident brotherhood and visiting defenders.",al={"what is grape used for","abbey wine"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Grape Manifest come from, and who made it?",a="The manifest is drawn up by Milly Osworth, a farmer working the vineyards of Northshire Valley. After you help her drive back the Defias brigands who overran her fields and recover her harvested crop, she prepares this record to document the saved yield.",al={"who wrote grape manifest","where did the grape manifest come from","grape manifest origin"},it="origin",add="a2f30a46"},{q="Why is the Grape Manifest needed?",a="Brother Neals manages the stores of food and drink for Northshire Abbey. Milly sends the manifest to notify him that her harvest has been rescued from the bandits, allowing the abbey's vintners to count on fresh fruit for pressing their wine.",al={"why does brother neals want the grape manifest","grape manifest purpose","why need grape manifest"},it="why_wanted",add="cbb35726"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For cooks, the manifest shows how field harvests supply the abbey's stores and help feed its monastic community.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the early struggles of Stormwind's heartland: even monastic life and simple harvests need armed defense against roaming outlaws."},kw={"brother neals","elwynn","grape manifest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","vineyard","wine"},rel={"quest:3905","npc:brother-neals","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},src={"Grape Manifest","Grape Manifest (quest)"}}
E["item:hallowed-letter"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Letter",z="elwynn",s="Priestess Anetta calls young priests from Northshire Valley to Northshire Abbey. Her letter begins their study of the Holy Light.",h="Priestess Anetta calls young priests from Northshire Valley to Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="A Call to Faith",b="The Hallowed Letter bears Priestess Anetta’s personal mark and reaches fledgling priests after their first trials against the kobold camps of Northshire Valley. She sees the Holy Light’s spark within each novice and urges them to enter the abbey and dedicate themselves to its service. Dark forces still linger across Azeroth in the wake of the Third War. The priesthood gathers those able to heal, protect, and guide an empire struggling to keep order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Letter?",a="The Hallowed Letter is Priestess Anetta’s introductory missive to newly arrived priests in Northshire Abbey, summoning them for their first class instruction.",al={"what is hallowed letter","hallowed letter item","priest letter northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the letter?",a="Priestess Anetta’s insignia marks the letter. She trains and guides young human priests arriving at Northshire.",al={"who sent the letter","who is the author","letter sender"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the priesthood calling for new initiates right now?",a="Azeroth remains in turmoil, and remnants of the Burning Legion still haunt it. Kalimdor faces new trials, while Stormwind needs compassionate healers and leaders to rebuild and protect its people.",al={"why do priests need help","state of the world","priest lore 25 adp"},it="motive"},{q="What should I do after reading the letter?",a="Carry the letter into Northshire Abbey and speak with Priestess Anetta. She will accept your pledge to the Light and train you in new priestly disciplines as your journey unfolds.",al={"where do i take the letter","hallowed letter quest turn in","who to talk to"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Anetta want you to have the Hallowed Letter?",a="Priestess Anetta sends the letter to summon promising initiates of the Holy Light within Northshire Abbey. Recognizing that you have shown promise in defending the valley, she wishes to introduce herself, guide your spiritual devotion, and offer deeper instruction in the priesthood's sacred arts.",al={"why hallowed letter","why did anetta send the letter","purpose of hallowed letter"},it="why_wanted",add="0a342f04"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, this missive recognizes you as an instrument of the Holy Light and binds you to the trainers of Northshire Abbey.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you carry on Northshire Valley’s tradition of holy duty, practiced there since before the First War."},kw={"anetta","elwynn forest","hallowed letter","holy light","northshire abbey","priest","priestess anetta"},rel={"quest:3103","npc:priestess-anetta","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:priest","topic:light","zone:elwynn","topic:burning-legion","topic:kobold"},src={"Hallowed Letter","Hallowed Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:heartswood-core"] = {t="item",n="Heartswood Core",z="elwynn",s="Warlocks in Stormwind City use the Heartswood Core to summon a succubus. Gakin the Darkbinder provides the enchanted ritual focus, crafted from an ancient tree’s wood, to pierce the Twisting Nether and draw the demon into an arcane summoning circle.",h="Warlocks in Stormwind City use the Heartswood Core to summon a succubus.",sec={{t="A Focus for the Nether",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter, warlocks perform rites beyond the city watch’s gaze. The Heartswood Core channels the magic needed to begin a binding ritual. Crafted from the wood of an ancient tree, it holds enough lingering magic to pierce the veil between worlds. At a consecrated summoning circle, an initiate focuses dark arts through the core and opens a passage to the Twisting Nether, drawing a succubus across the divide.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Binding",b="A warlock who summons a demon must still prove dominance over its cunning and seductive nature to control it. Gakin gives the Heartswood Core to promising practitioners so they can face the summoned demon in combat. Succubi prey on weakness and can overwhelm feeble minds, making the encounter a deadly rite of passage. The aspiring warlock must subdue the fiend and return the spent core to Gakin to prove their will is strong enough to bind the servant permanently.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Heartswood Core used for?",a="Warlocks use the Heartswood Core at the summoning circle beneath the Slaughtered Lamb to open a portal to the Twisting Nether and draw a succubus into our realm. You must fight and bind the summoned demon.",al={"what does heartswood core do","heartswood core use","purpose of heartswood core"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Heartswood Core?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder, a master warlock, provides the Heartswood Core and trains novices in the hidden catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter.",al={"where do i get heartswood core","who gives heartswood core"}},{q="Where must the core be used?",a="Use the core at the summoning circle in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, deep below Stormwind’s streets.",al={"heartswood core location","where to summon succubus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the ritual is finished?",a="After you summon the succubus, defeat it in combat and send it back to the void. Then return the Heartswood Core to Gakin the Darkbinder to learn how to command the demon at will.",al={"what do i do after summoning","turn in heartswood core"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Heartswood Core?",a="The Heartswood Core is an enchanted occult relic crafted specifically for summoning rituals. Prepared by dark magic practitioners, it acts as a magical catalyst powerful enough to pierce the veil between worlds and draw a succubus out of the Twisting Nether into a summoning circle.",al={"heartswood core lore","what is heartswood core","heartswood item"},it="identity",add="34d5c17e"},{q="Where does the Heartswood Core come from, and who made it?",a="The core is prepared using raw Heartswood recovered from the ruins of Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale, fashioned and empowered under the direction of Gakin the Darkbinder. Gakin entrusts the completed relic to promising warlocks studying beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind.",al={"who made heartswood core","heartswood core origin","how was heartswood core made"},it="origin",add="a2df89b9"},{q="Why does Gakin want the Heartswood Core used?",a="A warlock seeking to bind a succubus requires an anchor of immense power to open a gateway into the void. Without the Heartswood Core, you cannot complete the ritual spell needed to manifest the demon and subdue its treacherous mind.",al={"why use heartswood core","heartswood core purpose lore","why want heartswood core"},it="why_wanted",add="cef9a99d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As an Alliance warlock, you use the Heartswood Core as an essential training relic to summon and master your first succubus."},kw={"gakin the darkbinder","heartswood core","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","succubus","summoning circle","the binding","warlock"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","quest:1739","quest:1738","quest:1685","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:elwynn"},src={"Heartswood Core","The Binding (Succubus, Stormwind)"}}
E["item:huge-gnoll-claw"] = {t="item",n="Huge Gnoll Claw",z="elwynn",s="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger’s huge claw is sought as proof of his death. Stormwind’s authorities in Goldshire require it for the bounty.",h="In southwestern Elwynn, Hogger’s huge claw is sought as proof of his death.",sec={{t="Bounty Hunter's Proof",b="Hogger has terrorized the southern woodlands of Forest's Edge for months. Patrols have failed to stop the brute, and the local garrison cannot corral or subdue him. The Stormwind Army, stretched thin across Elwynn, posted an open bounty on his head. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire requires clear proof before paying it. Hogger's oversized claw leaves no doubt that the notorious marauder has fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw used for?",a="Bring Hogger's claw to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire as proof of his death, and you can collect the posted bounty.",al={"what do i do with hogger claw","huge gnoll claw use","who wants the claw"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where does this claw come from?",a="The claw comes from Hogger, an elite gnoll who wanders near the Riverpaw camps along the southwestern borders of Forest's Edge in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who drops the claw","how to get huge gnoll claw","where to find huge gnoll claw"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want a claw instead of the head?",a="Hogger is abnormally large for a gnoll, and his immense claws are distinct and instantly recognizable. One proves to the Stormwind Army that the notorious marauder has been slain.",al={"why proof of demise claw","why not hoggers head","dughan bounty proof"},it="motive"},{q="Can I get another claw if I lose it?",a="Yes. If you lose the claw before taking it to Marshal Dughan, you can hunt Hogger again in southwestern Elwynn Forest and claim a replacement.",al={"lost huge gnoll claw","can i get claw again","hogger claw respawn"},gp=true},{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw?",a="The Huge Gnoll Claw is severed physical proof of the demise of Hogger, a notorious and massive gnoll terrorizing southwestern Elwynn Forest. Because Hogger has overpowered every attempt at capture by the local authorities, this distinctive talon serves as undeniable evidence for Marshal Dughan that the brute has finally been slain.",al={"what is huge gnoll claw","huge gnoll claw info","hogger claw"},it="identity",add="d9093290"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want the Huge Gnoll Claw?",a="Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army posted a bounty on Hogger after the giant beast evaded and overpowered their patrols. Dughan requires the gnoll's massive claw as proof of his death before he will disburse the bounty reward in Goldshire, finally putting an end to the headache Hogger caused his men.",al={"why does dughan want the claw","who wants huge gnoll claw","why want huge gnoll claw"},it="why_wanted",add="7983cdb8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, claiming Hogger's claw rids the kingdom's heartland of its most infamous woodland terror. The claw proves your valor to Marshal Dughan and the beleaguered garrison at Goldshire.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, securing the claw of a predator who routinely overpowered armed squads shows your skill at tracking and hunting beasts."},kw={"bounty","elwynn forest","goldshire","hogger","huge gnoll claw","marshal dughan","riverpaw"},rel={"npc:hogger","quest:176","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","subzone:forest-s-edge","topic:stormwind-army","topic:gnoll"},src={"Huge Gnoll Claw","Wanted: \"Hogger\""}}
E["item:invisibility-liquor"] = {t="item",n="Invisibility Liquor",z="elwynn",s="Invisibility Liquor gives Maybell Maclure a way to slip from her family's sight and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield. Their households are locked in a feud.",h="Invisibility Liquor gives Maybell Maclure a way to slip from her family's sight and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",sec={{t="A Potion for Star-Crossed Lovers",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield seeks a quiet meeting with Maybell Maclure, though their families' feud keeps the households apart. Their kin watch closely, and ordinary secrecy is not enough. Invisibility Liquor lets the drinker pass unseen across the disputed farmland.",sp=0},{t="Unorthodox Elwynn Alchemy",b="Crystal Kelp Fronds from waters where murlocs dwell go into the brew. When Maybell Maclure drinks it, she vanishes from sight and slips into the woods for a secret meeting.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Invisibility Liquor do?",a="Invisibility Liquor is an alcoholic drink with magic that makes the drinker invisible for a short time.",al={"liquor effects","invisibility brew","what does it do"},it="power"},{q="Who uses the Invisibility Liquor?",a="Maybell Maclure receives Invisibility Liquor so she can leave her family's sight and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield, despite their households' feud.",al={"who drinks it","maybell maclure liquor"},it="target"},{q="How is the liquor made?",a="The liquor is brewed with Crystal Kelp Fronds gathered from riverbeds and lake shores in Elwynn Forest, where murlocs hoard the plants.",al={"liquor ingredients","crystal kelp liquor"},it="origin"},{q="Can players drink the Invisibility Liquor themselves?",a="No. Invisibility Liquor is meant for delivery to Maybell Maclure, so she can slip away from her family.",al={"can i drink it","drink invisibility liquor"},gp=true},{q="What is Invisibility Liquor?",a="Invisibility Liquor is a potent alchemical draught concocted in Elwynn Forest. While ostensibly an alcoholic beverage, it carries magical properties derived from crystal kelp fronds, temporarily granting whoever drinks it complete invisibility from mortal eyes.",al={"what is invisibility liquor","invisibility liquor lore","what kind of drink is invisibility liquor"},it="identity",add="19edabb3"},{q="Why does anyone want Invisibility Liquor?",a="The liquor is sought to resolve a forbidden romance. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught on opposite sides of their families' bitter Elwynn feud, and the draught allows Maybell to slip away unseen past her watchful kin to visit her beloved.",al={"why need invisibility liquor","who wants invisibility liquor","why do they want the liquor"},it="why_wanted",add="f0e7bc08"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the Kirin Tor arcanists spend years mastering illusions and invisibility spells. Elwynn locals make a rough imitation with fermented spirits and waterlogged kelp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know the Stonefield and Maclure clans' rural feud reaches bitter extremes."},kw={"crystal kelp","elwynn forest","invisibility liquor","maybell maclure","stonefield feud","the escape","tommy joe stonefield"},rel={"quest:114","npc:maybell-maclure","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","item:crystal-kelp-frond","zone:elwynn","topic:alliance"},src={"Invisibility Liquor","The Escape (Alliance)"}}
E["item:jennea-s-flask"] = {t="item",n="Jennea's Flask",z="elwynn",s="At the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind, Jennea Cannon sends apprentices to Mirror Lake for water. They bring the sample back for arcane analysis.",h="At the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind, Jennea Cannon sends apprentices to Mirror Lake for water.",sec={{t="A Vessel for Arcane Research",b="After magical struggles across Azeroth, arcane currents have torn loose from their ancient channels. Jennea Cannon seeks to learn how these shifts have affected Elwynn Forest. She gives promising apprentices a glass flask and sends them southwest of Stormwind's gates to the base of Mirror Lake's waterfall. The flask protects the water sample on the journey back to the Wizard's Sanctum, where it can be examined for arcane disturbances.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Waters",b="Jennea's flask lets Stormwind's mages check whether shifting ley lines have tainted Mirror Lake. If the water carries harmful magic, the surrounding life and anyone who drinks from it could suffer strange afflictions. A sample can reveal magical residue before tainted currents spread through the countryside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Jennea's Flask used for?",a="You use Jennea's Flask to gather water from the waterfall at Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest.",al={"flask purpose","what does the flask do","use of flask"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you this flask?",a="Jennea Cannon, a mage trainer in Stormwind City's Wizard's Sanctum, gives you the flask.",al={"who gives flask","jennea flask source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Jennea want water from Mirror Lake?",a="Recent mystical conflicts have disrupted the flow of magic across the world. Jennea fears stray currents may be seeping into Elwynn's waters and endangering anyone who drinks from the lake.",al={"why mirror lake water","why water sample"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do you fill the flask?",a="Fill the flask at the base of the waterfall that flows into Mirror Lake, southwest of Stormwind's main gates in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where to fill flask","flask location","lake location"},gp=true},{q="What is Jennea's Flask?",a="It is a specialized sample container provided by Jennea Cannon, an instructor in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind. She entrusts it to promising apprentices to collect water directly from the waterfall at Mirror Lake so she can inspect it for magical contamination.",al={"what is jenneas flask","jennea flask","jennea's flask"},it="identity",add="b836f408"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, carrying this flask is one of your first field tasks for the Wizard's Sanctum. It tests your ability to handle delicate arcane research and watch for changes in ley lines."},kw={"elwynn forest","jennea cannon","jennea's flask","mirror lake","stormwind","water sample","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","quest:1861","item:mirror-lake-water-sample","quest:1860","zone:elwynn","subzone:stormwind-gate","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Jennea's Flask","Mirror Lake (quest)"}}
E["item:large-candle"] = {t="item",n="Large Candle",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn's mines, kobolds carry Large Candles on their heads for light and wax. Their flames guide them through dark tunnels, and apothecaries value the wax.",h="In Elwynn's mines, kobolds carry Large Candles on their heads for light and wax.",sec={{t="Subterranean Light and Wax",b="Kobolds use candle flame to find their way through the dark shafts beneath Elwynn Forest. They fasten the tapers to their heads, and Kobold Miners, Tunnelers, and Geomancers defend them fiercely from intruders. Though crudely made, the Large Candles carried in Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine hold valuable wax. Surface tradesmen cannot easily produce it in bulk, so the candles are both tools for the kobolds and a commodity for alchemists.",sp=0},{t="Trade and the Apothecary",b="William Pestle, an apothecary operative from Stormwind City, gathers Large Candles at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. His family runs an apothecary, and he needs rendered wax for its concoctions, balms, and ointments. Pestle hires passing adventurers to clear the infested mines and take candles from the kobolds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Large Candles used for?",a="William Pestle collects Large Candles in Goldshire for the apothecary he runs with his brother in Stormwind City. They render the candles down for wax used in ointments, balms, and alchemical recipes.",al={"large candle use","why get large candles","who wants large candles"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Large Candles be found?",a="Kobolds carry Large Candles in Elwynn Forest's mines, especially Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the east. Tunnelers, Miners, and Geomancers carry them.",al={"large candle location","where to get large candles","kobold candle drops"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why do kobolds carry candles on their heads?",a="Kobolds use candlelight to dig and find their way through dark underground tunnels. They fasten candles to their heads to keep their hands free for pickaxes, geomantic spellcasting, and weapons.",al={"why do kobolds have candles","kobold head candle lore"},it="history"},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary operative from Stormwind City who conducts business at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn. He gathers raw ingredients from the wilderness and mines to supply the apothecary shop he runs with his brother.",al={"william pestle lore","who is the apothecary guy in goldshire"},it="people"},{q="What is a Large Candle?",a="A Large Candle is a crude, substantial wax taper carried by the kobolds dwelling in the mines of Elwynn Forest. Kobolds are notoriously protective of their light sources, using these hefty candles to pierce the darkness of subterranean tunnels like the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines while they dig for gold and minerals.",al={"what is large candle","large candle elwynn","large candle lore"},it="identity",add="05873d56"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners working the veins in Fargodeep and Jasperlode regularly run afoul of kobold infestations that covet both the gold and the light of Large Candles.",["faction:Alliance"]="By taking candles from kobolds in Elwynn, Alliance adventurers weaken the vermin in the mines and supply critical materials to Stormwind's apothecary trade."},kw={"fargodeep mine","goldshire","goldtooth","jasperlode mine","kobold candles","large candle","wax","william pestle"},rel={"quest:60","npc:william-pestle","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:87"},src={"Large Candle","Kobold Candles"}}
E["item:marshal-haggard-s-badge"] = {t="item",n="Marshal Haggard's Badge",z="elwynn",s="At his farm in Elwynn, Marshal Haggard has lost the badge he carried in Stormwind's service. Dead-tooth Jack stole it by trickery, and the Defias may use it to impersonate city officials.",h="At his farm in Elwynn, Marshal Haggard has lost the badge he carried in Stormwind's service.",sec={{t="A Stolen Insignia",b="Marshal Haggard retired to a small farmstead in the hills of Elwynn Forest, but his old Stormwind Marshal's badge still carries official weight. One night, Dead-tooth Jack, a Defias rogue, wore a Stormwind tabard and posed as Marshal Dughan, Goldshire's garrison commander. He tricked Haggard into believing his former peers needed the insignia for official business. The aging marshal handed it over without suspicion. Jack fled into the woods before Haggard saw through the ruse. In Defias hands, the emblem of Stormwind authority could let outlaws pass checkpoints or confuse local patrols.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Marshal Haggard's Badge?",a="It is an official badge of rank Marshal Haggard carried while serving the kingdom of Stormwind. Even in retirement, such a badge carries genuine authority.",al={"haggard badge","marshal badge","haggards badge"},it="identity"},{q="How did Dead-tooth Jack get the badge?",a="Dead-tooth Jack came to Marshal Haggard's home at night wearing a Stormwind tabard. Haggard mistook him for Marshal Dughan of Goldshire and handed over the badge when Jack asked for it.",al={"how was badge stolen","who stole the badge","dead-tooth jack trick"}},{q="Why is the badge dangerous in the hands of the Defias?",a="A Defias agent carrying the genuine badge and wearing a disguise could impersonate a high-ranking Stormwind official, bypass sentries, enter garrisons, or give false orders to town guards.",al={"why does jack want the badge","defias badge use","badge danger"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the badge kept?",a="Dead-tooth Jack locked the badge in his strongbox at his campsite south of Marshal Haggard's farm in Elwynn Forest.",al={"badge location","where to find badge","dead tooth strongbox"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, recovering Haggard's badge proves your mettle to a veteran of Stormwind's military. He rewards promising warriors with well-maintained surplus arms from his fighting days.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, retrieving the badge protects Stormwind's military command and keeps the Defias Brotherhood from undermining local defenses from within."},kw={"dead-tooth jack","defias","elwynn forest","marshal dughan","marshal haggard","marshal haggard's badge","stormwind","strongbox"},rel={"quest:1667","quest:1666","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Marshal Haggard's Badge","Dead-tooth Jack"}}
E["item:milly-s-harvest"] = {t="item",n="Milly's Harvest",z="elwynn",s="In the Northshire Vineyards, Milly's grapes lie abandoned after the Defias arrive. Crates and buckets of fruit remain at risk of theft or being crushed beneath the abbey guards' boots.",h="In the Northshire Vineyards, Milly's grapes lie abandoned after the Defias arrive.",sec={{t="A Fragile Yield",b="Milly Osworth gathers grapes in the Northshire Vineyards, where the harvest matters to local vintners and the abbey community. When armed brigands in red masks push into the fields, Milly flees to the abbey grounds. Her fresh-picked grapes remain scattered between the rows.",sp=0},{t="Collateral Damage",b="Stormwind guards watch the valley entrance, but too few soldiers leave Northshire vulnerable. The garrison promises to drive out the Defias, while Milly fears a drawn-out fight between guards and thieves will ruin her harvest. The crates may be trampled or carried off as provisions, costing Northshire one of its few peaceful harvests.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Milly's Harvest?",a="Milly's Harvest is the grapes Milly Osworth picked and packed into crates and buckets before Defias thugs seized the Northshire Vineyards.",al={"millys harvest","what is the harvest","milly osworth grapes"},it="identity"},{q="Why were the crates left behind in the vineyard?",a="Defias bandits raided the vineyards while Milly was harvesting, forcing her to leave the grapes behind and flee to Northshire Abbey.",al={"why abandoned","why did milly leave the grapes","why leave harvest"},it="origin"},{q="Why couldn't the Northshire guards retrieve the harvest?",a="Northshire's guards are stretched thin by Defias incursions and local threats. Milly also fears their boots could crush the grapes if they drive off the bandits.",al={"why not guards","why cant guards get it","stormwind guards northshire"}},{q="Who are the bandits threatening the harvest?",a="The bandits threatening the harvest belong to the Defias Brotherhood, a ring of outlaws and brigands causing unrest throughout Elwynn Forest.",al={"who took the vineyards","who is attacking the vineyard","vineyard bandits"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Milly want her harvest recovered?",a="Milly Osworth gathered the crop herself and relies on it for her livelihood, but had to abandon it when Defias bandits overran the vineyard. She fears that if the thieves do not make off with the fruit first, the Abbey's guards will trample the fragile grapes into the dirt while driving the brigands out.",al={"why does milly want the harvest","why recover milly's harvest","why are the grapes important"},it="why_wanted",add="1d7cbab4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The threat to Northshire's farmers shows how thin Stormwind's garrison has become. Everyday people rely on passing adventurers to protect their livelihoods.",["race:Human"]="As a human starting in Northshire, you may first meet the Defias Brotherhood's lawlessness on your own doorstep when you recover Milly's grapes."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","grapes","milly osworth","milly's harvest","northshire abbey","northshire vineyards"},rel={"quest:3904","quest:3903","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Milly's Harvest","Milly's Harvest (quest)"}}
E["item:mirror-lake-water-sample"] = {t="item",n="Mirror Lake Water Sample",z="elwynn",s="At Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, a flask of water is gathered for Jennea Cannon in Stormwind. The mages will test it for signs of altered arcane currents in local water.",h="At Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, a flask of water is gathered for Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.",sec={{t="Testing the Waters of Elwynn",b="Jennea Cannon sends promising apprentices to collect water from Mirror Lake. The lake lies just southwest of the Stormwind Gate, and they fill a specially prepared flask at the base of its waterfall. The Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind is concerned that the world's mystic channels remain unsettled after catastrophic conflicts. Its mages will examine the sample for stray magical taint in the waterways used by people nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mirror Lake Water Sample?",a="It is water from the waterfall at Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, held in Jennea's Flask. Novice mages gather it for testing at the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"mirror lake sample","water sample item","jennea water"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Jennea Cannon want this water sample?",a="Recent mystical upheavals across Azeroth disrupted stable magical currents. Jennea Cannon fears rogue magical energy may be altering the natural environment and poisoning local drinking water.",al={"why test mirror lake","jennea cannon purpose","magical taint water"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the sample collected?",a="The sample comes from the base of the waterfall flowing into Mirror Lake, southwest of the Stormwind Gate in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where to get sample","mirror lake location","sample waterfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens if the water turns out to be magically tainted?",a="Jennea Cannon worries that prolonged drinking from Mirror Lake could cause adverse magical effects if ley currents have contaminated the water supply.",al={"tainted water effects","is mirror lake poisoned"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Mirror Lake Water Sample come from, and who collected it?",a="The sample is collected directly from the base of the waterfall cascading into Mirror Lake, just southwest of Stormwind's gates in Elwynn Forest. Using an empty flask supplied by the mage trainer Jennea Cannon, you scoop up the water yourself on behalf of Stormwind's spellcasters so they can examine the state of the surrounding wild currents.",al={"where does mirror lake water sample come from","who made mirror lake water sample","origin of mirror lake water sample"},it="origin",add="935f4959"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage training under the Wizard's Sanctum, you fetch this sample as an early duty. It teaches you to watch environmental ley lines and recognize wild magical seepage."},kw={"arcane taint","elwynn forest","flask","jennea cannon","mirror lake","stormwind","water sample","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","quest:1861","item:jennea-s-flask","zone:elwynn","subzone:stormwind-gate","quest:1860"},src={"Mirror Lake Water Sample","Mirror Lake (quest)"}}
E["item:osric-s-crate"] = {t="item",n="Osric's Crate",z="elwynn",s="At Sentinel Hill, Osric's Crate brings armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia. The defenders face the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls without the Stormwind army.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Osric's Crate brings armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia.",sec={{t="Supplies for the Front",b="Westfall faces the Defias Brotherhood and marauding gnolls, while the Stormwind army remains absent. At Sentinel Hill, the People's Militia must make do without the crown's formal support. Osric's Crate holds freshly made armor from the capital, sent to Quartermaster Lewis to distribute among the volunteer fighters.",sp=0},{t="Winged Courier Network",b="Gryphons carry the crate from Dungar Longdrink's roost in Stormwind's Trade District to Thor at Sentinel Hill. The flight avoids the dangerous roads through Elwynn Forest and across the Westfall border, where bandits may ambush travelers. Gryphons help keep frontier garrisons supplied during wartime.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Osric's Crate?",a="Osric's Crate holds protective armor crafted in Stormwind. Quartermaster Lewis receives the delivery and prepares to distribute it among the fighters defending Sentinel Hill.",al={"what's in the crate","contents of osrics crate","osric crate contents"},it="item"},{q="Who is Osric?",a="Osric is an armorer in Stormwind who prepared the shipment for the People's Militia holding Westfall.",al={"who is osric","who sent osrics crate"}},{q="Who receives the crate?",a="Quartermaster Lewis receives the crate. He manages supplies and equipment for the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",al={"where does the crate go","who do i give osric's crate to","crate recipient"},it="target"},{q="Why is the crate delivered by gryphon?",a="Bandits and outlaws make the roads through Stormwind, Elwynn Forest, and Westfall perilous. The gryphon flight from Dungar Longdrink in Stormwind to Thor at Sentinel Hill carries the armor quickly and safely.",al={"why fly the crate","why use gryphons","osric crate flight"}},{q="What is Osric's Crate?",a="Osric's Crate is a shipment of armor dispatched from Stormwind City. It is prepared for the defenders stationed at Sentinel Hill in Westfall, who are desperately short on gear while holding out against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what is osrics crate","osric crate item","whats in osrics crate"},it="identity",add="34d354cb"},{q="Where does Osric's Crate come from, and who made it?",a="The crate comes from Stormwind City, prepared and dispatched by Osric to supply the People's Militia. Gryphon Master Dungar Longdrink entrusts it to you to carry by gryphon across the kingdom to Westfall.",al={"who made osrics crate","where did osric crate come from","osric crate origin"},it="origin",add="091b5cbb"},{q="Why does anyone want Osric's Crate?",a="Quartermaster Lewis and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill urgently need the armor inside. With Westfall abandoned by royal forces and overrun by outlaws, every scrap of protective gear is vital to keeping the defenders alive.",al={"why deliver osrics crate","why does lewis want osrics crate","osrics crate purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="11fb3015"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, every shipment of arms and armor that reaches Sentinel Hill helps keep the kingdom's western borders from falling to the Defias Brotherhood."},kw={"dungar longdrink","gryphon","osric","osric's crate","peoples militia","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"quest:6285","npc:quartermaster-lewis","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","quest:6261","npc:thor","quest:6281","quest:6181"},src={"Osric's Crate","Return to Lewis"}}
E["item:painted-gnoll-armband"] = {t="item",n="Painted Gnoll Armband",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Painted Gnoll Armbands prove that Riverpaw gnolls have been slain. The marked bands come from packs pressing against Elwynn Forest's western border.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Painted Gnoll Armbands prove that Riverpaw gnolls have been slain.",sec={{t="Tokens of the Riverpaw",b="Riverpaw warriors and scavengers wear rough armbands painted with crude tribal patterns. The bands come from gnolls along Elwynn Forest's wilderness borders. For Stormwind's defenders, the packs pose a growing threat near Stone Cairn Lake and in the woods south of Westbrook Garrison.",sp=0},{t="Bounty for Westbrook Garrison",b="Stormwind's Army is stretched thin across the kingdom, leaving Westbrook Garrison hard pressed to secure the western border. Deputy Rainer offers a standing bounty for slaying Riverpaw outrunners and runts. Their painted armbands prove the kills, helping the deputies count the bounties and thin the packs near nearby farmlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Westbrook Garrison want these armbands?",a="Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison collects the armbands as proof that Riverpaw gnolls have been slain. Garrison troops cannot manage the encroaching packs alone, so Stormwind pays bounties to adventurers who bring back the tokens.",al={"why armbands","who wants painted gnoll armbands","deputy rainer bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which gnolls wear these painted armbands?",a="Riverpaw gnolls wear the painted armbands. Riverpaw Outrunners and Riverpaw Runts infest the woods south of Westbrook Garrison and the shores around Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"where do armbands drop","who drops painted gnoll armband","which gnolls have armbands"},it="origin"},{q="Why are Riverpaw gnolls in Elwynn Forest?",a="Riverpaw packs have pushed east along Elwynn Forest's borders, setting up camps near Stone Cairn Lake and the forest margins. With the kingdom's military presence depleted, they hunt, scavenge, and threaten nearby settlements.",al={"why are gnolls here","gnoll invasion elwynn","riverpaw elwynn"}},{q="What is the significance of the paint on the armbands?",a="The paint marks trophies taken from Riverpaw gnolls and helps prove the kills to Deputy Rainer. The patterns have no stated rank or meaning.",al={"why are they painted","gnoll armband markings"}},{q="What is a Painted Gnoll Armband?",a="A Painted Gnoll Armband is a crude piece of personal adornment worn by Riverpaw gnolls. Crafted and painted by the pack, these armbands mark their presence in the borderlands of Elwynn Forest. To the Stormwind Army, they serve as undeniable physical proof that a marauding gnoll has been slain.",al={"what is painted gnoll armband","painted gnoll armband lore","gnoll armband"},it="identity",add="586b453e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, collecting these armbands helps Westbrook Garrison hold Stormwind's western frontier while the city's standing army is diverted elsewhere."},kw={"bounty","deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gnolls","painted gnoll armband","riverpaw","stone cairn lake","westbrook garrison"},rel={"quest:11","npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison","zone:elwynn","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","quest:239","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Painted Gnoll Armband","Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty"}}
E["item:pork-belly-pie"] = {t="item",n="Pork Belly Pie",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Billy Maclure wants a pie from the Stonefield farm before he speaks about a missing necklace. Auntie Bernice Stonefield bakes it despite the feud between their families.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Billy Maclure wants a pie from the Stonefield farm before he speaks about a missing...",sec={{t="A Bribe Between Feuding Farms",b="The Stonefield and Maclure families have quarreled over land and pride for years in Elwynn Forest. Young Billy Maclure has a weakness for Auntie Bernice's pork belly pie. When a valuable Stonefield family necklace goes missing, Billy refuses to share what he knows until an adventurer brings him a warm slice. Bernice bakes the pie reluctantly, wishing the greedy boy would choke on it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pork Belly Pie used for?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield bakes the pie to get young Billy Maclure to talk. He knows something about the missing Stonefield family necklace, but refuses to speak until he gets her cooking.",al={"pie use","why pork belly pie","what do i do with the pie"},it="purpose"},{q="Who bakes the Pork Belly Pie?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield bakes the pie at Stonefield Farm. She resents Billy Maclure and his family, but prepares it to help recover her family's lost necklace.",al={"who made the pie","pie baker","granny stonefield pie"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Billy Maclure want food from a rival family?",a="Billy Maclure wants Auntie Bernice's cooking despite the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures. He wants pork belly pie more than he cares about keeping his family's grudge.",al={"why billy wants pie","why maclure wants stonefield food"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can players eat the Pork Belly Pie?",a="No. The pie is meant for Billy Maclure and cannot be eaten to restore health or mana.",al={"can i eat it","is pork belly pie edible"},gp=true},{q="What is the Pork Belly Pie?",a="It is a savory meat pie baked with pork belly, renowned for being delicious despite the bitter feud between the two farming households of southern Elwynn Forest. Freshly prepared in the Stonefield kitchen, it serves as a mouth-watering bribe to coax information out of the Maclure boy, Billy, who claims his memory only works on a full stomach.",al={"what is pork belly pie","pork belly pie lore","about pork belly pie"},it="identity",add="6505ed9f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Auntie Bernice's home-cooked pie has sway even in the families' feud, though her recipe remains a secret.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers helping in rural Elwynn, delivering pies reveals the deep-rooted quarrels in Stormwind's agrarian heartland."},kw={"auntie bernice stonefield","back to billy","billy maclure","elwynn forest","maclure","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},src={"Pork Belly Pie","Back to Billy"}}
E["item:powers-of-the-void"] = {t="item",n="Powers of the Void",z="elwynn",s="A stolen tome draws Drusilla La Salle's attention in Northshire. Powers of the Void was kept in a restricted wing of Northshire Abbey's library until a novice took it while defecting to the Defias Brotherhood. Drusilla seeks its recovery for her own study of dark magic.",h="A stolen tome draws Drusilla La Salle's attention in Northshire.",sec={{t="A Restricted Northshire Text",b="Powers of the Void was kept behind guarded shelves in Northshire Abbey's library. The abbey archives hold holy scripture and clerical records, along with scholarly works on shadow and nether energies. The tome was presumably penned by the archmage Khadgar. Because its subject was dangerous, abbey authorities kept the book under guard and away from casual visitors. That barred Northshire's warlock mentor, Drusilla La Salle, from browsing it without drawing the priesthood's suspicion.",sp=0},{t="Defias Theft and Recovery",b="A Northshire novice carried the tome away while abandoning his vows to join the Defias Brotherhood. As he fled into the neighboring vineyards, he took several valuable volumes from the abbey. Drusilla sends promising warlock initiates into the Defias bandit camp to recover the book from their tents. She wants the dark knowledge for her own study, and the effort tests whether an initiate has the nerve to bind otherworldly demons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Powers of the Void?",a="Powers of the Void is a rare occult book about shadow and nether energies, believed to have been penned by the archmage Khadgar. It was kept in a restricted wing of Northshire Abbey's library before it was stolen.",al={"what is powers of the void","powers of the void book","what is the stolen tome"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the book locked up in Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey keeps historic archives, including dangerous texts on illicit magic. Books about Void energies and demonology are locked away to keep novices and wayward practitioners from abusing them.",al={"why was it in the abbey","why did the priests have it","northshire library wing"},it="history"},{q="How did the Defias Brotherhood get the book?",a="A Northshire Abbey novice defected to the Defias Brotherhood and took several valuable volumes from the restricted library. He hid them in the bandit camp in the Northshire vineyards.",al={"who stole the book","defias stolen books","how did defias get it"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Drusilla La Salle want Powers of the Void?",a="Drusilla La Salle is Northshire's warlock mentor and wants the tome's knowledge for her own dark craft. She could not enter the abbey's secure library without raising suspicion.",al={"why does drusilla want it","who wants the book","drusilla la salle stolen tome"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does retrieving the tome prove to Drusilla?",a="Retrieving the tome tests whether an initiate has the nerve to bind demons. Drusilla uses that test before teaching them to summon their first imp.",al={"why do warlocks need the book","imp summoning test","stolen tome reward"},it="for_you"},{q="Who wrote Powers of the Void?",a="The arcane treatise is believed to have been penned by the legendary archmage Khadgar, who studied many profound and perilous aspects of magic before venturing beyond the Dark Portal. Its forbidden insights into the deeper void were deemed far too dangerous for casual reading, prompting the priests and scholars of Northshire Abbey to seal it away within a protected wing of their library until a treacherous novice stole it.",al={"powers of the void author","who made powers of the void","powers of the void creator"},it="origin",add="082e56cb"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, retrieving the stolen tome tests whether you have the will to earn instruction in summoning an imp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see that Northshire's Holy Order keeps dangerous magical records alongside clerical texts, hidden from novice eyes."},kw={"defias brotherhood","drusilla la salle","imp","khadgar","northshire abbey","powers of the void","stolen books","the stolen tome","warlock"},rel={"quest:1598","npc:drusilla-la-salle","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:warlock","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","quest:65"},src={"Powers of the Void","The Stolen Tome"}}
E["item:red-burlap-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Burlap Bandana",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem gathers red bandanas from slain Defias thieves near the abbey vineyards. The cloth marks low-ranking highwaymen and cutpurses of the Brotherhood.",h="In Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem gathers red bandanas from slain Defias thieves near the abbey vineyards.",sec={{t="A Mark of the Brotherhood",b="Red burlap masks mark the Defias Brotherhood's rank-and-file. Cheap, rough cloth dyed red hides a thief's features and signals allegiance to the growing rebellion. In Northshire, young recruits and common thugs carry these scarves into the eastern orchards. The local guards recognize the striking red fabric as proof of thieves slain nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Deputy Willem want these bandanas?",a="Deputy Willem collects the bandanas as proof that an adventurer has killed Defias thugs near Northshire Abbey. The thieves wear the red cloth openly, confirming the bounty has been claimed.",al={"why collect bandanas","willem bandanas","brotherhood of thieves turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wears the red burlap bandanas?",a="Footpads and thugs of the Defias Brotherhood wear the red burlap bandanas. The coarse cloth conceals their faces and marks their loyalty to the outlaws.",al={"who wears red bandana","defias mask lore","who drops red bandanas"},it="people"},{q="Why are Defias thieves operating in Northshire?",a="Defias scouts and brigands camp across the stream east of Northshire Abbey to scavenge and steal supplies. The abbey garrison is stretched thin, leaving the nearby orchards open to highwaymen.",al={"why are defias in northshire","thieves near abbey"},it="motive"},{q="What makes the bandanas red?",a="Cheap burlap treated with crimson dye gives the bandanas their red color. The hue is the Defias Brotherhood's banner and uniform, so members can recognize one another in the field.",al={"why are defias masks red","red cloth meaning"}},{q="What is a Red Burlap Bandana?",a="A Red Burlap Bandana is the signature cloth mask worn by members of the Defias Brotherhood. Cheaply made from rough burlap and dyed red, it conceals the wearer's face and marks their allegiance to the outlaw guild. In Northshire, it serves as direct proof of a thug's presence and activity east of the river.",al={"red burlap bandana identity","what are red bandanas","defias bandana lore"},it="identity",add="c4ebebb0"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a developing rogue, you can learn from Northshire's clumsy footpads how quickly undisciplined outlaws become easy targets for local law enforcement.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the red bandanas reaching Northshire Abbey's doorstep as a sign that Stormwind is losing control of the kingdom's rural borders."},kw={"bandana","brotherhood of thieves","defias","mask","northshire","red burlap bandana","willem"},rel={"quest:18","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:willem","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Red Burlap Bandana","Brotherhood of Thieves"}}
E["item:red-linen-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Linen Bandana",z="elwynn",s="Across Elwynn Forest, Red Linen Bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood. Its cloth hides a wearer’s face and can be put to use by local settlers.",h="Across Elwynn Forest, Red Linen Bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="Mark of the Defias",b="Across Elwynn Forest, full Defias operatives wear woven red linen bandanas. In Northshire Valley, lower-ranking initiates and common thugs use coarse burlap masks instead. The crimson cloth hides a face and marks allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's rogue fraternity. It also signals their rebellion against Stormwind's crown.",sp=0},{t="Repurposed Cloth",b="Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp asks travelers to gather bandanas from outlaw encampments. Though tied to bandits, the masks are made from respectable linen. After washing and needlework, settlers can turn the cloth into sturdy clothing and bandages for the forest's working folk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red linen bandanas?",a="Defias operatives wear red linen bandanas to hide their faces and show allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's brotherhood and defiance of Stormwind.",al={"defias mask meaning","why red masks","defias red bandana"},it="identity"},{q="How do these differ from the masks worn in Northshire?",a="Northshire Valley thugs wear coarse burlap masks, while established Defias operatives across Elwynn Forest wear finer red linen.",al={"burlap vs linen","northshire masks","burlap bandana"}},{q="Who wants to collect these bandanas?",a="Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp wants the bandanas. She washes and unravels the masks to weave practical garments.",al={"who takes red linen bandanas","sara timberlain bandana","bandana quest turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Which enemies carry red linen bandanas?",a="Defias operatives across Elwynn Forest carry red linen bandanas, including Defias Bandits, Ambushers, Rogue Wizards, dockworkers, and ringleaders such as Morgan the Collector.",al={"who drops red linen bandana","where to farm bandanas","defias bandana drops"},it="target",gp=true}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="In rural Elwynn, weavers can put the linen in bandit masks to use as working clothes.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the crimson cloth tied across the lower face as the mark of highwaymen and cutpurses in the woods around the capital."},kw={"defias mask","eastvale","elwynn forest","linen","red linen bandana","sara timberlain"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","npc:morgan-the-collector","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:rogue"},src={"Red Linen Bandana","Red Linen Goods"}}
E["item:rolf-and-malakai-s-medallions"] = {t="item",n="Rolf and Malakai's Medallions",z="elwynn",s="Rolf and Malakai's Medallions bear the realm's insignia, but their owners vanished on patrol in eastern Elwynn Forest. Guard Thomas seeks the tokens to learn what became of his men.",h="Rolf and Malakai's Medallions bear the realm's insignia, but their owners vanished on patrol in eastern...",sec={{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Guard Thomas, station commander in eastern Elwynn, feared the worst when Rolf and Malakai vanished along the riverbanks. Their medallions confirm the guards died at the hands of encroaching murlocs. For the Stormwind garrison, these tokens mark the loss of soldiers who held the line against wilderness threats while the kingdom's military was stretched thin.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Service",b="Human guards on city watch and rural patrols carry identification medallions that show their allegiance and authority under the crown. Returning Rolf and Malakai's tokens to Guard Thomas lets him account for his missing men, record their sacrifice in his field report, and warn of aggressive murloc tribes settling near the trade roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Rolf and Malakai's Medallions?",a="They are the service identification tokens carried by Rolf and Malakai, Stormwind guards ambushed and killed by murlocs while posted in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"what are the medallions","rolfs medallion","malakais medallion"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Who do these medallions belong to?",a="They belonged to Guards Rolf and Malakai, stationed under Guard Thomas to watch the river and roads between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"who were rolf and malakai","whose medallions"}},{q="Who should I bring these medallions to?",a="Bring them to Guard Thomas, who keeps watch at the eastern bridge on the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"who wants the medallions","where do i turn these in","medallion turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why are these medallions important to Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas sent both guards on patrol and feared they had met a foul end. Their medallions confirm their deaths, letting him record their sacrifice and warn Stormwind of the rising murloc threat.",al={"why does thomas want them","guard thomas reaction"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Even in the heart of the Alliance, local guardsmen face deadly peril while guarding rural trade routes.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Elwynn, these tokens mark the loss of sons and defenders. Their deaths show the kingdom's vulnerability while its military is occupied elsewhere."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn","guard thomas","malakai","medallions","murloc","rolf","stormwind guard"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","quest:71","quest:39","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Rolf and Malakai's Medallions","Report to Thomas"}}
E["item:stormwind-armor-marker"] = {t="item",n="Stormwind Armor Marker",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind Armor Marker lets those who aid the realm claim crafted gear from sanctioned artisans. Sara Timberlain accepts one at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",h="Stormwind Armor Marker lets those who aid the realm claim crafted gear from sanctioned artisans.",sec={{t="Military Requisitions",b="Stormwind's commanders issue armor markers to those who serve the realm. Keeping law and order across Elwynn Forest stretches Stormwind's resources thin, so commanders sometimes use these official requisition slips instead of handing out standard gear at military outposts. A marker confirms the bearer's service and authorizes local craftsmen under contract to provide tailored armor.",sp=0},{t="Eastvale Provisioning",b="At the Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain and other artisans work under commission from the Stormwind Army. The camp lies on Elwynn's eastern frontier, where they use local materials to make protective cloth and leather garments. Present a marker there to receive custom-fitted defense for guarding the surrounding woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="The Stormwind Armor Marker is an official military voucher for those who aid Stormwind's guards. It proves your service and lets you claim protective armor from an artisan under contract with the army.",al={"what is armor marker","marker purpose","stormwind marker use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who accepts the marker?",a="Sara Timberlain accepts the marker at the Eastvale Logging Camp, just east across the river in Elwynn Forest. She is under contract with the Stormwind Army to provide tailored cloth and leather equipment.",al={"who takes the marker","where to turn in marker","sara timberlain marker"},it="target"},{q="Why does Stormwind use markers instead of handing out armor directly?",a="Stormwind uses markers because outlying guard posts may lack the storage, blacksmithing or tailoring setups to outfit recruits on site. Field commanders can send recruits to local artisans like Sara Timberlain, who have dedicated workshops.",al={"why tokens instead of armor","why army markers","military vouchers elwynn"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of equipment does the marker provide?",a="The marker lets its bearer choose a newly crafted cloth or leather armor piece made to order by an army supplier under contract.",al={"what armor do i get","marker rewards","cloth or leather"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="It is an official military voucher issued on behalf of the Stormwind Army. Rather than hauling bulky suits of protective gear across Elwynn Forest, local commanders issue this token as a guarantee of requisition, entitling the bearer to claim freshly crafted cloth or leather armor from an authorized armorer.",al={"what is stormwind armor marker","armor marker","what is the marker"},it="identity",add="e5398b12"},{q="Where does the Stormwind Armor Marker come from, and who made it?",a="The marker is issued on behalf of the Stormwind Army by Guard Thomas at his post by the eastern bridge in Elwynn, awarded to defenders who prove their shrewdness and valor. It carries the authority of the kingdom's army, commissioning local artisans to supply recruits on the crown's coin.",al={"who made the armor marker","where did the marker come from","who gives the armor marker"},it="origin",add="3e7f2980"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain want the Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="Sara Timberlain has been commissioned by the Stormwind Army to outfit their recruits and volunteers with cloth and leather armor. She requires the marker as official proof of authorization before surrendering her handcrafted gear, ensuring the kingdom's supplies go only to recognized defenders.",al={"why does sara want the marker","why take marker to eastvale","why need armor marker"},it="why_wanted",add="618263b5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Eastvale Logging Camp connects frontier settlements to Stormwind's military command."},kw={"armor marker","cloth and leather armor","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","requisition","sara timberlain","stormwind armor marker"},rel={"quest:59","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Stormwind Armor Marker","Cloth and Leather Armor"}}
E["item:surena-s-choker"] = {t="item",n="Surena's Choker",z="elwynn",s="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder seeks the choker he gave his former apprentice, Surena Caledon. After Surena fled to join the Defias Brotherhood, Gakin sent aspiring acolytes to take it back by force.",h="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder seeks the choker he gave his former apprentice, Surena Caledon.",sec={{t="A Master's Lost Investment",b="Gakin the Darkbinder works quietly beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, where he took Surena Caledon on as a promising student of the dark arts. Drawn to her youthful charm and magical aptitude, he gave her a valuable bloodstone choker to aid her studies. Surena abandoned her training and fled with Erlan Drudgemoor, a rogue aligned with the Defias Brotherhood. Gakin will not leave a potent artifact in a traitor’s hands. He sends initiates seeking mastery over the void to find Surena at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch and reclaim the necklace by force. Their deed will show where true loyalty lies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want Surena's Choker back?",a="Gakin gave the bloodstone choker to Surena when she was his apprentice. She abandoned her studies and fled with a member of the Defias Brotherhood, but Gakin will not let a traitor keep a prized artifact of dark magic.",al={"why does gakin want the choker","gakin surena necklace","why steal the choker back"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Surena Caledon?",a="Surena Caledon is a former apprentice warlock in Stormwind, where she showed natural talent under Gakin the Darkbinder. She turned from her tutor and fled with Erlan Drudgemoor, hiding among the Defias outlaws in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is surena","surena caledon lore","who has the choker"},it="people"},{q="Where can the choker be found?",a="Surena Caledon carries the choker at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, where she is holed up among the Defias bandits.",al={"where is surena","choker location","where is surena caledon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the choker used for after it is retrieved?",a="Taking back the choker proves an acolyte’s ruthlessness and loyalty to Gakin the Darkbinder. He does not say what he will do with it; he laments Surena’s wasted talent and hopes his investment in the new student brings different results.",al={"what does gakin do with the choker","choker purpose","why do warlocks need the choker"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Surena's Choker?",a="It is an ornate bloodstone necklace originally owned by Gakin the Darkbinder, the master warlock residing in the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. Gakin gifted the precious piece of jewelry to his former apprentice, Surena Caledon, when he was infatuated with her youth and beauty before she betrayed him.",al={"what is surenas choker","surena choker what is it","bloodstone choker"},it="identity",add="195efbf9"},{q="Where does Surena's Choker come from, and who made it?",a="The choker's precise artisan is unknown, but it was originally in the possession of Gakin the Darkbinder. Gakin presented the bloodstone necklace to his young student Surena Caledon during her tutelage under him, long before she ran off with a Defias rogue to the pumpkin patch in Elwynn.",al={"who made surenas choker","origin of surenas choker","where did the choker come from"},it="origin",add="7b9593ae"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Human or Gnome warlock, retrieving Surena Caledon’s choker is a foundational trial. It shows that sentimentality has no place in the pursuit of demonic power."},kw={"bloodstone choker","brackwell pumpkin patch","erlan drudgemoor","gakin the darkbinder","slaughtered lamb","surena caledon","surena's choker"},rel={"quest:1688","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1471","quest:1685","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn","topic:warlock"},src={"Surena's Choker","Surena Caledon (quest)"}}
E["item:tainted-letter"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Letter",z="elwynn",s="Drusilla La Salle sends the Tainted Letter to human warlock initiates near Northshire Abbey. It bears her seal and directs them to seek her tutelage discreetly.",h="Drusilla La Salle sends the Tainted Letter to human warlock initiates near Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="A Covert Summons",b="The Tainted Letter bears Drusilla La Salle’s insignia and reaches initiates returning from nearby kobold camps. While priests, paladins, and soldiers train openly across Northshire Abbey’s lawns, fel practitioners must keep their path quiet. The letter directs novice warlocks to find their mentor near the abbey grounds without drawing the notice of town guards or clerics.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Ambition",b="Drusilla La Salle meets her pupils on the fringes, where sentries are less likely to pry. Elwynn’s ordinary folk distrust warlocks, so the letter begins a lesson in discipline. Arcane and nether magic bring the risk of corruption. Those who commune with denizens of the Twisting Nether must temper ambition with patient self-control.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the Tainted Letter?",a="Drusilla La Salle, the warlock trainer near Northshire Abbey, sent the letter.",al={"who wrote tainted letter","drusilla letter","sender of tainted letter"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the letter considered tainted?",a="The letter bears Drusilla La Salle’s insignia and traces of fel magic, marking it as the work of a practitioner of demonic arts.",al={"why is it tainted","what makes the letter tainted","tainted seal"}},{q="Why are Northshire guards watching Drusilla La Salle?",a="Northshire’s guards and priests distrust fel magic and demonic summoning. Drusilla keeps to the abbey’s outskirts to avoid the authorities’ close watch.",al={"drusilla guards","why do guards suspect drusilla","warlock hiding in northshire"}},{q="What advice does Drusilla give upon reading the letter?",a="Drusilla warns that dealing with entities from the Twisting Nether brings temptation and corruption. She urges her pupils to use self-control and prudence while holding to their ambition.",al={"drusilla advice","what does drusilla say","drusilla training"}},{q="What is the Tainted Letter?",a="The Tainted Letter is a sealed message left for you upon your return to Northshire Abbey, stamped with the unmistakable personal insignia of Drusilla La Salle. Addressed to fledgling practitioners of the dark arts, the correspondence serves as an urgent summons to speak with her directly. It carries the faint mark of fel corruption, setting it distinctly apart from the pious and orderly affairs of the Holy Light practiced within the abbey's walls.",al={"what is tainted letter","tainted letter identity","about tainted letter"},it="identity",add="63258adc"},{q="Why is the Tainted Letter given to you?",a="The letter is handed to you so you can establish contact with your trainer, Drusilla La Salle, as soon as your initial tasks around Northshire are complete. Drusilla operates quietly on the fringes of the abbey, keeping a watchful eye out for emerging warlocks. The letter directs you to seek her out before other abbey matters distract you, allowing her to impart vital warnings about self-control, ambition, and the corrupting nature of the Twisting Nether.",al={"why do I need tainted letter","who wants the tainted letter","why give tainted letter"},it="why_wanted",add="3c923280"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive the Tainted Letter as your introduction to the shadowy craft in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Power over the Nether calls for constant vigilance and discretion.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you live in a society that broadly champions the Holy Light. Practitioners of dark magic train in secret on the margins of places like Northshire Abbey."},kw={"drusilla la salle","elwynn forest","northshire abbey","tainted letter","twisting nether","warlock"},rel={"quest:3105","npc:drusilla-la-salle","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},src={"Tainted Letter","Tainted Letter (quest)"}}
E["item:the-collector-s-schedule"] = {t="item",n="The Collector's Schedule",z="elwynn",s="Near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, The Collector's Schedule marks when illicit gold shipments move through Elwynn Forest. Gnolls carry the handwritten itinerary, and Marshal Dughan recognizes the name it records.",h="Near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, The Collector's Schedule marks when illicit gold shipments move through...",sec={{t="Stolen Gold and Secret Shipments",b="The Collector's Schedule marks dates and times for gold shipments from Elwynn's mines. Stormwind has not officially worked the mines for months, driven off by banditry and creature incursions, yet ore still leaves in an orderly flow. The itinerary names the days and hours when a figure called The Collector receives each shipment. The trail points to a camp near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. When Marshal Dughan sees the schedule, he recognizes the Collector's name. Who pays for the stolen gold remains unknown.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Collector's Schedule?",a="The Collector's Schedule records when gold shipments leave Elwynn Forest's abandoned mines for an operative called The Collector.",al={"what is this note","collectors schedule item","gold schedule"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the schedule come from?",a="Gnolls carry the schedule along Elwynn Forest's riverbanks and hillsides. They may have taken it from a courier or may be involved in moving the gold.",al={"who drops the schedule","where to find schedule"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the Collector?",a="The Collector is an agent stationed near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Dughan recognizes the name but does not know whom the agent serves.",al={"who is collector","collector identity"},it="people"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan alarmed by this schedule?",a="Marshal Dughan is alarmed because Stormwind has had no official miners in Elwynn's mines for months, yet substantial gold shipments still leave them. That points to an organized, illicit mining operation within the kingdom.",al={"why does dughan care","elwynn mines gold"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how little control Stormwind has over its own territory when unauthorized crews take its resources near the capital.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see that Elwynn's mines are not idle: rich gold veins are being stripped and hauled away."},kw={"brackwell","collector","dughan","elwynn","gold","goldshire","mines","schedule"},rel={"quest:123","quest:147","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},src={"The Collector's Schedule","The Collector (Classic)"}}
E["item:torn-murloc-fin"] = {t="item",n="Torn Murloc Fin",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, Torn Murloc Fins show the Stormwind Army's bounty is being answered. Taken from foragers and lurkers along the riverbanks, they show that local waterways are being systematically cleared.",h="In eastern Elwynn, Torn Murloc Fins show the Stormwind Army's bounty is being answered.",sec={{t="A Bountied Threat",b="Murlocs have grown numerous along eastern Elwynn's streams and lakes, and the Stormwind Army offers a bounty to reduce their numbers. Guard Thomas, who watches the bridge over the eastern river, collects the severed fins as proof of kills. Stormwind's soldiers are stretched thin by unrest at home and threats nearby, so local authorities depend on travelers to bring proof that murloc camps have been cleared.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who buys or collects Torn Murloc Fins?",a="Guard Thomas collects Torn Murloc Fins at Elwynn Forest's eastern bridge for Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army.",al={"who wants fins","fin turn in","guard thomas fins"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where are the murlocs carrying these fins located?",a="The fins come from murloc foragers and lurkers around Stone Cairn Lake to the north and the southern stream fork near eastern Elwynn's border.",al={"where to farm fins","murloc fin locations","fin drops"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormwind require fins as proof?",a="Fins are unmistakable and easy to carry, giving the Stormwind Army physical proof of slain murlocs before it pays the bounty hunters.",al={"why fins","proof of kill murlocs","bounty proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Stormwind Army paying for dead murlocs?",a="Murloc villages have spread quickly along the waterways, threatening travelers, fishermen, and local infrastructure while the Stormwind Army's forces are occupied elsewhere.",al={"why murloc bounty","murloc problem elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Torn Murloc Fin?",a="A Torn Murloc Fin is a physical trophy sliced from the hide of murlocs infesting eastern Elwynn Forest. Rather than an ornamental trinket or alchemical ingredient, it serves as tangible proof that a roaming amphibian raider has been slain, presenting reliable verification for local authorities offering bounties.",al={"what is torn murloc fin","torn fin lore","about murloc fin"},it="identity",add="afa68c63"},{q="Where do Torn Murloc Fins come from?",a="These fins are harvested directly from the bodies of murloc foragers and lurkers inhabiting the freshwater shallows of Elwynn Forest. In particular, aggressive tribes have established encampments along the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and the southern fork of the eastern rivers, menacing local travelers and farmlands.",al={"torn murloc fin origin","where do murloc fins come from","source of torn murloc fin"},it="origin",add="5ee7d3aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, clearing eastern Elwynn's waterways protects vital routes between Goldshire, Lakeshire, and Stormwind City.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know local authorities rely more and more on mercenaries to protect homesteads and riverbanks from aggressive murloc settlements."},kw={"bounty on murlocs","elwynn murlocs","guard thomas","murloc fin","murloc forager","murloc lurker","stone cairn lake","torn murloc fin"},rel={"quest:46","npc:guard-thomas","topic:murloc","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Torn Murloc Fin","Bounty on Murlocs"}}
E["item:tough-wolf-meat"] = {t="item",n="Tough Wolf Meat",z="elwynn",s="Northshire and Coldridge wolves prowl their valleys, leaving raw Tough Wolf Meat for hungry locals. Coarse and stringy, it feeds people in Elwynn Forest and supplies dwarven outfitters in Dun Morogh.",h="Northshire and Coldridge wolves prowl their valleys, leaving raw Tough Wolf Meat for hungry locals.",sec={{t="Frontier Rations",b="Wolves prowl near Northshire Valley and Dun Morogh, threatening nearby settlements and providing a hard-won source of food. Their meat is coarse, stringy, and chewy, but resource-strapped frontiersmen prize it. Outside Northshire Abbey, Eagan Peltskinner hates the vicious beasts yet cooks their meat into steaks. He trades basic supplies and gear to those willing to cull the packs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Tough Wolf Meat come from?",a="Hunting young wolves and timber wolves in Northshire Valley in Elwynn Forest, and ragged wolves in Coldridge Valley in Dun Morogh, provides Tough Wolf Meat.",al={"tough wolf meat source","how to get tough wolf meat","where to farm tough wolf meat"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants to collect this meat in Elwynn Forest?",a="Eagan Peltskinner, outside Northshire Abbey, collects the meat. He hates the wolves but cooks their meat into steaks and trades spare equipment to new recruits who bring him eight cuts.",al={"who needs wolf meat","eagan peltskinner meat","wolf meat turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is this meat useful outside of human lands?",a="Yes. Dwarven outfitters in frigid Dun Morogh accept meat from ragged wolves in Coldridge Valley to keep their supplies stocked.",al={"wolf meat dun morogh","dwarf wolf meat","dwarven outfitters meat"}},{q="Is Tough Wolf Meat used in normal cooking recipes?",a="No. Tough Wolf Meat is strictly a bounty for local frontiersmen such as Eagan Peltskinner and Coldridge outfitters, not an ingredient in standard camp cooking recipes.",al={"can you cook tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat recipes"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Tough Wolf Meat?",a="It is coarse, lean meat harvested from wild wolves prowling the wilderness of Northshire and Dun Morogh. While stringy and far from tender, it serves as a hearty staple for local trappers and hungry frontiersmen who know how to cook it into sustaining steaks.",al={"what is tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat lore","tough wolf meat"},it="identity",add="877dd280"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human recruit in Northshire Valley, you can gather wolf meat for Eagan Peltskinner outside the abbey. It is one of the earliest survival tasks beyond its quiet cloisters.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf in Coldridge Valley, you can cull ragged timber wolves for meat to supply local outfitters before setting off across Dun Morogh."},kw={"dun morogh","eagan peltskinner","elwynn forest","northshire abbey","timber wolf","tough wolf meat","young wolf"},rel={"quest:33","quest:5261","quest:179","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Tough Wolf Meat","Wolves Across the Border"}}
E["item:william-s-shipment"] = {t="item",n="William's Shipment",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, William Pestle packs candles from Elwynn's kobolds for his brother Morgan in Stormwind.",h="In Goldshire, William Pestle packs candles from Elwynn's kobolds for his brother Morgan in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Familial Trade",b="William Pestle keeps trade moving between Goldshire and the capital. He gathers materials in Elwynn Forest, while his brother Morgan runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. William cannot leave his duties to travel north, so he depends on couriers to carry the parcel of wax and candles into the city.",sp=0},{t="Kobold Wax",b="Kobold candles from Elwynn's mines fill the shipment. William gathers the large candles for their wax and packs them for Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary. The wax joins the stock used in the capital's alchemical trade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside William's Shipment?",a="The shipment holds candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn Forest's mines. William collects them from passing adventurers and packs them as raw ingredients for his family's alchemy shop.",al={"shipment contents","what is in the box","what does william send"},it="item"},{q="Who is William sending this package to?",a="William sends the package to his brother, Morgan Pestle, who runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"who gets the shipment","who is the delivery for","shipment destination"},it="target"},{q="Why does an apothecary need so many candles?",a="William says he and his brother need the large candles for their wax. He does not say which preparations will use it.",al={"why candles for alchemy","what does pestle do with candles","candle use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why doesn't William deliver the package himself?",a="William is busy managing his affairs and gathering goods in Goldshire, with no time for the overland trip to Stormwind. He hires travelers bound for the capital to carry the package.",al={"why can't william go","why does william need a courier"},it="why_me"},{q="What is William's Shipment?",a="William's Shipment is a securely packed bundle of large wax candles prepared by William Pestle in Goldshire. The candles were taken from kobolds in Elwynn Forest's mines and boxed up for delivery to Morgan Pestle in Stormwind.",al={"what is williams shipment","williams shipment package","williams delivery"},it="identity",add="bf7eefd8"},{q="Where does William's Shipment come from, and who made it?",a="The shipment comes directly from William Pestle, an alchemist residing at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. William packed the crates himself using large wax candles taken from the kobolds infesting the nearby Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines.",al={"who made williams shipment","where did williams shipment come from","origin of williams shipment"},it="origin",add="2b07f2a7"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how Goldshire's trade connects rural hamlets to the capital, Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Elwynn's mines from kobolds and supply the capital's shops with raw alchemy goods."},kw={"candles","goldshire","kobold candles","morgan pestle","pestle's apothecary","stormwind","trade district","william pestle","william's shipment"},rel={"quest:61","npc:morgan-pestle","quest:60","subzone:trade-district","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"William's Shipment","Shipment to Stormwind"}}
E["npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At the Stonefield homestead in south-central Elwynn Forest, “Auntie” Bernice Stonefield keeps watch over the neighborhood. Widowed when her husband fell in the kingdom’s military campaigns, she is known throughout the valley for her pork belly pies. She stays outside the farmhouse beside Ma Stonefield and remains deeply suspicious of the rival Maclure family.",h="At the Stonefield homestead in south-central Elwynn Forest, “Auntie” Bernice Stonefield keeps watch over the...",sec={{t="A Life of Hardship",b="Bernice carries the cost of war, as many common folk in the Kingdom of Stormwind do. Her husband fell in military campaigns, and she now lives with her kin at the family homestead. She helps Ma Stonefield manage the farm’s daily affairs, keeping the household fed and running. Her pork belly pies have made her famous among the people of the valley.",sp=0},{t="The Feud and the Missing Necklace",b="For Bernice, the old bitterness between the Stonefields and the Maclures runs deep. When her prized family necklace went missing, she suspected young Billy Maclure of taking it. Recovering it proves more complicated than settling a neighbor’s prank. Billy swears he did not steal the necklace, but nearly admits he dropped it near the Fargodeep Mine. There, he saw the gold-toothed kobold Goldtooth snatch it and carry it to his den.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield?",a="“Auntie” Bernice Stonefield is an elder of the Stonefield family who lives at the Stonefield Farm in southern Elwynn Forest. Widowed by the kingdom’s wars, she tends the farm with Ma Stonefield and is known for her pork belly pies.",al={"who is auntie bernice","bernice stonefield lore","stonefield auntie"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Auntie Bernice's husband?",a="Bernice’s husband fell during a military campaign fought for the Kingdom of Stormwind, leaving her a widow.",al={"auntie bernice husband","who was bernice married to","stonefield widow"},it="history"},{q="What is Auntie Bernice famous for?",a="Bernice is known across the local countryside for her pork belly pies, which even mischievous neighbors will bargain for a slice of.",al={"bernice stonefield pie","pork belly pie elwynn"},it="fame"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice angry with Billy Maclure?",a="Bernice suspects Billy Maclure took her cherished family necklace, deepening the long-standing feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures.",al={"billy maclure feud","bernice necklace thief","why does bernice hate billy"},it="conflict"},{q="Did Billy Maclure actually steal the necklace?",a="Billy swears he did not steal Bernice’s necklace, though he nearly admits he dropped it near the Fargodeep Mine. He says the gold-toothed kobold Goldtooth picked it up and carried it to his den.",al={"did billy steal the necklace","who has the stonefield necklace","goldtooth necklace"},sp=1},{q="Where is Auntie Bernice located?",a="Bernice can be found outside the main farmhouse at Stonefield Farm, south of the road between Goldshire and Westfall, beside Ma Stonefield.",al={"auntie bernice location","where is bernice stonefield"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Auntie Bernice Stonefield on?",a="Auntie Bernice is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Stonefield family. She firmly stands with her kin in their longstanding, bitter feud against their neighbors, the Maclures, holding little patience for anyone bearing that name.",al={"auntie bernice faction","who does bernice support","bernice stonefield alliance"},it="side",add="0a2ddc6d"},{q="What does Auntie Bernice Stonefield want?",a="Auntie Bernice primarily wants the return of her treasured family necklace, which went missing and caused her to suspect young Billy Maclure. To solve the mystery and retrieve her heirloom, she is willing to bake one of her famous pork belly pies to coax the truth out of him.",al={"what does auntie bernice need","auntie bernice goal","bernice stonefield quest motive"},it="wants",add="0e5ea09d"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice Stonefield here?",a="The Stonefield Farm is Auntie Bernice's home. Having lost her husband to one of Stormwind's military campaigns, she remains on the family homestead in Elwynn Forest alongside Ma Stonefield and the rest of the clan, tending to domestic chores and farm life.",al={"why is bernice at the farm","bernice stonefield location why","what brings auntie bernice here"},it="why_here",add="f6bb7867"},{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield tied to?",a="She is an elder matriarch of the Stonefield clan, living side-by-side with Ma Stonefield on their Elwynn farm. Her family is entangled in a bitter, ongoing rivalry with the nearby Maclure household, which colors nearly all her interactions with their kin.",al={"auntie bernice family","bernice stonefield relatives","who is auntie bernice related to"},it="ties",add="21972eac"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Bernice’s pork belly pie is famous across Elwynn Forest as a staple of hearty human frontier cooking.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Bernice shows the resilience of Stormwind’s rural folk, carrying on daily life and family pride after her husband fell in the kingdom’s wars."},kw={"auntie","bernice","elwynn","goldtooth","maclure","necklace","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:ma-stonefield","npc:billy-maclure","quest:85","quest:86","quest:84","quest:87","zone:elwynn"},src={"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield"}}
E["npc:billy-maclure"] = {t="npc",n="Billy Maclure",z="elwynn",s="At Maclure Vineyards, Billy Maclure's pranks stir trouble between two neighboring farms. The young human boy dodges chores and plays at the feud between his family and the Stonefields, but fresh pastries can win his cooperation.",h="At Maclure Vineyards, Billy Maclure's pranks stir trouble between two neighboring farms.",sec={{t="A Boy at the Vineyards",b="Billy Maclure spends his days outside the barn at Maclure Vineyards, near farmer Gerard Tiller. He grows up among the grapevines in southern Elwynn Forest, often dodging chores and roaming the meadows. The Maclures and Stonefields have long been hostile toward each other. Billy treats their feud as a chance for pranks and petty theft.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Necklace",b="Billy Maclure stole Auntie Bernice Stonefield's treasured heirloom necklace. While running near Fargodeep Mine, he lost hold of it. Goldtooth, a massive and vicious kobold, snatched the necklace and vanished into the mine's tunnels. Billy fears the kobolds and the neighboring elders' anger, so he hesitates to confess. Auntie Bernice's hot pork belly pie can coax the truth from him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Billy Maclure?",a="Billy Maclure is a young human boy at Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. He dodges farm work, plays pranks, and aggravates the neighboring Stonefields.",al={"who is billy","billy maclure lore","maclure kid"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Billy Maclure be found?",a="Billy waits outside the main barn at Maclure Vineyards, in southern Elwynn Forest east of Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy maclure"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What did Billy do to Auntie Bernice?",a="Billy stole Auntie Bernice Stonefield's heirloom necklace during the feud between their families.",al={"bernice necklace","what did billy steal","stolen necklace elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to the necklace Billy stole?",a="Billy lost the necklace near Fargodeep Mine. Goldtooth picked it up and carried it into the mine.",al={"where is the necklace","lost necklace elwynn","who has bernice necklace"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="How do you get Billy to confess what happened to the necklace?",a="Offer Billy a freshly baked pork belly pie from Auntie Bernice. His appetite can coax him to confess.",al={"pie for billy","how to bribe billy","bribing billy maclure"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is an exceptionally large and vicious kobold leader in Fargodeep Mine. He took Auntie Bernice's necklace near the mine entrance and keeps it in the tunnels.",al={"who is goldtooth","goldtooth lore","fargodeep kobold"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Billy Maclure on?",a="Billy is a loyal member of the Maclure family in Elwynn Forest, firmly allied with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. While his family maintains a bitter and long-standing feud with their neighbors, the Stonefields, Billy is still just a young boy who gets caught between family grudges and his personal appetite.",al={"billy maclure faction","which side is billy on","who does billy support"},it="side",add="324ac528"},{q="What does Billy Maclure want?",a="Billy wants little more than to stay out of trouble and indulge his appetite. Above all, he craves Auntie Bernice Stonefield's famous pork belly pies, despite the fierce rivalry between their families. He is even willing to confess his mischievous misdeeds if someone brings him one of her fresh, savory pies.",al={"what does billy want","what does billy maclure crave","billy maclure favorite food"},it="wants",add="c9c2f9db"},{q="Why is Billy Maclure here?",a="Billy resides at the Maclure Vineyards, which is his family's home and livelihood in Elwynn Forest. He spends his days loitering outside the barn near Gerard Tiller, running errands, and playing around the surrounding countryside when he is not sneaking over toward the neighboring Stonefield farm.",al={"why is billy maclure here","why is billy at maclure vineyards","what is billy doing here"},it="why_here",add="f69aaa51"},{q="Who is Billy Maclure tied to?",a="Billy is part of the Maclure farming family, residing alongside kin and workers like Gerard Tiller at the vineyards. Through his mischievous antics, he is also intimately entangled with the rival Stonefield family, particularly Auntie Bernice Stonefield, whose prized necklace he swiped and whose baking he secretly loves.",al={"billy maclure family","who is billy maclure related to","billy maclure connections"},it="ties",add="275e906f"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Billy's troubles show the everyday quarrels of the Elwynn countryside. Farm feuds and childhood mischief continue amid Stormwind's political turmoil.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer newly arrived from Northshire, helping with Billy's pranks introduces you to dangers in Fargodeep Mine.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can see how Auntie Bernice's pork belly pie helps settle local disputes and coax confessions from tight-lipped farm boys."},kw={"bernice stonefield","billy maclure","fargodeep mine","goldtooth","lost necklace","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield"},rel={"subzone:maclure-vineyards","quest:85","quest:86","quest:87","quest:84","subzone:fargodeep-mine","topic:kobold","npc:gerard-tiller"},src={"Billy Maclure"}}
E["npc:brother-neals"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Neals",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Neals keeps watch over the food and drink stores. He oversees shipments and samples wine from the local vineyard.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Neals keeps watch over the food and drink stores.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Cellar",b="Brother Neals keeps Northshire Abbey supplied with food and drink from his rooms in the upper belfry. He follows the grape manifests from the Northshire vineyards and tastes the wine to check its quality. He also watches the shipments arriving from the fields around the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals belongs to Northshire Abbey and manages its stores of food, drink, and wine for the clergy and recruits in the valley.",al={"brother neals","neals","who is neals"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Brother Neals be found?",a="Brother Neals stays in the uppermost room of Northshire Abbey. Climb the stone staircases inside the main hall to reach the quiet chamber near the top of the tower.",al={"where is brother neals","brother neals location","find neals"},gp=true},{q="What is his role regarding the vineyard?",a="Brother Neals tracks grape harvests and wine shipments from the nearby Northshire Vineyard. He spends time sampling the vintage as well as keeping the ledgers.",al={"grape manifest quest","neals wine","what does neals do"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Brother Neals on?",a="Brother Neals is a loyal member of the Brotherhood of Northshire, serving Northshire Abbey and the Grand Alliance of Stormwind. He carries out his clerical duties peacefully inside the abbey walls.",al={"brother neals faction","who does brother neals serve","brother neals alliance"},it="side",add="340be3c1"},{q="What does Brother Neals want?",a="Brother Neals needs to keep proper accounting of Northshire's stores, in particular the wine inventory from the local vineyard. He requires shipments and records like the grape manifest brought directly up to his quarters so he can manage supplies—and enjoy a generous sample of the abbey's vintage.",al={"brother neals grape manifest","what does brother neals need"},it="wants",add="0d7c1646"},{q="Why is Brother Neals here?",a="As a brother of the abbey, Neals resides in the quiet upper tower of Northshire Abbey to oversee the community's stores of food and drink. His post keeps him close to the cellar reserves and accounting documents necessary to sustain the clergy and new recruits.",al={"why is brother neals in the tower","why is brother neals at northshire"},it="why_here",add="bb6478cd"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As someone who manages the monastery's provisions and spirits, Brother Neals has a role tied to the culinary arts."},kw={"brother neals","elwynn forest","grape manifest","northshire abbey","northshire valley","vineyard","wine"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","quest:3905","zone:elwynn"},src={"Brother Neals"}}
E["npc:brother-wilhelm"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Wilhelm",z="elwynn",s="Behind Goldshire's blacksmith, Brother Wilhelm trains young paladins in the Holy Light. He guides them as they leave Northshire Abbey and take their first steps into Elwynn Forest.",h="Behind Goldshire's blacksmith, Brother Wilhelm trains young paladins in the Holy Light.",sec={{t="A Guide in Goldshire",b="Brother Wilhelm trains new paladins behind Goldshire's smithy. Northshire Valley shelters those who begin their path in the Light, but many seek his guidance when they enter the wider forest. He teaches them their sacred duties as they leave the abbey and take up the work of protecting the realm.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Tome",b="Brother Wilhelm guides aspiring paladins toward the Tome of Divinity. Its rite teaches initiates the weight of sacrifice and the power of divine redemption. Through it, they test their devotion and learn to wield the Light to resurrect fallen comrades and uphold justice across the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brother Wilhelm?",a="Brother Wilhelm is in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest, just behind the village blacksmith workshop. He trains and guides aspiring paladins there.",al={"wilhelm location","where is brother wilhelm","find brother wilhelm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Brother Wilhelm provide?",a="Brother Wilhelm trains young paladins in new spells, martial blessings, and holy techniques as they travel through Elwynn Forest.",al={"what does wilhelm do","paladin trainer goldshire","brother wilhelm trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Brother Wilhelm part of the Brotherhood of Northshire?",a="Brother Wilhelm's title and his closeness to Northshire Abbey suggest ties to the Brotherhood of Northshire. He serves the Church of the Holy Light and the Kingdom of Stormwind from Goldshire.",al={"is wilhelm brotherhood of northshire","wilhelm faction","who does brother wilhelm serve"},it="ties"},{q="What is his role in the Tome of Divinity quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm guides human paladins who have grown in power toward the Tome of Divinity and its trials, which lead to the sacred blessing of resurrection.",al={"tome of divinity wilhelm","resurrection quest wilhelm","goldshire paladin quest"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="Who is Brother Wilhelm?",a="Brother Wilhelm is a human paladin mentor stationed in Goldshire. Devoted to the Holy Light and the defense of the kingdom, he offers guidance and training to fledgling paladins who venture beyond Northshire Valley into the broader regions of Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is brother wilhelm","brother wilhelm identity","who is wilhelm"},it="identity",add="0af03050"},{q="Whose side is Brother Wilhelm on?",a="Brother Wilhelm is firmly aligned with the Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. He serves the holy orders of the Light, dedicating himself to strengthening the realm's paladins against internal strife and regional threats.",al={"who does brother wilhelm serve","wilhelm faction","brother wilhelm alliance"},it="side",add="cccf7116"},{q="Why is Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire?",a="Stationed behind the Goldshire smithy, Brother Wilhelm serves as an instructor for young paladins who have recently left Northshire Abbey. He remains on hand in Elwynn Forest to oversee their continuous development and spiritual readiness as they step into active duty.",al={"why is brother wilhelm here","brother wilhelm goldshire","why is wilhelm in elwynn"},it="why_here",add="3fb91c50"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find your first mentor in Brother Wilhelm after leaving Northshire Valley. He guides your growth and opens the path to mastering the Tome of Divinity.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see in Brother Wilhelm the faith of the Church of the Holy Light, which defends Elwynn's heartland."},kw={"brother wilhelm","brotherhood of northshire","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","paladin trainer","tome of divinity"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:2997","topic:light","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Brother Wilhelm"}}
E["npc:deputy-rainer"] = {t="npc",n="Deputy Rainer",z="elwynn",s="Outside Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer holds Elwynn's western border. The Stormwind Army officer faces gnolls and bandits from Westfall, coordinating local defenses while reinforcements fail to arrive.",h="Outside Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer holds Elwynn's western border.",sec={{t="Holding the Western Border",b="At Westbrook Garrison, Elwynn Forest's westernmost post, the road crosses into Westfall. Political paralysis in Stormwind City leaves much of the army abroad or caught in bureaucracy, and border posts like this one lack troops. Deputy Rainer organizes the defense from outside the tower with the few forces at hand. Riverpaw gnolls and wandering thieves threaten the local roads, so he depends on passing travelers and mercenary adventurers to keep the forest trails secure.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Westfall",b="Deputy Rainer watches for the Riverpaw pack and warns travelers about Hogger, the infamous gnoll chieftain. He also carries word of the troubled lands beyond the river. The chaos at Elwynn's border begins in Westfall's lawless farmlands, so he sends capable volunteers across the border toward Gryan Stoutmantle and the struggling People's Militia.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer is a Stormwind Army officer stationed at Westbrook Garrison on Elwynn Forest's western edge. He oversees road security and hires adventurers to fight nearby threats.",al={"rainer elwynn","who is rainer","westbrook garrison officer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Westbrook Garrison undermanned?",a="Most of the Stormwind Army is deployed elsewhere, and political disorder in the capital keeps regular reinforcements from reaching outlying regions. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire must rely on independent adventurers to help Rainer.",al={"why no guards at westbrook","why is the garrison struggling","westbrook needs help"}},{q="What threats is Rainer trying to counter?",a="Rainer works to contain the Riverpaw gnolls in the woods south of the garrison, roving thieves, and Hogger, the notorious gnoll chieftain who preys on travelers along the border.",al={"what enemies are near westbrook","riverpaw gnolls westbrook","westbrook gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Rainer send adventurers after clearing the gnolls?",a="After the gnolls near the garrison are driven back, Rainer sends seasoned adventurers across the western border into Westfall to help Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",al={"where to go after rainer","rainer quest westfall","after westbrook garrison"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Deputy Rainer on?",a="Rainer is a loyal officer of the Stormwind Army, serving the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at Westbrook Garrison, he answers to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and strives to protect Elwynn's western marches from encroaching chaos.",al={"deputy rainer faction","who does rainer serve","is rainer alliance"},it="side",add="8453208a"},{q="What does Deputy Rainer want?",a="Rainer wants capable volunteers to defend Elwynn Forest's western border. With the army stretched thin, he seeks to cull the aggressive Riverpaw gnoll pack to the south, secure the trade roads against thieves, and put an end to the menace of Hogger.",al={"what does rainer want","deputy rainer goals","what is rainer asking for"},it="wants",add="b0214c4a"},{q="Why is Deputy Rainer here?",a="Rainer is stationed at Westbrook Garrison to guard the border between Elwynn Forest and Westfall. As beasts and bandits spill eastward across the river, he stands watch outside the guard tower, coordinating patrols and enlisting travelers to hold the frontier.",al={"why is rainer at westbrook","why is deputy rainer here"},it="why_here",add="5835f036"},{q="Who is Deputy Rainer tied to?",a="Rainer reports to Marshal Dughan, commander of the garrison forces in Goldshire. He also cooperates across the border with Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia in Westfall, directing tested fighters westward to aid their struggle against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who is rainer affiliated with","rainer connections","who does rainer report to"},it="ties",add="b3def1b5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance heroes, Deputy Rainer shows how Stormwind's outlying garrisons adapt when regular royal support does not reach them."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gryan stoutmantle","hogger","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison","westfall"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","quest:11","quest:109","quest:239","quest:176","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:westfall"},src={"Deputy Rainer"}}
E["npc:drusilla-la-salle"] = {t="npc",n="Drusilla La Salle",z="elwynn",s="Outside Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle teaches warlocks in the graveyard. The human trainer works beyond the Holy Order’s reach, guiding new spellcasters in shadow and summoning. When forbidden knowledge leaves the abbey, she moves to claim it.",h="Outside Northshire Abbey, Drusilla La Salle teaches warlocks in the graveyard.",sec={{t="Shadows in Holy Ground",b="Drusilla La Salle teaches novice warlocks among the headstones outside Northshire Abbey. Paladins and priests practice beneath the abbey’s stained glass, while warlocks keep to society’s edges because demonology and fel magic are taboo in Stormwind. Recruits receive tainted correspondence before Drusilla shows them how to wield shadow power without drawing the abbey authorities’ immediate anger.",sp=0},{t="Powers of the Void",b="Northshire Abbey’s library wing holds hazardous, forbidden books, including Powers of the Void. Drusilla has long wanted the manuscript, but a warlock in the guarded archives would invite suspicion. Her opening comes when an apostate novice flees the abbey to join the Defias Brotherhood, carrying the book. Drusilla sends her apprentices after the turncoat to bring her the grimoire, claiming they are recovering abbey property.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a warlock allowed near Northshire Abbey?",a="The Church of the Holy Light and Stormwind’s leaders deeply distrust warlocks. Drusilla teaches outside the abbey, in the nearby graveyard, away from the priests and clerics studying within.",al={"why is drusilla at abbey","warlock in holy abbey","why is she in the graveyard"},it="why_here"},{q="What book is Drusilla trying to obtain?",a="Drusilla seeks Powers of the Void, a grimoire once locked in a protected part of Northshire Abbey’s Library Wing. A Defias defector steals it, putting the book beyond the abbey’s reach.",al={"what book does she want","powers of the void book","the stolen tome quest book"},it="wants"},{q="Who stole the book from the library?",a="A novice from Northshire Abbey steals the tome after breaking his vows and joining the Defias Brotherhood. He flees to a nearby camp in Northshire Valley.",al={"who took the tome","defias book thief","who stole powers of the void"}},{q="What role does she play for new human warlocks?",a="Drusilla is the first trainer for human warlocks. She accepts the tainted letters sent to recruits and teaches basic curses and summoned servitors.",al={"human warlock trainer northshire","who trains warlocks in northshire"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Drusilla La Salle?",a="Drusilla La Salle is a human warlock stationed in the abbey graveyard in Northshire Valley. While holy clerics and paladins train within the abbey walls, she quietly instructs novice humans who possess an affinity for darker arts, teaching them to bend fel and shadow energies to their will.",al={"who is drusilla","drusilla la salle lore","drusilla identity"},it="identity",add="fe9579dd"},{q="Whose side is Drusilla La Salle on?",a="She is aligned with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Although the Light-worshipping clergy at Northshire Abbey view warlocks with suspicion, Drusilla serves the realm by training fledgling practitioners to direct their dangerous talents against Stormwind's enemies.",al={"is drusilla evil","drusilla alliance","drusilla faction"},it="side",add="89e305f6"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn the dark arts from Drusilla, your first mentor. She teaches practical curses and fel summoning, and urges you to hide your ambition in plain sight.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see Drusilla outside Northshire’s holy halls, practicing shadow and demonic pacts beside the consecrated graveyard."},kw={"abbey","drusilla la salle","graveyard","northshire","powers of the void","stolen tome","warlock trainer"},rel={"quest:1598","subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:library-wing-northshire","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn"},src={"Drusilla La Salle"}}
E["npc:gerard-tiller"] = {t="npc",n="Gerard Tiller",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works under the warm sun and longs for spring water. He offers a shiny red apple to any traveler who brings him a skin of it.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works under the warm sun and longs for spring water.",sec={{t="A Thirsty Farmhand",b="Gerard Tiller works the grounds outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards, south of Goldshire. The vineyard is known for its grapes, and keeping the harvest going takes hard labor. The chores leave Gerard thirsty, so he welcomes travelers who bring him a skin of fresh spring water. In return, he gives them shiny red apples gathered from local orchards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerard Tiller?",a="Gerard Tiller works as a human farmhand outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest.",al={"gerard tiller identity","who is gerard","tiller elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gerard Tiller?",a="Look outside the large wooden barn at the Maclure Vineyards, south of Goldshire and east of the Stonefield Farm.",al={"gerard tiller location","where is gerard","find gerard elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Gerard Tiller trade?",a="Gerard trades a Shiny Red Apple for a skin of Refreshing Spring Water.",al={"gerard apple trade","gerard tiller water","what does gerard want"},gp=true},{q="Does Gerard get involved in the Maclure and Stonefield feud?",a="No. Gerard works at the Maclure Vineyards and focuses on his chores and getting water, rather than the rivalry between the Maclures and Stonefields.",al={"gerard tiller feud","maclure feud gerard"},it="side"},{q="What does Gerard Tiller want?",a="Working under the hot sun at the Maclure Vineyards is parching work, and Gerard wants little more than a simple skin of Refreshing Spring Water to quench his thirst. If you bring him a drink, he will gladly trade you a crisp, Shiny Red Apple from the orchard in return.",al={"what does gerard tiller need","gerard tiller trade","what does gerard want"},it="wants",add="467277ed"},{q="Why is Gerard Tiller here?",a="Gerard Tiller makes his living as a laborer tending the grounds outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards. While the surrounding lands of Elwynn face unrest, Gerard remains focused on everyday farm work and looking after the harvest.",al={"why is gerard tiller at the vineyards","gerard tiller location reason","what does gerard tiller do"},it="why_here",add="9aadf23d"},{q="Who is Gerard Tiller tied to?",a="Gerard is tied to the Maclure family, working their vineyards south of Stormwind City. Though he labors directly on their land beside their barns, he minds his own business and avoids the bitter feud raging between the Maclures and their neighboring rivals, the Stonefields.",al={"gerard tiller connections","who does gerard tiller work for","gerard tiller allies"},it="ties",add="9f9d4e60"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gerard trades fresh apples for plain spring water, making him a source of fruit for travelers who want simple ingredients."},kw={"elwynn forest","gerard tiller","give gerard a drink","maclure vineyards","refreshing spring water","shiny red apple"},rel={"quest:16","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},src={"Gerard Tiller"}}
E["npc:gramma-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Gramma Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At the Stonefield farm in Elwynn, Gramma Stonefield quietly works to ease a family feud.",h="At the Stonefield farm in Elwynn, Gramma Stonefield quietly works to ease a family feud.",sec={{t="A Secret Peacemaker",b="Gramma Stonefield has watched the Stonefields and the Maclures bicker for decades across the road. The oldest living member of the Stonefield clan, she sees their rivalry as senseless and harmful. When her grandson Tommy Joe Stonefield falls in love with Maybell Maclure, Gramma chooses compassion over clan loyalty. She turns to her old friend William Pestle in Goldshire and quietly plans ways for the sweethearts to meet in secret, despite the hostility between their farms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gramma Stonefield?",a="Gramma Stonefield, whose given name is Mildred, is the elderly matriarch of the Stonefield family at their farm in Elwynn Forest. She is Tommy Joe Stonefield's grandmother.",al={"who is gramma","mildred stonefield","stonefield grandma"},it="identity"},{q="How does she feel about the feud with the Maclures?",a="Mildred wants no part in the feud with the Maclures. She sees the grudge as foolish and harmful, and would rather the households live in harmony than keep bickering.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","does she hate maclures"},it="side"},{q="Why is she helping Tommy Joe and Maybell?",a="Mildred loves her grandson Tommy Joe and wants him to be happy. She rejects the family feud and asks her old friend William Pestle to devise a solution for Tommy Joe's romance with Maybell Maclure.",al={"why help tommy joe","gramma love potion","help lovers"},it="wants"},{q="Who is William Pestle to her?",a="William Pestle is an old, trusted friend of Gramma Stonefield. He lives at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where he works as an alchemist, and she sends trusted couriers to ask him for remedies and other help for Tommy Joe.",al={"william pestle connection","william pestle gramma"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Gramma Stonefield here?",a="This cottage is her lifelong home. As the matriarch and oldest living member of the Stonefield clan, Mildred resides right here on the family farmstead in Elwynn Forest, quietly watching over her kin while striving to keep their petty rivalries from destroying young lives.",al={"why is gramma stonefield at the farm","stonefield farm gramma location","why is mildred stonefield here"},it="why_here",add="d471da09"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, Gramma Stonefield shows how local conflicts in the heartland can call for quiet diplomacy and empathy."},kw={"elwynn","gramma stonefield","maclure","maybell","mildred","stonefield farm","tommy joe","william pestle"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","npc:maybell-maclure","npc:william-pestle","subzone:stonefield-farm","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Gramma Stonefield"}}
E["npc:guard-thomas"] = {t="npc",n="Guard Thomas",z="elwynn",s="At the bridge west of Eastvale Logging Camp, Guard Thomas watches Elwynn’s eastern frontier. The Stormwind soldier guards local workers from wild predators and murlocs.",h="At the bridge west of Eastvale Logging Camp, Guard Thomas watches Elwynn’s eastern frontier.",sec={{t="On the Eastern Border",b="At the stone bridge over the river toward Eastvale Logging Camp, Guard Thomas holds a quiet but exposed post. The woods around him shelter aggressive creatures, and the logging workers depend on the Stormwind guard for protection. With the army stretched thin, Thomas must rely on travelers to help keep order and carry messages to central command.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Troubles",b="Aggressive bears and prowlers threaten lumberjacks and travelers along Elwynn’s eastern treeline. Murloc tribes have made camps by the waterways, and Guard Thomas tracks them and offers bounties to reduce their numbers. Patrols sent along the river sometimes vanish, leaving Thomas to work out what became of his fellow guards as troubles mount in the region.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas stands on the stone bridge over the river, just west of Eastvale Logging Camp on Elwynn Forest’s eastern road.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","guard thomas bridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Guard Thomas's duty in Elwynn Forest?",a="Guard Thomas protects Elwynn’s eastern frontier for the Stormwind Army. He guards the trade bridge, defends nearby workers from predators, and watches for murlocs along the riverbanks.",al={"what does thomas do","guard thomas role","thomas eastvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas asking for help with lost guards?",a="Patrols sent into the river basins have failed to return. Unable to leave his post without enough guards to replace him, Thomas asks travelers to search the waterways for his missing comrades.",al={"lost guards elwynn","guard thomas missing scouts","what happened to the guards"},it="motive"},{q="Why are murlocs a problem for Guard Thomas?",a="Murloc tribes are pressing farther up eastern Elwynn’s rivers. They threaten logging work and supply routes, so Thomas offers bounties to keep the waterways clear.",al={"murlocs eastvale","why kill murlocs","guard thomas murloc bounty"},it="threat"},{q="Who does Guard Thomas report to?",a="Guard Thomas serves in the Stormwind Army and reports through its hierarchy to regional command in Goldshire and the capital. As trouble grows along the borders, his dispatches also coordinate with Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.",al={"thomas superior","stormwind army chain of command","who does thomas work for"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Guard Thomas send adventurers once their work in Elwynn is done?",a="After threats near Eastvale and the eastern river are dealt with, Thomas directs seasoned travelers toward Westfall to help Gryan Stoutmantle and the struggling People's Militia.",al={"after guard thomas","where to go after eastvale","westfall report"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas is an officer of the Stormwind Army stationed on the eastern frontier of Elwynn Forest. While Stormwind's forces are stretched thin across the kingdom, Thomas holds down the post near Eastvale Logging Camp, safeguarding travelers and workers along the bridge from gnolls and encroaching murlocs.",al={"who is thomas","guard thomas identity","who is guard thomas"},it="identity",add="2ef4fdb3"},{q="Whose side is Guard Thomas on?",a="Thomas serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As a loyal soldier of the Stormwind Army, he acts under the authority of the throne and works directly to secure the realm's borders for its citizens and laborers.",al={"guard thomas faction","who does guard thomas serve","guard thomas alliance"},it="side",add="26bccfb6"},{q="What does Guard Thomas want?",a="Thomas needs capable hands to protect the eastern edge of Elwynn. Between aggressive river murlocs and hostile gnolls threatening the Eastvale woodcutters, he wants the surrounding wilderness secured, the fate of missing patrolmen discovered, and regular intelligence sent back to high command in Stormwind and Westfall.",al={"what does thomas want","guard thomas goals","what does guard thomas need"},it="wants",add="8313e011"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas here?",a="Thomas is posted at the eastern bridge to guard the main crossing into the Eastvale Logging Camp and the borderlands beyond. With Eastvale vital for Stormwind's timber supply and local beasts pressing in from the rivers and hills, a military presence is necessary to keep the road open.",al={"why is guard thomas at the bridge","why is thomas here","guard thomas location reason"},it="why_here",add="c7700b23"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how thinly the Stormwind Army is stretched: Guard Thomas holds a vital frontier post with little support from the crown.",["class:Warrior"]="As a young Alliance warrior, you can look to Thomas for an example of frontline discipline and the hard work of defending a regional border."},kw={"eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","guard thomas","lost guards","murloc","stormwind army","thomas"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","quest:37","quest:46","quest:52","quest:39","npc:gryan-stoutmantle"},src={"Guard Thomas"}}
E["npc:henze-faulk"] = {t="npc",n="Henze Faulk",z="elwynn",s="Near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, Henze Faulk lies gravely wounded. He shielded his companion Gazin Tenorm from the Defias Brotherhood, and now awaits a paladin's aid.",h="Near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, Henze Faulk lies gravely wounded.",sec={{t="A Sacrifice at Heroes' Vigil",b="Henze Faulk lies near the stone ring east of Stormwind, at Heroes' Vigil. Defias marauders ambushed him and his friend Gazin Tenorm there. Henze took the attack so Gazin could survive, and fell to the bandits' blades. Gazin reached the Cathedral of Light to seek help. Henze remains between life and death, awaiting the aid of a paladin carrying a Symbol of Life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Henze Faulk?",a="Henze Faulk is an Ironforge dwarf lying gravely wounded near the stone circle at Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest. Defias bandits struck him down while he protected his friend Gazin Tenorm.",al={"henze faulk","dwarf at heroes vigil","dying dwarf elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Henze Faulk lying on the ground?",a="Henze Faulk lies wounded because the Defias Brotherhood ambushed him and Gazin Tenorm as they traveled. Henze took the brunt of the attack so Gazin could escape, and now awaits the aid of an initiate of the Holy Light.",al={"why is henze dying","is henze dead","henze faulk dead"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Henze's connection to paladins?",a="Henze Faulk is the subject of a rite of passage for young paladins undertaking the trials of the Tome of Divinity. Paladin initiates carry a Symbol of Life to Elwynn and use it to restore Henze, showing their mastery of the Light's blessing of redemption.",al={"henze paladin quest","tome of divinity dwarf"}},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is Henze Faulk's companion. When Defias outlaws cornered them, Henze protected Gazin, who survived and sought help from the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"who is gazin","gazin tenorm friend"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Henze Faulk on?",a="Henze Faulk is firmly allied with the Alliance and the Holy Light. A loyal friend and fellow dwarf of Gazin Tenorm, he fell while bravely defending his friend from the ruthless outlaws of the Defias Brotherhood in Elwynn Forest.",al={"henze faulk faction","is henze alliance","henze faulk allegiance"},it="side",add="162be787"},{q="What does Henze Faulk want?",a="Having fallen to a vicious ambush by the Defias Brotherhood, Henze Faulk's immediate need is the miracle of the Light to restore his life. Beyond survival, his selfless intent was simply to protect his companion, Gazin Tenorm, from harm.",al={"what does henze want","henze faulk goal","henze faulk objective"},it="wants",add="47ed07eb"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a test of mercy when you bring Henze Faulk back from the brink with a Symbol of Life. The Light can do more than aid you in battle; it can defy death.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing Henze Faulk laid low in human lands reminds you that Defias outlaws threaten travelers of every race, not only Stormwind's people."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","gazin tenorm","henze faulk","heroes' vigil","resurrection","symbol of life","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:gazin-tenorm","quest:1641","subzone:heroes-vigil","zone:elwynn","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:dwarf"},src={"Henze Faulk"}}
E["npc:hogger"] = {t="npc",n="Hogger",z="elwynn",s="In southwestern Elwynn Forest, Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls in raids on farms and travelers. His violent attacks have earned him a bounty from the Stormwind Marshals.",h="In southwestern Elwynn Forest, Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls in raids on farms and travelers.",sec={{t="Terror of the Riverpaw",b="Hogger commands the Riverpaw pack from Hogger Hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest. Since the Third War, the gnolls have grown bolder and more coordinated in their raids on nearby homesteads. The Riverpaw have joined forces with the Defias Brotherhood, exchanging their raw ferocity for arms, tactical direction, and magical support. To protect Elwynn's borders and trade routes from further bloodshed, Marshal Dughan has posted a bounty on Hogger's head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger leads the Riverpaw pack in southwestern Elwynn Forest. This massive, dangerous gnoll is known for raiding nearby farmsteads and is wanted by Stormwind authorities for his attacks on human settlements.",al={"hogger lore","who is hogger","riverpaw leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a bounty on Hogger?",a="Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind guard issued a bounty on Hogger for his raids on rural farms and travelers. To prove the deed, bring his huge claw back to Goldshire.",al={"wanted hogger","why kill hogger","hogger bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the Riverpaw gnolls working with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Yes. The Riverpaw pack has joined forces with the Defias Brotherhood, which supplies the gnolls with refined weapons, tactical guidance, and magical support to weaken Stormwind's hold on the region.",al={"hogger defias","gnoll defias connection","riverpaw defias"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Hogger make his camp?",a="Hogger makes his camp atop Hogger Hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest, near the Westfall border with his Riverpaw packmates.",al={"hogger location","where is hogger","hogger hill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Hogger on?",a="Hogger leads the Riverpaw gnolls of southern Elwynn, but his pack does not act alone. They are conspiring with the Defias Brotherhood, trading chaos in the woods for weapons, tactical leadership, and arcane assistance. While gnolls fight chiefly for plunder and territory, Hogger's alliance with the Defias aligns his pack directly against the kingdom of Stormwind and its people.",al={"hogger side","who does hogger work for","who is hogger allied with"},it="side",add="cd1f1084"},{q="Why is Hogger in Elwynn Forest?",a="Hogger has established his stronghold on a hill in southwestern Elwynn Forest to oversee his pack's aggressive expansion. From this camp, the Riverpaw gnolls raid nearby human farms and settlements, capitalizing on the kingdom's stretched defenses while coordinating under the influence and backing of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"why is hogger here","hogger elwynn forest reason","why did hogger come here"},it="why_here",add="3ddc17ac"},{q="Why is Hogger so feared?",a="Hogger is feared throughout Elwynn Forest for his vicious strength and cunning leadership. Unlike ordinary wandering gnolls, he is an exceptionally formidable chieftain who easily overpowers lone travelers and inexperienced adventurers. His raids against local homesteads have proven so destructive that the Stormwind Marshals consider him a priority threat to the realm.",al={"why is hogger famous","why is hogger feared","why is hogger notorious"},it="fame",add="d88533c5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, facing Hogger is an early trial for Stormwind's young defenders and a response to threats in Elwynn's heartland.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Hogger's raids stretch the Stormwind army, leaving the Marshals to rely on roaming adventurers to keep order near the capital."},kw={"bounty","defias","dughan","elwynn","gnoll","goldshire","hogger","riverpaw"},rel={"quest:176","topic:riverpaw-pack","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:goldshire","topic:gnoll"},src={"Hogger"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-farley"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Farley",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Innkeeper Farley welcomes travelers with food, beds, and hearthstones. Well-liked and observant, he keeps misplaced mail and hears the troubles of those on the road.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Innkeeper Farley welcomes travelers with food, beds, and hearthstones.",sec={{t="A Goldshire Fixture",b="Travelers bound for Stormwind, Westfall, and Duskwood find Innkeeper Farley behind the Lion's Pride Inn counter in Goldshire. He offers meals, ale, cheese, and a bed, and sets hearthstones for those who need one. With a welcoming hand and a sharp eye, Farley serves all who pass through this busy waystation and keeps order at the inn.",sp=0},{t="The Courier's Abandoned Chest",b="At the crossroads of Stormwind, Westfall, and Duskwood, Innkeeper Farley hears rumors and deals with strange travelers. Once, a courier fled into the night in terror, leaving his satchel behind. Farley safely stowed the leftover missives in an upstairs chest. Among them lies an undelivered letter addressed to former schoolmaster Stalvan Mistmantle, a clue for investigators tracing the fallen tutor's movements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley?",a="Innkeeper Farley serves travelers at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, offering rest and supplies to those traversing Elwynn Forest.",al={"innkeeper farley","fredrik farley","who is the goldshire innkeeper"},it="identity"},{q="What does Farley know about Stalvan Mistmantle?",a="Farley recalls a terrified courier who fled the Lion's Pride Inn at night, leaving several deliveries behind. He safely stored the abandoned letters in an upstairs chest, including an undelivered letter addressed to Stalvan Mistmantle for investigators to retrieve.",al={"farley stalvan","stalvan letter goldshire","legend of stalvan farley"}},{q="What services does Farley provide at the inn?",a="Farley sets hearthstones, rents rooms, and sells a wide variety of drinks, juices, and cheeses from across the Alliance. The cheeses include Alterac Swiss, Dalaran Sharp, and local Stormwind Brie.",al={"lion's pride services","farley food and drink","goldshire hearthstone"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Farley on?",a="Innkeeper Farley is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Alliance. From the Lion's Pride Inn he offers shelter, food, and hospitality to fellow Alliance citizens, travelers, and soldiers traversing the heartlands of Elwynn.",al={"innkeeper farley faction","who does farley serve","farley alliance"},it="side",add="bf81c39e"},{q="What does Innkeeper Farley want?",a="Farley's primary concern is keeping the Lion's Pride Inn running smoothly. Between breaking up tavern brawls and pouring ale, he wants to provide a warm haven for weary travelers.",al={"what does farley want","farley goals","innkeeper farley motive"},it="wants",add="f8150ed8"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Farley here?",a="Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. As Goldshire sits at the crossroads of Elwynn Forest, Farley remains to tend the hearth and manage one of the realm's busiest taverns.",al={"why is farley at the inn","why is innkeeper farley here"},it="why_here",add="5df540c8"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley tied to?",a="Farley is a fixture of Goldshire, well known to the travelers who pass through Elwynn Forest. The traveling bard Falkhaan Isenstrider sends young adventurers his way to rest at the Lion's Pride.",al={"farley family","who is innkeeper farley related to","farley connections"},it="ties",add="a88a382c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a fresh recruit leaving Northshire Valley, you can bind your hearthstone and buy provisions at Farley's counter in the Lion's Pride Inn."},kw={"elwynn forest","fredrik farley","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","stalvan"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:66","topic:alliance","zone:duskwood"},src={"Innkeeper Farley"}}
E["npc:katie-hunter"] = {t="npc",n="Katie Hunter",z="elwynn",s="At the Eastvale Logging Camp stables, Katie Hunter tends horses for Stormwind and trusted Alliance champions. She works with Randal Hunter to keep travelers and soldiers mounted for the kingdom’s roads.",h="At the Eastvale Logging Camp stables, Katie Hunter tends horses for Stormwind and trusted Alliance champions.",sec={{t="Stables of Eastvale",b="Katie Hunter tends the horses at the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. While lumberjacks cut timber for Stormwind’s reconstruction, she raises dependable pintos, mares, and swift steeds for riders. Her horses carry people along the kingdom’s roads and the dangerous routes of southern Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Katie Hunter?",a="Katie Hunter breeds and sells horses for the Kingdom of Stormwind at the Eastvale Logging Camp stables in Elwynn Forest.",al={"katie hunter elwynn","who is katie hunter","katie hunter horse vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Katie Hunter?",a="You can find Katie in the northern part of the Eastvale Logging Camp, tending the corral and stables near Randal Hunter, a riding trainer, in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"katie hunter location","where is katie hunter","find katie hunter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can non-humans buy horses from her?",a="Yes. Non-human buyers need exalted standing with the Kingdom of Stormwind. Human adventurers can buy her horses without special standing.",al={"dwarf buy horse","night elf horse mount","stormwind reputation mount"},gp=true},{q="What horses does she sell?",a="Katie sells standard riding horses, including pinto, brown, and chestnut varieties, as well as swift, armored steeds such as the Swift Palomino, Swift Brown Steed, and Swift White Steed.",al={"what mounts does katie sell","katie hunter horse types"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Katie Hunter on?",a="Katie Hunter is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a member of the Alliance. Operating out of Eastvale Logging Camp, she caters directly to Stormwind's citizens, providing dependable mounts to travelers and champions who have proven their dedication to the crown.",al={"katie hunter faction","is katie hunter alliance","who does katie hunter serve"},it="side",add="d7735dfa"},{q="What does Katie Hunter want?",a="Katie Hunter focuses on tending and selling Eastvale's renowned horses. She seeks to supply capable mounts to reliable adventurers, ensuring that only trusted allies of Stormwind acquire her prized stock to aid their travels across the kingdom.",al={"what does katie hunter want","katie hunter purpose","katie hunter goal"},it="wants",add="d5257f59"},{q="Why is Katie Hunter here at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Katie Hunter makes her home at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest to run the camp's stables. Working alongside Randal Hunter, she manages the breeding and care of riding horses away from the bustle of Stormwind City, using the camp's open pasture.",al={"why is katie hunter in eastvale","why is katie hunter here","what is katie hunter doing in elwynn"},it="why_here",add="5cab52df"},{q="Who is Katie Hunter tied to?",a="Katie Hunter works closely with Randal Hunter, who also oversees the stables at Eastvale Logging Camp. Together, they manage the camp's equine trade and serve as the primary source of horses for Stormwind's allies.",al={"katie hunter connections","who is katie hunter related to","katie hunter randal hunter"},it="ties",add="85933b18"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can buy a classic Stormwind horse from Katie once you have mastered the basics of horsemanship.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an allied race, you can earn the privilege of riding Katie’s prized steeds into battle by gaining high standing and respect with Stormwind’s court."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn forest","horse vendor","katie hunter","logging camp","mounts","stables","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Katie Hunter"}}
E["npc:khelden-bremen"] = {t="npc",n="Khelden Bremen",z="elwynn",s="On the upper floor of Northshire Abbey, Khelden Bremen teaches human mages their first spells. He prepares novices to serve Stormwind through the arcane arts.",h="On the upper floor of Northshire Abbey, Khelden Bremen teaches human mages their first spells.",sec={{t="Tutor of the Arcane",b="Khelden Bremen teaches new human mages in a study on the upper floor of Northshire Abbey. While clergy and defenders pursue their work below, he shows novices how to focus and shape magical energy safely. His lessons prepare them for the road through Elwynn Forest and for further study in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Khelden Bremen?",a="Khelden Bremen trains new mages at Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. He teaches their first spells and the foundations of arcane study.",al={"who is khelden","bremen","mage trainer northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Khelden Bremen?",a="Khelden Bremen is on the second floor of Northshire Abbey. Enter the abbey and take the staircase in the second room on the left.",al={"where is khelden","khelden bremen location","northshire mage trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play for new adventurers?",a="Human mages arriving in Northshire are directed to Khelden Bremen, often with a Glyphic Letter of introduction. He teaches their first spells and helps them control their magical aptitude.",al={"what does khelden do","bremen quests","glyphic letter recipient"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Khelden Bremen on?",a="Khelden Bremen stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed within Northshire Abbey, he serves the realm by mentoring the next generation of spellcasters and preparing them to defend humanity's lands against rising dangers.",al={"khelden bremen faction","who does khelden serve","is khelden bremen alliance"},it="side",add="7cfd66d2"},{q="What does Khelden Bremen want?",a="Khelden's goal is to instruct novice mages in the arcane arts. He seeks dedicated apprentices ready to learn basic incantations, master their burgeoning intellect, and harness their power responsibly for the safety of Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"khelden bremen goal","what does khelden want"},it="wants",add="032606f2"},{q="Why is Khelden Bremen here at Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey acts as a recruitment and training haven for young defenders answering Stormwind's call. Bremen resides on the upper floor of the abbey specifically to receive fledgling human practitioners and guide their initial steps into magic before they venture deeper into the wider realm.",al={"why is khelden in northshire","khelden bremen why here"},it="why_here",add="8660ec47"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a human mage, Khelden Bremen offers your first formal arcane instruction before you continue your studies in the towers of Stormwind City."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage trainer","northshire abbey"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:3104","zone:elwynn"},src={"Khelden Bremen"}}
E["npc:lyria-du-lac"] = {t="npc",n="Lyria Du Lac",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Lyria Du Lac trains young warriors behind the village smithy. She teaches them to master their stances and arms.",h="In Goldshire, Lyria Du Lac trains young warriors behind the village smithy.",sec={{t="Warrior Trainer of Goldshire",b="Lyria Du Lac trains young warriors in the yard behind Goldshire's forge. She teaches those fresh from Northshire Abbey, judges their readiness, and introduces specialized combat techniques. Warriors take up shield and blade for Stormwind, facing the threats of Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Lyria Du Lac?",a="In Goldshire, find Lyria Du Lac outside behind the blacksmith shop, just west of the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"lyria du lac location","where is lyria","warrior trainer goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What service does Lyria Du Lac provide?",a="Lyria Du Lac trains warriors in combat maneuvers, stances, and battle disciplines as they advance in skill.",al={"what does lyria do","lyria du lac role","what does lyria teach"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Lyria Du Lac?",a="Lyria Du Lac gives developing warriors 'A Warrior's Training'. She sends them to veteran Harry Burlguard at the Pig and Whistle tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"lyria du lac quests","warrior quest goldshire"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lyria Du Lac?",a="Lyria Du Lac is a veteran human warrior who serves as a combat instructor in Elwynn Forest. Stationed behind the smithy in Goldshire, she evaluates and instructs novice fighters making their way into the wider kingdom, teaching them how to harness their martial prowess and survive the threats encroaching on Stormwind's borders.",al={"who is lyria","lyria du lac lore","who is lyria du lac"},it="identity",add="f698c0e4"},{q="Whose side is Lyria Du Lac on?",a="Lyria stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. By preparing fresh recruits to defend Elwynn Forest from local dangers like bandits and gnolls, she helps reinforce the kingdom's military readiness during a time when regular garrison forces are stretched thin.",al={"lyria du lac faction","lyria du lac allegiance","who does lyria serve"},it="side",add="34434421"},{q="Why is Lyria Du Lac here in Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is the natural staging point for travelers leaving Northshire Valley, making it the ideal post to drill promising adventurers in weaponcraft. Stationed right behind the blacksmith, Lyria ensures that any fledgling warrior who arrives in town is properly conditioned and disciplined before facing greater perils.",al={"why is lyria in goldshire","lyria du lac location purpose","what brought lyria here"},it="why_here",add="afd6a9c2"},{q="What does Lyria Du Lac want?",a="Lyria seeks capable pupils ready to master the art of combat. She wants to see young warriors hone their discipline, master the stances and techniques of battle, and use their training to defend the realm from whatever chaos threatens its peace.",al={"what does lyria want","lyria du lac goal","lyria du lac motive"},it="wants",add="277e5774"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior fresh from Northshire Abbey, you meet Lyria Du Lac, your first major trainer in Elwynn Forest. She helps you master your stance and sharpen your melee tactics.",["faction:Alliance"]="Behind Goldshire's forge, Lyria Du Lac trains local recruits to defend Stormwind's heartland from Defias brigands and gnoll raiders."},kw={"a warrior's training","blacksmith","elwynn forest","goldshire","lyria du lac","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:1638"},src={"Lyria Du Lac"}}
E["npc:ma-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Ma Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, Ma Stonefield tends to hardships close to home. Beside Auntie Bernice, she faces farm troubles, neighboring rivalries, and pests.",h="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, Ma Stonefield tends to hardships close to home.",sec={{t="Homestead Troubles",b="Ma Stonefield watches over the farm beside her family cottage in southwestern Elwynn Forest, with Auntie Bernice Stonefield at her side. The neighboring Maclure homestead and nearby pumpkin patches bring little peace. Wild boars threaten the Stonefield crops, and Princess causes the greatest trouble. The enormous prize sow tramples fields and devours the harvest the family worked hard to grow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ma Stonefield?",a="Ma Stonefield is an elder of the Stonefield family, living at their farmstead in southwestern Elwynn Forest with relatives such as Auntie Bernice.",al={"who is ma stonefield","ma stonefield","stonefield mother"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ma Stonefield?",a="Ma Stonefield stands outdoors in front of the main house at Stonefield Farm, west of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.",al={"ma stonefield location","where is ma stonefield","stonefield farm loc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What problem does Ma Stonefield need solved?",a="Ma Stonefield wants help stopping Princess, a massive prize pig that repeatedly rampages through nearby fields and devours local crops.",al={"ma stonefield quest","princess sow quest","princess must die questgiver"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ma Stonefield on?",a="Ma Stonefield is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a member of the Alliance. Like most rural folk living in the heart of Elwynn Forest, her focus remains squarely on her family's farm, though she relies on Alliance adventurers to step in when local troubles grow too big for simple farmers to handle.",al={"is ma stonefield alliance","ma stonefield faction"},it="side",add="51af3003"},{q="Why is Ma Stonefield here?",a="The Stonefield Farm is Ma Stonefield's lifelong home. She lives and works the land in Elwynn Forest alongside her kin, tending to the daily chores of country life right outside the family homestead near \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield.",al={"why is ma stonefield at the farm","what does ma stonefield do here"},it="why_here",add="02537c40"},{q="Who is Ma Stonefield tied to?",a="Ma Stonefield is a matriarch of the Stonefield clan, living alongside relatives such as \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield at their homestead in Elwynn Forest. Her family has long-standing roots in the valley, though they also share a bitter, enduring feud with their neighbors, the Maclures.",al={"ma stonefield family","who is ma stonefield related to"},it="ties",add="ae4d5db0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in Elwynn Forest, helping hardworking homesteaders like Ma Stonefield helps protect Stormwind's agricultural backbone."},kw={"bernice stonefield","elwynn forest","ma stonefield","princess","princess must die","stonefield farm"},rel={"subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:88","zone:elwynn"},src={"Ma Stonefield"}}
E["npc:marshal-dughan"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal Dughan",z="elwynn",s="Goldshire's marshal faces threats on every road and mine. Marshal Dughan commands the Stormwind Army detachment there, but kobolds, gnolls, and bandits stretch his small garrison. He depends on independent adventurers to help protect the town and nearby farms.",h="Goldshire's marshal faces threats on every road and mine.",sec={{t="Commander of the Crossroads",b="Marshal Dughan directs Elwynn Forest's defense from Goldshire, outside the Lion's Pride Inn. Stormwind's soldiers are tied up elsewhere, while trouble grows in the woods. Kobolds crowd the mines, gnolls gather along the riverbanks, and highwaymen harass travelers on the King's Road. With too few footmen under his command, Dughan sends new recruits to reinforce outposts and scout dangerous ground.",sp=0},{t="Threats on Every Border",b="Kobolds overrun Fargodeep and Jasperlode Mines, threatening Goldshire's mineral supply. West of town, Hogger's Riverpaw gnolls press against Westbrook Garrison. Eastward, Guard Thomas reports vicious murlocs killing patrols along the river. Dughan has too few soldiers to meet each threat, so he needs capable mercenaries to help contain them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands a Stormwind Army detachment in Goldshire. He coordinates Elwynn Forest's defenses against thieves, gnolls, and kobolds.",al={"dughan","marshal dughan lore","goldshire marshal"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't Dughan send more guards to help Westbrook Garrison or the east?",a="Stormwind's forces are spread thin, leaving Dughan with barely enough guards to keep order in Goldshire. He has too few soldiers for every farm and border post, so he relies on visiting adventurers to scout danger, carry dispatches, and confront local threats.",al={"why no guards","goldshire garrison strength","dughan troops"}},{q="What is Dughan's view on the murloc threat in Elwynn?",a="Dughan first dismissed Remy 'Two Times' warnings that murlocs threatened the region. Guard Thomas's reports of Rolf Hartford and Malakai Stone's deaths along the eastern waterways convinced him of the danger.",al={"dughan murlocs","remy two times murloc","dughan fish men"},sp=1},{q="How does Dughan handle local crime and rowdy civilians?",a="Dughan is charged with keeping peace in Goldshire and the surrounding lands. He says keeping order is hard enough amid Elwynn's new troubles, and focuses on kobolds to the north and gnolls and thieves to the west.",al={"dughan crime","goldshire law","stockade threat"}},{q="Why is Dughan concerned about the mines?",a="Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine supply Stormwind with gold and ore. Kobolds have overrun both mines, driven out the miners, and threaten to tunnel beneath Elwynn's settlements.",al={"fargodeep mine dughan","jasperlode mine dughan","kobold infestation"}},{q="Does Marshal Dughan coordinate with Westfall?",a="Yes. After an adventurer proves capable in Elwynn Forest, Dughan sends them to report to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. The People's Militia needs veteran help against the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"dughan gryan","report to westfall","dughan sentinel hill"}},{q="Whose side is Marshal Dughan on?",a="Marshal Dughan serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As an officer in the Stormwind Army, he answers directly to the realm's military hierarchy, carrying out the crown's orders to maintain order and protect the heartland despite dwindling royal reinforcements.",al={"dughan faction","who does dughan serve","marshal dughan allegiance"},it="side",add="72888056"},{q="What does Marshal Dughan want?",a="Dughan aims to secure Elwynn Forest and safeguard Goldshire against multiplying threats. With his garrison stretched thin, he seeks capable adventurers to scout the infested Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines, contain the Defias bandits and gnolls in the west, and assess the growing danger along the riverbanks.",al={"dughan goal","what does dughan need","dughan objectives"},it="wants",add="9141816c"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan stationed in Goldshire?",a="Dughan is stationed in Goldshire as commander of the local Stormwind Army detachment. Tasked with the defense of central Elwynn, he oversees town peacekeeping, coordinates outposts like Westbrook Garrison, and manages the defense against encroaching beasts, kobolds, and criminals who threaten the capital's breadbasket.",al={"why is dughan in goldshire","marshal dughan purpose here","dughan post"},it="why_here",add="8808e7de"},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan tied to?",a="Dughan works closely with local outpost commanders across Elwynn, such as Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison and Guard Thomas along the eastern bridges. Outside Elwynn, he maintains communication with military peers like Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall, sharing intelligence on regional criminal activity.",al={"dughan connections","who does dughan work with","dughan allies"},it="ties",add="156c33b1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn, you receive your first military assignments from Marshal Dughan, Stormwind's local authority.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see Stormwind's footmen hold the line with discipline despite impossible odds and too few soldiers."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","goldshire","hogger","jasperlode","marshal dughan","stormwind army","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","npc:guard-thomas","npc:remy-two-times","quest:176","subzone:westbrook-garrison","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Marshal Dughan"}}
E["npc:marshal-mcbride"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal McBride",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Marshal McBride commands Stormwind's garrison and defends the valley. Kobolds threaten its farms and mines, so he directs new recruits against them.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Marshal McBride commands Stormwind's garrison and defends the valley.",sec={{t="Commander of Northshire",b="Marshal McBride commands Stormwind's garrison outside Northshire Abbey. The abbey is a place of faith and learning, while unrest across the kingdom has left military garrisons short of soldiers. With only a handful of sworn guards, McBride must keep the valley peaceful and protect its food and resources. Green recruits arrive seeking training from the abbey's masters, and he must put them to work.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Incursion",b="Kobolds have grown more aggressive around Northshire. Once a nuisance, they have spread through the woods and seized Echo Ridge Mine, an important local resource. Short of regular soldiers, McBride calls on paladins, warriors, and other novices to drive back the tunneling kobolds and learn how far the infestation reaches before the valley is cut off.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride commands Stormwind's garrison at Northshire Abbey. He defends Northshire Valley and directs new recruits into service.",al={"marshal mcbride","who is mcbride","northshire commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why is McBride having recruits fight kobolds?",a="Kobolds have overrun the woods around Northshire and seized Echo Ridge Mine. With Stormwind's forces stretched thin, McBride sends newly arrived adventurers to drive them out and secure the area.",al={"why kill kobolds","kobold problem","echo ridge problem"},it="motive"},{q="Where does McBride send recruits next?",a="After a recruit has handled the threats in Northshire Valley, McBride sends them south along the road to Goldshire to help Marshal Dughan.",al={"where do i go after mcbride","after northshire","next town"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine is a mineral-rich cavern on the northern edge of Northshire Valley. Kobolds have overrun it, and McBride has ordered several efforts to reclaim it.",al={"echo ridge","the mine in northshire"},it="place"},{q="Does McBride command the abbey itself?",a="No. Northshire Abbey is maintained by the holy orders and priests of the Light. McBride commands the military garrison defending the abbey and the surrounding valley.",al={"does mcbride lead northshire abbey","who is in charge of the abbey"},it="in_charge"},{q="Is McBride concerned about threats beyond kobolds?",a="Kobolds are McBride's most immediate concern, but bandits and outlaws linger at the valley's edges, signs of wider unrest across Elwynn Forest.",al={"defias in northshire","is northshire safe"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Marshal McBride on?",a="Marshal McBride is a loyal officer of the Stormwind Army and the Grand Alliance. He answers to the crown of Stormwind and stands watch over Northshire Valley to ensure the safety of the kingdom's citizens and training recruits.",al={"who does mcbride serve","mcbride allegiance","what faction is mcbride"},it="side",add="05ea779e"},{q="What does Marshal McBride want?",a="McBride wants to secure Northshire Valley against growing local threats. With the Stormwind Army stretched thin, he seeks to mobilize new recruits, paladins, and volunteers to purge the aggressive kobolds infesting the valley and reclaim Echo Ridge Mine.",al={"mcbride goal","what is mcbride trying to do","mcbride plans"},it="wants",add="b6028054"},{q="Why is Marshal McBride here?",a="McBride is stationed outside Northshire Abbey as the commander of the valley's military garrison. Stormwind tasked him with maintaining order, organizing defenses, and training fresh arrivals before sending proven soldiers into Elwynn Forest and beyond.",al={"why is mcbride in northshire","mcbride post","why is marshal mcbride at the abbey"},it="why_here",add="cc66b2df"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride tied to?",a="McBride is bound to the high command of the Stormwind Army and coordinates with local authorities across Elwynn, eventually directing capable fighters to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. He works alongside the abbey's clergy and trainers to prepare new defenders for the kingdom.",al={"mcbride connections","who does mcbride report to","mcbride stormwind army"},it="ties",add="307fdf7d"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human beginning in Northshire, you first meet Marshal McBride, Stormwind's royal authority in the valley.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can serve the kingdom by helping McBride clear kobolds from Echo Ridge's tunnels.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you begin at the Grand Alliance's frontier in humanity's heartland, where McBride brings recruits into the Crown's service."},kw={"douglas mcbride","echo ridge","elwynn","kobold","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","quest:15","quest:21","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Marshal McBride"}}
E["npc:maybell-maclure"] = {t="npc",n="Maybell Maclure",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest, Maybell Maclure loves a Stonefield in secret. Her family’s bitter feud with the neighboring Stonefields keeps her apart from Tommy Joe Stonefield.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest, Maybell Maclure loves a Stonefield in secret.",sec={{t="Star-Crossed in the Vineyards",b="Maybell Maclure works the family vineyards under the shadow of a long feud with the Stonefields next door. She has fallen in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield, heir to the rival farm. Their relatives keep them apart, and Maybell searches for a way to speak with him beyond her family’s watchful eyes.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction for True Love",b="Unable to cross between the farms openly, Maybell turns to sympathetic travelers and Gramma Stonefield for help. William Pestle, Goldshire’s alchemist, brews an invisibility liquor. Maybell drinks it to slip away from the Maclure homestead unseen and meet Tommy Joe by the riverbank.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why can't Maybell and Tommy Joe see each other?",a="The Maclure and Stonefield families have kept a bitter rivalry for years. Both forbid contact between their households, so Maybell and Tommy Joe hide their romance from their kin.",al={"why family feud","maclure stonefield feud","why cant they be together"},it="conflict"},{q="What prevents Maybell from leaving the vineyard?",a="Maybell’s family watches her closely because of the feud with the Stonefields. She needs help meeting Tommy Joe without drawing their attention.",al={"how does maybell sneak out","invisibility potion elwynn","how does she meet tommy"},sp=1},{q="Where does Maybell meet Tommy Joe?",a="Tommy Joe waits by the riverbank on the border between the Maclure Vineyards and Stonefield Farm, out of direct view of both farmsteads.",al={"meeting spot","where are they meeting","where is tommy joe"},it="place"},{q="Who helps Maybell with her romance?",a="Gramma Stonefield sympathizes with the lovers and directs willing travelers to William Pestle, the alchemist in Goldshire, who provides what they need for a secret meeting.",al={"who helps maybell","stonefield helpers"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell Maclure is a young human woman living at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. She is caught in the middle of a bitter, longstanding feud between her family and their neighbors, the Stonefields, after falling deeply in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who is maybell","who is maybell maclure","maybell maclure lore"},it="identity",add="c4338ded"},{q="Whose side is Maybell Maclure on?",a="She is a loyal subject of the Alliance and a daughter of the Maclure household. However, when it comes to the petty, bitter rivalry between the Maclures and the Stonefields, she rejects the hatred entirely, choosing her love for Tommy Joe over her family's grudge.",al={"is maybell alliance","whose side is maybell on","maybell faction"},it="side",add="9f94442c"},{q="What does Maybell Maclure want?",a="Maybell wants nothing more than to be with Tommy Joe Stonefield. Because their families harbor an intense mutual hatred, she seeks the aid of sympathetic travelers and trusted confidants to find ways to meet him in secret without being caught.",al={"what does maybell want","maybell maclure goal","why does maybell need help"},it="wants",add="cbd5fa72"},{q="Why is Maybell Maclure here?",a="Maybell resides at the Maclure Vineyards, her family's estate in southern Elwynn Forest. She remains confined to the vineyard grounds under the watchful eyes of her relatives, hoping for a chance to slip away and see her beloved.",al={"why is maybell maclure here","why is maybell at the vineyards"},it="why_here",add="b079e731"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure tied to?",a="Maybell is part of the Maclure family of vineyard owners. She is romantically entwined with Tommy Joe Stonefield, the heir to the rival Stonefield farmstead, and maintains secret ties with Gramma Stonefield, who supports the young couple's clandestine romance.",al={"maybell maclure relationships","who is maybell related to","maybell ties"},it="ties",add="26be6d7a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers crossing Elwynn Forest, Maybell’s romance shows how personal troubles and old grudges persist in the kingdom’s heartlands."},kw={"lovers","maclure","maybell","stonefield","tommy joe","vineyards"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","subzone:maclure-vineyards","npc:gramma-stonefield","npc:william-pestle","quest:114","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Maybell Maclure"}}
E["npc:merissa-stilwell"] = {t="npc",n="Merissa Stilwell",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Merissa Stilwell welcomes newcomers to Northshire Valley. The young human townsperson offers a cheerful greeting and a helping hand to those training nearby.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Merissa Stilwell welcomes newcomers to Northshire Valley.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Face in Northshire",b="Merissa Stilwell greets fresh recruits arriving in Northshire Valley from her place at Northshire Abbey. She offers newcomers simple hospitality and practical advice on resting and finding their way. Her surname is shared by craftsmen and homesteaders across the kingdom, including the blacksmith Jordan Stilwell and the Westfall defender Daphne Stilwell. Merissa remains a peaceful local presence amid the kingdom's rising tensions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Merissa Stilwell?",a="Merissa Stilwell is a friendly human resident of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. She offers advice and a warm welcome to travelers arriving there.",al={"merissa stilwell","who is merissa","stilwell girl northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Merissa Stilwell?",a="You can find Merissa Stilwell at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley, within Elwynn Forest.",al={"merissa stilwell location","where is merissa","find merissa"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Merissa related to the other Stilwells in the kingdom?",a="Merissa Stilwell shares her surname with the smith Jordan Stilwell and Daphne Stilwell in Westfall. She lives quietly at Northshire Abbey, welcoming travelers rather than fighting bandits or forging blades.",al={"stilwell family","daphne stilwell relative","jordan stilwell relative"},it="ties"},{q="Does Merissa Stilwell offer any quests?",a="No. Merissa Stilwell has no task for travelers; she simply greets newcomers passing through Northshire.",al={"merissa quests","merissa stilwell quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Merissa Stilwell on?",a="Merissa Stilwell is a loyal subject of the Grand Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. Residing peacefully at Northshire Abbey, she welcomes the travelers and recruits arriving in the valley.",al={"merissa stilwell faction","is merissa stilwell alliance"},it="side",add="a071eba0"},{q="Why is Merissa Stilwell in Northshire?",a="Merissa spends her days around Northshire Abbey. Like many ordinary folk of the kingdom, she makes her life in Elwynn Forest and welcomes the newcomers who arrive in the valley.",al={"why is merissa stilwell here","what is merissa doing in northshire"},it="why_here",add="57a6fac4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit leaving Northshire's sheltered cloister, you find in Merissa the warm hospitality of Elwynn before the harsh realities of the Defias threat set in."},kw={"elwynn","merissa","northshire","stilwell"},rel={"zone:elwynn","npc:jordan-stilwell","npc:daphne-stilwell"},src={"Merissa Stilwell"}}
E["npc:morgan-the-collector"] = {t="npc",n="Morgan the Collector",z="elwynn",s="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Morgan the Collector directs Defias extortion and gathering across Elwynn Forest. A high-ranking operative, he coordinates local theft from the farmhouse while Goldshire's guard keeps watch nearby.",h="At the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Morgan the Collector directs Defias extortion and gathering across Elwynn...",sec={{t="The Tithe of Elwynn",b="Morgan the Collector skims gold from Elwynn Forest's mines for the Defias Brotherhood. While common bandits harass travelers on the roads, he directs organized shakedowns and gathers stolen coin and supplies for the Brotherhood's wider network. His headquarters is the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, where loyal enforcers including Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor surround him.",sp=0},{t="A Signet of the Past",b="Morgan carries a distinctive signet ring that marks his authority. Investigators in Goldshire see the ring as evidence connecting the masked thieves terrorizing the heartland to the disgraced Stonemasons Guild, which rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. Recovering the ring reveals who directs the bandits in the woods.",sp=1,bt={"q123.3"}}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan the Collector?",a="Morgan is a high-ranking officer in the Defias Brotherhood who collects gold taken from Elwynn Forest's mines and coordinates bandit activity in the region.",al={"who is morgan","morgan lore","collector in elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Morgan found?",a="Morgan keeps his stolen goods in the farmhouse at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"morgan location","where is morgan the collector","brackwell pumpkin patch house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Stormwind hunting him?",a="Marshal Dughan and local authorities want Morgan eliminated to sever Defias leadership in Elwynn and recover proof of who organizes the rural uprisings.",al={"why kill morgan","manhunt target"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is special about the ring he carries?",a="Morgan carries a signet ring that gives authorities evidence as they investigate his activities in Elwynn Forest.",al={"collectors ring","collector signet ring","morgan ring lore"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Whose side is Morgan the Collector on?",a="Morgan the Collector is a dedicated operative of the Defias Brotherhood. Rather than a common highwayman, he serves as an officer within the criminal organization, working directly against the Kingdom of Stormwind and orchestrating brotherhood activity throughout the heart of Elwynn Forest.",al={"morgan collector faction","what faction is morgan","is morgan defias"},it="side",add="8321821e"},{q="What does Morgan the Collector want?",a="Morgan acts as the ringleader overseeing Defias operations across Elwynn Forest. Bearing the moniker 'the Collector,' his aim is to gather wealth, resources, and influence for the Brotherhood's uprising, establishing a fortified foothold in the pumpkin patch right under the noses of Stormwind's guards.",al={"what is morgan trying to do","morgan collector goal","morgan collector motive"},it="wants",add="5f1d52ce"},{q="Why is Morgan the Collector in Elwynn Forest?",a="Morgan has established himself at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch to personally direct the Defias Brotherhood's local operations. By taking refuge in the farmhouse alongside lieutenants Surena Caledon and Erlan Drudgemoor, he keeps tight coordination over the bandits spreading throughout the region.",al={"why is morgan at brackwell pumpkin patch","what brought morgan here"},it="why_here",add="2a29f808"},{q="Who is Morgan the Collector tied to?",a="His signet ring becomes evidence in an investigation of the outlaws troubling Elwynn Forest and their connections.",al={"who does morgan work with","morgan collector associates","morgan stonemasons"},it="ties",add="ceb85f69"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see how Morgan's discipline turns scattered thieves into an organized underground syndicate that funds an insurgency.",["race:Human"]="As a Human, taking down Morgan strikes back at the traitors who have turned Stormwind's peaceful farms into fortified bandit dens."},kw={"brackwell","brotherhood","defias","dughan","manhunt","morgan","pumpkin patch","signet","the collector"},rel={"quest:147","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stonemasons-guild","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:1688","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Morgan the Collector"}}
E["npc:priestess-anetta"] = {t="npc",n="Priestess Anetta",z="elwynn",s="Inside Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta teaches new priests their first rites of the Holy Light. She is a human cleric and a member of the Brotherhood of Northshire.",h="Inside Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta teaches new priests their first rites of the Holy Light.",sec={{t="Tender of the Faithful",b="On the ground floor of Northshire Abbey, Priestess Anetta keeps to the quiet library wing. Defias bandits and kobolds trouble the valley, and she reminds those who pass that the Light may be the one thing that saves them someday.",sp=0},{t="Guiding Novice Priests",b="New human priests come to Priestess Anetta in the cloister with a hallowed letter of introduction. She teaches them to channel holy words to mend flesh and call down smiting radiance against evil. Under her guidance, the young acolytes prepare to carry the Light beyond Northshire's secluded walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Priestess Anetta?",a="Priestess Anetta is a human cleric of the Holy Light and a member of the Brotherhood of Northshire. On the ground floor of Northshire Abbey, she mentors newly arrived priests in their first sacred rites.",al={"who is anetta","priestess anetta lore","priestess anetta northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Priestess Anetta?",a="Priestess Anetta is inside Northshire Abbey in northern Elwynn Forest. Enter the front gates, go into the main hall, and look on the ground floor of the library wing.",al={"where is priestess anetta","anetta location","find anetta"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does she play in the Abbey's defense?",a="Stormwind marshals and recruits fight to reclaim the valley from Defias bandits and kobolds, while Priestess Anetta trains priests to heal and protect their comrades with the Light.",al={"what does anetta do","anetta role"},it="purpose"},{q="What training does she offer?",a="Priestess Anetta teaches young priests entry-level prayers and clerical spells, including how to heal and smite enemies in the name of the Holy Light.",al={"can anetta teach me spells","anetta priest spells"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Priestess Anetta on?",a="Priestess Anetta stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind, the Holy Light, and the Brotherhood of Northshire. Serving within Northshire Abbey, she works to aid the realm's defenders and uphold the peaceful sanctuary against surrounding threats.",al={"anetta faction","who does anetta serve","priestess anetta loyalty"},it="side",add="d2501181"},{q="What does Priestess Anetta want?",a="Priestess Anetta wants to prepare a new generation to wield the Holy Light. Her calling is to guide fledgling priests in their spiritual discipline and teach them the fundamentals of healing and protecting others with the Light.",al={"anetta goal","what is anetta trying to do","anetta objective"},it="wants",add="bbb44d1e"},{q="Why is Priestess Anetta here?",a="Priestess Anetta resides at Northshire Abbey as an ordained sacerdotal member of the Brotherhood of Northshire. She remains stationed in the abbey's library wing to pass down the fundamentals of the Light to initiates answering Stormwind's call.",al={"why is anetta at northshire","anetta purpose here","why is priestess anetta in the abbey"},it="why_here",add="00624d11"},{q="Who is Priestess Anetta tied to?",a="Anetta is a devoted member of the Brotherhood of Northshire and serves alongside the abbey's clergy and guards. Through her holy vows and training duties, she remains closely bound to the Church of the Holy Light and the defense of Stormwind.",al={"anetta connections","who is anetta affiliated with","anetta faction ties"},it="ties",add="1b4a2e6e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a young human priest beginning in Northshire, you meet Priestess Anetta as your first mentor. She affirms your holy calling and teaches you to commune directly with the Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="Priestess Anetta prepares young priests to support those defending Northshire Valley."},kw={"anetta","brotherhood of northshire","elwynn forest","holy light","library wing","northshire abbey","priest trainer","priestess anetta"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:light","subzone:library-wing-northshire","quest:3103","quest:5623","zone:elwynn","topic:alliance"},src={"Priestess Anetta"}}
E["npc:priestess-josetta"] = {t="npc",n="Priestess Josetta",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Priestess Josetta guides young priests beyond their first trials in Northshire. She teaches faith, devotion, and the work of serving others.",h="In Goldshire, Priestess Josetta guides young priests beyond their first trials in Northshire.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Goldshire",b="Priestess Josetta tends to the people of Elwynn Forest from an upstairs room in the Lion's Pride Inn. Travelers, guards, and local workers come within her reach there. She offers spiritual care among ordinary folk, showing that service to the Holy Light can be given wherever people need comfort.",sp=0},{t="Guiding Young Acolytes",b="Priestess Josetta guides young priests who have finished their first studies at Northshire Abbey. She sends them into the countryside to help wounded guards and comfort those who suffer. Their work teaches them that priesthood asks more than prayers learned by heart. They must put the Light to work and help mend a broken world.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Regret",b="Priestess Josetta regrets that she did not travel farther when she was young. She chose familiar ground over the wider roads of Azeroth. Though she is content with her sacred service in Goldshire, she urges the young disciples who visit her to be bolder and carry their faith to distant frontiers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Priestess Josetta?",a="Priestess Josetta lives in the second-floor room beside Michelle Belle at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"josetta location","where is priestess josetta","goldshire priest trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Priestess Josetta serve?",a="Priestess Josetta trains Alliance priests in holy spells, discipline, and the duties of their calling after Northshire.",al={"what does josetta do","priestess josetta role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Josetta operate out of an inn instead of a church?",a="Goldshire has no separate chapel, and the Lion's Pride Inn is the town center. From her room upstairs, Josetta can care for weary travelers, injured guards, and local residents.",al={"why in an inn","why lions pride inn"},it="why_here"},{q="What personal regret does Josetta share with disciples?",a="Priestess Josetta regrets that she lacked the courage to leave home and travel when she was young. She urges young adventurers to explore beyond Elwynn.",al={"josetta backstory","josetta travel regret"}},{q="What kind of duties does Josetta assign to new priests?",a="Priestess Josetta sends acolytes to help wounded defenders in the field. They learn healing prayers and see that the Light must reach those in need.",al={"josetta quests","garments of the light quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Josetta teach racial priest spells?",a="Yes. As a human priestess in Elwynn, Josetta teaches human priests prayers favored by their people, including Desperate Prayer.",al={"desperate prayer trainer","human priest spells"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Priestess Josetta on?",a="Priestess Josetta stands firmly with the Holy Light, the Church, and the Grand Alliance. Operating within Goldshire under the banner of Stormwind, she dedicates herself to mentoring aspiring priests of the Kingdom, ensuring they uphold their holy vows in service to their people and allies.",al={"priestess josetta faction","is priestess josetta alliance","who does josetta serve"},it="side",add="41d8cc17"},{q="What does Priestess Josetta want?",a="Priestess Josetta desires to foster devotion and discipline in the next generation of holy practitioners. Though she privately regrets lacking the courage to wander Azeroth when she was younger, she channels her purpose into guiding you and other novitiates to aid the wounded and carry the Light far beyond Goldshire.",al={"what are josetta's goals","what does priestess josetta want","josetta motive"},it="wants",add="165cad46"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest leaving Northshire, you can learn core spells from Josetta and how to put your healing vows into practice.",["race:Human"]="As a human priest, you will hear the Church of the Light's teachings in Josetta's counsel and learn prayers from your people's traditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member in Elwynn, you can turn to Josetta for spiritual and healing support for local defenders."},kw={"desperate prayer","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","josetta","lion's pride inn","priest trainer","priestess josetta"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:light","quest:5624","quest:5634","quest:5623","quest:5628"},src={"Priestess Josetta"}}
E["npc:remy-two-times"] = {t="npc",n="Remy \"Two Times\"",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" trades goods and pays for raw materials. He came from the Redridge Mountains and repeats the ends of his sentences.",h="In Goldshire, Remy \"Two Times\" trades goods and pays for raw materials.",sec={{t="A Merchant with an Odd Quirk",b="Remy \"Two Times\" trades from Goldshire, where he deals with travelers. He came west from the Redridge Mountains. When he speaks, he usually repeats the last words of each sentence twice. The odd habit gives him his nickname, but it does not keep him from seeking a profit in troubled Elwynn Forest.",sp=0},{t="Business in Troubled Waters",b="Kobolds overrun the local gold mines, and aggressive murlocs infest the riverbanks, disrupting trade in Elwynn. Remy turns to travelers for help. He pays for pouches of gold dust gathered from kobolds in the mines and keeps watch on suspicious murloc movements near Crystal Lake.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is he called 'Two Times'?",a="Remy earned his nickname by habitually repeating the final words of his sentences twice when he speaks.",al={"remy two times name","why does remy repeat words","two times meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where does Remy come from originally?",a="Remy came to Goldshire from the Redridge Mountains to trade in Elwynn Forest.",al={"remy origin","where is remy from"},it="origin"},{q="What does Remy do with all the gold dust he buys?",a="Remy collects gold dust gathered from kobolds in local mines to smelt, trade, or resell for profit.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","gold dust exchange lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Remy be found in Goldshire?",a="Remy can be found outdoors in Goldshire near the Lion's Pride Inn, ready to barter with passing travelers.",al={"where is remy two times","remy location goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a human merchant who has set up shop in Goldshire. Originally from the Redridge Mountains, he is known around Elwynn Forest for his eccentric verbal tic of repeating the final words of his sentences twice.",al={"who is remy","remy two times identity","who is remy two times"},it="identity",add="99a83a18"},{q="Whose side is Remy \"Two Times\" on?",a="Remy is loyal to the Grand Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. He conducts his trade openly in Goldshire, dealing peacefully with local authorities, townspeople, and passing adventurers.",al={"remy two times faction","is remy alliance","who does remy work for"},it="side",add="e326d54d"},{q="What does Remy \"Two Times\" want?",a="As an enterprising merchant, Remy wants profitable commodities and local security. He eagerly trades with travelers for gold dust gathered from nearby mines, and he is keen to resolve any nearby perils that threaten commerce in Goldshire.",al={"what does remy want","remy two times goals","why does remy need adventurers"},it="wants",add="85133ed8"},{q="Why is Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire?",a="Having traveled down from his home in the Redridge Mountains, Remy settled in Goldshire to pursue trade. The busy crossroads village offers a steady stream of miners, travelers, and adventurers willing to buy, sell, and run errands.",al={"why is remy in goldshire","why did remy leave redridge","remy two times why here"},it="why_here",add="7f55543c"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="If you work in the Fargodeep or Jasperlode mines, you may meet Remy, who trades for gold dust gathered from the kobolds there.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit arriving in Goldshire, you can take on Remy's straightforward work to help clear local threats and earn quick coin."},kw={"elwynn","gold dust","goldshire","merchant","murloc","redridge","remy","two times"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:47","quest:40","zone:redridge"},src={"Remy \"Two Times\""}}
E["npc:sara-timberlain"] = {t="npc",n="Sara Timberlain",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain stitches gear for the Stormwind Army. She makes useful armaments from salvaged cloth and leather.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain stitches gear for the Stormwind Army.",sec={{t="Needlework on the Frontier",b="Sara Timberlain works with needle and thread outside a small cottage on the western edge of Eastvale Logging Camp. Axes sound through the camp as workers fell trees. Though Eastvale lies far from settled lands, wolves and murlocs prowl nearby, and Sara still offers travelers hospitality. She turns scraps of linen and salvaged bandanas into sturdy gear. Her skill has earned official recognition and commissions to supply cloth and leather armaments to Stormwind's military forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain is a skilled seamstress at Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest. She makes practical gear from reclaimed fabrics and has contracts to supply the Stormwind Army.",al={"who is sara timberlain","sara timberlain","eastvale tailor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain sits outside a house on the western side of Eastvale Logging Camp, in eastern Elwynn Forest along the road to Redridge.",al={"sara timberlain location","where is sara timberlain","timberlain house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Sara gathering cloth for the army?",a="The Stormwind Army depends on local crafters to maintain its equipment stores. Sara uses salvaged cloth, including linen gathered by adventurers, to make sturdy garments and armor linings for the kingdom's soldiers.",al={"why does sara need linen","stormwind army armor","cloth and leather armor quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Sara Timberlain on?",a="Sara is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at the Eastvale Logging Camp, she works directly to support the realm's defense, fulfilling tailoring commissions for the Stormwind Army to keep its soldiers equipped with sturdy armor.",al={"sara timberlain faction","who does sara timberlain serve","sara timberlain alliance"},it="side",add="693a4fc8"},{q="What does Sara Timberlain want?",a="Sara needs raw crafting materials, particularly bolts of linen cloth salvaged from local bandits, to continue her tailoring work. By turning reclaimed cloth into tailored goods and armor, she helps supply the realm's fighting forces while rewarding travelers who bring her supplies.",al={"what does sara timberlain need","sara timberlain materials","why does sara want linen"},it="wants",add="94680b13"},{q="Why is Sara Timberlain at the logging camp?",a="Sara resides on the western side of the Eastvale Logging Camp, where she plies her trade away from the crowded streets of Stormwind City. The frontier outpost offers a quiet place to work her needle while keeping her close to travelers and local suppliers who gather the salvaged materials she relies upon.",al={"why is sara in eastvale","sara timberlain eastvale logging camp","why is sara timberlain here"},it="why_here",add="414da08e"},{q="Who is Sara Timberlain tied to?",a="Sara maintains close ties with the Stormwind Army, which has officially commissioned her to craft both cloth and leather armor for their troops. She also works alongside the local woodsmen and loggers stationed at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"sara timberlain connections","who does sara timberlain work for","sara timberlain stormwind army"},it="ties",add="59756f86"},{q="Why is Sara Timberlain famous?",a="Sara is renowned throughout the region for her exceptional tailoring skills, specifically her rare talent for transforming rough, salvaged scraps of cloth into finely crafted garments and reliable armor worthy of the realm's standing army.",al={"sara timberlain reputation","is sara timberlain well known","what is sara timberlain famous for"},it="fame",add="42dfe0df"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Sara shows how frontier tailors make useful garments from scraps of rough linen and bandit cloth for military commissions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Outlying settlements such as Eastvale help defend the kingdom, as local craftspeople supply basic armor to the under-resourced Stormwind Army."},kw={"eastvale","linen","logging camp","sara timberlain","seamstress","stormwind army","tailor"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","quest:59","quest:83","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Sara Timberlain"}}
E["npc:supervisor-raelen"] = {t="npc",n="Supervisor Raelen",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen keeps timber moving toward Stormwind. She manages the laborers, tracks daily quotas, and oversees the lumber supply.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Supervisor Raelen keeps timber moving toward Stormwind.",sec={{t="Keeping the Camp on Schedule",b="Supervisor Raelen directs the woodcutters at Eastvale Logging Camp, near Marshal Patterson and the camp’s wagons. The camp stands on the edge of eastern Elwynn, near the Redridge Mountains, where the work brings its share of trouble. Raelen coordinates the crews and keeps them focused on their quotas despite hazards in the surrounding woods. She sees that gathered timber is processed, bundled, and sent on toward Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen oversees the logging crews at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. She manages their work and keeps their timber quotas on schedule.",al={"who is raelen","raelen elwynn","eastvale supervisor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen is in the center of Eastvale Logging Camp, near the loaded wood wagons and Marshal Patterson.",al={"where is raelen","supervisor raelen location","find raelen"},gp=true},{q="Why does Supervisor Raelen need help from adventurers?",a="Timber gathering near the forest’s edge can be dangerous. When wildlife or other disruptions trouble the workers, cut lumber bundles may be abandoned or scattered among the trees.",al={"raelen quest","bundle of trouble quest","why help raelen"},it="wants"},{q="What role does the Eastvale Logging Camp play in Elwynn Forest?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is the main logging operation in eastern Elwynn Forest. Its lumber supports rebuilding and maintenance in Stormwind and nearby settlements.",al={"what is eastvale","eastvale logging role","why is eastvale important"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Supervisor Raelen on?",a="Supervisor Raelen is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. She manages lumber operations on behalf of the kingdom at the Eastvale Logging Camp, working directly alongside Stormwind guards and laborers to keep timber flowing to the capital.",al={"raelen faction","who does supervisor raelen serve","is raelen alliance"},it="side",add="5e9ae7c9"},{q="Why is Supervisor Raelen here at Eastvale?",a="Raelen oversees day-to-day logging at the Eastvale Logging Camp. She directs the local laborers, monitors lumber wagons, and ensures wood collection meets Stormwind's quotas, keeping the operation running despite the surrounding wilderness hazards.",al={"why is supervisor raelen here","raelen purpose eastvale","what does raelen do here"},it="why_here",add="93ff040d"},{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen tied to?",a="Raelen works closely with the local Stormwind authorities stationed at Eastvale, notably Marshal Patterson, who oversees the camp's defense. She also directs the camp's workforce of local peasants and woodcutters.",al={"raelen connections","who does raelen work with","supervisor raelen allies"},it="ties",add="e5fd1368"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind needs timber for its defenses and construction, so Raelen’s lumber quotas matter to the kingdom’s war effort."},kw={"a bundle of trouble","eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","lumber","raelen","supervisor raelen","wood quotas"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","quest:5545","zone:elwynn"},src={"Supervisor Raelen"}}
E["npc:theocritus"] = {t="npc",n="Theocritus",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn, Theocritus watches over the kingdom and opposes Morganth. The eccentric human archmage lives apart from others, surrounded by servants and magical scrying devices.",h="At the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn, Theocritus watches over the kingdom and opposes Morganth.",sec={{t="Master of the Tower",b="Archmage Theocritus keeps his own stronghold in the kingdom of Stormwind. He lives in the Tower of Azora, near the eastern road to Redridge. Eccentric in his habits, he enjoys a comfortable life with a large household staff, including gnomish attendants and his clothier, Morley Eberlein. He keeps apart from the everyday concerns of local villagers, yet his magic guards eastern Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="The War Against Morganth",b="The fallen mage Morganth is Theocritus's greatest concern. Morganth works from the Tower of Ilgalar in the nearby Redridge Mountains, and Theocritus sees him as both a personal enemy and a danger to Stormwind. For months, Theocritus has used arcane research to undermine him. With scrying devices such as the Eye of Azora, he watches Morganth's actions and probes his thoughts. He also studies the magical pendants worn by Morganth's Shadowhide gnolls, hoping to turn their master's creations against him with an arcane pulse that can immobilize the entire pack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Archmage Theocritus lives independently in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. Eccentric and somewhat isolated, he turns his magic toward protecting the region from dark magical threats.",al={"theocritus lore","who is the mage in the tower","tower of azora mage"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Theocritus live in Elwynn Forest?",a="Theocritus keeps his own sanctum in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn. His household attends him as he pursues his studies and watches the border with Redridge, where his rival Morganth lives in the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"why is theocritus in elwynn"}},{q="Who is Theocritus fighting against?",a="Theocritus's chief rival is Morganth, a fallen human mage who practices dark magic in the Tower of Ilgalar across the border in Redridge. Theocritus regards Morganth as a personal enemy and a grave threat to Stormwind.",al={"theocritus enemy","who is morganth","theocritus rival"}},{q="What is the Eye of Azora?",a="The Eye of Azora is a scrying device housed atop Theocritus's tower. He uses it to peer into distant lands, track threats, and try to read Morganth's thoughts.",al={"eye of azora lore","how does theocritus spy","theocritus crystal ball"},it="item"},{q="Why does Theocritus want Shadowhide gnoll pendants?",a="The Shadowhide gnolls serve Morganth and wear enchanted pendants linked to him. Theocritus studies the pendants to learn how that link works, hoping to send an arcane attack through it and paralyze the gnolls in battle.",al={"gnoll pendants theocritus","theocritus retrieval","why collect gnoll pendants"}},{q="Who serves Theocritus in his tower?",a="Theocritus's household includes gnomish servants who tend to his daily affairs and his personal clothier, Morley Eberlein, who cares for his wardrobe.",al={"tower of azora staff","who lives in tower of azora","theocritus servants"}},{q="Whose side is Theocritus on?",a="Archmage Theocritus acts independently, pursuing his own esoteric studies. While he remains detached from the day-to-day politics of Stormwind and the Alliance, he still considers it his duty to defend the realm against dark sorcery. He stands firmly against the rogue wizard Morganth and the dark forces encroaching on Elwynn and Redridge.",al={"theocritus alliance or horde","who does theocritus serve","theocritus faction"},it="side",add="ffea707c"},{q="What does Theocritus want?",a="Theocritus focuses his formidable arcane skills on countering his bitter rival, the fallen mage Morganth. Through the magical scrying device known as the Eye of Azora and recovered Shadowhide gnoll pendants, he seeks to penetrate Morganth's mind and disrupt the dark wizard's control over the gnolls terrorizing the region.",al={"theocritus goal","what is theocritus trying to do","theocritus purpose"},it="wants",add="09c566f6"},{q="Why is Theocritus in Elwynn Forest?",a="Theocritus established himself in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. The secluded tower provides him a tranquil sanctum to conduct research in isolation, surrounded by his gnomish attendants, while keeping watch over the nearby border with Redridge.",al={"why is theocritus in elwynn","why is theocritus here","theocritus tower of azora why"},it="why_here",add="a72df9dd"},{q="Who is Theocritus tied to?",a="Though eccentric and solitary, Theocritus is attended in his tower by a devoted staff of gnomish servants and his personal tailor, Morley Eberlein, while remaining locked in a deep personal enmity with the rogue mage Morganth.",al={"theocritus connections","theocritus friends","theocritus dalaran allies"},it="ties",add="f1864285"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Theocritus shows how a wizard can work alone, without belonging to an order. He keeps a private sanctum and uses magic to scry across long distances.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though eccentric and aloof, Theocritus uses his arcane vision and resources to defend eastern Elwynn and Redridge from rogue spellcasters.",["race:Human"]="The conflict between Theocritus and Morganth reflects two paths for human sorcery: disciplined study devoted to defense, and corruption driven by dark ambition."},kw={"archmage","elwynn forest","eye of azora","morganth","morley eberlein","shadowhide","theocritus","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","quest:178","quest:94","quest:249","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Theocritus"}}
E["npc:tommy-joe-stonefield"] = {t="npc",n="Tommy Joe Stonefield",z="elwynn",s="At the river west of Stonefield Farm, Tommy Joe Stonefield longs for Maybell Maclure. Their families have feuded for years, so he relies on secret notes and quiet banks to keep their love hidden.",h="At the river west of Stonefield Farm, Tommy Joe Stonefield longs for Maybell Maclure.",sec={{t="A Star-Crossed Feud",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield waits by the river west of Stonefield Farm, looking toward the Maclure homestead across the water. The Stonefields and Maclures have clashed for years over land, pride, and farmyard squabbles. Their elders keep the feud alive, but Tommy Joe has fallen in love with Maybell Maclure. The two cannot meet openly without angering both households. Gramma Stonefield, Tommy Joe’s sympathetic grandmother, helps them exchange secret notes and tokens of affection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield is a young human who lives on Stonefield Farm in Elwynn Forest. He is secretly in love with Maybell Maclure, daughter of his family’s bitter rivals.",al={"tommy joe","who is tommy joe","stonefield son"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield stands on the riverbank west of Stonefield Farm, looking across the water toward the Maclure farmstead where Maybell lives.",al={"tommy joe location","where is tommy joe","find tommy joe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Stonefields and Maclures fighting?",a="No one says what began the feud. The Stonefields and Maclures have kept up their bitter rivalry for years, and neither family wants its young ones associating with the other.",al={"family feud","why do they hate each other","stonefield maclure feud"},it="conflict"},{q="Who helps Tommy Joe and Maybell meet?",a="Gramma Stonefield knows of their affection and helps their secret courtship. She uses travelers to carry discreet messages between Tommy Joe and Maybell.",al={"gramma stonefield help","secret lovers help","who helps the lovers"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Tommy Joe Stonefield on?",a="He belongs to the Stonefield family, but his heart is not in their bitter feud. While he lives upon the Stonefield farm, his loyalty is torn between his kin and his love for Maybell Maclure, who belongs to their sworn rivals.",al={"tommy joe allegiance","which family tommy joe","stonefield or maclure"},it="side",add="3c95bb6e"},{q="What does Tommy Joe Stonefield want?",a="Tommy Joe desires nothing more than to be with Maybell Maclure. The long-standing hatred between the Stonefields and the Maclures keeps them apart, so he longs to find a way to meet her in secret and keep their love alive despite the feud.",al={"what does tommy joe want","tommy joe goal","tommy joe wish"},it="wants",add="8a9aad66"},{q="Why is Tommy Joe Stonefield here?",a="Tommy Joe waits quietly along the riverbank near his family's farmstead. Tucked away from prying eyes, it is a secluded spot where he can slip away from his chores and hope for a chance to rendezvous with Maybell away from their warring kin.",al={"why is tommy joe at the river","what is tommy joe doing here","tommy joe stonefield location why"},it="why_here",add="96565570"},{q="Who is Tommy Joe Stonefield tied to?",a="He is a member of the Stonefield clan, closely guided by his grandmother, Gramma Stonefield, who actively aids him. His most significant tie, however, is to Maybell Maclure, the daughter of his family's bitter rivals, with whom he is deeply in love.",al={"tommy joe connections","tommy joe family","who is tommy joe related to"},it="ties",add="b663afb0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in southern Elwynn, you may find Tommy Joe’s secret romance a reminder of the quiet personal lives that continue amid banditry and political unrest."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:maybell-maclure","npc:gramma-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm","quest:111","zone:elwynn"},src={"Tommy Joe Stonefield"}}
E["npc:willem"] = {t="npc",n="Willem",z="elwynn",s="Outside Northshire Abbey, Willem sends recruits to meet the valley's threats. He serves under Marshal McBride in the Stormwind Army, with the Defias Brotherhood pressing into Northshire.",h="Outside Northshire Abbey, Willem sends recruits to meet the valley's threats.",sec={{t="A Watchman at the Abbey",b="Deputy Willem watches the gates of Northshire Abbey, where the Stormwind Army keeps a foothold in the valley. The kingdom's soldiers are spread across many territories, leaving local defense to small groups like Marshal McBride's garrison. Willem meets incoming volunteers and sends them to aid residents and guard the valley's edges.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Defias",b="The Defias Brotherhood is Willem's most pressing concern. Red-bandana bandits have entered Northshire, stolen supplies, threatened farmer Milly Osworth, and taken footholds among nearby vineyards and hills. Willem offers bounties on known cutthroats such as Garrick Padfoot, hoping to break their leadership before they can take the abbey grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deputy Willem?",a="Deputy Willem serves in the Stormwind Army outside Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. Under Marshal McBride, he directs recruits against threats in the valley.",al={"who is willem","deputy willem role","willem northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Who does Deputy Willem report to?",a="Deputy Willem reports to Marshal McBride, who commands Northshire Valley's defense and military operations.",al={"willem commander","who is willems boss","willem leader"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Willem issuing bounties on the Defias?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has entered Northshire Valley, threatening the abbey and terrorizing local laborers. Willem sends fighters after the bandits and leaders such as Garrick Padfoot to restore order.",al={"why defias bounty","willem red bandanas","willem defias"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Deputy Willem be found?",a="Willem waits outside the main entrance of Northshire Abbey in northern Elwynn Forest, where he greets travelers and recruits entering the courtyard.",al={"willem location","where is deputy willem","find willem"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does Willem assist the local workers?",a="Willem sends fighters to help residents whose livelihoods are threatened, including orchardist Milly Osworth and peltskinner Eagan.",al={"willem milly osworth","willem eagan","willem quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are troops like Willem struggling to maintain order alone?",a="Stormwind faces internal strain, political tension, and distant military commitments. With King Varian missing, garrisons like Northshire must depend on untested recruits and volunteers to handle unrest at home.",al={"why is stormwind army weak","why northshire undefended","stormwind manpower northshire"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Deputy Willem on?",a="Deputy Willem is a loyal soldier of the Stormwind Army, serving the Alliance. Standing guard outside Northshire Abbey, he upholds the kingdom's laws and directs able-bodied recruits to defend the valley from brigands and thieves.",al={"willem faction","who does deputy willem serve","willem alliance or horde"},it="side",add="cea9f32f"},{q="Why is Deputy Willem here in Northshire?",a="Deputy Willem is stationed outside Northshire Abbey to maintain order and direct new recruits to where they are needed most. With the kingdom's defenses stretched thin, he serves as the primary liaison organizing the valley's response to local threats.",al={"why is willem in northshire","what brought willem here","deputy willem duty"},it="why_here",add="29d9c6b5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human stepping out of Northshire Abbey, you may meet Deputy Willem, one of the first Stormwind officers to welcome you into the kingdom's service.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see through Willem how the Defias unrest reaches even Elwynn's peaceful heartland.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can put your strength to use under Willem's direction, driving out bandits and restoring order to the realm."},kw={"defias","deputy willem","elwynn forest","garrick padfoot","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey","willem"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-valley","quest:783","quest:18","quest:6","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn"},src={"Willem"}}
E["npc:william-pestle"] = {t="npc",n="William Pestle",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle gathers supplies for Stormwind's apothecary. He and his brother Morgan run the shop in the Trade District, and William hires travelers to find candles, kelp, and herbs.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle gathers supplies for Stormwind's apothecary.",sec={{t="Apothecary Abroad",b="William works from Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn while his brother Morgan Pestle tends the counter at Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District. From Elwynn Forest, William works with local gatherers to secure raw materials the city shops need. He sends regular shipments to the capital, where Stormwind's citizens rely on a steady supply of restorative salves, draughts, and powders.",sp=0},{t="Curious Reagents",b="William often needs more than common garden herbs for his craft. He hires newcomers to gather wax candles carried by Elwynn's kobolds and crystal kelp from the murlocs of Crystal Lake, just east of Goldshire. The ingredients may seem strange to those unfamiliar with alchemy, but William believes they have potent virtues in a mixture.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction for Young Love",b="William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. When Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught between their families' bitter feud, William agrees to brew an Invisibility Liquor. Made with kelp gathered from local waters, the brew lets Maybell slip away unseen to meet Tommy Joe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist who works from the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He and his brother Morgan gather and prepare supplies for the apothecary in Stormwind City.",al={"william pestle","goldshire alchemist","who is pestle"},it="identity"},{q="Where can William Pestle be found?",a="William Pestle can be found inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"pestle location","where is william pestle","william pestle goldshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does William do with kobold candles?",a="William gathers wax candles carried by kobolds in Elwynn's mines, then melts them and refines the tallow for alchemical mixtures and the apothecary's stock.",al={"why does pestle want candles","kobold candles use"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does William need Crystal Kelp?",a="William uses Crystal Kelp from local Elwynn lakes to make an Invisibility Liquor. It helps Maybell Maclure slip past her family to meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"collecting kelp why","murloc kelp use"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What is William Pestle's connection to Stormwind City?",a="William and his brother Morgan run the apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District. William gathers ingredients in Goldshire and sends shipments to the city shop.",al={"pestle stormwind","william pestle apothecary shop"},it="ties"},{q="How is William involved with the Stonefields and Maclures?",a="William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. He brews a covert drink to help Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure get around their families' bitter feud.",al={"stonefield maclure pestle","william pestle love quest"},sp=1},{q="Whose side is William Pestle on?",a="William is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a proud member of the Alliance. Operating out of the Lion's Pride Inn, he serves his local community by providing alchemical expertise, brewing remedies, and assisting local townsfolk with their everyday troubles.",al={"william pestle faction","is william pestle alliance","william pestle loyalty"},it="side",add="520b1b0a"},{q="What does William Pestle want?",a="William seeks rare and unconventional reagents for his alchemical concoctions. He often enlists passing adventurers to gather large supplies of kobold candles for their wax and crystal kelp from the local lakes, putting these ingredients to use in brews such as his potent Invisibility Liquor.",al={"what does william pestle need","william pestle goals","william pestle ingredients"},it="wants",add="2d067923"},{q="Why is William Pestle in Goldshire?",a="While William and his brother Morgan manage an apothecary shop in Stormwind City's Trade District, William stays at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn to gather rural reagents firsthand and assist long-time friends like Mildred Stonefield in the Elwynn countryside.",al={"why is william pestle here","why is william in goldshire","why is william pestle at lions pride inn"},it="why_here",add="8d6a9bd2"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist in Goldshire, you can see how plant gathering serves William's trade. He turns wild growth and strange aquatic kelp into useful mixtures.",["faction:Alliance"]="William helps supply Stormwind's Trade District with medicines and other goods. He depends on Alliance recruits passing through Goldshire to gather materials from the surrounding forest."},kw={"apothecary","collecting kelp","goldshire","kobold candles","lion's pride inn","maclure","morgan pestle","pestle","stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:morgan-pestle","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","quest:60","quest:112","quest:114","quest:61","npc:maybell-maclure"},src={"William Pestle"}}
E["npc:zaldimar-wefhellt"] = {t="npc",n="Zaldimar Wefhellt",z="elwynn",s="On Goldshire's upper floor, Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches young mages their first spells. When they outgrow his lessons, he sends them to Stormwind City for further training.",h="On Goldshire's upper floor, Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches young mages their first spells.",sec={{t="The Mage in Goldshire",b="Upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches novice mages the first arts of arcane, fire, and frost. When an apprentice outgrows those lessons, he sends them north to the Mage Quarter in Stormwind, where Jennea Cannon can teach them more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zaldimar Wefhellt?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt teaches novice mages their first spells at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He guides them toward further training in Stormwind City.",al={"who is zaldimar","zaldimar wefhellt role","goldshire mage trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Zaldimar Wefhellt?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt is on the second floor of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, inside the leftmost room at the top of the stairs.",al={"zaldimar location","where is zaldimar","how to find zaldimar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Zaldimar send novice mages?",a="After a mage learns the basics, Zaldimar sends them to Stormwind's Mage Quarter to speak with Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"zaldimar quest","who does zaldimar send you to","speak with jennea quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Zaldimar related to any other mages?",a="No relatives of Zaldimar are known. He teaches at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"wefhellt family","zalna wefhellt","zaldimar relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Zaldimar Wefhellt on?",a="Zaldimar is a loyal member of the Grand Alliance and serves the Kingdom of Stormwind. Stationed right in the heart of Elwynn Forest, he dedicates his arcane craft to mentoring young spellcasters stepping forward to defend the realm and uphold the crown's authority.",al={"zaldimar wefhellt faction","is zaldimar alliance"},it="side",add="10a0eae6"},{q="What does Zaldimar Wefhellt want?",a="Zaldimar wants to guide fledgling mages through the perils of arcane study. Once apprentices grasp the foundational principles of spellcasting in Goldshire, he directs them onward to more advanced instructors, such as Jennea Cannon in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind, to further refine their craft.",al={"zaldimar wefhellt motive","what does zaldimar want"},it="wants",add="063cda12"},{q="Why is Zaldimar Wefhellt in Goldshire?",a="Zaldimar stays on the upper floor of the Lion's Pride Inn to serve as Goldshire's resident mage trainer. Goldshire is an essential stopping ground for adventurers fresh out of Northshire Valley, making it the ideal post for him to intercept budding wizards and tutor them in essential arcane spells.",al={"why is zaldimar here","zaldimar lions pride inn"},it="why_here",add="d06c7379"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a young human mage leaving Northshire Abbey, you meet Zaldimar first in the wider world. He teaches you early spells, then directs you to the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Zaldimar teaches Alliance spellcasters in Elwynn Forest, so you can learn magic before traveling to Stormwind."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","lion's pride inn","mage trainer","wefhellt","zaldimar"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","quest:1860","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan"},src={"Zaldimar Wefhellt"}}
E["quest:11"] = {t="quest",n="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty",z="elwynn",s="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty is an official contract issued by Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison to cull the encroaching gnolls threatening Elwynn Forest's western borders. The Stormwind Army offers a reward for painted armbands taken from the Riverpaw packs infesting the woods and waterways.",h="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty is an official contract issued by Deputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison to cull the...",sec={{t="A Threat on the Border",b="Westbrook Garrison guards the critical borderlands between Elwynn Forest and Westfall. However, depleted garrison forces have left the outpost struggling to contain an aggressive influx of Riverpaw gnolls. These savage creatures have established encampments directly south of the guard tower and further east around the shores of Stone Cairn Lake, encroaching close enough to threaten peaceful travelers and local homesteads.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Order",b="Unable to spare regular infantry to sweep the woods, Deputy Rainer places a bounty on the raiders. To confirm the kills, Rainer requires proof of martial victory: painted gnoll armbands stripped from the slain beasts. By hiring wandering adventurers and recruits to thin the pack's numbers, the garrison hopes to blunt the Riverpaws' advance before they overrun the western marches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Riverpaw gnolls be found in Elwynn Forest?",a="Riverpaw gnolls gather primarily in two areas in Elwynn: in the dense woods directly south of Westbrook Garrison near the riverbanks, and farther east around the perimeter of Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"gnoll locations","where are the gnolls","riverpaw locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the garrison asking adventurers for help with gnolls?",a="Westbrook Garrison is understaffed and facing pressure along the borders of Elwynn. With too few guards to patrol the perimeter and simultaneously launch offensive sweeps, Deputy Rainer turns to independent champions to hunt the gnolls.",al={"why deputy rainer needs help","why garrison hiring mercenaries"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof does Deputy Rainer require?",a="Deputy Rainer requires eight Painted Gnoll Armbands as physical proof that the encroaching beasts have been put down.",al={"bounty proof","what to collect for rainer"},it="item"},{q="Who are the Riverpaw gnolls?",a="The Riverpaws are a notoriously vicious tribe of hyena-like humanoids known for infesting river valleys and borders across human lands. They frequently raid settlements, travelers, and farmlands for food and plunder.",al={"what are riverpaw gnolls","riverpaw tribe lore"},it="target"},{q="Does this quest connect to any other threats in Elwynn?",a="Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty is the conclusion of the short Westbrook Garrison alert chain, though Deputy Rainer and Westbrook Garrison also monitor other lawless elements in the area, such as the notorious outlaw Hogger.",al={"quest continuation","what comes after riverpaw bounty"},it="threat"},{q="Who pays the bounty for these gnolls?",a="The bounty is officially sanctioned and backed by the Stormwind Army, which authorizes local garrisons to commend and compensate those who assist in pacifying royal territories.",al={"who funds the bounty","bounty reward source"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Deputy Rainer want the gnolls culled?",a="Deputy Rainer views the Riverpaw gnolls as brutish interlopers who have no business on Elwynn's borders. With large packs entrenching themselves south of the guard tower and east near Stone Cairn Lake, they directly threaten Westbrook Garrison's perimeter and surrounding settlers. Rainer wants them culled to halt their encroaching infestation before the outpost is completely overrun.",al={"why cull gnolls","deputy rainer motive","why does rainer want riverpaws dead"},it="motive",add="139c22ee"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the realm, hunting down the Riverpaws is a direct effort to protect Elwynn's frontiers and support the overextended crown guards.",["faction:Alliance"]="Taking on border bounties builds standing with the Stormwind Army while securing vital trade routes through the heart of the kingdom."},kw={"bounty","deputy rainer","elwynn","gnoll","painted gnoll armband","riverpaw","stone cairn lake","westbrook garrison"},rel={"npc:deputy-rainer","subzone:westbrook-garrison","quest:239","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Deputy Rainer",faction="Alliance",id=11,ri={"Painted Gnoll Armband"}},src={"Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty"}}
E["quest:111"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Gramma",z="elwynn",s="Tommy Joe Stonefield seeks Gramma Stonefield's help to meet Maybell Maclure. Their families' bitter feud keeps the young lovers apart, and Tommy Joe hopes his grandmother can find a way for them to see each other.",h="Tommy Joe Stonefield seeks Gramma Stonefield's help to meet Maybell Maclure.",sec={{t="A Feud and Forbidden Love",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure keep their romance secret from their feuding families. The Stonefields and Maclures have fought over their farms for years, making their neighboring homesteads hostile ground. Tommy Joe wants to meet Maybell without provoking violence between their kin, so he turns to his grandmother for help.",sp=0},{t="Gramma's Cunning",b="Gramma Stonefield stays indoors, but she knows the feud well. She understands that the families cannot truly unite while their bad blood remains. Still, she will not let their grudge crush young love. Rather than urge caution, Gramma begins looking for small chances to bring Tommy Joe and Maybell together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Tommy Joe want me to speak with his Gramma?",a="Tommy Joe loves Maybell Maclure, but their families' feud keeps them from meeting. He hopes his grandmother can help arrange secret meetings without stirring an uproar.",al={"why gramma","tommy joe gramma","speak with gramma purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Gramma Stonefield be found?",a="Gramma Stonefield stays inside the main Stonefield farmhouse, south of Goldshire and east of the riverbank where Tommy Joe hides.",al={"gramma stonefield location","where is gramma","find gramma stonefield"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures?",a="The neighboring farming families have a long personal and territorial grudge. They accuse each other of theft and compete over crops, while distrust keeps both households near violence. Their children must keep any contact secret.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","why are they fighting","family feud elwynn"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Gramma Stonefield oppose Tommy Joe's relationship?",a="No. Gramma knows the feud makes a lasting future difficult, but she cares for the young lovers and is willing to devise ways for them to meet.",al={"is gramma against maybell","does gramma support lovers"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after speaking to Gramma?",a="Gramma begins making a plan to bring Tommy Joe and Maybell together in secret. She sends you to gather what she needs for an invisibility liquor to get past their watchful families.",al={"what next speak with gramma","gramma quest follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell Maclure is the daughter of the rival family, living across the road from the Stonefields. She is secretly courting Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who is maybell","maybell maclure"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tommy Joe need an outsider to speak with his grandmother?",a="Tommy Joe is hiding on the riverbank near the Stonefield Farm to secretly rendezvous with Maybell Maclure. Returning to the family farmhouse himself risks drawing attention to his forbidden romance, especially with tensions running high between the two feuding families. As a passing traveler, you can approach Gramma Stonefield quietly without alerting the rest of the household.",al={"why me tommy joe","why send player to gramma","why can't tommy talk to gramma"},it="why_me",add="ba5df8a9"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you see how deeply local grudges run in Stormwind's heartlands, even amid wider troubles across the realm.",["faction:Alliance"]="While Stormwind faces Defias unrest and beast attacks, you may find yourself mediating quarrels between neighboring farmers."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","speak with gramma","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:gramma-stonefield","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Tommy Joe Stonefield",["end"]="Gramma Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=111},src={"Speak with Gramma"}}
E["quest:112"] = {t="quest",n="Collecting Kelp",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Maybell Maclure seeks a way to visit Tommy Joe Stonefield unseen. William Pestle needs rare crystal kelp to brew an invisibility liquor for her.",h="In Goldshire, Maybell Maclure seeks a way to visit Tommy Joe Stonefield unseen.",sec={{t="A Remedy for Forbidden Love",b="The feud between the Stonefield and Maclure families keeps Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield from meeting openly. Maybell wants to see her beloved without provoking an armed clash between their kin, so she seeks a way to cross the valley unseen. William Pestle, an herbalist and apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, plans to brew an invisibility liquor. The rare ingredients he needs are not in the inn's cupboards.",sp=0},{t="The Scavengers of Crystal Lake",b="Crystal kelp is the catalyst William Pestle needs for his brew. The fronds usually grow far out in saltwater oceans, but tribal murlocs have carried stashes inland to their crude camps along Crystal Lake, just east of Goldshire. Their peculiar instincts have led them to haul the marine plants to the freshwater shore. You need to recover enough fronds from the murlocs before returning to Goldshire with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does William Pestle need crystal kelp?",a="William Pestle needs crystal kelp to brew an invisibility liquor for Maybell Maclure. The drink is meant to help her leave her family's vineyard unseen and visit Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"why crystal kelp","what is kelp for","william pestle ingredients"},it="item"},{q="Why is ocean kelp found near freshwater Crystal Lake?",a="Crystal kelp grows in the ocean, but tribal murlocs around Crystal Lake scavenge the fronds and carry them inland. They hoard the kelp in lakeside camps, making those camps the only local source near Goldshire.",al={"why is kelp at crystal lake","kelp in fresh water","murloc kelp lore"},it="place"},{q="Who are Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are young lovers from rival farming families in southern Elwynn Forest. Their families despise each other, so the pair must rely on secrecy and alchemical tricks to meet.",al={"who is maybell","who is tommy joe","maclure stonefield feud"},it="people"},{q="Where is Crystal Lake located?",a="Crystal Lake lies just east of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest. Hostile murlocs infest its waters and shores.",al={"where is crystal lake","crystal lake location","find crystal lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after collecting the kelp?",a="After you deliver four crystal kelp fronds, William Pestle distills them into an Invisibility Liquor. He then asks you to bring it to Maybell Maclure so she can slip away unseen.",al={"next quest after kelp","what does pestle make"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary and alchemical dabbler at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He helps locals with folk remedies, strange potions, and confidential favors.",al={"who is william pestle","pestle goldshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why does William Pestle want to help Maybell and Tommy Joe?",a="William Pestle is Goldshire's local apothecary and alchemist, and he is willing to lend his craft to help the young lovers. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield are caught on opposite sides of their families' bitter, long-standing feud. A secret potion of invisibility offers Maybell a clever way to slip away from her family's watchful eyes at the Maclure Vineyards without provoking further strife between the clans.",al={"why help maybell","william pestle motive","why does william care"},it="motive",add="ff0f7883"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?",a="Murlocs have crept inland from the coastlines, establishing camps along Elwynn Forest's freshwater bodies like Crystal Lake and Stonecairn Lake. With Stormwind's military stretched thin defending borders elsewhere, these aggressive amphibians have grown bold, encroaching on local settlements and scavenging materials—including ocean kelp they carry with them inland.",al={"why are murlocs at crystal lake","crystal lake murlocs","murlocs in elwynn"},it="target",add="cc419076"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="For you as a gatherer, crystal kelp is an odd find: an ocean herb taken from the pouches of freshwater murlocs, not from soil or seabed.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, clearing the murloc camps around Crystal Lake for Pestle helps quiet the aggressive menace near Goldshire's eastern road."},kw={"collecting kelp","crystal kelp","crystal lake","goldshire","invisibility liquor","maybell maclure","murloc","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","subzone:crystal-lake","quest:114","subzone:goldshire","subzone:maclure-vineyards","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="William Pestle",faction="Alliance",id=112,ri={"Crystal Kelp Frond"}},src={"Collecting Kelp"}}
E["quest:114"] = {t="quest",n="The Escape",z="elwynn",s="Maybell Maclure waits for a way to slip away from her family and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield. You bring her William Pestle's Invisibility Liquor, brewed from crystal kelp gathered across the region.",h="Maybell Maclure waits for a way to slip away from her family and meet Tommy Joe Stonefield.",sec={{t="A Concoction for True Love",b="The Maclures and Stonefields have feuded for generations, leaving no room for courtship. Gramma Stonefield turns to William Pestle, an alchemist in the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. With crystal kelp from nearby lakes, Pestle brews Invisibility Liquor strong enough to hide Maybell's escape from the Maclure homestead.",sp=0},{t="Vanishing into the Woods",b="Maybell Maclure takes the flask and slips into the trees toward Tommy Joe. Guilt over deceiving her kin troubles her, but her devotion outweighs her fear of discovery. She drinks the liquor and vanishes before your eyes, gaining a few moments with Tommy Joe beyond the watchful eyes of their feuding elders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Escape?",a="William Pestle, the apothecary and alchemical assistant in Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn, gives you the Invisibility Liquor after you bring him crystal kelp.",al={"quest giver the escape","who starts the escape","where to pick up the escape"},gp=true},{q="What is the Invisibility Liquor used for?",a="The Invisibility Liquor lets Maybell Maclure turn invisible long enough to leave her family's farm and visit Tommy Joe Stonefield without provoking her relatives.",al={"why invisibility liquor","what does the potion do","invisibility liquor purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do Maybell and Tommy Joe have to hide their relationship?",a="The Maclure and Stonefield families are bitter rivals, and their deep hostility forbids an open courtship between their children.",al={"why are they hiding","stonefield maclure feud","why can't maybell and tommy joe be together"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens when you deliver the potion to Maybell?",a="Maybell thanks you, torn between guilt and excitement, then drinks the brew. She vanishes before your eyes to slip away toward Tommy Joe.",al={"what happens at the end","does maybell vanish","the escape quest completion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What quest leads directly into The Escape?",a="The Escape follows Collecting Kelp, where you gather crystal kelp from murlocs at Crystal Lake for William Pestle to brew the invisibility potion.",al={"prerequisite for the escape","quest before the escape","what leads to the escape"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest resolve the feud between the families?",a="No. The potion gives the lovers only a brief, secret meeting. The feud between Gramma Stonefield and the Maclures remains bitter and unresolved.",al={"do the families make peace","is the feud over","does the feud end"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why does William Pestle help Tommy Joe and Maybell?",a="William Pestle is an apothecary who is willing to lend a sympathetic hand to young love. After Gramma Stonefield sent him a note asking for a way around the bitter Stonefield and Maclure family feud, William agreed to brew a batch of Invisibility Liquor once provided with crystal kelp. He has nothing personal to gain other than helping the two star-crossed lovers meet in secret without triggering another brawl between their warring kin.",al={"why does william help","william pestle motive","why help maybell escape"},it="motive",add="245b9158"},{q="Why does William Pestle send you to deliver the liquor instead of doing it himself?",a="William runs his busy shop out of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire and cannot easily abandon his trade to run errands across the forest. More importantly, wandering onto the Maclure vineyards carrying suspicious alchemical draughts would immediately draw the suspicion of Maybell's protective relatives. You, as a wandering adventurer who already served as the courier between the lovers and gathered the ingredients, can slip unnoticed onto the farm to hand her the draught.",al={"why does william send you","why do i deliver the invisibility liquor","why cant william deliver the potion"},it="why_me",add="53ceb805"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer starting in Elwynn Forest, helping Tommy Joe and Maybell offers a lighthearted break from fighting Defias bandits and gnolls. Rural grudges persist even near Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you know stubborn family grudges run deep, and small acts of secret aid between neighbors can help keep the peace."},kw={"elwynn forest","invisibility liquor","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","the escape","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:maybell-maclure","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","npc:william-pestle","quest:112","zone:elwynn"},m={start="William Pestle",["end"]="Maybell Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=114},src={"The Escape (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:119"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Verner",z="elwynn",s="You carry fifty freshly forged horseshoes from Goldshire back to Lakeshire. Smith Argus has finished the order, and Verner Osgood is waiting across the border in Redridge.",h="You carry fifty freshly forged horseshoes from Goldshire back to Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Courier Across the Border",b="Smith Argus has forged fifty horseshoes for Lakeshire, and you carry them east from Goldshire. Redridge faces supply shortages and gnoll attacks. The iron shoes help keep horses and draft animals working on its rugged mountain roads.",sp=0},{t="The Note on the Crate",b="Verner Osgood is relieved when the horseshoes arrive, but Smith Argus has attached a bill to the crate. Verner is annoyed that the Goldshire smith expects payment. Redridge faces pressing dangers, leaving little time to argue over the charge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I take the Crate of Horseshoes?",a="Take the crate to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains just east of the bridge and lakeside docks.",al={"where is verner","turn in location","who gets horseshoes"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sent this delivery back to Redridge?",a="Smith Argus, the blacksmith outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends the crate after finishing the horseshoes.",al={"who gave the quest","smith argus","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Verner upset when he receives the crate?",a="Smith Argus attached a bill demanding payment for all fifty horseshoes, and Verner is irritated. He had apparently hoped for a free favor or easier terms.",al={"why is verner mad","argus note","verner reaction"},it="motive"},{q="What quests open up after completing this delivery?",a="After this delivery, Verner offers work against local threats: hunt the Redridge gnolls in 'A Baying of Gnolls' and fetch 'Underbelly Scales'.",al={"next quest","followup quests","what unlocks"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Lakeshire need supplies imported from Goldshire?",a="Gnolls and Blackrock orcs besiege Lakeshire, stretching local craftsmen thin. The town often needs everyday goods like bulk iron horseshoes from quieter places such as Goldshire.",al={"why elwynn shoes","why import horseshoes","redridge supplies"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Smith Argus accompany you back to Redridge?",a="No. Smith Argus stays at his forge in Goldshire while you carry the crate to Redridge.",al={"does argus come with","escort smith argus"},gp=true},{q="Why does Smith Argus want this crate delivered to Verner?",a="Smith Argus is fulfilling Verner Osgood's urgent request for fifty horseshoes, but not out of sheer goodwill. He has boxed them up and attached a pointed bill demanding payment for his labor and materials. Handing the delivery over to you ensures Redridge gets its supplies while making sure Verner knows the ironwork in Goldshire does not come for free.",al={"why does argus send horseshoes","smith argus motive","argus horseshoes verner why"},it="motive",add="a0846e84"},{q="Why does Smith Argus ask you to carry the horseshoes instead of delivering them himself?",a="Argus is Goldshire's resident blacksmith, tied to his anvil and forge keeping travelers and local guards outfitted. Hauling a heavy crate of fifty iron horseshoes across the border through the Redridge passes takes time away from his work and exposes a lone artisan to gnolls and brigands along the road. You are an able adventurer already headed east.",al={"why doesn't argus deliver the shoes","why me return to verner","why send player to lakeshire"},it="why_me",add="f67540ab"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know frontier mounts need steady supplies of horseshoes when local forges are overwhelmed by war.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep outlying settlements like Lakeshire connected to the kingdom's heart through supply lines between Elwynn Forest and Redridge."},kw={"crate of horseshoes","elwynn forest","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","the price of shoes","verner osgood"},rel={"quest:118","npc:verner-osgood","npc:smith-argus","quest:124","quest:122","quest:126","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Smith Argus",["end"]="Verner Osgood",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=119},src={"Return to Verner"}}
E["quest:123"] = {t="quest",n="The Collector",z="elwynn",s="An intercepted dispatch from gnoll raiders in Elwynn Forest lays out when gold shipments leave the abandoned mines. It is addressed to a figure called 'The Collector' and points to an organized operation near Stormwind's garrison.",h="An intercepted dispatch from gnoll raiders in Elwynn Forest lays out when gold shipments leave the abandoned...",sec={{t="A Paper Trail in the Paws of Gnolls",b="Riverpaw gnoll packs in western Elwynn Forest carry more than furs and crude weapons. Among them, a parchment called the Gold Pickup Schedule lays out dates and times for gold taken from local mines. The intercepted note directs each shipment to an overseer identified only as 'The Collector.'",sp=0},{t="Unsettling News for Goldshire",b="Marshal Dughan hears the news at the Lion's Pride Inn and learns that gold is still being mined and moved. Official mines across Elwynn have been closed for months because of gnoll attacks, kobold infestations, and roaming bandits. Gnolls carrying shipping schedules point to an organized criminal network stealing the kingdom's wealth.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Brackwell Patch",b="The schedule places the suspected Collector near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Dughan has heard whispers of the name, but has no clear proof of who leads the ring or where the gold goes. The dispatch gives the garrison its first solid lead in the hunt for whoever directs the shipments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Gold Pickup Schedule?",a="The Gold Pickup Schedule is an intercepted note carried by gnolls in Elwynn Forest. It lists dates and times for mined gold to be handed over to a figure called 'The Collector.'",al={"pickup schedule","collector note","elwynn gold schedule"},it="item"},{q="Who is 'The Collector'?",a="'The Collector' is a criminal figure believed to be near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn Forest, coordinating an illicit gold trade.",al={"collector identity","who is the collector","brackwell collector"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan shocked by the schedule?",a="Marshal Dughan is shocked because gold is still being mined and shipped despite the official mines being closed for months. Gnoll attacks, kobold infestations, and roaming bandits forced the closures, so the schedule reveals a hidden operation stealing from the crown.",al={"why is dughan surprised","dughan reaction","elwynn mines closed"},it="motive"},{q="Why do gnolls have this note?",a="The Riverpaw gnolls of western Elwynn appear to carry the schedule as couriers, guards, or collaborators in the gold smuggling, bearing orders for the pickups.",al={"gnolls gold","why gnolls drop schedule","gnoll involvement"},it="ties"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Giving the schedule to Marshal Dughan leads to Manhunt, which sends you to find and eliminate the Collector near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.",al={"collector follow up","manhunt quest","after the collector"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch located?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, north of the river and east of the Maclure and Stonefield vineyards.",al={"brackwell location","where is brackwell","pumpkin patch elwynn"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every ounce of gold smuggled from Elwynn denies the Crown tax revenue and raw materials while the kingdom struggles to protect its borders.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can read the intercepted schedule and trace contraband through the criminal networks in Elwynn's wilderness.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know Elwynn's shuttered mines still hold copper and precious metals. Someone is working those veins unlawfully while honest miners stay home in fear."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","elwynn forest","gold pickup schedule","goldshire","manhunt","marshal dughan","mines","the collector"},rel={"quest:147","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Gold Pickup Schedule#Classic",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=123},src={"The Collector (Classic)"}}
E["quest:147"] = {t="quest",n="Manhunt",z="elwynn",s="Marshal Dughan sends you after a Defias bagman called the Collector in Elwynn Forest. The Collector works from the overrun Brackwell Pumpkin Patch and sends stolen gold from the forest's mines into the Brotherhood's coffers.",h="Marshal Dughan sends you after a Defias bagman called the Collector in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="Justice in the Pumpkin Patch",b="Marshal Dughan sends you to Brackwell Pumpkin Patch after Elwynn's gnolls are found carrying a schedule for gold pickups. Defias bandits and gnolls have taken over the once quiet homestead. The Collector hides among its overgrown vines, skimming ore from the kingdom's mines and arranging shipments for the growing rebellion.",sp=0},{t="An Artisan's Seal",b="After the Collector is slain, you recover his ring and deliver it to Marshal Dughan. The marshal is bewildered: its band bears the mark of Stormwind's old Stonemasons Guild, not a common criminal crest. The ring suggests the highwaymen choking Elwynn Forest are more than opportunists. Some were craftsmen who turned bitter and became outlaws after Stormwind was rebuilt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find the Collector?",a="The Collector hides at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest, just east of the Maclure Vineyards and north of the river boundary.",al={"collector location","where is collector","collector spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Collector stealing gold from Elwynn's mines?",a="The Collector gathers smuggled ore and extortion payments from the kobold-infested Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines to fund the Defias Brotherhood's covert operations across the kingdom.",al={"why steal gold","defias mines","what is collector doing"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the significance of the Collector's ring?",a="The ring is a membership ring of the old Stonemasons Guild, whose craftsmen rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War. Marshal Dughan cannot explain why a lowly thief working with the Defias carries an artisan guild ring, and hopes the question will one day be answered.",al={"collectors ring lore","stonemason ring","what does the ring mean"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan figure out who is behind the Brotherhood?",a="Not immediately. Marshal Dughan recognizes the artisan insignia on the ring, but cannot explain why a common thief carries an artisan guild signet. The wider conspiracy remains an open question in Goldshire.",al={"does dughan know","dughan reaction","marshal dughan Stonemasons"},sp=1},{q="Who sends you on this manhunt?",a="Marshal Dughan, the garrison commander at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, offers you this work after you recover the Defias pickup schedule.",al={"who gives manhunt","quest giver manhunt","marshal dughan quest"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the Brackwell family?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch lies in ruin, abandoned by its owners and occupied by Defias rogues, bandits, and encroaching Riverpaw gnolls that prowl the southeastern woodlands.",al={"brackwell lore","who owns pumpkin patch","brackwell farm"},it="history"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want the Collector stopped?",a="Gold plundered from Elwynn's mines is property of the kingdom of Stormwind. By systematically siphoning that wealth, the Collector is actively robbing the realm and funding illicit operations. Marshal Dughan cannot permit thieves to freely loot Crown resources, especially when the stolen coin suggests an organized conspiracy behind the local banditry.",al={"why kill the collector","marshal dughan motive manhunt","why does dughan care about the collector"},it="motive",add="1901992d"},{q="Who is the Collector and why is he at the pumpkin patch?",a="The Collector is an operative working with the Defias thieves to gather and transport illicit gold extracted from Elwynn's mines. He is using the abandoned Brackwell Pumpkin Patch as a secluded hideout, waiting for shipments according to the pickup schedule before smuggling the kingdom's wealth out of the forest.",al={"who is the collector","why is the collector at brackwell pumpkin patch","target of manhunt"},it="target",add="535c4316"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send an adventurer instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="The Stormwind City Guard and Goldshire's garrison are stretched perilously thin across Elwynn Forest, bogged down by gnoll incursions, kobold infestations in the mines, and rampant Defias bandits. Dughan simply lacks the spare soldiers to dispatch a manhunt to a remote pumpkin patch, forcing him to rely on capable, trustworthy adventurers.",al={"why does dughan need me","why send adventurers manhunt","why don't guards kill the collector"},it="why_me",add="e23a6feb"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how the Collector's covert work reflects the growing network of highwaymen and cutpurses taking root throughout Elwynn Forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Stormwind's local resources. Stopping the Collector cuts off an illicit flow of kingdom gold meant to fund rebellion near the capital.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may feel the weight of recovering the Stonemason's ring. It recalls the bitter labor disputes that divided the kingdom after Stormwind was rebuilt."},kw={"brackwell pumpkin patch","collector","defias","goldshire","manhunt","marshal dughan","ring","stonemasons guild"},rel={"quest:123","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=147},src={"Manhunt (Classic)"}}
E["quest:15"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate Echo Ridge",z="elwynn",s="Marshal McBride sends recruits north as kobolds gather at Echo Ridge Mine. The mine supplies ore and raw materials to Northshire Abbey and the Stormwind guard, and the growing threat puts both at risk.",h="Marshal McBride sends recruits north as kobolds gather at Echo Ridge Mine.",sec={{t="A Deepening Infestation",b="After early skirmishes with scattered vermin around Northshire's forested edge, scouts report a more organized threat. Kobolds have gathered in force at Echo Ridge Mine. Marshal McBride sends you north to face the workers at the entrance and learn how deeply they have settled in.",sp=0},{t="Threat to the Abbey's Wealth",b="Echo Ridge Mine supplies ore and raw materials to the Northshire brotherhood and the Stormwind guard stationed there. Kobolds have seized the tunnels, halting extraction and exposing the strain on local defenses. McBride asks you to cull ten workers, but the infestation runs deeper into the shafts than a surface patrol can reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of the Stormwind guards at Northshire Abbey, sends you to investigate after scouts find kobolds gathering to the north.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","marshal mcbride"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Echo Ridge Mine located?",a="Echo Ridge Mine lies in the far north of Northshire Valley, in the foothills above the abbey and its vineyards.",al={"echo ridge location","where is the mine","find echo ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are kobolds dangerous to Northshire?",a="Kobolds breed rapidly and swarm through underground tunnels in huge packs. Their hold on Echo Ridge Mine halts vital mining and threatens to overwhelm Northshire's undermanned valley.",al={"why kill kobolds","what makes kobolds a threat","kobold danger"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after I defeat the workers outside?",a="When you return, Marshal McBride's worst suspicions are confirmed: the mine is thoroughly infested. He immediately enlists your aid for a deeper push into the shafts in Skirmish at Echo Ridge.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Stormwind army clear the mine themselves?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources stretched thin across Elwynn and neighboring frontiers, Northshire's garrison is too small to spare full patrols for pest control. The guards rely on capable new recruits.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why use recruits","stormwind garrison"},it="why_me"},{q="What kind of kobolds are found around the mine entrance?",a="Kobold workers labor around the mine entrance and upper passages, digging tunnels and gathering candle wax for their underground colony.",al={"kobold types","what enemies to kill","kobold worker"},it="target"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the Echo Ridge Mine investigated?",a="Marshal McBride's scouts discovered that the kobold infestation is far larger than Northshire's garrison initially realized. The creatures have moved beyond minor camps and set up near the Echo Ridge Mine, threatening a vital local resource. McBride needs you to cull their front ranks and assess whether an even larger force is entrenching itself deeper within the mine before the valley's defenses are completely overrun.",al={"why clear echo ridge","mcbride motive","why investigate echo ridge mine"},it="motive",add="ffd728b0"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Copper from Echo Ridge Mine is essential to Northshire's smiths, so clearing its underground tunnels matters to miners' livelihoods.",["faction:Alliance"]="Kobolds have reached close to Stormwind's spiritual heart in Northshire, a sign of the kingdom's vulnerability while its regular forces are stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="As a young human beginning service in Northshire Valley, defending Echo Ridge from underground pests is an early chance to prove your worth to the kingdom."},kw={"echo ridge","elwynn","kobold","kobold worker","marshal mcbride","mine","northshire","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:echo-ridge-mine","npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:21","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn"},m={level="3",faction="Alliance",id=15},src={"Investigate Echo Ridge"}}
E["quest:1598"] = {t="quest",n="The Stolen Tome",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, a novice human warlock is sent to recover a forbidden tome and prove their skill. Drusilla La Salle hopes to claim Powers of the Void from the Defias, whose camp lies in the vineyards.",h="In Northshire Valley, a novice human warlock is sent to recover a forbidden tome and prove their skill.",sec={{t="A Forbidden Opportunity",b="Warlocks in Stormwind's lands hide their craft and keep prying eyes from their research. Northshire Abbey guards forbidden grimoires in its archives. Drusilla La Salle, the warlock mentor on the abbey grounds, covets Powers of the Void but cannot risk suspicion from the clerics and paladins by entering the library's protected wing herself.",sp=0},{t="Defias Opportunism",b="An abbey novice joins the Defias Brotherhood and steals several valuable texts on his way out. He flees to the Northshire Vineyards and takes refuge around the Defias campsite. The thieves stash their prize in a field tent, unaware of the danger in the book's dark arts.",sp=0},{t="The First Binding",b="Recovering the tome tests a novice warlock's nerve and opens the way to darker knowledge. Braving the bandit camp and returning the text satisfies Drusilla's ambition and proves the pupil is ready. She rewards the pupil with the dark rites to summon and bind an imp, the first demon an apprentice learns to command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Powers of the Void?",a="Powers of the Void is a forbidden grimoire about dark magic and control of the planes. Kept in a guarded wing of the Northshire Abbey library, it holds knowledge Drusilla La Salle covets for her study and teachings.",al={"powers of the void book","what is the book","what did the novice steal"},it="item"},{q="Why didn't Drusilla La Salle steal the book herself?",a="Drusilla La Salle must protect her standing at Northshire Abbey. Entering the library's secured archives would alert the clerics. When a novice stole the tome and joined the Defias, she had a chance to acquire it cleanly through an apprentice.",al={"why drusilla didn't steal it","why send me"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is the stolen tome hidden?",a="The Defias hid the tome in a tent at their campsite in the Northshire Vineyards, east of the abbey.",al={"where is the book","tome location","stolen tome tent"},gp=true},{q="Why did a Northshire novice join the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Discontent and strife across the kingdom drive laborers, farmers, and church students to join the Defias Brotherhood. The novice abandoned his vows, stole several important books from the library, then fled to the vineyard bandits.",al={"why novice joined defias","abbey defias traitor","who stole the book"},it="history"},{q="What reward does a warlock get for retrieving the tome?",a="Returning the tome proves the pupil has the nerve and resilience to practice the dark arts. Drusilla rewards the apprentice with the teachings to summon an imp, their first demon.",al={"what do you learn","warlock quest reward","why do this quest"},gp=true},{q="Do the Defias know how to use the book?",a="The bandits treat the stolen books as valuable plunder from the abbey. Though the Defias employ renegade spellcasters, the novice and his comrades tucked the tome into a tent crate instead of mastering its dark secrets.",al={"can defias use the tome","what defias do with book"}},{q="Why does Drusilla La Salle want the Powers of the Void?",a="Drusilla has long coveted the forbidden knowledge locked inside the Powers of the Void, but it was kept in a secured, protected wing of Northshire Abbey's library where she couldn't reach it without drawing suspicion. Having a stray novice steal it gave her the perfect opportunity to finally claim its dark secrets for herself while simultaneously testing whether you have the fortitude to study the warlock arts.",al={"why does drusilla want the book","drusilla la salle motive","why steal the tome"},it="motive",add="1f0061ae"},{q="Who are you sent against to recover the tome?",a="You are sent against the Defias Brotherhood bandits encamped in the Northshire Vineyards. A wayward Abbey novice stole several valuable volumes from the protected library before fleeing to join their rebellion, hiding the tome among their tents.",al={"who took the book","defias in vineyards","who stole the powers of the void"},it="target",add="a46315b9"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you prove you can cross dangerous ground without flinching. Securing the tome earns you the rites to call your first imp.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the Defias Brotherhood's reach in Northshire, where even abbey students steal sacred texts and join the insurrection.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you must tread softly around Northshire's paladins and clerics, using outlaws' mistakes to claim restricted occult knowledge."},kw={"defias brotherhood","drusilla la salle","northshire abbey","novice thief","powers of the void","stolen book","vineyards","warlock imp"},rel={"npc:drusilla-la-salle","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Drusilla La Salle",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=1598,ri={"Powers of the Void"}},src={"The Stolen Tome"}}
E["quest:16"] = {t="quest",n="Give Gerard a Drink",z="elwynn",s="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works long days in the fields and needs fresh spring water. He trades apples for water brought by passing travelers.",h="At the Maclure Vineyards, Gerard Tiller works long days in the fields and needs fresh spring water.",sec={{t="Thirsty Work in the Vineyard Fields",b="Elwynn Forest's farms supply grain, fruit, and vegetables to Stormwind's townsfolk and garrisons. Tending crops under the open sky is hot, demanding work. Gerard Tiller spends long days in the dirt at the Maclure Vineyards, keeping pests away and managing the harvest. With little time to return to town wells, he relies on passing recruits to bring clean spring water so he can keep working.",sp=0},{t="The Economy of Barter",b="Gerard trades provisions instead of coin. Travelers with extra flasks of Refreshing Spring Water can exchange them for fresh apples from the orchard. The kingdom stretches its resources to maintain order and feed its army, so direct barter between smallholders and recruits remains a practical way to get by in rural Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gerard Tiller?",a="Gerard Tiller is a farmer at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest. He tends the fields and orchards that supply local residents.",al={"gerard tiller","who is tiller","gerard"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gerard need water?",a="Working in the fields under the sun all day is exhausting. Gerard relies on passing travelers for fresh spring water so he can stay hydrated without leaving his chores.",al={"why spring water","gerard thirsty","why need drink"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Refreshing Spring Water be found?",a="Food and drink vendors and innkeepers throughout Elwynn Forest commonly sell Refreshing Spring Water. Brother Danil sells it inside Northshire Abbey.",al={"where get water","spring water source","how to get water"},gp=true},{q="Is this trade repeatable?",a="Yes. Gerard keeps working the fields and will trade fresh orchard apples for more bottles of water you can spare.",al={"repeatable quest","can i do this again","turn in more water"},gp=true},{q="What does Gerard offer in return for the drink?",a="Gerard trades a Shiny Red Apple for fresh water.",al={"gerard reward","what do i get","trade reward"},gp=true},{q="Where is Gerard located?",a="Gerard is outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards in southern Elwynn Forest.",al={"gerard tiller location","where is gerard","where is the farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Refreshing Spring Water used for?",a="Tending the fields at the Maclure Vineyards is exhausting labor, and Gerard Tiller simply needs a reliable supply of fresh, clean water to quench his thirst while working under the sun. Rather than leaving his crops unattended to fetch drink himself, he is glad to barter with passing travelers who carry some to spare.",al={"refreshing spring water use","why spring water","gerard spring water"},it="item",add="d51fec31"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting Elwynn's farmers at places like the Maclure Vineyards helps feed the forest's homesteads and garrisons while the kingdom defends itself.",["race:Human"]="As a human starting in Northshire, helping neighbors like Gerard Tiller shows the communal spirit that holds Elwynn together."},kw={"apples","barter","elwynn forest","gerard tiller","maclure vineyards","refreshing spring water"},rel={"npc:gerard-tiller","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Gerard Tiller",["end"]="Gerard Tiller",faction="Alliance",id=16,ri={"Refreshing Spring Water"}},src={"Give Gerard a Drink"}}
E["quest:1667"] = {t="quest",n="Dead-tooth Jack",z="elwynn",s="A stolen badge puts Marshal Haggard's authority in Defias hands. The retired officer lives in eastern Elwynn Forest, where Dead-tooth Jack tricked him into surrendering his official insignia. Jack wore a Stormwind tabard in the dark and posed as Marshal Dughan. Haggard needs the badge back before the Defias Brotherhood can use it to impersonate Stormwind officials.",h="A stolen badge puts Marshal Haggard's authority in Defias hands.",sec={{t="A Con in the Dark",b="Marshal Haggard lives in an isolated cottage on Elwynn's eastern ridges. One night, a figure in a Stormwind tabard approached, claiming official business and asking for Haggard's old marshal's badge. Believing he was handing it to a fellow officer, Haggard complied. The stranger laughed in his face and vanished into the woods. The thief was a Defias rogue called Dead-tooth Jack.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of False Authority",b="Marshal Haggard has retired, but his old badge still carries the legal weight of Stormwind. Defias bandits are creeping across Elwynn, Westfall, and Redridge, and the badge could help them pass guard checkpoints, redirect patrols, or take command of supplies. Jack retreated to a camp to the south and left the badge locked in a strongbox. Haggard needs it recovered before the Defias can cause serious harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dead-tooth Jack?",a="Dead-tooth Jack is a Defias operative in eastern Elwynn Forest. Under cover of darkness, he posed as Marshal Dughan and tricked retired Marshal Haggard into handing over his official Stormwind badge.",al={"dead tooth jack","who is dead tooth","dead tooth jack lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard need his badge back?",a="Marshal Haggard needs his badge back because it is an authentic symbol of Stormwind authority. He fears the Defias will use it to impersonate officials, bypass military patrols, and cause havoc across the realm.",al={"why recover badge","haggards badge","why does the badge matter"},it="motive"},{q="How did Jack manage to fool Marshal Haggard?",a="Jack approached Haggard's cottage at night wearing a Stormwind tabard. In the poor light, Haggard mistook him for Marshal Dughan of Goldshire and handed over the insignia, believing he was giving it to a fellow officer.",al={"how did he fool haggard","haggard tricked","why did haggard give the badge"},it="history"},{q="Where does Jack keep the stolen badge?",a="Jack keeps the badge locked in a strongbox at his bandit camp south of Marshal Haggard's house. He carries the key to the chest on his person.",al={"badge location","where is the badge","dead tooth camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sent you to Marshal Haggard in the first place?",a="Harry Burlguard, a veteran warrior who frequents the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind, sends adventurers to Marshal Haggard. He knows the retired marshal may part with spare weaponry in exchange for help.",al={"who sends you here","burlguard","questgiver start"},it="ties"},{q="What happens once the badge is returned?",a="Marshal Haggard is greatly relieved that the Defias cannot use his identity or rank against the kingdom. In gratitude, he salutes you and offers your choice of well-maintained military weapons from his years in service.",al={"quest turn in","haggard reaction","badge returned"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Marshal Haggard's Badge for?",a="Marshal Haggard's badge is a retired mark of high authority in the Stormwind Army. In honest hands, it is a treasured heirloom from Haggard's years of service. In the grip of the Defias Brotherhood, however, an official marshal's insignia allows thieves and bandits to impersonate Stormwind officers, bypass checkpoints, and orchestrate dangerous deceptions across the kingdom.",al={"haggards badge purpose","what does the badge do","why is the badge dangerous"},it="item",add="5b8b35d8"},{q="Why does Marshal Haggard need you to recover his badge?",a="Haggard is long retired and lives out in an isolated cottage, embarrassed that a rogue tricked him in the dark. Asking the town garrison or Marshal Dughan for help would mean admitting he handed his official badge straight to a Defias thief, and Stormwind's guards are already stretched thin defending the township. You arrived looking for his spare weapons, giving him the perfect capable, discreet hand to settle the score.",al={"why does haggard need me","why doesn't haggard get it himself","why not use guards"},it="why_me",add="55355d07"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For you, a human of Stormwind, this theft shows how vulnerable the kingdom's rural borders are to Defias infiltrators. They will wear the crown's own colors to deceive retired veterans.",["class:Warrior"]="Marshal Haggard was once a veteran frontline fighter. As a warrior, you can earn his thanks and choose from spare arms kept from his years of service.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how Dead-tooth Jack's caper depends on disguise, deception, and impudence as much as crude highway robbery."},kw={"badge","dead-tooth jack","defias","elwynn forest","guard burlguard","impersonation","marshal dughan","marshal haggard","strongbox"},rel={"quest:1666","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1667,ri={"Marshal Haggard's Badge"}},src={"Dead-tooth Jack"}}
E["quest:1688"] = {t="quest",n="Surena Caledon",z="elwynn",s="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, Gakin seeks his former pupil and a bloodstone choker. He sends an aspiring warlock after Surena Caledon, who betrayed him to join the Defias Brotherhood.",h="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, Gakin seeks his former pupil and a bloodstone choker.",sec={{t="A Bitter Master",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Gakin the Darkbinder teaches novices the forbidden arts of fel summoning. He once took a young woman named Surena Caledon as his pupil. He admired her natural magical talent and her beauty. Surena left her studies and Gakin's favor, then fled Stormwind with her lover, Erlan Drudgemoor, to join the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Bloodstone",b="Gakin has no concern for Surena's survival, but he wants the bloodstone choker he gave her during her apprenticeship. He sends his newest apprentice southeast to Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in Elwynn Forest, a farmstead overrun by Defias bandits. The apprentice is to take the jewel from Surena by any means necessary. The bloodstone will provide the magical catalyst for the next trial: summoning and binding a Voidwalker.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Surena Caledon?",a="Surena Caledon was Gakin the Darkbinder's apprentice in Stormwind. She had natural talent and earned his favor and gifts before abandoning her studies to flee with Erlan Drudgemoor, a Defias bandit.",al={"surena lore","who is surena","surena caledon backstory"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gakin want her choker back?",a="Gakin gave Surena the choker during her apprenticeship, and it holds a valuable bloodstone. He resents her betrayal and needs the stone as a ritual reagent to help his new apprentice bind a Voidwalker.",al={"why get the choker","bloodstone choker importance"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Surena Caledon be found?",a="Surena can be found with her Defias companions at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, an abandoned farmstead in southeastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"surena location","where is surena","where is the pumpkin patch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after recovering the choker?",a="Returning the bloodstone choker to Gakin completes the trial. The next step is to enter the summoning circle in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb and bind a Voidwalker from the Twisting Nether.",al={"what comes next","next quest after surena"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Erlan Drudgemoor?",a="Erlan Drudgemoor is a rogue with the Defias Brotherhood. He seduced Surena Caledon and persuaded her to leave her warlock training and flee Stormwind to live among the bandits.",al={"erlan lore","who is erlan drudgemoor"},it="identity"},{q="Does Gakin show any remorse over Surena's fate?",a="Gakin shows no remorse over Surena's fate. He says her life means nothing to him, and that wasting her magical talent is a shame, but her betrayal makes her elimination necessary.",al={"does gakin care","gakin reaction to surena"}},{q="What is Surena's Choker for?",a="The choker is an enchanted piece of bloodstone jewelry that Gakin the Darkbinder foolishly gifted to his former apprentice. To a warlock, bloodstone holds raw arcane and summoning potency. Gakin requires the artifact's lingering power to prepare the ritual circle beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, enabling you to summon and bind a voidwalker to your will.",al={"surena's choker purpose","why bloodstone choker","what does the choker do"},it="item",add="8bc53c35"},{q="Why does Gakin send an apprentice instead of handling Surena himself?",a="Warlocks in Stormwind operate in strict secrecy beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, forbidden by the kingdom's laws and hunted if exposed. Gakin cannot ask the city guard to retrieve an illicit magical heirloom from Defias outlaws, nor can he abandon his sanctum to settle a personal embarrassment. Sending you tests your ruthlessness and proves whether you possess the mettle required to master dark arts.",al={"why send me surena","why can't gakin get the choker","why doesn't gakin go himself"},it="why_me",add="703ff238"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face a proving ground in the hunt for Surena Caledon. Gakin teaches that betrayal carries a lethal cost and sentiment has no place in the dark arts.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how the Defias Brotherhood continues to tempt disgruntled citizens of the kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"bloodstone choker","brackwell pumpkin patch","defias","erlan drudgemoor","gakin the darkbinder","slaughtered lamb","surena caledon","voidwalker"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1471","quest:1685","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1688,ri={"Surena's Choker"}},src={"Surena Caledon (quest)"}}
E["quest:1739"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind warlocks seek to bind a succubus to their will. Beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, an initiate uses the enchanted core from the Heartswood to summon the demon and defeat it in combat.",h="Stormwind warlocks seek to bind a succubus to their will.",sec={{t="Descent into the Crypt",b="A crypt beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter shelters the city's warlocks. There, away from the city watch and the Cathedral of Light, they practice forbidden arts. Stone summoning circles channel the Nether's power and let initiates reach across the veil between worlds.",sp=0},{t="Subjugating the Seductress",b="A warlock needs the prepared Heartswood Core to summon a succubus. The ritual opens a breach at the summoning circle, but the demon can corrupt and overwhelm even a fortified mind. To master it, the warlock must defeat it in single combat. Its physical form returns to the Twisting Nether, while its true tether is secured.",sp=0},{t="Gakin's Secrets",b="After slaying the summoned creature, the initiate takes the depleted core back to Gakin the Darkbinder. Gakin then teaches the knowledge needed to call the succubus across the void. The rite marks an Alliance warlock's growth into an adept trusted to handle volatile, sapient demons.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The summoning takes place in the catacombs beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, a tavern in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Spiral stairs lead past the pub cellar to an underground sanctum with arcane summoning circles.",al={"where do i summon","succubus summoning location","crypt location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Heartswood Core?",a="The Heartswood Core anchors and fuels the summoning. Taken from the Heartswood, a tree that grew where two night elf lovers fell in Ashenvale during the War of the Ancients, it carries the spiritual resonance needed to open a rift and draw a succubus across the Twisting Nether.",al={"why heartswood core","what does heartswood do"},it="item"},{q="Why must the warlock kill the succubus?",a="A warlock must slay the succubus to establish dominance over it. Succubi use manipulation and mental subjugation, and allowing one to manifest without defeating it invites ruin. Combat imprints the warlock's authority on the spirit before it coalesces back in the Nether.",al={"why do i fight the succubus","why kill the demon to bind it"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is a senior warlock who lives in The Slaughtered Lamb and oversees Alliance practitioners' training in Stormwind. He arranges the secret procurement of demonology artifacts and judges whether acolytes have the will to command demons.",al={"who is gakin","gakin darkbinder lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Surena that Gakin mentions?",a="Surena Caledon was Gakin's former student. She ran off with the Defias, and you recovered her choker earlier. Gakin wonders wryly if she was a succubus in disguise sent to warp his mind, then decides he gives her too much credit.",al={"surena reference","who was surena"},it="people"},{q="Are succubi permitted in the streets of Stormwind?",a="The Church of the Holy Light and the kingdom's authorities strictly forbid open demonology. Bound demons may follow warlocks through the city, but in lore the practice stays in shadows, basements, and secluded sanctums such as The Slaughtered Lamb's crypts.",al={"can guards see my succubus","is demon summoning legal in stormwind"}},{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want this done?",a="Gakin is testing your discipline and mastery as an aspiring warlock. He seeks to verify that you possess the willpower to bend demonic forces to your command rather than succumb to their deceit. By proving you can best a summoned demon beneath the tavern, you show you are worthy of learning how to bind and control a succubus permanently.",al={"why does gakin want this","gakin motive","why summon succubus gakin"},it="motive",add="69ec55c9"},{q="What is the succubus you are sent to summon?",a="You are conjuring a succubus—a seductive, cunning demon from the Twisting Nether. Succubi are renowned for manipulating desires and overwhelming even resolute minds. It does not dwell in Stormwind naturally; your spell and the Heartswood Core rip open a localized rift specifically to pull the creature forth so you can defeat and enslave its essence.",al={"what is the succubus","who is the target the binding","summoned succubus"},it="target",add="2be029b1"},{q="Why does Gakin have you summon the succubus instead of doing it himself?",a="A demon cannot be bound to serve on another warlock's behalf; the pact of servitude demands that the summoner personally dominate the creature. Gakin already commands his own dark arts. For you to call upon the succubus as your minion, you must personally confront the danger, prove your dominance over its charms, and tether its will to yours.",al={"why must i summon the succubus","why me binding","why cant gakin fight the succubus"},it="why_me",add="f36093f2"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a human or gnome warlock, this rite marks a step from handling mindless imps and voidwalkers to commanding sapient, calculating demons.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Stormwind quietly tolerates shadow magic in hidden alcoves despite the Church's doctrines."},kw={"binding","crypt","darkbinder","gakin","heartswood","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","succubus","summoning circle"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","quest:1738","quest:1472","quest:1685","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:1471","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1739},src={"The Binding (Succubus, Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:176"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: \"Hogger\"",z="elwynn",s="Wanted: \"Hogger\" is an Alliance bounty posted outside Goldshire for the head of a massive, savage gnoll chieftain. Hogger prowls the southwestern woods of Elwynn Forest and has violently thwarted every attempt by the local authorities to bring him down.",h="Wanted: \"Hogger\" is an Alliance bounty posted outside Goldshire for the head of a massive, savage gnoll...",sec={{t="A Menace in the Woods",b="While Elwynn Forest struggles with banditry and kobold infestations, the gnoll tribes in the south have grown bolder and more organized under the brute leadership of Hogger. Towering over typical Riverpaw gnolls, Hogger has established camp near the Forest's Edge, ambushing travelers and overpowering the local militia patrols sent to subdue him.",sp=0},{t="Goldshire's Desperation",b="With the Stormwind Army stretched thin and unable to spare regular forces to police the outskirts of the capital, Marshal Dughan took the unusual step of posting an open bounty on the beast. Taking down Hogger requires venture into deeply hostile gnoll territory, and his ferocity has earned him a reputation as the deadliest threat facing novice adventurers in Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger is an unusually large and savage gnoll leader terrorizing southwestern Elwynn Forest. He commands local packs around the Forest's Edge and has violently defeated all previous attempts by Stormwind guards to capture or kill him.",al={"who is hogger","hogger lore","what is hogger"},it="target"},{q="Where can Hogger be found?",a="Hogger wanders among the gnoll encampments in southwestern Elwynn Forest, near the southern borders known as Forest's Edge, just north of the river boundary with Westfall and Duskwood.",al={"hogger location","where is hogger","find hogger"},gp=true},{q="Why is there a bounty on Hogger?",a="The Stormwind Army placed a bounty on Hogger because he has overpowered local patrols and poses a lethal danger to travelers. With official troops stretched thin across the kingdom, Marshal Dughan turned to independent adventurers and bounty hunters to eliminate the threat.",al={"why kill hogger","wanted poster hogger","who put bounty on hogger"},it="motive"},{q="Who collects the proof of Hogger's death?",a="Proof of the beast's demise—his Huge Gnoll Claw—must be brought directly to Marshal Dughan, who commands the local garrison stationed in Goldshire.",al={"turn in hogger","where to turn in hogger","who wants hogger claw"}},{q="Why is Hogger so dangerous compared to other gnolls?",a="Unlike the common gnolls prowling Elwynn, Hogger possesses immense physical stature and brutality. He hits significantly harder and can withstand far more punishment, often overwhelming single combatants who underestimate him.",al={"is hogger strong","why is hogger elite"},it="danger"},{q="Why can't the Stormwind guards handle Hogger themselves?",a="The kingdom's military resources are severely depleted and tied down defending major borders or dealing with the missing King Varian Wrynn. Marshal Dughan's small detachment in Goldshire lacks the manpower to safely hunt down such a resilient monster.",al={"why doesn't dughan kill hogger","where is stormwind army"},it="why_me"},{q="What is the Huge Gnoll Claw for?",a="The Huge Gnoll Claw serves as undeniable proof of Hogger's death. Because the brute has overpowered every attempt at his capture, Marshal Dughan and the Stormwind Army require unmistakable physical evidence before handing over the posted bounty reward.",al={"huge gnoll claw","why do i need hoggers claw","hogger claw use"},it="item",add="fccb34f1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Taking down Hogger is considered a rite of passage for young Alliance heroes testing their mettle in the defense of Stormwind's heartland.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Elwynn, slaying Hogger secures homesteads and road trade that have been terrorized by gnoll ambushes for months."},kw={"bounty","dughan","elwynn","forest's edge","gnoll","goldshire","hogger","wanted"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:goldshire","subzone:forest-s-edge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wanted Poster",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=176,ri={"Huge Gnoll Claw"}},src={"Wanted: \"Hogger\""}}
E["quest:18"] = {t="quest",n="Brotherhood of Thieves",z="elwynn",s="Deputy Willem sends recruits across Northshire's eastern river to face the Defias Brotherhood. Their red burlap bandanas give Stormwind its first tangible evidence of the brigands' organized presence in the valley.",h="Deputy Willem sends recruits across Northshire's eastern river to face the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="Bandits in the Valley",b="Northshire Valley has long been a safe haven in Elwynn Forest, guarded by Stormwind and used to train recruits and Clerics of the Holy Light. Recently, discipline along its perimeter has frayed. Vagrants and thieves have crossed the eastern river, lurking near the woods and making small camps close to the abbey. Deputy Willem maintains local order, but the guards cannot spare the manpower to watch every corner of the valley without volunteers.",sp=0},{t="The Crimson Sigil",b="These outlaws are coordinated and wear matching attire. They call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and their red burlap bandanas mark their allegiance. Deputy Willem sends recruits to drive back the brigands and recover their masks, hoping to curb their advance and learn how deeply the Defias have reached into the kingdom's heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is an organized band of brigands and outlaws operating across Elwynn Forest and Westfall. Northshire authorities first see them as bold thieves, but they wear matching red burlap masks and follow coordinated leadership.",al={"who are the defias","what is defias brotherhood","defias lore"},it="people"},{q="Why is Deputy Willem asking recruits for help instead of using the Stormwind Army?",a="The Stormwind Army and city guards are spread thin across the kingdom. Unrest is rising in neighboring regions, and Stormwind City's leadership is strained, so local deputies rely on eager volunteers and novice recruits to push back the bandits.",al={"why willem needs help","where are stormwind guards","why no army"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are these thieves coming from?",a="The thieves have gathered across the river east of the abbey. They skulk around the edges of local farmsteads and campsites near the vineyard.",al={"where are the bandits","defias location northshire"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the thieves wear red burlap bandanas?",a="The red burlap bandana marks allegiance to the Defias Brotherhood and masks each thief's identity. It also signals their allegiance to fellow outlaws across the human territories.",al={"why red bandanas","meaning of red masks","red burlap"},it="item"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Deputy Willem and the locals soon realize the bandit threat reaches farther into Northshire. Recruits then help Milly Osworth with her ruined harvest and track down Garrick Padfoot, a specific ringleader.",al={"what comes next","after brotherhood of thieves"},it="next_step"},{q="Does Deputy Willem know who leads the Defias?",a="Willem does not understand the full scope of the organization. He knows only that the brigands call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and he suspects their presence near the abbey bodes ill for Stormwind.",al={"does willem know vancleef","who leads defias northshire"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want you to fight the thieves?",a="Deputy Willem is tasked with protecting Northshire Abbey and the surrounding valley. A brazen criminal gang calling itself the Defias Brotherhood has crept into the eastern woods across the river, threatening the security of the abbey and local workers. Willem wants them suppressed immediately before they gain a stronger foothold or launch a direct assault on the valley.",al={"why does willem want this","willem motive","why stop the defias here"},it="motive",add="e491bbee"},{q="Who are the thieves across the river?",a="You are dispatched against the Defias Thugs, outlaws belonging to the Defias Brotherhood who have set up camp in the woods across the stream east of Northshire Abbey. They have gathered near the vineyards and surrounding fields, scouting the valley and harassing the locals while establishing an armed presence right under Stormwind's nose.",al={"who are the thieves","who am i fighting","defias in northshire"},it="target",add="4db9a478"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans beginning their training in Northshire, the Defias are a harsh reminder that the safety of the Kingdom of Stormwind is slipping from within.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind authorities rely on newly arrived Alliance recruits to keep peace in Northshire while the kingdom's formal military is stretched thin.",["class:Rogue"]="For novice rogues, the Defias offer a glimpse of how organized criminal networks operate in the shadows of the human heartland."},kw={"bandanas","brotherhood of thieves","defias","deputy willem","elwynn","northshire","stormwind army"},rel={"npc:willem","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:783","quest:65","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Deputy Willem",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=18,ri={"Red Burlap Bandana"}},src={"Brotherhood of Thieves"}}
E["quest:1861"] = {t="quest",n="Mirror Lake",z="elwynn",s="Novice Alliance mages in Stormwind's Mage Quarter are sent to sample Mirror Lake's waters for magical contamination. Jennea Cannon sends them southwest of the city gates to test the waterfall spray.",h="Novice Alliance mages in Stormwind's Mage Quarter are sent to sample Mirror Lake's waters for magical...",sec={{t="Ley Lines and Shifting Currents",b="Azeroth's arcane currents were shaken by conflicts from the opening of the Dark Portal through the Third War and the battle at Mount Hyjal. Those shocks tore ancient currents from their stable channels. In Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum, magi like Jennea Cannon watch the changes closely. They fear that displaced arcane power could reach the wilderness and corrupt local ecosystems.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Waters",b="Mirror Lake lies beneath the cliffs southwest of the Stormwind gates and is a primary natural reservoir fed by mountain falls. The surrounding countryside depends on its waters. Jennea sends novice mages with a glass flask to the waterfall's base, where they collect fresh spray. The Sanctum can then use scrying and reagent tests to learn whether wild magic is seeping into the public water supply.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Jennea Cannon want a water sample from Mirror Lake?",a="Conflicts across Azeroth have ruptured natural ley currents. Jennea Cannon fears unsettled arcane energies are reaching the water table around Stormwind and could harm anyone who drinks from the lake.",al={"why mirror lake water","jennea water sample","what is this quest for"},it="motive"},{q="Where exactly is Mirror Lake?",a="Mirror Lake lies in northwestern Elwynn Forest, against the high bluffs southwest of Stormwind's main gates. The sample comes from the pool at the foot of its waterfall.",al={"where is mirror lake","mirror lake location","find mirror lake"},gp=true},{q="What happens if the water is tainted?",a="Jennea fears that drinking magically tainted water for too long could harm those who depend on the lake. The precise effects are not known.",al={"is the water poisoned","what if water has magic","magical taint effects"}},{q="Who can undertake this mission?",a="Novice Alliance mages in training undertake this assignment as one of their earliest field studies for the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"who gets mirror lake quest","is mirror lake mage only"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest lead to further investigations?",a="The direct initial task begun with Jennea Cannon's summons ends here. It gives the apprentice their first formal mage implement and establishes their duty to watch for magical disturbances across the realm.",al={"what comes after mirror lake","mirror lake quest chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What caused the magical currents to destabilize in the first place?",a="Jennea traces the changed currents to the world's great mystic struggles, but names no specific battle or event.",al={"why are ley lines damaged","mystic struggles meaning","what broke the magic"},it="history"},{q="What is the Mirror Lake Water Sample for?",a="Jennea Cannon needs the sample to test the waters of Mirror Lake for magical contamination. Massive mystic upheavals across Azeroth have torn arcane currents from their normal paths, and the mages of the Mage Quarter worry these unstable energies are seeping directly into the local water supply. Testing the lake's water will reveal whether those drinking from it are in danger of magical corruption.",al={"mirror lake water sample use","why get water sample","what does the sample do"},it="item",add="66ca747e"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you move from study in the Wizard's Sanctum to investigating arcane phenomena in the world. This work brings your first dedicated mage staff or off-hand orb.",["race:Human"]="As a Human, you know Mirror Lake feeds Elwynn's farmlands and waterways, so its purity matters to Stormwind's citizens.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help the Wizard's Sanctum magi protect Elwynn's natural resources and the kingdom's heart."},kw={"arcane taint","elwynn forest","jennea cannon","ley lines","mirror lake","water sample","wizards sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","quest:1860","zone:elwynn","subzone:stormwind-gate","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Jennea Cannon",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1861,ri={"Mirror Lake Water Sample"}},src={"Mirror Lake (quest)"}}
E["quest:21"] = {t="quest",n="Skirmish at Echo Ridge",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, recruits strike at kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine. Marshal McBride ordered the attack after scouts found the mine overrun.",h="In Northshire Valley, recruits strike at kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine.",sec={{t="Purging the Mine",b="Marshal McBride sends recruits against the kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine. Scouts found the mine overrun, and the garrison fears the creatures will strengthen their hold if left alone. The kobolds dig through the tunnels, gather stolen resources, and multiply. Recruits must thin their numbers to protect Northshire Valley, with its farms and spiritual retreat.",sp=0},{t="A Thin Defense",b="New recruits are sent into the mine because the Stormwind Army is stretched thin. Garrison forces guard the southern borders, while unrest is rumored across Elwynn. Officers like McBride must call on willing hands. A recruit who proves reliable at Echo Ridge earns the army’s respect and is ready for more difficult work elsewhere in the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are kobolds infesting the Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds are drawn to mineral-rich tunnels and abandoned quarries. With Stormwind’s forces stretched thin, they can enter unguarded places like Echo Ridge to dig burrows, hoard gold, and claim underground shelter.",al={"why kobolds in mine","echo ridge kobolds","what are kobolds doing"},it="target"},{q="Who orders the skirmish?",a="Marshal McBride orders the skirmish. He commands the Stormwind Army forces at Northshire Abbey and oversees the valley’s defense with limited manpower.",al={"who gives skirmish quest","marshal mcbride orders"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the strategic importance of Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine holds stone and ore needed to maintain Northshire and help rebuild Stormwind. Kobolds on Northshire’s northern border threaten the abbey and nearby vineyards.",al={"why echo ridge matters","echo ridge mine importance"},it="place"},{q="Where does this mission lead next?",a="After the first kobold laborers are cleared from the mine, Marshal McBride sends you toward Goldshire to aid the region’s defense.",al={"what quest after skirmish","next step after echo ridge"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Stormwind Army clear the mine themselves?",a="Stormwind’s forces are short on soldiers, defending distant borders and answering bandit attacks across Elwynn. McBride relies on new recruits for local threats while seasoned guards hold defensive lines.",al={"why recruits","where are stormwind soldiers"},it="why_me"},{q="Are kobolds intelligent enough to be an organized military threat?",a="Kobold laborers are cowardly and simple-minded alone, but territorial and aggressive in numbers. Left unchecked, they dig winding tunnels, set traps in caverns, and draw larger, better-armed vermin.",al={"are kobolds smart","kobold danger level"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine culled?",a="Marshal McBride knows that the longer the kobolds remain unchallenged in Echo Ridge Mine, the deeper their foothold in Northshire becomes. Leaving them unmolested invites them to entrench themselves further and threaten the valley, making their eventual removal far bloodier and risking the security of Northshire Abbey itself.",al={"why kill kobolds in echo ridge","mcbride motive echo ridge","why clear echo ridge mine"},it="motive",add="a391cdc3"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, clearing Echo Ridge is your first true test of arms in defense of your ancestral kingdom. You prove your mettle to Stormwind’s officers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help reclaim mines that hold stone and ore for rebuilding and fortifying human settlements after the war.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face swarming kobold workers in close quarters, among the first entrenched foes you meet.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you help make it possible to safely dig and smelt valuable mineral veins across Northshire Valley."},kw={"echo ridge","echo ridge mine","elwynn","kobold","laborer","marshal mcbride","mcbride","northshire","skirmish","stormwind army"},rel={"quest:15","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:kobold","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="5",faction="Alliance",id=21},src={"Skirmish at Echo Ridge"}}
E["quest:239"] = {t="quest",n="Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!",z="elwynn",s="Marshal Dughan sends available adventurers west to Westbrook Garrison, the outpost at Elwynn Forest's border with Westfall. Stormwind's army is stretched thin across the kingdom, while Deputy Rainer and his guards face growing pressure from Riverpaw gnolls and wandering thieves without regular reinforcements.",h="Marshal Dughan sends available adventurers west to Westbrook Garrison, the outpost at Elwynn Forest's border...",sec={{t="A Frontier Stretched Thin",b="Westbrook Garrison guards the western edge of Elwynn Forest, where settled woodland meets Westfall's troubled plains. Gnoll warbands and bandits grow bolder along the waterways and western roads, and the small garrison has asked for more men. Marshal Dughan and Goldshire's administration have no Stormwind soldiers to spare. Local commanders must hire traveling mercenaries and wandering adventurers.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Across the Brook",b="Deputy Rainer and his men face the Riverpaw gnolls, whose raiding parties harass travelers and nearby homesteads. The pack operates in the borderlands between Elwynn and Westfall. With Stormwind distracted by political and military troubles, the gnolls press deeper into inhabited territory. Westbrook Garrison guards against their unchecked advance into the heart of the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't Stormwind send regular soldiers to Westbrook Garrison?",a="Stormwind's standing military is stretched thin across several frontiers. With King Varian Wrynn missing and the realm beset by internal strife, high command has refused or been unable to send regular soldiers to rural outposts. Town marshals like Dughan must rely on freelance volunteers.",al={"why no stormwind troops","why send adventurers","where is stormwind army"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is Westbrook Garrison located?",a="Westbrook Garrison sits on Elwynn Forest's western edge. Follow the main road west from Goldshire, past the small brook. The fortified tower stands on your right, just before the Westfall border.",al={"westbrook garrison location","how to get to westbrook","where is deputy rainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats are troubling the garrison?",a="Deputy Rainer faces repeated raids by Riverpaw gnolls, along with growing thief and bandit activity in the border country between Westfall and Elwynn Forest.",al={"what attacks westbrook","why does rainer need help","who is attacking westbrook garrison"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer is the Stormwind officer in command at Westbrook Garrison. He must hold the western border and rely on civilian volunteers and mercenaries because official military reinforcements are scarce.",al={"rainer lore","deputy rainer","who is rainer"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after reporting to Deputy Rainer?",a="Deputy Rainer enlists your help against the local Riverpaw gnolls. He places a bounty on their collars to thin their numbers and protect the border road.",al={"what comes next","westbrook quest chain","rainer quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the gnolls pushing into Elwynn Forest?",a="The Riverpaw gnolls have camps along the rivers that separate Elwynn and Westfall. With fewer soldiers along the border, they have grown bold enough to raid trade routes and press toward Elwynn's interior farms.",al={"riverpaw gnolls elwynn","why are gnolls here","gnoll problem"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want you to go to Westbrook Garrison?",a="Marshal Dughan is responsible for maintaining order and security across Elwynn Forest from Goldshire, but his resources are stretched to the breaking point. Westbrook Garrison guards the kingdom's western boundary, and Deputy Rainer has sent urgent word of rising banditry and encroaching gnolls. Without regular troops to dispatch as reinforcements, Dughan must rely on independent adventurers to answer the outpost's plea for help before the western border collapses entirely.",al={"why send to westbrook garrison","marshal dughan motive","why westbrook garrison needs help"},it="motive",add="76645dec"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see an unsettling sign of the kingdom's neglect. The crown's defenses have worn thin since the King's disappearance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance volunteer, you take up the work of regular soldiers and help keep core territories from descending into complete chaos."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","gnolls","goldshire","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","npc:deputy-rainer","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:11","quest:76","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Deputy Rainer",faction="Alliance",id=239},src={"Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!"}}
E["quest:248"] = {t="quest",n="Looking Further",z="elwynn",s="Looking Further is an Alliance espionage mission directed by the wizard Theocritus via an enchanted conduit. To investigate tensions between the rogue mage Morganth and the Blackrock orcs, you must infiltrate the watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep and plant an enchanted glyph inside an unnoticed container.",h="Looking Further is an Alliance espionage mission directed by the wizard Theocritus via an enchanted conduit.",sec={{t="A Rift in Redridge",b="From his sanctum in Elwynn Forest, the wizard Theocritus maintains a vigilant watch over eastern Redridge through scrying magic. While monitoring the Tower of Ilgalar, he detects sudden contention between the renegade human warlock Morganth and the Blackrock orcs entrenched in Stonewatch Keep. Rather than working together against the Kingdom of Stormwind, these hostile factions are locked in conflict over an unknown prize, prompting Theocritus to intervene before the balance shifts.",sp=0},{t="The Eye on Stonewatch",b="To pierce the defenses of Stonewatch Keep, Theocritus requires a second magical anchor point. He commands adventurers to scale the intact watch tower standing adjacent to the ruined fortress. There, among the garrison's clutter, an empty jar discarded by orcish sentries provides the perfect mundane hiding spot. Once the Glyph of Azora is affixed inside the vessel, Theocritus can telepathically sift through the minds within Stonewatch to uncover what drove Morganth and the Blackrocks apart.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="The quest is imparted by Theocritus, the Mage of Azora, speaking through the Old Lion Statue in the Redridge Mountains after you completed his prior task.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","old lion statue"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Theocritus spying on Stonewatch Keep?",a="Theocritus detected active hostility brewing between Morganth, the rogue dark wizard in the Tower of Ilgalar, and the Blackrock orcs occupying Stonewatch Keep. He wishes to discover what sparked their conflict.",al={"why spy on orcs","theocritus purpose","why stonewatch"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the container located?",a="The container is an empty jar resting atop barrels at the very summit of the intact watch tower standing right beside the main entrance of Stonewatch Keep.",al={"empty jar location","where to plant glyph","where is watch tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the Glyph of Azora do?",a="It serves as a magical scrying and divination focus, allowing Theocritus to remotely monitor the surrounding area and delve into the minds of the Blackrock orcs inside the keep.",al={"glyph of azora purpose","what does glyph do"},it="item"},{q="What follows after planting the glyph?",a="Once Theocritus divines the source of the conflict, he assigns you to hunt down Morganth himself in the Tower of Ilgalar and bring back his Pendant of Shadow.",al={"next quest","what happens next","looking further follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why use an empty jar?",a="A magical spy rune needs an inconspicuous vessel so guards do not spot or destroy it. The abandoned, foul-smelling liquor jar left forgotten on barrels makes an ideal hiding spot.",al={"why the jar","empty jar lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Who am I spying on at Stonewatch Keep?",a="You are spying on the Blackrock orcs who have seized Stonewatch Keep. From his vantage point, the mage Theocritus has detected strife brewing between these hostile orcs and the dark wizard Morganth over at the Tower of Ilgalar. Planting the glyph allows the mage to probe the minds within Stonewatch to uncover the true cause of this friction.",al={"who is in stonewatch keep","stonewatch keep target","looking further target"},it="target",add="3912e7be"},{q="Why does Theocritus need an adventurer to place the glyph?",a="Theocritus is tied to the Tower of Azora, channeling his magic through enchanted relics like the Old Lion Statue to monitor threats across Redridge. Stonewatch Keep is swarming with dangerous Blackrock orcs, and infiltrating the stronghold requires someone capable of fighting their way to the tower unseen rather than a solitary, vulnerable wizard leaving his post.",al={"why send me looking further","why doesn't theocritus do it","why me stonewatch"},it="why_me",add="6347ef38"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Theocritus relies on sophisticated long-range scrying magic through the Glyph of Azora, demonstrating how the mage of Azora establishes magical surveillance across hostile territories.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stonewatch Keep remains the primary stronghold of the Blackrock clan in Redridge. Gathering intelligence on their infighting with Morganth is vital to defending Lakeshire."},kw={"empty jar","glyph of azora","looking further","morganth","old lion statue","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","theocritus","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"quest:94","quest:249","quest:178","npc:theocritus","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Old Lion Statue",["end"]="An Empty Jar",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=248},src={"Looking Further"}}
E["quest:3103"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Letter",z="elwynn",s="The Hallowed Letter is a formal summons given to promising young priests by Marshal McBride on behalf of Northshire Abbey's resident trainer, Priestess Anetta. It marks the start of a fledgling priest's formal mentorship in the tenets of the Holy Light amidst a troubled and vulnerable world.",h="The Hallowed Letter is a formal summons given to promising young priests by Marshal McBride on behalf of...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Cloth",b="After proving their mettle against the kobold camps around Northshire, novitiate priests are handed a missive bearing the sacred seal of Priestess Anetta. Delivered through Marshal McBride, the letter serves as an invitation to begin serious study of the Holy Light within the abbey's quiet halls.",sp=0},{t="A World in Need",b="When presented with the letter, Priestess Anetta impresses upon her new pupil the grim state of the realm. Lingering threats from the Burning Legion cast long shadows across Azeroth, while the continents struggle with fresh wounds and unrest. In her eyes, taking up the mantle of a priest is not merely an academic devotion, but an urgent moral responsibility to bring healing and solace to a suffering world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Letter?",a="It is a sealed letter bearing the crest of Priestess Anetta, delivered to newly arrived human priests by Marshal McBride in Northshire Valley. It directs the novice to formalize their training inside Northshire Abbey.",al={"hallowed letter","priest intro quest northshire","anetta letter"}},{q="Who sends the Hallowed Letter?",a="Priestess Anetta, the priest trainer stationed inside Northshire Abbey, pens and seals the missive, asking Marshal McBride to hand it over once the initiate returns from scouting the kobold infestation.",al={"who wrote hallowed letter","who sent the letter"}},{q="Why does Priestess Anetta summon new priests?",a="Anetta recognizes the novice's calling to the Holy Light and seeks to guide their training. With perils like remnants of the Burning Legion lingering in the world, she stresses that disciplined healers and guides are urgently needed.",al={"why does anetta want me","purpose of the letter"}},{q="Where can Priestess Anetta be found?",a="She resides inside the main hall of Northshire Abbey, ready to train human priests as they master their first prayers and rituals.",al={"where is anetta","priestess anetta location"}},{q="What happens after presenting the letter to Priestess Anetta?",a="Upon reading the letter and greeting Anetta, she accepts the player as her student, imparting basic wisdom and inviting them to return for more training as they grow in experience.",al={"next quest after hallowed letter","what follows hallowed letter"}},{q="Why is the Burning Legion mentioned in Northshire?",a="Although the Third War ended, demonic remnants from the Legion still haunt Azeroth. Priestess Anetta mentions this global threat to emphasize the broader dangers awaiting any adventurer leaving the valley.",al={"burning legion northshire","why does anetta talk about demons"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest marks your official induction as a student of the Holy Light under Priestess Anetta, framing your divine magic as a vital duty to heal a fractured world.",["race:Human"]="Northshire Abbey has long been a sanctuary of faith and recuperation for the Kingdom of Stormwind, carrying on its traditions despite the encroaching troubles around Elwynn."},kw={"elwynn","hallowed letter","holy light","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey","priest","priestess anetta"},rel={"npc:priestess-anetta","subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:light","zone:elwynn","topic:burning-legion","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Priestess Anetta",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=3103},src={"Hallowed Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:3104"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Letter",z="elwynn",s="A sealed summons reaches novice human mages in Northshire Valley, sent by Marshal McBride. Khelden Bremen calls promising spellcasters to Northshire Abbey to begin their arcane tutelage.",h="A sealed summons reaches novice human mages in Northshire Valley, sent by Marshal McBride.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Arcane",b="Marshal McBride gives the rune-marked letter to an aspiring apprentice who has proved capable by helping him against local vermin. Khelden Bremen, Northshire's resident mage trainer, wrote it. He watches new recruits arriving at the abbey for signs of magical discipline and talent.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of Wizardry",b="Northshire Abbey has long been a sanctuary of the Holy Light, but Stormwind's dangers call for practitioners of every discipline. The letter brings you upstairs to Khelden Bremen. He offers no easy praise. Instead, he warns that mastering arcane power means defying natural limits, earning both profound respect and deep fear from ordinary folk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who delivers the Glyphic Letter?",a="Marshal McBride gives the letter to newly arrived mages outside Northshire Abbey after they help clear nearby kobold vermin.",al={"who gives glyphic letter","glyphic letter quest giver"}},{q="Who wrote the Glyphic Letter?",a="Khelden Bremen, the resident mage trainer in Northshire Abbey's upper chambers, wrote and sealed the letter.",al={"author of glyphic letter","who sent glyphic letter"}},{q="Where do I find Khelden Bremen?",a="Enter Northshire Abbey behind Marshal McBride, take the left hallway, then climb the stairs. Khelden waits in the rear chambers to teach.",al={"khelden bremen location","where is khelden"}},{q="Why is the mage trainer located in an abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a holy sanctuary, yet Stormwind uses the valley to train defenders in every discipline. Arcane tutors work there alongside clerics and marshals.",al={"why are mages in northshire abbey","mage trainer in holy abbey"}},{q="What happens after turning in the letter?",a="Khelden Bremen accepts you as his student, welcomes your resolve to wield the arcane despite its dangers, and offers direct access to basic spell training.",al={"what comes after glyphic letter","next quest after glyphic letter"}},{q="Why does Khelden warn that mages will be feared?",a="Arcane magic can bend reality and is volatile. Khelden warns that the pursuit of supreme knowledge crosses boundaries ordinary folk find deeply unsettling.",al={"why are mages feared","khelden bremen dialogue"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you begin your recognized apprenticeship in Stormwind's arcane arts under Khelden Bremen.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you carry Northshire's legacy of arcane magic, reaching back to Dalaran's first human arcanists and the Kirin Tor, into the Kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"arcane","elwynn forest","glyphic letter","khelden bremen","mage","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey"},rel={"npc:khelden-bremen","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Khelden Bremen",level="3",faction="Alliance",id=3104},src={"Glyphic Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:3105"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Letter",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire, Tainted Letter calls novice human warlocks away from the Abbey guards for instruction in the fel arts. Drusilla La Salle entrusts it to Marshal McBride, who delivers it to her recruits.",h="At Northshire, Tainted Letter calls novice human warlocks away from the Abbey guards for instruction in the...",sec={{t="A Discreet Summons",b="Novice warlocks receive a letter from Marshal McBride after proving themselves against the kobold menace. While priests and paladins study openly in Northshire Abbey, warlocks must tread carefully. Drusilla La Salle's insignia marks the letter, which directs each fledgling spellcaster to her secluded post outside the abbey's main walls before taking on other duties.",sp=0},{t="Temptation and Ambition",b="Drusilla warns that warlocks walk a precarious path under the watchful eyes of Stormwind's guards, whom she calls 'pathetic mundanes.' Drawing power from the Twisting Nether and communing with demons always risk corruption. She counsels patience, prudence, and firm self-control when handling those dark energies, but says caution must not extinguish a warlock's ambition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Tainted Letter?",a="Drusilla La Salle writes and seals the letter from her post just outside Northshire Abbey. She asks Marshal McBride to deliver it when you return from clearing the nearby kobold camps.",al={"who wrote tainted letter","tainted letter author","who gives the tainted letter"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride deliver a warlock letter?",a="Marshal McBride carries messages to promising recruits in the valley. He knows the letter bears Drusilla's seal and says it takes priority, while his main concern remains Northshire's defense and administration, not policing the defenders' magical practices.",al={"why does mcbride have it","does mcbride know what the letter is","mcbride warlock letter"}},{q="Where can I find Drusilla La Salle?",a="Drusilla La Salle waits outside Northshire Abbey's main entrance, near the outer walls and tents, away from the clerics inside.",al={"drusilla location","where is drusilla la salle","find drusilla"}},{q="Why are warlocks allowed in Northshire Abbey?",a="Warlocks in Alliance territory face heavy suspicion and keep a low profile. Drusilla trains recruits outdoors in Northshire, away from the sanctuary, to avoid direct confrontation with the Holy Order of Northshire clerics and paladins.",al={"warlocks in northshire","is fel magic legal in northshire","why allow warlocks"}},{q="What lesson does Drusilla teach upon receiving the letter?",a="Drusilla warns that drawing on the Twisting Nether risks corruption for any practitioner without discipline. She urges self-control and prudence, while insisting fear of corruption must not crush a warlock's ambition.",al={"drusilla's advice","what does drusilla say","lesson from tainted letter"}},{q="What comes after delivering the Tainted Letter?",a="Speaking with Drusilla completes the summons and makes her your trainer. She invites you to return as you grow more powerful to learn more of the warlock's ways.",al={"next quest after tainted letter","tainted letter follow up"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive formal instruction in Northshire while keeping out of the guards' judgment and learning to master dangerous nether magic.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you live in a culture that reveres the Holy Light and the Kirin Tor's disciplined arcane. Warlocks practice their summoning quietly on the fringes of settlements like Northshire."},kw={"corruption","drusilla la salle","elwynn forest","marshal mcbride","northshire abbey","tainted letter","twisting nether","warlock"},rel={"npc:drusilla-la-salle","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Drusilla La Salle",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=3105},src={"Tainted Letter (quest)"}}
E["quest:33"] = {t="quest",n="Wolves Across the Border",z="elwynn",s="Eagan Peltskinner asks you to hunt wolves prowling Northshire Valley and bring him their meat. He waits outside Northshire Abbey, where the valley’s needs continue despite the guards’ focus on Defias bandits.",h="Eagan Peltskinner asks you to hunt wolves prowling Northshire Valley and bring him their meat.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Request",b="Eagan Peltskinner waits by Northshire Abbey’s walls with a grudge against the local timber wolves. Marshal McBride and the Stormwind guards have limited strength to defend the abbey from Defias bandits, while tradesfolk still have daily needs. Eagan asks you to thin the wolves’ numbers and bring back their tough meat for his cooking.",sp=0},{t="Wilds of Northshire",b="Wolves roam closer to Northshire Abbey as patrols weaken. The Kingdom of Stormwind has too few troops and is strained by missing leadership. Young wolves and timber wolves now prowl the abbey’s paths and orchards. Hunting them supplies Eagan’s pantry and makes nearby trails safer for novitiates, laborers, and newly arrived defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Eagan Peltskinner is a hunter and tradesman near the entrance to Northshire Abbey. He dislikes the local timber wolves and is happy to cook and eat their meat.",al={"who is eagan","peltskinner","eagan peltskinner"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Eagan want wolf meat?",a="Eagan enjoys eating wolf steaks. He offers useful starter gear and coin to recruits who bring him fresh meat.",al={"why wolf meat","eagan hungry","what does eagan do with meat"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the wolves located?",a="Timber wolves and young wolves roam Northshire Valley’s fields, hills, and riverbanks, especially south and east of the abbey.",al={"where are the wolves","wolf locations","find wolves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are wolves a problem in Northshire?",a="Reduced patrols and Defias bandits have left Northshire’s roads and farms exposed to wildlife, making unescorted travel dangerous for clergy and workers.",al={"why wolves attacking","northshire wolf problem"},it="threat"},{q="Do I need to talk to anyone before taking this quest?",a="No. Deputy Willem may send newcomers to Eagan through an introductory errand, but Eagan offers the hunt directly to anyone who approaches him outside the abbey.",al={"quest prereqs","prerequisites","who gives this quest"},gp=true},{q="Is tough wolf meat used for cooking recipes?",a="Eagan plans to cook the meat himself. Novitiate cooks often learn that wolf meat gathered in Elwynn Forest is a basic ingredient for outdoor cooking.",al={"tough wolf meat cooking","can players cook wolf meat"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Tough Wolf Meat for?",a="Eagan Peltskinner intends to cook it up into wolf steaks for himself. Despite despising the beasts prowling the valley, he has developed a hearty appetite for their meat and gladly trades useful gear to anyone willing to supply his table.",al={"what is tough wolf meat for","why tough wolf meat","tough wolf meat use"},it="item",add="12d6ae41"},{q="Why are wolves roaming Northshire?",a="Young wolves and timber wolves naturally prowl the forested borders and open meadows of Northshire Valley. However, with local Stormwind guards preoccupied by the rising threat of the Defias Brotherhood, the predators roam closer to the abbey grounds unchecked.",al={"why are there wolves here","northshire timber wolves","wolves in northshire"},it="target",add="acd05579"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn a frontier truth from Eagan’s craving for wolf steak: what you hunt can often be cooked and eaten.",["race:Human"]="As a human recruit in Northshire, you find this among your first practical ways to help secure Stormwind’s nearby borders."},kw={"abbey","eagan","elwynn","meat","northshire","peltskinner","timber wolf","wolves"},rel={"quest:5261","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Eagan Peltskinner",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=33,ri={"Tough Wolf Meat"}},src={"Wolves Across the Border"}}
E["quest:35"] = {t="quest",n="Further Concerns",z="elwynn",s="Marshal Dughan sends an Alliance courier east from Goldshire to check reports of danger. You cross Elwynn Forest to speak with Guard Thomas, who watches the river crossing toward Redridge.",h="Marshal Dughan sends an Alliance courier east from Goldshire to check reports of danger.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Eastern Crossing",b="Rumors tell of hostile aquatic creatures creeping along Elwynn's riverbanks. Marshal Dughan commands the Goldshire garrison, where banditry and vermin already trouble the center of the forest. He will not dismiss the reports, but he cannot spare guards from town. Instead, he sends you east to consult Guard Thomas, the sentry at the bridge over the river toward Redridge.",sp=0},{t="A Frontier Stretched Thin",b="Guard Thomas has held the bridge outpost for more than a week and has seen what Goldshire's leaders only feared. Hostile, semi-intelligent murlocs have made camps along the waterways of eastern Elwynn. Stormwind's army is absent, while local garrisons protect town walls and supply lines. That leaves rural bridge posts like Thomas's isolated before the growing danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send me to Guard Thomas?",a="Marshal Dughan sends you to Guard Thomas because reports tell of murlocs creeping into the eastern waterways. Thomas has been stationed at the eastern Elwynn bridge for a week, so Dughan trusts him to confirm the threat.",al={"why guard thomas","dughan purpose","talk to thomas"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Guard Thomas stationed?",a="Guard Thomas watches the wooden bridge over the river in far eastern Elwynn Forest, on the road toward the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","eastern bridge guard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threat does Guard Thomas confirm?",a="Guard Thomas confirms that hostile, semi-intelligent murlocs have settled along eastern Elwynn's streams and waterways, threatening travelers and nearby farmsteads.",al={"murloc threat","what did thomas find","eastern river threat"},it="threat"},{q="How do you reach Guard Thomas?",a="Take the road east from Goldshire across Elwynn Forest to the bridge over the eastern river, where Guard Thomas keeps watch.",al={"fast travel to thomas","horse ride dughan","charger to bridge"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send an army to help eastern Elwynn?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin with King Varian Wrynn missing and resources diverted from the countryside. Sentries such as Guard Thomas are left largely to rely on passing adventurers.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why is elwynn undefended","stormwind military help"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after reporting to Guard Thomas?",a="After confirming the murloc presence, Guard Thomas asks you to investigate what became of the other sentries who patrolled the riverbank and failed to return.",al={"next quest after further concerns","thomas follow up","lost guards quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Marshal Dughan is stretched thin keeping Goldshire secure against Defias bandits and gnolls. With Stormwind denying additional troops and resources, the local garrison cannot spare soldiers for routine courier runs or distant scouting. Because you brought him the initial warning and showed concern for Elwynn's safety, he entrusts you with heading east to confer with Guard Thomas at the eastern bridge.",al={"why send me","why not use guards","why does dughan need me"},it="why_me",add="01d891f6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the thin defenses near the capital reveal growing operational cracks in the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Elwynn, you face murlocs whose spread threatens the breadbasket farms and the trade routes connecting Goldshire to Lakeshire."},kw={"eastern bridge","elwynn forest","further concerns","goldshire","guard thomas","marshal dughan","murloc"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","npc:guard-thomas","quest:40","quest:37","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:murloc"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=35},src={"Further Concerns"}}
E["quest:37"] = {t="quest",n="Find the Lost Guards",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas is waiting at Elwynn's eastern bridge for word of two missing guards. Rolf and Malakai were sent north along the river to watch for murlocs, but neither has returned.",h="Guard Thomas is waiting at Elwynn's eastern bridge for word of two missing guards.",sec={{t="A Patrol Vanished",b="Guard Thomas watches the eastern crossing of Elwynn Forest, where the King's road approaches Redridge. Murlocs have made the nearby waters more dangerous. Days ago, Thomas sent two Stormwind guards, Rolf and Malakai, north along the riverbanks to scout the threat and clear out nests. Neither has returned, and Thomas fears violence stopped their patrol.",sp=0},{t="Grim Discovery",b="Following the river north toward Stone Cairn Lake brings you into swarming murloc territory. At the water's edge, you find a half-eaten corpse in the mud. An engraved medallion beside the remains bears the name Footman Malakai Stone. It confirms Malakai's fate, but Rolf is still missing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gave this quest and where are they located?",a="Guard Thomas gave you this work. He is at the eastern border of Elwynn Forest, beside the bridge leading toward Redridge Mountains.",al={"quest giver","where is guard thomas","who starts find the lost guards"},gp=true},{q="Who are the missing guards?",a="The missing guards are Rolf and Malakai, two Stormwind city footmen sent by Guard Thomas to scout the riverbanks and watch for aggressive murlocs.",al={"missing guards elwynn","who are rolf and malakai","lost guards names"},it="people"},{q="Where are the remains found?",a="Footman Malakai Stone's half-eaten remains lie on the river's eastern bank, just north of Guard Thomas's post and near the edge of a murloc settlement.",al={"where is malakai corpse","half-eaten body location","lost guards location"},sp=1,it="place",gp=true},{q="What killed Malakai?",a="Local river murlocs overran Malakai and ate him. They infest the shores of eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"how did malakai die","who killed the guards"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What happened to Rolf?",a="You find Malakai's remains alone by the river. Rolf is still missing, and his fate remains unknown as you track deeper into the murloc camps.",al={"where is rolf","did rolf survive"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why were the guards sent out alone?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across several territories, so small garrisons like Guard Thomas's rely on patrols of two to watch the wilderness borders.",al={"why were they sent","stormwind guard shortage"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want you to find the lost guards?",a="Guard Thomas dispatched Rolf and Malakai north along the river days ago on an investigative patrol. They never reported back. As the officer overseeing this stretch of eastern Elwynn Forest, Thomas must account for his missing men to finish his official report for the Stormwind City Guard, whether that means bringing them home or confirming their deaths.",al={"why find lost guards","guard thomas motive","why look for rolf and malakai"},it="motive",add="5aa1fbbd"},{q="Why does Guard Thomas ask an adventurer instead of sending more guards?",a="Guard Thomas and his remaining men are stretched thin defending the bridges and borders of eastern Elwynn Forest from increasing murloc raids and gnoll incursions. With Stormwind's military spread across the kingdom and already missing two footmen, he cannot afford to pull more sentries off post to conduct a search party.",al={"why cant thomas find them","why ask me lost guards","why does thomas need help"},it="why_me",add="18be7cf7"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you can see how beast and murloc attacks threaten Elwynn's outer borders, even so close to Stormwind.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can honor fallen defenders by recovering their insignia and bringing justice to those guarding the kingdom's frontier."},kw={"elwynn forest","find the lost guards","guard thomas","half-eaten body","malakai","malakai stone","murlocs","rolf"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","quest:35","quest:45","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="A half-eaten body",faction="Alliance",id=37},src={"Find the Lost Guards"}}
E["quest:39"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver Thomas' Report",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, Guard Thomas sends word of two dead guards and rising danger. He asks you to carry the report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, where the garrison has few hands to spare.",h="In eastern Elwynn, Guard Thomas sends word of two dead guards and rising danger.",sec={{t="Bad Tidings from the East",b="Guard Thomas watches the bridges into eastern Elwynn, where river traffic meets the wilderness. Guards Malakai and Rolf have been killed by aggressive murloc tribes. With his remaining guards too few to contain them, Thomas sends you down the road to Goldshire with an urgent report.",sp=0},{t="A Garrison Stretched to the Brink",b="Marshal Dughan receives Thomas' report in Goldshire, already struggling to keep patrols on the roads. Kobolds infest the area, Defias bandits threaten travelers, and Stormwind City has sent no reinforcements. The deaths of two experienced guards add to his burden. Murlocs may soon threaten Goldshire itself, while the defenses across the region grow ever thinner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are Malakai and Rolf?",a="Malakai and Rolf were Stormwind guards stationed in eastern Elwynn under Guard Thomas. Murloc tribes overwhelmed and killed them while they patrolled near the rivers and lakes.",al={"malakai and rolf","who died","dead guards"},it="people"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas asking an adventurer to deliver the report?",a="Guard Thomas has too few troops to spare. If he leaves his post or sends one of his few surviving sentries, the eastern bridges will be left undefended.",al={"why guard thomas needs help","why courier","cant thomas send a guard"},it="why_me"},{q="What threat do the murlocs pose to Goldshire?",a="The murloc tribes along the eastern rivers are spreading west. Marshal Dughan fears they may reach Goldshire's outskirts within the week, and he has too few guards to hold the perimeter.",al={"murloc threat","will murlocs attack goldshire","how bad are murlocs"},it="threat"},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind City send reinforcements to Elwynn?",a="Stormwind's military resources are stretched across several fronts, and the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn has left the capital politically paralyzed. Outlying settlements and frontier bridges are largely left to local town watches and hired adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are the troops","why are defenses thin"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Marshal Dughan reads the report?",a="Marshal Dughan knows his garrison lacks the strength to stop the murlocs directly. He turns to securing supplies and armor for those willing to hold the line.",al={"next quest","what does dughan do","chain after report"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Guard Thomas stationed?",a="Guard Thomas is stationed in eastern Elwynn Forest, guarding the bridges over the rivers between the heart of the forest and the wilder borders near the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas location","where is thomas","thomas location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want his report delivered to Marshal Dughan?",a="Guard Thomas cannot contain the murlocs spreading across eastern Elwynn with the handful of men stationed at the river bridges. Having just confirmed the deaths of his guardsmen, Rolf and Malakai, he urgently needs Marshal Dughan to understand that the eastern border is collapsing. Without reinforcements or aid organized from Goldshire, the murloc incursions will sweep unchecked into the heart of the forest.",al={"why send the report","guard thomas report motive","why report to dughan"},it="motive",add="a496bd3c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Carrying Thomas' report shows how vulnerable the Alliance's central kingdom has become, with even roads outside the capital slipping from garrison control.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior serving the realm, you see the cost of frontier duty in the deaths of Malakai and Rolf, killed by relentless foes.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you feel these losses in your homeland, where too few defenders face more hostile incursions."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","guard thomas","malakai","marshal dughan","murlocs","report","rolf"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:71","quest:59","subzone:goldshire","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=39},src={"Deliver Thomas' Report"}}
E["quest:3903"] = {t="quest",n="Milly Osworth",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Deputy Willem sends you to help Milly Osworth. Her wagon and livelihood are in jeopardy, and she needs help across the abbey grounds. The work takes you from defending the abbey to aiding Elwynn Forest's civilians.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Deputy Willem sends you to help Milly Osworth.",sec={{t="A Dependable Pair of Hands",b="After you prove your mettle against the Defias thieves encroaching on Northshire Valley, Deputy Willem recognizes you as capable and willing to help. He sends you to assist his friend Milly Osworth. This favor is personal, outside the abbey's official guard duties, and Milly is a civilian caught in the valley's growing unrest.",sp=0},{t="Trouble by the Stables",b="Milly waits beside her wagon on the far side of Northshire Abbey, near the stables. Deputy Willem must stay at his post to defend the abbey. Milly's troubles lie out in the valley, where the stretched guard garrison has too few hands to help her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Milly Osworth?",a="Deputy Willem sends you to speak with Milly after you prove reliable by dealing with the Defias bandits.",al={"who gives milly osworth","quest giver milly osworth","where to get milly osworth quest"}},{q="Where can Milly Osworth be found?",a="Milly waits beside her wagon on the far side of Northshire Abbey, near the stables and the vineyards to the southeast.",al={"milly osworth location","where is milly","where is milly osworth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't Deputy Willem help Milly himself?",a="Willem's guard duties keep him at Northshire Abbey. With bandits and vermin pressing the valley, the garrison has too few hands for private civilian troubles.",al={"why doesnt willem help","willem duties","why help milly"},it="why_me"},{q="What prerequisites are needed for this quest?",a="You need to complete Brotherhood of Thieves for Deputy Willem before he trusts you to help Milly.",al={"milly osworth requirements","brotherhood of thieves follow up","how to unlock milly osworth quest"},gp=true},{q="What does Milly need help with?",a="Milly is struggling with her crop and wagon amid the local turmoil. Her harvest needs securing from the surrounding valley.",al={"what does milly want","milly problem","milly harvest troubles"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Milly Osworth to Deputy Willem?",a="Willem calls Milly a friend in need from the Northshire community, someone he looks out for while bound to his post.",al={"willem and milly","is milly related to willem","how does willem know milly"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want to help Milly Osworth?",a="Deputy Willem considers Milly a dear personal friend and knows she has run into trouble near the stables. While he cares deeply about her well-being, his official post as deputy keeps him tethered to Northshire Abbey. Sending a capable, trustworthy adventurer like you is his best way to ensure she gets the protection and help she desperately needs.",al={"why help milly osworth","willem motive milly","why does deputy willem care"},it="motive",add="c87a8d77"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="In Northshire, you see how stretched Alliance guards rely on passing adventurers to protect local townspeople from emerging threats.",["race:Human"]="As a young human in Northshire, you can help Willem and show the community spirit that helps hold Elwynn together."},kw={"deputy willem","elwynn forest","harvest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","stables","wagon"},rel={"npc:willem","quest:18","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Deputy Willem",["end"]="Milly Osworth",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3903},src={"Milly Osworth (quest)"}}
E["quest:3904"] = {t="quest",n="Milly's Harvest",z="elwynn",s="Defias brigands have driven Milly Osworth from the Northshire vineyards. Her harvest lies scattered in buckets and crates among the occupied rows, where it may be stolen or crushed.",h="Defias brigands have driven Milly Osworth from the Northshire vineyards.",sec={{t="A Crop Left Behind",b="Milly Osworth fled the southeastern fields of Northshire Valley when Defias brigands swarmed the vines. She left her gathered grapes behind in buckets and crates among the occupied rows. Northshire's garrison is stretched thin, and Milly fears that boots and fighting will crush any fruit the bandits leave behind.",sp=0},{t="Northshire Under Pressure",b="Defias bandits now occupy working vineyards, a sign of how little safety Northshire can offer. Stormwind's attention is elsewhere, and the valley has too few guards. Farmers like Milly must depend on recruits and wanderers to protect their property and secure the food and wine that supply the abbey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Milly Osworth?",a="Milly Osworth farms the Northshire Vineyards. She tends and harvests the valley's grapes, but the arriving Defias Brotherhood drove her from her fields.",al={"milly osworth","who is milly","grape lady"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't the Northshire guards retrieve the harvest?",a="Northshire Valley's guards are too few and occupied with the widespread bandit threat and kobold infestations. Milly also fears that a military sweep could trample her grapes into the mud.",al={"why don't guards help","northshire guards","lazy guards"},it="why_me"},{q="What are the Defias doing in the vineyards?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has entered Northshire Valley to disrupt regional production, harass the local people, and seize resources under Stormwind's guards' noses.",al={"why defias in vineyards","defias grapes","defias northshire"},it="target"},{q="Where are the crates located?",a="The harvest buckets and crates are scattered across the ground in the Northshire Vineyards, just southeast of Northshire Abbey, among Defias brigands patrolling the rows.",al={"crate locations","where to find grapes","where is harvest"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Milly gets her grapes back?",a="After her harvest is safe, Milly asks you to bring her Grape Manifest to Brother Neals inside Northshire Abbey, so the yield can be accounted for and processed into wine.",al={"next quest","after milly's harvest","what next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are grapes important to Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Valley produces famous wine and supplies the clerical community at the abbey. Milly's crop sustains local trade and the cellars maintained by the Brotherhood of Northshire.",al={"northshire wine","why grapes matter"},it="item"},{q="Why does Milly Osworth need you to retrieve her harvest?",a="Milly was in the middle of picking grapes when the Defias gang overran the vineyards. She fears that if the thieves do not make off with the fruit, the Abbey's guards will inevitably trample the crates in the chaos of battle. Her livelihood depends on recovering those buckets before they are ruined.",al={"why does milly need the harvest","why save the grapes","milly osworth motive"},it="motive",add="23083d02"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering Milly's crop gives young Alliance recruits a first look at the Defias threat only miles from Stormwind City.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your journey in Northshire, protecting smallholder farmers like Milly is part of defending Elwynn's working folk."},kw={"crates","defias","elwynn forest","grapes","milly osworth","milly's harvest","northshire abbey","northshire vineyards"},rel={"quest:3903","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Milly Osworth",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3904,ri={"Milly's Harvest"}},src={"Milly's Harvest (quest)"}}
E["quest:3905"] = {t="quest",n="Grape Manifest",z="elwynn",s="Milly Osworth records her rescued grape harvest for Northshire Abbey. She writes a manifest of the yield recovered from Defias thieves, then sends it to Brother Neals so the brotherhood can replenish its wine stores.",h="Milly Osworth records her rescued grape harvest for Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="The Valley's Vintage",b="Northshire Valley's soil and orchards have long supported local food and the abbey's wine. When thieves and bandits seized the eastern fields, they cut off the abbey's supply of grapes and food. With the harvest recovered from the occupied fields, Milly Osworth records the yield in a manifest.",sp=0},{t="A Tipple in the Belfry",b="Brother Neals oversees food and drink at Northshire Abbey. He is known for sampling Northshire's vintages in the quiet of the bell tower. Brigands still threaten the gates, but fresh grapes give the brotherhood a moment to toast the Light and take heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grape Manifest?",a="Milly Osworth writes the Grape Manifest to record her harvest recovered from Defias thieves. The ledger lets the abbey's quartermaster restock its cellars.",al={"grape manifest item","what is manifest","millys manifest"},it="item"},{q="Who is Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals is a monk at Northshire Abbey who oversees its food and drink. He often samples the vintages in the bell tower.",al={"brother neals","who is neals","monk in bell tower"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Brother Neals?",a="Brother Neals is inside Northshire Abbey, in the bell tower overlooking the grounds.",al={"neals location","where is brother neals","find brother neals"},gp=true},{q="Why is Northshire's grape crop so important?",a="Northshire's grapes provide celebrated wine and fresh food for the local clergy and soldiers. A lost harvest threatens daily stores and the abbey's sacramental wine across Elwynn.",al={"why grapes matter","northshire wine lore","milly harvest significance"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was threatening Milly's harvest?",a="Defias brigands occupied Northshire Valley's eastern fields, drove Milly Osworth out, and hid her boxed harvest throughout the vineyards. They were driven back by adventurers.",al={"who stole the grapes","grape thieves","bandits in vineyards"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after giving Brother Neals the manifest?",a="Brother Neals gives his blessings in the name of the Light. He is overjoyed that the abbey's cellars will have fresh wine despite the bandit troubles across the valley.",al={"quest aftermath","does neals make wine","what follows grape manifest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Milly Osworth want this done?",a="With her crop finally saved from the Defias bandits who overran her vineyards, Milly needs Northshire Abbey to know fresh supplies have survived. Brother Neals oversees all the food and drink for the valley, and this manifest officially documents that her grapes are ready for the abbey's wine cellars.",al={"milly osworth grape manifest motive","why send grape manifest","why does milly need this delivered"},it="motive",add="7b371529"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Northshire's food stores helps Stormwind's main place of recruitment and recovery remain self-sufficient.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your journey, helping Milly and Brother Neals protects one of the kingdom's cherished pastoral traditions.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know wine has a place in both hospitality and sacramental rites at Northshire Abbey, where farming sustains the brotherhood's worship."},kw={"brother neals","defias","elwynn","grape manifest","harvest","milly osworth","northshire abbey","vineyard","wine"},rel={"npc:brother-neals","quest:3903","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},m={start="Milly Osworth",["end"]="Brother Neals",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=3905},src={"Grape Manifest (quest)"}}
E["quest:40"] = {t="quest",n="A Fishy Peril",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, A Fishy Peril begins with reports of murlocs moving inland through the waterways. Remy \"Two Times\" asks travelers to alert Marshal Dughan, whose guards are already stretched thin.",h="In Goldshire, A Fishy Peril begins with reports of murlocs moving inland through the waterways.",sec={{t="A Plea from the East",b="Remy \"Two Times\" grows uneasy over a new threat while seeking business in Goldshire. Murlocs are creeping up the streams and into inland shallows, disrupting fishing and menacing innocent travelers. Remy fears the local guard is overlooking a danger that is still growing, so he asks passersby to carry word to the heart of the township.",sp=0},{t="A Strained Garrison",b="Marshal Dughan hears the report in Goldshire but remains skeptical. He is charged with protecting the realm while royal forces are stretched thin elsewhere, and Riverpaw gnolls and Defias highwaymen already demand his attention. With no confirmed military intelligence, he will not divert his scarce men to pursue rumors of fish-men in the eastern streams.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Fishy Peril?",a="Remy \"Two Times\", a merchant from Redridge, gives the dispatch in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"quest giver a fishy peril","who starts a fishy peril","remy quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="Why is Remy \"Two Times\" worried about murlocs?",a="Remy has seen murlocs swimming up the rivers of eastern Elwynn, driving away local fish and attacking travelers along the waterways.",al={"why remy scared","murloc problem elwynn","fishy peril lore"},it="motive"},{q="Why won't Marshal Dughan send troops immediately?",a="Marshal Dughan considers the reports unverified. His garrison is occupied by gnoll attacks and organized banditry, and he cannot commit soldiers without formal scout reports.",al={"why dughan ignores murlocs","marshal dughan response","why no troops east"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Marshal Dughan follows up with Further Concerns, seeking reliable confirmation from scouts before committing royal resources to the east.",al={"what comes after a fishy peril","next quest after fishy peril","further concerns quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where does the player turn in A Fishy Peril?",a="You deliver the report to Marshal Dughan just outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"where turn in fishy peril","fishy peril turn in","dughan location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What larger threat are the murlocs part of in Elwynn?",a="Murlocs appear primitive and erratic, yet their spread into inland lakes such as Stonecairn Lake and Crystal Lake threatens rural trade and agriculture alongside gnoll and bandit attacks.",al={"murlocs in elwynn","are murlocs dangerous elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Remy send an adventurer instead of talking to Marshal Dughan himself?",a="Remy has already warned Marshal Dughan directly, but the marshal dismissed his warnings as merchant rumors. With Dughan focused entirely on the gnoll incursions and Defias bandits, Remy needs an outside voice—an independent adventurer—to emphasize the danger and convince the garrison to send troops east.",al={"why me a fishy peril","why cant remy talk to dughan","why does remy need me"},it="why_me",add="3afc8cff"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this dispatch shows the strain on Stormwind's home guard and the township's reliance on independent adventurers to investigate rumors.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see eastern waterways close to home turn into dangerous hunting grounds for aquatic beasts."},kw={"a fishy peril","elwynn forest","further concerns","goldshire","marshal dughan","murloc","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:35","topic:murloc","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Remy \"Two Times\"",["end"]="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=40},src={"A Fishy Peril"}}
E["quest:45"] = {t="quest",n="Discover Rolf's Fate",z="elwynn",s="In eastern Elwynn, two Stormwind guards are missing near Stone Cairn Lake. Malakai's half-eaten remains and webbed tracks lead toward a murloc village, where the search for Rolf continues.",h="In eastern Elwynn, two Stormwind guards are missing near Stone Cairn Lake.",sec={{t="A Trail of Webbed Tracks",b="Guard Thomas sent patrols around eastern Elwynn Forest as threats grew, but Malakai and Rolf vanished near Stone Cairn Lake. Malakai's half-eaten remains lie by the shore. Webbed footprints pressed into the mud lead east along the water's edge, straight to a ramshackle murloc camp.",sp=0},{t="The End of Patrol",b="You follow the tracks into the heart of the coastal murloc settlement. Another corpse lies there, stripped by the creatures. An inscribed medallion hangs around the fallen soldier's neck: Footman Rolf Hartford. Neither guard survived the ambush.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Rolf?",a="Rolf Hartford was a Stormwind footman assigned to patrol eastern Elwynn Forest under Guard Thomas, alongside Guard Malakai. Murlocs overwhelmed and killed both guards near Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"who is rolf","footman rolf","rolf hartford"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where is Rolf's body located?",a="Rolf's corpse lies farther east along the southern shore of Stone Cairn Lake, inside a murloc village near the lake's border.",al={"rolf location","where is rolf","find rolf"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Why were the guards out near Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Guard Thomas stationed guards along eastern Elwynn's rivers and lakes to monitor incursions from murlocs and gnolls. The understaffed patrols were vulnerable to sudden, coordinated attacks.",al={"why were guards lost","what were guards doing","guard patrol elwynn"},it="why_here"},{q="How do you confirm the corpse belongs to Rolf?",a="A metal medallion hangs around the torn corpse's neck, inscribed with the name Footman Rolf Hartford.",al={"rolf medallion","identifying rolf"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What happens after finding Rolf?",a="With the fates of Malakai and Rolf confirmed, you are tasked with returning west to the bridge at Eastvale Logging Camp to report the grim news to Guard Thomas.",al={"next quest after rolf","what to do after rolf"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the murlocs in Stone Cairn Lake an unusual threat?",a="Murloc activity in Elwynn has grown unusually aggressive and coordinated. Murlocs are pushing inland into Stone Cairn Lake and the rivers, threatening local trade and lone patrols alike.",al={"murloc threat elwynn","why murlocs attacking"},it="threat"},{q="Why investigate the half-eaten body further?",a="The half-eaten body by the river belongs to Malakai Stone, but his patrol partner Rolf remains unaccounted for. Webbed tracks leading away from the carnage offer the only clue to Rolf's whereabouts, compelling you to press forward and determine whether he managed to escape or met a grim demise deeper within murloc territory.",al={"why search for rolf","half eaten body motive","why look for signs of rolf"},it="motive",add="51025c24"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding Rolf reveals how exposed Stormwind's rural borders are, with garrison shortages leaving basic patrols open to deadly wild attacks.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see in Rolf Hartford's body the bloody reality faced by footmen serving the realm."},kw={"elwynn forest","guard thomas","malakai","murlocs","rolf","rolf hartford","stone cairn lake"},rel={"quest:37","quest:71","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn"},m={start="A half-eaten body",["end"]="Rolf's corpse",faction="Alliance",id=45},src={"Discover Rolf's Fate"}}
E["quest:46"] = {t="quest",n="Bounty on Murlocs",z="elwynn",s="Murlocs are spreading through eastern Elwynn, and the Stormwind Army has put a bounty on them. With the garrison stretched thin, Guard Thomas turns to travelers to clear the shoreline camps around Stone Cairn Lake and the southern waterways before the murlocs overrun nearby farms and roads.",h="Murlocs are spreading through eastern Elwynn, and the Stormwind Army has put a bounty on them.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Waterways",b="Murlocs have made shoreline camps around Stone Cairn Lake and along the fork of the southern streams. Lurkers and foragers now attack travelers and press toward human settlements. What began as a minor nuisance has grown into a threat across eastern Elwynn, while the western roads remain comparatively secure.",sp=0},{t="Stretched Defenses",b="Guard Thomas is stationed at the eastern bridge beside the Redridge Mountains, where dangers beyond the bridge and disorder at home compete for his attention. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and Stormwind's military command is mired in bureaucracy. Town garrisons rarely get the reinforcements they request. Marshal Dughan and local officers have turned to public bounties, offering coin for murloc fins to slow the attacks along the waterways.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a bounty on murlocs in Elwynn?",a="Murlocs have established growing camps around Stone Cairn Lake and the southern streams of eastern Elwynn. Their foraging parties threaten nearby farms, roads, and travelers, so the Stormwind Army pays travelers to cull their numbers.",al={"why kill murlocs","murloc bounty reason","why bounty on murlocs"},it="motive"},{q="Who is paying for the bounty?",a="The Stormwind Army funds the bounty through Goldshire's command under Marshal Dughan. Guard Thomas is the field contact at the eastern river crossing who pays travelers.",al={"who rewards this quest","who pays the bounty","stormwind army bounty"}},{q="Where are the murloc settlements located?",a="Murloc camps line the shores and islands of Stone Cairn Lake to the north, and the riverbanks to the south where the eastern stream forks.",al={"murloc locations elwynn","where are elwynn murlocs","stone cairn lake murlocs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't the Stormwind guards handle this themselves?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the kingdom by political strife, missing leadership, and banditry. Outposts like Guard Thomas's bridge have only a handful of men, too few to sustain attacks on the shoreline tribes.",al={"why guard thomas needs help","why aren't guards fighting murlocs","guard shortage elwynn"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof of the cull does Guard Thomas require?",a="Guard Thomas asks for torn fins taken from the lurkers and foragers in Elwynn's eastern waterways.",al={"what drops torn murloc fins","quest proof","murloc fins"},it="item"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan know about the severity of the murloc problem?",a="Yes. Guard Thomas says Marshal Dughan is anxious about the murloc threat across eastern Elwynn, so reports of cleared camps matter to local morale.",al={"marshal dughan murlocs","is goldshire aware","dughan reaction"}},{q="What are the murlocs doing in eastern Elwynn?",a="Murloc lurkers and foragers have pushed deep into eastern Elwynn Forest, setting up hostile settlements around Stone Cairn Lake to the north and along the southern river forks. These primitive, aggressive amphibians attack travelers and encroach on farmlands, turning eastern waterways into hazardous ground that the Stormwind Army must actively push back.",al={"why are murlocs in elwynn","murloc threat elwynn","murloc lurkers and foragers"},it="target",add="d8a52c2e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the waterways protects supply lines and rural homes between Goldshire and the Redridge border.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how thin Stormwind's protection has grown just beyond the capital's heartland.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find marshy shores and reed-lined banks around Stone Cairn Lake suited to stalking nimble aquatic predators that move in swarms."},kw={"bounty","elwynn","fins","foragers","guard thomas","lurkers","marshal dughan","murlocs","stone cairn lake"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army","topic:murloc","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Guard Thomas",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=46,ri={"Torn Murloc Fin"}},src={"Bounty on Murlocs"}}
E["quest:47"] = {t="quest",n="Gold Dust Exchange",z="elwynn",s="At Goldshire's crossroads, Gold Dust Exchange brings Remy \"Two Times\" coin for gold dust from kobolds in Elwynn's mines. Travelers gather the dust and trade it to the nervous broker for pay.",h="At Goldshire's crossroads, Gold Dust Exchange brings Remy \"Two Times\" coin for gold dust from kobolds in...",sec={{t="A Town of Pockets and Picks",b="Goldshire sits where Elwynn Forest's roads meet, and travelers, merchants, and guards pass through town. Remy \"Two Times\" is a shady broker with a habit of repeating his words and a sharp eye for profit. Instead of paying mining crews to dig for raw minerals, he turns to travelers passing through the Lion's Pride Inn. He offers coin for gold dust taken from the kobolds in the region.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Plunder",b="Kobolds have overrun Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the northeast. These rat-like tunnelers chip through the dark for candles and shiny baubles, gathering flecks of unrefined ore in their pouches. Pushing them back serves the kingdom, and gathering their dust turns the work into a trade for coin.",sp=0},{t="Shadows Behind the Counter",b="Remy says he pays well for ordinary trade, but each payment carries a warning. When he receives the dust, he gives his helpers a small token for his \"associates.\" With bandits, unpaid stonemasons, and hidden networks active in the shadows of Stormwind, Remy's quiet brokers may have plans for the gold beyond village commerce.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a shady local broker outside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He repeats the ends of his sentences, buys precious materials from travelers, and keeps ties with shadowy associates.",al={"remy two times","who gives gold dust exchange","remy in goldshire"},it="identity"},{q="Where do kobolds get gold dust?",a="Kobolds spend their lives tunneling through Elwynn's mineral veins, including those in Fargodeep and Jasperlode. As they dig through rock for treasure and candle wax, raw gold flakes and dust gather in their pockets and pouches.",al={"why do kobolds have gold dust","where does gold dust come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where can I find the mines mentioned by Remy?",a="Kobolds carrying gold dust are found mainly within and around Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire, and Jasperlode Mine, northeast near the border toward the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"where are the mines","where to find kobolds elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormwind allow kobolds to control their mines?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and the House of Nobles refusing troops for the outskirts, the Stormwind City Guard is stretched thin. Local garrisons cannot clear the mines, leaving kobolds there while independent travelers fight them.",al={"why aren't the mines guarded","why did stormwind lose the mines"},it="conflict"},{q="Is gold dust used for blacksmithing or trade?",a="In the kobolds' raw gold dust, the particles are too fine and impure for ordinary forge work. Brokers like Remy take it as a raw commodity, consolidate it, then refine it through their own private channels.",al={"what is gold dust used for","can you smelt gold dust"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does Remy \"Two Times\" want gold dust?",a="Remy operates as a shrewd local opportunist buying up valuable resources on the cheap. Rather than braving the dangerous kobold-infested tunnels himself, he relies on adventurous travelers to extract the raw gold dust from the vermin. He turns a quick profit trading in precious metals and uses the dealings to reward you with coin and connections to his associates.",al={"why does remy want gold dust","remy two times motive","why gold dust remy"},it="motive",add="9de6b9cb"},{q="Why does Remy need you instead of getting the gold dust himself?",a="Remy is a merchant and hustler, not a frontline fighter, and he clearly prefers staying safe within Goldshire rather than delving into dark mine shafts. Meanwhile, the local Stormwind garrison is already stretched thin dealing with rampant bandits, gnolls, and the broader kobold problem, leaving little interest or manpower for collecting scattered mineral dust. That makes independent mercenaries like you the ideal solution.",al={"why doesnt remy get gold dust","why does remy need me","why not the stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="3c82823a"},{q="Why are kobolds in the Elwynn mines carrying gold dust?",a="Kobolds are natural burrowers who have overrun abandoned and lightly defended mines across Elwynn, including Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine. Driven by an obsessive urge to dig and hoard shiny trinkets, they chip away at the subterranean veins day and night. The loose gold dust accumulates on their paws, clothes, and pouches as they scramble through the shafts.",al={"why are kobolds in the mines","why do kobolds have gold dust","kobolds fargodeep mine"},it="target",add="27e84318"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners searching Fargodeep and Jasperlode find kobolds clinging to the richest copper veins, so clearing them out is necessary to harvest ore.",["class:Rogue"]="Remy's hushed manner and token from unnamed \"associates\" point to underground syndicates beneath Goldshire's placid surface.",["faction:Alliance"]="Elwynn's vital gold and mineral deposits lie in the hands of feral kobolds rather than royal excavators, showing how depleted the kingdom's military forces are."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode mine","kobold","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","topic:kobold","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","quest:62","quest:76","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Remy \"Two Times\"",faction="Alliance",id=47,ri={"Gold Dust"}},src={"Gold Dust Exchange"}}
E["quest:52"] = {t="quest",n="Protect the Frontier",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn's eastern bridge as predators threaten the frontier. Stormwind's forces are thin here, and wolves and bears have grown bold near the Eastvale Logging Camp. He asks capable adventurers to cull the beasts threatening travelers and workers.",h="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn's eastern bridge as predators threaten the frontier.",sec={{t="A Thinning Defense",b="Guard Thomas watches the bridge over the river at Elwynn Forest's eastern edge. Goldshire and the Northshire Valley have a visible Stormwind garrison, but this frontier receives far less protection. With Stormwind's forces stretched across the realm, Thomas is one of few sentries between the settled heartlands and the wilderness. Travelers help keep vital supply roads open.",sp=0},{t="The Predatory Threat",b="Eastvale Logging Camp supplies timber to Stormwind City, but woodsmen felling trees at the forest's edge meet dangerous wildlife. Prowlers, gray forest wolves, and young forest bears now roam near roads and lumber yards. Culling them eases the danger to local workers for a time. Thomas suspects a disturbance deeper in the woods is driving the beasts toward settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Protect the Frontier?",a="Guard Thomas gives the order. He watches the eastern bridge on Elwynn Forest's main road, between the forest interior and the Eastvale region.",al={"quest giver protect the frontier","who starts protect the frontier","guard thomas quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are wolves and bears attacking the frontier?",a="Wolves and bears are pressing near roads and work sites around Eastvale Logging Camp. Thomas suspects something deeper in the wilderness is agitating them and driving them toward settled ground.",al={"why are bears aggressive","why are wolves attacking eastvale","animal attacks elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, just east of Guard Thomas's bridge. It supplies vital lumber to Stormwind and border settlements.",al={"eastvale location","where is logging camp elwynn","eastvale camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Guard Thomas watching the bridge alone?",a="Stormwind's army and city guard are stretched thin across the kingdom. River and crossroads outposts often have only one or two guards watching the highways, so they rely on travelers to handle large wildlife threats.",al={"why is guard thomas alone","guard thomas post","stormwind guards eastvale"},it="why_me"},{q="What animals need to be culled for this task?",a="You need to slay eight wolves, either prowlers or gray forest wolves, and five young forest bears roaming eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"protect the frontier targets","wolves and bears to kill","what mobs for protect the frontier"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens once the wildlife is culled?",a="When you report back, Guard Thomas thanks you, and logging caravans can travel more safely. He remains wary that the dark influence that stirred the beasts may bring further trouble to the forest.",al={"protect the frontier follow up","turn in protect the frontier"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Guard Thomas want the wild beasts culled?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp is under constant assault from increasingly aggressive wolves and bears prowling eastern Elwynn Forest. Guard Thomas is stationed at the eastern bridge to protect workers and travelers along the road, but the predators are bold enough to disrupt vital logging operations and threaten anyone stepping beyond the camp perimeter.",al={"why cull wolves guard thomas","protect the frontier why","why protect eastvale"},it="motive",add="ad29ae35"},{q="What animals are you sent against in Protect the Frontier?",a="You are sent to cull the prowlers, gray forest wolves, and young forest bears roaming the woods surrounding the Eastvale Logging Camp. Typically timid wildlife in western Elwynn has turned unusually vicious and bold here on the frontier, making everyday travel and lumber work perilous.",al={"what wolves and bears protect the frontier","protect the frontier beasts","which animals guard thomas"},it="target",add="ce43057a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the eastern roads secure helps Eastvale's lumber reach Alliance lands, where it supports reconstruction and defense.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your tracking and marksmanship against the wolves and bears stalking eastern Elwynn Forest."},kw={"eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","gray forest wolf","guard thomas","protect the frontier","prowler","young forest bear"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=52},src={"Protect the Frontier"}}
E["quest:5261"] = {t="quest",n="Eagan Peltskinner",z="elwynn",s="Outside Northshire Abbey, Eagan Peltskinner has work for recruits as timber wolves threaten the valley. The local furrier needs hunters to thin the packs and bring back pelts.",h="Outside Northshire Abbey, Eagan Peltskinner has work for recruits as timber wolves threaten the valley.",sec={{t="A Word with the Furrier",b="Deputy Willem often sends recruits from the abbey to find Eagan Peltskinner, who works nearby on its grounds. Northshire Valley's orchards and fields lie beside wild woods where timber wolves prowl. Eagan wants newcomers to hunt the aggressive packs and gather pelts for his craft.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Perimeter",b="Timber wolves threaten workers, acolytes, and supplies moving in and out of Northshire. Sending young champions to Eagan helps keep nearby paths safe while sparing Stormwind's few remaining guards. They are already occupied by rising tensions across Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Deputy Willem, outside Northshire Abbey's entrance, directs promising recruits to Eagan after introducing the valley's security concerns.",al={"who gives this quest","who starts eagan peltskinner quest"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Eagan Peltskinner located?",a="Eagan Peltskinner works near Northshire Abbey's outer walls, around the left side of the main building, among his drying racks and gear.",al={"where is eagan","eagan peltskinner location","find eagan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Eagan Peltskinner need help with?",a="Eagan needs a hunter to kill the aggressive timber wolves in the surrounding woods and bring back their pelts, clearing Northshire's perimeter.",al={"what does eagan want","why hunt wolves","eagan purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Can you skip this quest and talk to Eagan directly?",a="Yes. Eagan offers his hunting work directly to anyone who approaches him. Speaking with him first simply means you miss Deputy Willem's introduction.",al={"can i skip eagan quest","wolves across the border directly"},gp=true},{q="Why are there so many wolves in Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Valley borders dense, untamed woodlands where timber wolves roam freely. Local guards are stretched thin by other threats across the kingdom, leaving the predators unchecked.",al={"why wolves in northshire","wolf problem elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="What task follows speaking with Eagan Peltskinner?",a="After you speak with Eagan, he asks you to hunt timber wolves beyond the abbey grounds and collect their tough pelts.",al={"next quest after eagan","what does eagan offer next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem send you to Eagan Peltskinner?",a="Deputy Willem is tasked with maintaining security around Northshire Abbey. With wolf sightings surging across the valley, a hunter requesting help culling the pack is a welcome opportunity. Willem directs willing recruits to Eagan so the abbey's limited guards can focus on larger concerns while still curbing the predators encroaching on the settlement.",al={"why willem sends you to eagan","willem motive eagan peltskinner","why visit eagan"},it="motive",add="b90d340a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every small task in Northshire helps secure Stormwind's home territory while the kingdom's core army remains stretched thin elsewhere.",["race:Human"]="As a young human leaving Northshire Abbey, helping local tradesfolk like Eagan is your first lesson in defending your homeland."},kw={"deputy willem","eagan peltskinner","northshire abbey","northshire valley","timber wolves","wolves across the border"},rel={"quest:783","quest:33","subzone:northshire-valley","zone:elwynn"},m={level="2",faction="Alliance",id=5261},src={"Eagan Peltskinner (quest)"}}
E["quest:5545"] = {t="quest",n="A Bundle of Trouble",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, A Bundle of Trouble begins with timber left in the woods and a deadline near. Supervisor Raelen needs the cut wood brought back before the shipment falls behind.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, A Bundle of Trouble begins with timber left in the woods and a deadline near.",sec={{t="A Looming Deadline",b="Supervisor Raelen has a shipment of timber due soon. Eastvale Logging Camp cuts wood for Stormwind, and her crew has fallen behind schedule. With the deadline close, Raelen needs the timber sent on its way.",sp=0},{t="Predators in the Timber",b="Wolves and bears north of the camp have driven the woodcutters away from bundles of cut timber. The workers left the wood where it lay. Raelen cannot wait for guards to clear the area, so she asks you to bring the bundles back to camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Supervisor Raelen?",a="Supervisor Raelen manages the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. She oversees the woodcutters and the timber shipments bound for Stormwind and nearby settlements.",al={"supervisor raelen","raelen","eastvale supervisor"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the wood abandoned in the woods?",a="The laborers had cut and bundled the logs before bears and wolves drove them from the clearing. They fled to camp without the wood.",al={"why wood left","abandoned lumber","forest wood"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Raelen mention Deputy Rainer?",a="Raelen says she contacted Deputy Rainer about the predators. He is stationed at Westbrook Garrison, far across Elwynn Forest, so the message may have traveled through the guards, or local authority may be stretched thin.",al={"deputy rainer raelen","why deputy rainer","rainer connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the lumber needed?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp sends timber throughout the kingdom for rebuilding towns and strengthening palisades and bridges. A missed deadline can hurt Elwynn's economy and delay construction.",al={"who needs the wood","lumber delivery","timber purpose"},it="item"},{q="Why can't the loggers collect the wood themselves?",a="The woodcutters are laborers who fell trees, not fighters trained to face predators. Wolves and bears drove them off, and they will not return to the thicket unarmed.",al={"why loggers scared","why not loggers","loggers wolves"},it="why_me"},{q="Where can the bundles of wood be found?",a="The bundles lie in the woods just north of Eastvale Logging Camp, where the laborers were working before local beasts drove them away.",al={"wood location","where are bundles","find bundles"},gp=true},{q="Why does Supervisor Raelen need this lumber so quickly?",a="Supervisor Raelen is facing a strict delivery deadline for an order of timber. If she fails to supply the promised wood on time, Eastvale's logging operations and her reputation suffer. The wood is already chopped, but the camp's laborers were forced to flee when wild predators moved in, putting the entire shipment at risk.",al={"why does raelen need wood","raelen deadline","why rush lumber order"},it="motive",add="d8093908"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help keep Stormwind's rebuilding and regional outposts supplied with lumber from Eastvale.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track through predator-filled groves and face the local beasts while recovering the supplies."},kw={"bears","bundle of wood","deputy rainer","eastvale","elwynn forest","logging camp","supervisor raelen","timber","wolves"},rel={"npc:supervisor-raelen","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","npc:deputy-rainer","zone:elwynn","subzone:westbrook-garrison"},m={start="Supervisor Raelen",faction="Alliance",id=5545,ri={"Bundle of Wood"}},src={"A Bundle of Trouble"}}
E["quest:5623"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of the Light",z="elwynn",s="Priestess Anetta sends you south from Northshire Abbey to continue your training in Goldshire. Priestess Josetta is waiting at the Lion's Pride Inn to guide your next steps in the Holy Light.",h="Priestess Anetta sends you south from Northshire Abbey to continue your training in Goldshire.",sec={{t="Stepping Beyond Northshire",b="Northshire Abbey gives you shelter and your first lessons in the Holy Light. After you learn prayer and divine healing, Priestess Anetta sends you south along the road to Goldshire. There, you leave the abbey's sheltered study for service among the people of Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="Tutelage in Goldshire",b="Priestess Josetta tends to Goldshire's spiritual needs from the Lion's Pride Inn and guides rising acolytes. She builds on the lessons you learned at the abbey, teaching you to offer comfort, protect the faithful, and heal the injured. Under her guidance, you begin learning the duties of the Church's servants across the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest and who do I report to?",a="Priestess Anetta gives you your instructions inside Northshire Abbey and sends you down the road to meet Priestess Josetta in Goldshire.",al={"who gives in favor of the light","quest turn in","where to turn in in favor of the light"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Why is a priest sent away from Northshire so early?",a="Northshire teaches you the foundations of the Holy Light, and Goldshire gives you a chance to serve a real community. Under Josetta's direction, you can help townspeople and town guards.",al={"why go to goldshire","why leave northshire abbey"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Priestess Josetta be found in Goldshire?",a="Priestess Josetta is inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where she trains priests.",al={"where is priestess josetta","find josetta","josetta location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Priestess Josetta?",a="After you meet Priestess Josetta, she tests your training by asking you to care for a wounded guard and receive ceremonial clerical vestments.",al={"next quest after in favor of the light","what follows in favor of the light"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest restricted to priests?",a="Yes. This instruction is for priest initiates learning to serve the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"can any class do in favor of the light","is this priest only"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="What role does the Church of the Holy Light play in Elwynn?",a="The Church of the Holy Light offers comfort, spiritual guidance, and healing to townspeople and defenders facing bandits and dangerous wildlife in Elwynn.",al={"church of the holy light role","priests in elwynn"},it="history"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you leave your sheltered studies in Northshire to serve the people and garrisons of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can seek the priesthood's guidance in Goldshire as you help uphold your kingdom's moral and spiritual life.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to the Church of the Holy Light for healers who tend to those defending the Alliance."},kw={"anetta","church","elwynn forest","goldshire","holy light","josetta","northshire","priest quest"},rel={"quest:5624","npc:priestess-josetta","npc:priestess-anetta","topic:light","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Priestess Anetta",["end"]="Priestess Josetta",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5623},src={"In Favor of the Light (Elwynn Forest)"}}
E["quest:5624"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of the Light",z="elwynn",s="At Goldshire, Garments of the Light mark a novice priest’s first trial under Priestess Josetta. She sends you east to Crystal Lake to tend the wounded Guard Roberts. The work tests your healing and earns you vestments recognized by the Church of the Holy Light.",h="At Goldshire, Garments of the Light mark a novice priest’s first trial under Priestess Josetta.",sec={{t="A Practical Test of Faith",b="Priestess Josetta teaches acolytes who come to Goldshire from Northshire Abbey. Before the Church of the Holy Light formally recognizes a novice, she tests their skill with divine power. When Guard Roberts is reported wounded by the lake east of Goldshire, Josetta sends you to care for him. His need gives you a chance to prove your healing in practice.",sp=0},{t="Sustaining the Realm",b="You need to do more than close Guard Roberts’s wounds. Mend him with restorative prayers, then strengthen him with a blessing of fortitude. Stormwind’s forces are stretched thin, and local garrisons face kobolds and bandits. Josetta teaches that priests help defenders endure danger. Healing Roberts will aid the township and show that you can support its guards.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Order",b="After treating Guard Roberts, return to the Lion’s Pride Inn. There you receive your first formal robes, a sign of approval and fellowship from the priesthood in Stormwind. The robes are not required for further training, but they show that the Church recognizes you as a servant of the Holy Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Guard Roberts?",a="Guard Roberts is just east of Goldshire, near Crystal Lake. He rests by the roadside at the water’s edge while recovering from wounds suffered on watch.",al={"guard roberts location","where is guard roberts","find guard roberts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What spells are required to complete this quest?",a="Use Lesser Heal Rank 2 to restore Guard Roberts’s health, then cast Power Word: Fortitude to strengthen him. Return to Priestess Josetta afterward.",al={"spells needed","what spells do i cast on roberts","how to heal guard roberts"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who is Priestess Josetta?",a="Priestess Josetta trains priests for the Church of the Holy Light at the Lion’s Pride Inn in Goldshire. She guides young acolytes from Northshire Abbey in practical service and divine magic.",al={"josetta lore","priestess josetta goldshire","who gives garments of the light"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Church give out robes for this task?",a="The robes show that the Church of the Holy Light approves of the acolyte and supports their ministry. Caring for Guard Roberts demonstrates the skill and discipline needed to wear the church’s vestments.",al={"why garments of the light","priest robe reward lore","church robes meaning"},it="purpose"},{q="Can other classes complete this quest?",a="No. Only Alliance priests can complete this trial in their introductory training, after learning fundamental healing and warding prayers.",al={"is garments of the light priest only","can paladins do garments of the light","priest class quest"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing Garments of the Light?",a="After you complete the early priest training in Goldshire, there is no immediate follow-up. Priestess Josetta and other trainers throughout the kingdom offer further training and trials as you gain experience.",al={"next quest after garments of the light","garments of the light followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Josetta want this done?",a="Priestess Josetta usually sets a minor challenge to test novice priests before the Church of the Holy Light officially recognizes them with their vestments. Hearing word that a town guard lies wounded near the lake east of Goldshire, she sees an opportunity to test your healing and protective magic in the field while helping secure the safety of the town.",al={"why does josetta send you","priestess josetta motive","why heal guard roberts"},it="motive",add="45956511"},{q="Who is Guard Roberts?",a="Guard Roberts is a Stormwind guard stationed around Goldshire who was wounded near the lake east of town. With threats pressing in on Elwynn Forest, every able defender counts, making his recovery vital to the township's protection.",al={"guard roberts","who is the injured guard","injured guard roberts"},it="target",add="010a8804"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you carry your learning from Northshire into service in the field. Healing and fortifying allies helps keep those on the front line alive.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how local church disciples help town guards hold their ground while Stormwind’s army is stretched thin and absent from hamlets.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you belong to a culture that honors the Church of the Holy Light. Earning vestments from a township priestess marks an important civic and spiritual milestone."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn forest","garments of the light","goldshire","guard roberts","lesser heal","power word fortitude","priest robe","priestess josetta"},rel={"npc:priestess-josetta","subzone:goldshire","quest:5623","zone:elwynn","topic:light"},m={start="Priestess Josetta",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5624},src={"Garments of the Light (Elwynn Forest)"}}
E["quest:59"] = {t="quest",n="Cloth and Leather Armor",z="elwynn",s="In Goldshire, Cloth and Leather Armor sends a trusted traveler east for gear. Marshal Dughan issues an armor marker redeemable with Sara Timberlain at Eastvale Logging Camp. The trip carries recruits beyond Guard Thomas's bridge to obtain armor for the realm's defense.",h="In Goldshire, Cloth and Leather Armor sends a trusted traveler east for gear.",sec={{t="The Marshal's Token",b="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn's eastern river crossing, where murlocs and gnolls threaten the border. After you carry his report to Goldshire, Marshal Dughan recognizes your service with an official Stormwind Armor Marker. Goldshire's garrison has meager stores, so Dughan gives you a marker instead of drawing equipment from them. The marker is a military voucher that records your service to the crown.",sp=0},{t="The Weaver of Eastvale",b="East of Guard Thomas's bridge lies Eastvale Logging Camp, Elwynn's main timber operation. Sara Timberlain works there under an official commission from the Stormwind Army to make cloth and leather gear. The kingdom's central armories are strained, leaving local artisans like Sara to outfit troops and auxiliary scouts on the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Stormwind Armor Marker?",a="A Stormwind Armor Marker is an official military requisition slip issued by officers such as Marshal Dughan. Trusted recruits can use it to claim custom-fitted armor from civilian artisans commissioned by the army, instead of officers keeping bulky armor sets at their posts.",al={"armor marker","stormwind voucher","what is the marker"},it="item"},{q="Who is Sara Timberlain?",a="Sara Timberlain is a tailor and crafter who lives at Eastvale Logging Camp. Under contract with the Stormwind Army, she makes cloth and leather equipment for kingdom personnel and authorized auxiliary fighters.",al={"sara timberlain","eastvale tailor","who makes the armor"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in far eastern Elwynn Forest. From Guard Thomas's river bridge post, take the road east into the wooded valley, where woodcutters harvest timber for the kingdom.",al={"eastvale location","where is eastvale","how to get to timberlain"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan send adventurers to Eastvale?",a="Marshal Dughan directs recruits to Sara Timberlain at Eastvale because he does not hand out finished gear from his Goldshire post. He sends travelers east after brave deeds so they can obtain proper protection for Elwynn's defense.",al={"why marshal dughan marker","dughan purpose","why eastvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the army relying on local tailors for supplies?",a="King Varian Wrynn is missing, and Stormwind's military is spread thin responding to Defias activity and wild beasts. Local defense posts rely heavily on contracted regional workers to keep their supply lines going.",al={"stormwind supply problems","why local artisan","army logistics"},it="history"},{q="Who is Guard Thomas defending against?",a="Guard Thomas watches Elwynn Forest's eastern border and the bridge against river murlocs, prowling beasts, and the dangerous wilderness by the Redridge Mountains.",al={"guard thomas enemies","threats at bridge","eastern elwynn threats"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want this done?",a="Marshal Dughan wants to reward your valor and shrewdness after you carried Guard Thomas's report from the eastern border. By handing you an official requisition marker for Sara Timberlain, he ensures you are properly outfitted in sturdy cloth or leather to continue defending Elwynn Forest against mounting threats.",al={"marshal dughan motive","why send to sara timberlain","why give armor marker"},it="motive",add="ebb61187"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you see how local contracts help Elwynn's rural communities keep the Alliance functioning while the capital is politically paralyzed.",["race:Human"]="As a human, your service to Marshal Dughan and dealings with Sara Timberlain reflect the civic bonds that hold Elwynn's small homesteads together.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see in Sara Timberlain's army commission that cloth crafting is an officially sponsored military trade in the kingdom."},kw={"armor marker","cloth and leather armor","eastvale","elwynn forest","guard thomas","logging camp","marshal dughan","sara timberlain","stormwind army"},rel={"npc:guard-thomas","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","quest:39","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",["end"]="Sara Timberlain",faction="Alliance",id=59},src={"Cloth and Leather Armor"}}
E["quest:6"] = {t="quest",n="Bounty on Garrick Padfoot",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire, an Alliance bounty names Garrick Padfoot, a notorious local thief. Deputy Willem at Northshire Abbey calls for recruits to hunt him near the vineyards.",h="In Northshire, an Alliance bounty names Garrick Padfoot, a notorious local thief.",sec={{t="A Plague on the Valley",b="Northshire Valley once offered a safe place to train recruits and tend its sacred vineyards. As order falters across Elwynn, thieves have reached the valley. Garrick Padfoot, a cutthroat, quickly rose to lead them. For weeks, he and his gang have plundered shipments, robbed merchants on the roads, and threatened local farmers.",sp=0},{t="Deputy Willem's Justice",b="Stormwind's guards are stretched thin, protecting the capital and its outer borders. Local marshals and deputies rely on volunteers to keep Northshire peaceful. Deputy Willem places a public bounty on Garrick's head, hoping to rid the valley of his gang. Bringing Padfoot down at his rundown shack east of the river strikes at the lawlessness spreading through the human heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Garrick Padfoot?",a="Garrick Padfoot is a bandit and cutthroat in Northshire Valley. For weeks, he has harassed local farmers and ambushed merchants, gathering a small ring of thugs near the vineyards.",al={"garrick padfoot","who is garrick","padfoot"},it="target"},{q="Where can Garrick Padfoot be found?",a="Garrick Padfoot hides in a small wooden shack east of Northshire Abbey, across the river bridge and near the vineyards. Fellow thugs guard him.",al={"where is garrick padfoot","garrick location","garrick shack"},gp=true},{q="Who issues the bounty on Garrick?",a="Deputy Willem, stationed outside Northshire Abbey, posts the bounty. With too few city guards to police the valley, he calls on wandering recruits to bring the outlaw to justice.",al={"who gives bounty on garrick padfoot","willem bounty"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Stormwind not sending regular soldiers to deal with him?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched too thin. With King Varian Wrynn missing and tensions rising across Elwynn Forest and beyond, the capital cannot spare veteran garrisons for every small-time thug. Local deputies must call on recruits.",al={"why don't guards kill garrick","where are stormwind guards"},it="why_me"},{q="Is Garrick Padfoot working alone?",a="No. Garrick has gathered a small gang of outlaws and bandits who camp around his shack near the Northshire vineyards to protect him.",al={"is garrick solo","padfoot gang"},it="allies"},{q="What proof does Deputy Willem require?",a="Deputy Willem requires physical proof before paying the coin: bring Garrick Padfoot's severed head back to Northshire Abbey.",al={"proof of garrick death","garricks head"},it="item"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem want Garrick Padfoot killed?",a="Garrick Padfoot has spent weeks terrorizing Northshire Valley. As a cutthroat leading a gang of thieves, he actively preys upon the local farmers and traveling merchants who sustain the valley. Deputy Willem wants him dead to put an end to his raids, restore safety to the vineyards and roads, and protect the abbey's community from further violence.",al={"why kill garrick padfoot","deputy willem motive","why does willem want garrick dead"},it="motive",add="38d5a8ce"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Bringing down Garrick Padfoot is an early service for an aspiring Alliance adventurer, helping restore stability to the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human raised in the kingdom, you have reason to protect your homeland's sacred ground and local farmers from cutthroats like Padfoot.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how outlaws operate in Elwynn's shadows. A poorly hidden hideout invites a swift blade."},kw={"bounty","cutthroat","elwynn","garrick","northshire","padfoot","thieves","vineyard","willem"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:18","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Deputy Willem",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=6,ri={"Garrick's Head"}},src={"Bounty on Garrick Padfoot"}}
E["quest:60"] = {t="quest",n="Kobold Candles",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle seeks candles from kobolds that have overstocked Elwynn Forest's mines. Visiting from his shop in Stormwind, the alchemist needs their thick wax, and the errand introduces adventurers to the subterranean pests encroaching on the kingdom's valuable gold veins.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, William Pestle seeks candles from kobolds that have overstocked Elwynn...",sec={{t="Apothecary's Errands",b="William Pestle runs Pestle's Apothecary with his brother in Stormwind City's Trade District. Wax is always in short supply as he brews remedies, ointments, and concoctions. Instead of buying polished candles from city merchants, Pestle turns to the vermin in Elwynn. The kobolds carry hefty lumps of tallow and wax on their brows, ready for an adventurer willing to pry them loose.",sp=0},{t="The Mines of Elwynn",b="Kobolds have overrun Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the northeast. These snuffling creatures prize their candles above almost all else. The flickering flames guide them through dark shafts as they dig for gold and shiny trinkets. Taking the candles replenishes Pestle's alchemy stocks and chips away at the vermin choking off the kingdom's precious mining claims.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does William Pestle need kobold candles?",a="William Pestle and his brother run an apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. They use the rendered tallow and wax from large candles in sealing, salves, and other alchemical preparations.",al={"why pestle wants candles","what are candles used for","candle wax use"},it="motive"},{q="Where do you find the large candles?",a="Kobold workers, vermin, and diggers carry the candles in Elwynn Forest's mines, especially in Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire and Jasperlode Mine to the east.",al={"where are kobold candles","candle locations","how to get large candles"},gp=true},{q="Why are kobolds so obsessed with candles?",a="Kobolds live in pitch-black underground tunnels and rely on the flames strapped to their heads to see as they dig. Their fear of the dark is superstitious and almost frantic, so they fiercely defend their candles from anyone who tries to take them.",al={"why do kobolds have candles","you no take candle meaning","kobold candle lore"}},{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is a human merchant and alchemist from Stormwind. When he is away from his shop in the city's Trade District, he travels to Goldshire to secure cheap materials from adventurers.",al={"who is william pestle","william pestle lore","goldshire pestle"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest connect to other troubles in Elwynn?",a="Yes. The kobold infestation in Fargodeep and Jasperlode Mines threatens Goldshire and Stormwind's economy. Human miners have been driven out, and securing the tunnels is one of Marshal Dughan's top priorities.",al={"elwynn mine problems","why are kobolds in mines","goldshire kobold threat"},it="ties"},{q="Are there any other mines infested by kobolds in Elwynn?",a="Fargodeep Mine and Jasperlode Mine are the two main kobold sites near Goldshire. Their activity also reaches the forest's riverbanks and extends east toward the borders of Redridge.",al={"other kobold mines","elwynn mines list"}},{q="What is the Large Candle used for?",a="William Pestle needs the large candles for their wax. He and his brother run Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District of Stormwind. The quests do not specify the particular preparations for which they use that wax.",al={"large candle use","why large candles","what are the candles for"},it="item",add="13eaf00c"},{q="Why are kobolds in the Elwynn mines?",a="Kobolds are subterranean scavengers drawn to dark, mineral-rich tunnels where they can dig for gold and precious ore. With Stormwind's military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn missing, Elwynn's local mines like Fargodeep and Jasperlode were left poorly defended, allowing the kobolds to overrun the shafts and drive out human miners.",al={"why are kobolds here","fargodeep kobolds why","kobold infestation elwynn"},it="target",add="decb568d"},{q="Why does William Pestle ask you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist, not a soldier. With kobolds aggressively guarding the tunnels of Fargodeep and Jasperlode, venturing into the mines himself would be lethal. Meanwhile, the local Stormwind guards and Elwynn Marshals are completely overwhelmed dealing with Defias bandits and gnolls, leaving trivial errands like gathering wax to passing adventurers.",al={"why doesn't william get candles himself","why hire adventurers for candles","why not stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="27573e3c"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Clearing kobolds for their candles brings prospectors directly to Elwynn's richest copper and gold veins, abandoned by human miners.",["race:Human"]="As a human, reclaiming Elwynn's stolen mines and supplying Stormwind's artisans are early duties for a young subject of the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure local infrastructure while the royal army is stretched thin by internal political strife and missing crown forces."},kw={"apothecary","candle","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","wax","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold","quest:62","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="William Pestle",faction="Alliance",id=60,ri={"Large Candle"}},src={"Kobold Candles"}}
E["quest:61"] = {t="quest",n="Shipment to Stormwind",z="elwynn",s="William Pestle sends a parcel from Goldshire to his brother Morgan in Stormwind. Its candles carry wax supplies from Elwynn Forest to Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District.",h="William Pestle sends a parcel from Goldshire to his brother Morgan in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Family Trade",b="William gathers herbs, reagents, and raw goods in Goldshire, while his brother Morgan runs Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. William cannot easily leave his post at the Lion's Pride Inn, so he depends on travelers heading into the city to carry goods for him.",sp=0},{t="From Kobold Wax to Capital Potions",b="William's parcel holds large candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn's mines. He says he collects them for their wax. Delivering the shipment brings those supplies to Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside William's shipment?",a="The shipment contains candles gathered from kobolds in Elwynn Forest. William collected them for their wax and packed them for Morgan at Pestle's Apothecary.",al={"shipment contents","what is in the package","what did william send"},it="item"},{q="Where do I find Morgan Pestle?",a="Morgan Pestle works inside Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District, a short walk past the main gates.",al={"morgan pestle location","where is morgan","find morgan pestle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How are William and Morgan Pestle related?",a="William and Morgan Pestle are brothers who run an alchemical enterprise together. William procures materials in Elwynn Forest, while Morgan operates their shop in Stormwind.",al={"pestle brothers","who is william pestle brother"},it="ties"},{q="Why doesn't William deliver the package himself?",a="William is occupied with his trade and collecting alchemical ingredients in Goldshire. He relies on travelers already heading toward the capital to carry the package.",al={"why doesn't william go to stormwind","why hire a courier"},it="why_me"},{q="Do kobold candles have an actual alchemical use?",a="William says he and his brother need the candles for their wax. He does not describe how they use it at the apothecary.",al={"why kobold candles","kobold wax alchemy"},it="power"},{q="What comes after delivering the shipment?",a="Delivering the shipment concludes the short chain that began with gathering kobold candles in Elwynn Forest. Morgan pays you for carrying the parcel and welcomes your business in his shop.",al={"what next after shipment to stormwind","follow up quest shipment to stormwind"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does William Pestle want this shipment delivered?",a="Morgan is waiting at the brothers' apothecary in Stormwind for the shipment of candles. William gathered them for their wax but lacks time to make the journey, so he asks a traveler to carry the supplies.",al={"why send the shipment","william pestle motive","why deliver the candles"},it="motive",add="e0018b76"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The Pestle family trade depends on local reagents from Elwynn. Their Stormwind shop is a familiar stop for gatherers and potion-makers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you carry supplies along the king's road into Stormwind, moving from countryside skirmishes toward the capital."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","kobold candles","morgan pestle","pestle's apothecary","shipment to stormwind","trade district","william pestle"},rel={"quest:60","npc:william-pestle","npc:morgan-pestle","subzone:trade-district","zone:elwynn","topic:kobold","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="William Pestle",["end"]="Morgan Pestle",level="7",faction="Alliance",id=61},src={"Shipment to Stormwind"}}
E["quest:62"] = {t="quest",n="The Fargodeep Mine",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds have overrun The Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire, between the Stonefield and Maclure farms. The mine's fall points to a growing pest problem across Elwynn Forest.",h="Kobolds have overrun The Fargodeep Mine south of Goldshire, between the Stonefield and Maclure farms.",sec={{t="Trouble South of Goldshire",b="While Northshire Valley faces its own vermin, reports reach Goldshire that kobolds have claimed another vital site. Between the feuding Stonefield and Maclure homesteads south of town, the Fargodeep Mine once supplied stone and ore for the realm. Now shrill chattering and tallow candles fill its damp tunnels. Marshal Dughan sends you to scout the depths and learn how bad the trouble is.",sp=0},{t="A Strained Guard",b="The report of kobolds in the mine adds to the Stormwind Guard's strain. Its troops are already stretched thin defending against Defias bandits and gnoll incursions, leaving too few to clear the tunnels. When Dughan hears the report, he worries about other mineral sites, including the Jasperlode Mine to the northeast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Fargodeep Mine located?",a="The Fargodeep Mine lies almost due south of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, between the Stonefield and Maclure homesteads.",al={"fargodeep location","where is fargodeep mine","fargodeep mine map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends you to scout the Fargodeep Mine?",a="Marshal Dughan, the Stormwind Guard's commanding officer in Goldshire, sends you to scout the tunnels.",al={"who gives fargodeep quest","marshal dughan quest"}},{q="What creatures have taken over the mine?",a="Kobolds have overrun the mine, lit their candles, and driven out the human workers.",al={"who is in fargodeep","what monsters in fargodeep"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan need adventurers to check the mine?",a="The Stormwind Guard is stretched thin by local banditry, orc remnants, and gnoll raids, leaving Dughan without spare soldiers even to confirm scout reports.",al={"why send scouts","why doesn't the guard go"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after scouting the Fargodeep Mine?",a="After you report the trouble to Marshal Dughan, he fears it is widespread and sends you northeast to investigate the Jasperlode Mine.",al={"next quest after fargodeep","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the infestation of Fargodeep Mine significant?",a="The fall of the Fargodeep Mine shows that the kobold infestation in Northshire was not isolated. Wild threats are pressing rapidly into settled farmland just outside Stormwind's gates.",al={"why does fargodeep matter","lore of fargodeep mine"},it="motive"},{q="Why have kobolds taken over Fargodeep Mine?",a="Kobolds are natural tunnel-dwellers constantly seeking gold and precious minerals beneath the earth. With Stormwind's guards spread thin protecting the region from Defias bandits and wild beasts, the local mines have been left largely undefended. Drawn to rich deposits of ore and gold, the vermin swarmed into Fargodeep Mine, digging in deep and driving out any workers.",al={"why are kobolds in fargodeep mine","kobolds fargodeep mine why","who is in fargodeep mine"},it="target",add="88321243"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find rich copper veins inside the Fargodeep Mine, but territorial kobolds stand in your way.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the overrun mine as another sign that Stormwind struggles to protect Elwynn's essential sites."},kw={"dughan","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","maclure","stonefield"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:76","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold","subzone:jasperlode-mine","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=62},src={"The Fargodeep Mine"}}
E["quest:6285"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Lewis",z="elwynn",s="Dungar Longdrink sends armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill. Osric's Crate crosses Elwynn and Westfall by gryphon, carrying supplies to defenders under pressure.",h="Dungar Longdrink sends armor from Stormwind to the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",sec={{t="A Lifeline by Air",b="Westfall is slipping from the kingdom's grasp. Defias bandits, ravenous gnolls, and mechanical harvest reapers threaten the land. Overland supply routes face harassment, and roads are dangerous for solitary wagons. The flight master network offers a crucial lifeline. Osric, an armorer in Stormwind's Old Town, prepared a heavy crate of armor for the battered volunteers of the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill.",sp=0},{t="The Ways of Gryphons",b="Gryphons are loyal, well-trained beasts, but travel across the lands depends on established familiarity. Dungar Longdrink explains that gryphons instinctively know how to return to their capital roost in Stormwind. To carry a rider to a remote outpost, though, they need the traveler to have met its flight master in person. You have already checked in with Thor at Sentinel Hill, opening the skies over the frontier to rapid travel.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Militia",b="At Sentinel Hill, Quartermaster Lewis receives the crate. He is the officer tasked with outfitting Gryan Stoutmantle's volunteer force, and he sets to work distributing the armor among the frontier defenders. For Sentinel Hill, reliable aerial contact with the capital can mean the difference between holding the line and being overrun by the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Osric's Crate?",a="Osric's Crate holds freshly made suits of armor arranged by the Stormwind armorer Osric. The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill urgently needs them; the volunteers lack standard royal provisioning and rely on donations and private shipments for their gear.",al={"osrics crate contents","what is in the box","what am i delivering"},it="item"},{q="Who is Quartermaster Lewis?",a="Quartermaster Lewis is the People's Militia's supply officer, stationed beside the tower at Sentinel Hill. He manages rations, gear, and arms for the volunteer defenders facing the Defias Brotherhood across Westfall.",al={"lewis westfall","quartermaster lewis role","who is lewis"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Dungar Longdrink?",a="Dungar Longdrink is Stormwind's veteran human gryphon master, at the roost in the capital's Trade District. He oversees the kingdom's aerial courier and passenger routes.",al={"dungar stormwind","stormwind gryphon master","flight master stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why do gryphons only fly to places you've already visited?",a="Dungar says gryphons are trained to navigate straight back to the capital city. They rely on established waypoints and personal familiarity before carrying riders to remote frontier roosts like Thor's station at Sentinel Hill.",al={"gryphon flight rule","how flight paths work","why must i visit thor first"}},{q="Who is Thor?",a="Thor is the flight master stationed at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. He tends the outpost's gryphons and receives aerial couriers from Stormwind.",al={"thor westfall","sentinel hill gryphon master","flight master thor"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Stormwind just send royal wagons with supplies?",a="Defias bandits, riverpaw gnolls, and thieves heavily harass the roads between Elwynn Forest and Westfall. Overland supply trains risk ambush and confiscation, while the aerial gryphon route is faster and safer.",al={"why use gryphons","why not overland delivery","roads in westfall"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Dungar Longdrink want Osric's Crate delivered?",a="Dungar oversees Stormwind's gryphon network, which serves as a vital lifeline between the capital and the beleaguered frontiers. Quartermaster Lewis and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill desperately need reinforcements and armor to hold Westfall against Defias thugs and gnolls. Dungar ensures that critical military aid reaches remote outposts swiftly, relying on trustworthy travelers to ferry the supplies back by wing.",al={"dungar motive","why send osrics crate","why dungar helps lewis"},it="motive",add="24b76519"},{q="Why does Dungar need you to deliver the crate instead of sending a courier?",a="Dungar manages the capital's busy roost and cannot abandon his post, while Stormwind's official garrison rarely spares men for the neglected defense of Westfall. Because Lewis originally sent you to coordinate this supply run, you have already secured the trust of both Thor and the Sentinel Hill militia. Entrusting the crate to a willing adventurer returning on gryphonback is the fastest way to get the armor into hands that need it.",al={"why not send a courier","why me dungar","why deliver the crate myself"},it="why_me",add="74eea5bf"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Gryphon routes between Stormwind and outlying settlements like Sentinel Hill help bind together a kingdom that is increasingly fractured.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know gryphons as your people's ancestral mounts. The kingdom's aerial transit flies them from Dungar Longdrink's capital roost to Thor out in Westfall.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know every crate of breastplates and greaves flown to Sentinel Hill gives another militia fighter a chance to withstand the blows of Defias brigands."},kw={"dungar longdrink","flight path","gryphon","osric","osric's crate","people's militia","quartermaster lewis","sentinel hill","thor","westfall"},rel={"quest:6261","quest:6281","quest:6181","npc:quartermaster-lewis","npc:thor","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Dungar Longdrink",["end"]="Quartermaster Lewis",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6285},src={"Return to Lewis"}}
E["quest:7"] = {t="quest",n="Kobold Camp Cleanup",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire, Kobold Camp Cleanup puts new recruits to their first test defending Stormwind's borders. Marshal McBride sends volunteers after kobolds in the northern woods, where their growing numbers threaten the abbey grounds.",h="At Northshire, Kobold Camp Cleanup puts new recruits to their first test defending Stormwind's borders.",sec={{t="A Valley Under Pressure",b="Northshire Valley once offered quiet for prayer, farming, and novice training. In recent years, Stormwind's forces have grown thin. With the King missing and royal garrisons scattered, wild creatures and opportunists press at civilization's edge. Marshal McBride directs the valley's defense from Northshire Abbey. He depends on fresh volunteers to keep threats from disrupting the abbey or endangering the surrounding vineyards.",sp=0},{t="The Vermin in the Woods",b="Kobolds are timid cave-dwellers with a strong attachment to candles. They usually pick at underground seams, far from direct sunlight. Now an entire clan has reached Northshire's northern timberline. If left unchecked, their numbers can turn scavenging into open raids. McBride sends recruits to thin their vanguard and test their resolve to defend the realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the culling of the kobold camp?",a="Marshal McBride gives the order. From Northshire Abbey, he oversees recruit intake and the valley's security for Stormwind.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","marshal mcbride role"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are kobolds in the northern woods instead of a mine?",a="Kobolds usually live in burrows and mines, but Northshire's growing population has spilled into the open forest. They have made primitive camps among the northern trees, near the edge of civilized land.",al={"why are kobolds outside","kobolds above ground","why woods"},it="why_here"},{q="Why are these kobolds considered a threat to Stormwind?",a="Alone, kobold vermin are timid and weak. In packs, they can ambush travelers, raid supplies, and overwhelm unguarded outposts, a threat Stormwind can ill afford while its forces are stretched thin.",al={"are kobolds dangerous","why kill vermin"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this mission lead next?",a="After thinning the kobolds on the surface, recruits are sent to investigate deeper into Echo Ridge Mine, where the heart of the infestation lies.",al={"what quest is next","next step","after camp cleanup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is Northshire receiving regular royal army backup?",a="No. Political tension and troop shortages after King Varian's disappearance leave commanders like McBride relying on civilian volunteers, adventurers, and trainees for border security.",al={"where are stormwind guards","why volunteers"},it="allies"},{q="What makes kobolds so attached to their candles?",a="Kobolds revere candles as their main defense against the smothering darkness of underground tunnels. Their flames give them safety, sight, and a sense of ownership.",al={"why candles","candle obsession"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride want the kobold camp cleaned up?",a="A clan of kobolds has begun infesting the woods north of the abbey, and Marshal McBride wants their numbers reduced before they overrun the valley. Stormwind is already strained by threats elsewhere, leaving Northshire to protect itself. While individually cowardly, the kobolds grow bold in packs. Culling them now keeps the settlement safe and begins the effort to drive them out of Northshire entirely.",al={"why cull kobolds","mcbride kobold motive","why clean kobold camp"},it="motive",add="afae4267"},{q="What are the kobold vermin you are sent to hunt?",a="Kobold vermin are the scouts and scavengers of a clan that has crept into the northern forest. Naturally subterranean rat-like humanoids, they are cowardly thieves on their own, but they have gathered in the woods outside Northshire in alarming numbers. Left unchecked, their encroaching camps threaten travelers, orchards, and the abbey itself.",al={"who are the kobold vermin","what are kobold vermin","kobold vermin target"},it="target",add="35967b57"},{q="Why does Marshal McBride send you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="Stormwind's royal army has stretched its forces thin dealing with crises across the kingdom, leaving Northshire Valley garrisoned by only a handful of guards. McBride must keep his soldiers stationed around the abbey and primary roads to maintain defensive perimeters. With no spare troops to patrol the wilderness, he relies on capable new recruits and passing volunteers to root out emerging dangers.",al={"why not send guards","why does mcbride need me","why recruit adventurers kobolds"},it="why_me",add="921e514b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Northshire, driving back kobold vermin is a civic duty that helps protect the abbey and farmland from being overrun.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the strain on Stormwind's home territories, where even scavenger infestations call for urgent help from volunteer militia."},kw={"echo ridge","elwynn forest","kobold","marshal mcbride","northshire","northshire abbey","vermin"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:783","quest:15","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:human"},m={start="Marshal McBride",level="2",faction="Alliance",id=7},src={"Kobold Camp Cleanup"}}
E["quest:71"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Thomas",z="elwynn",s="Guard Thomas waits at the eastern bridge between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp. The fate of his missing men may show whether the river murlocs threaten more than scouts.",h="Guard Thomas waits at the eastern bridge between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",sec={{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Guard Thomas holds the crossing between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp with few men to spare. When Malakai and Rolf vanished into the riverlands, he hoped they had only been cut off or delayed. Their recovered service medallions leave no such hope. Both guards were slain near the waterways.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Along the Water",b="For months, Stormwind's leaders have treated murlocs as nuisance river-dwellers, focusing instead on bandits and the kingdom's wider borders. Now two armed Stormwind guards have been slaughtered along the inland streams. The medallions show Thomas that Elwynn's eastern frontier faces an active assault, and he calls for a response before the logging routes and settlements are overwhelmed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Guard Thomas stand?",a="Guard Thomas is posted at the stone bridge over the river in eastern Elwynn Forest, on the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"thomas location","guard thomas bridge","where is guard thomas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who were Rolf and Malakai?",a="Rolf and Malakai were Stormwind guards sent to patrol eastern Elwynn Forest. Murlocs along the riverbanks and Stonecairn Lake overwhelmed and killed them.",al={"missing guards elwynn","who was rolf","who was malakai"},sp=1,it="people"},{q="Why were their medallions necessary?",a="The medallions identify Stormwind city guards. Returning them gives Guard Thomas proof that his missing men died in the line of duty.",al={"why medallions","guard medallions purpose"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Why is the murloc attack such a big deal?",a="Murlocs are commonly dismissed as primitive, cowardly pests. The deaths of two armed guards show that river tribes can carry out coordinated ambushes and threaten trained soldiers.",al={"why murlocs threat","are murlocs dangerous elwynn"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What happens after reporting back to Thomas?",a="Thomas asks you to carry a report of the guards' deaths and the growing murloc threat to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. Dughan warns that the region's defenses are already stretched thin.",al={"next quest after report to thomas","what does thomas do next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Guard Thomas posted alone at the bridge?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the realm, with King Varian Wrynn missing and resources strained. The eastern bridge and other outlying posts have few guards to protect vital routes.",al={"why is thomas alone","stormwind bridge guard alone"},it="why_here"},{q="Why deliver the medallions to Guard Thomas?",a="Guard Thomas sent patrols out toward the river, only for them to vanish without word. Finding Rolf and Malakai fallen among the reeds provides grim certainty of their end. Delivering their recovered medallions back to Thomas proves beyond doubt what happened to his men and warns him of the lethal murloc presence along the eastern water.",al={"why report to thomas","why bring medallions to thomas","purpose of report to thomas"},it="motive",add="d4d51b05"},{q="Why are you the one returning the medallions to Thomas?",a="Rolf and Malakai are dead, slain by the murlocs deep within the hostile riverbank village. Guard Thomas is stationed alone guarding the eastern bridge and cannot leave his post unguarded. As the traveler who found the fallen guards and braved the murlocs to recover their insignia, the task falls on you to bring the grim news back.",al={"why me report to thomas","why do i bring the medallions"},it="why_me",add="3744e02c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Rolf and Malakai's deaths show how exposed Elwynn Forest's borders are. Even routine river patrols can be overwhelmed when guards are scarce.",["race:Human"]="As a human, recovering the fallen guards' medallions gives Stormwind soldiers who died defending the kingdom's interior roads a measure of honor and finality."},kw={"bridge","elwynn forest","goldshire","guard thomas","malakai","medallions","murlocs","rolf"},rel={"quest:45","npc:guard-thomas","quest:39","quest:59","topic:murloc","zone:elwynn","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Rolf's corpse",["end"]="Guard Thomas",faction="Alliance",id=71},src={"Report to Thomas"}}
E["quest:76"] = {t="quest",n="The Jasperlode Mine",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds have overrun the Jasperlode Mine in eastern Elwynn. Marshal Dughan sends scouts to learn how far the infestation has spread.",h="Kobolds have overrun the Jasperlode Mine in eastern Elwynn.",sec={{t="A Second Incursion",b="After kobolds swarmed the Fargodeep tunnels south of Goldshire, Marshal Dughan feared they had reached other mines. Jasperlode lies in the rocky foothills northeast of the Tower of Azora and supplies raw stone and metal to the kingdom. Dughan cannot spare Stormwind guards from their town patrols, so he sends independent adventurers east to see whether kobolds have taken this mine too.",sp=0},{t="Overextended Defenses",b="Scouts who reach Jasperlode's chambers find kobolds have driven out the human miners and fortified the dark passages. Marshal Dughan faces another blow as the crisis grows. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and royal troops are withheld from outlying territories. The local garrison has too few soldiers to clear the mines, leaving the kingdom's heart short of minerals and hemmed in by threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Jasperlode Mine located?",a="Jasperlode Mine lies in the northern foothills of eastern Elwynn Forest. Travel east from Goldshire along the main road, pass the Tower of Azora, then head north into the hills.",al={"where is jasperlode","jasperlode mine location","how to find jasperlode"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan need a scout instead of sending guards?",a="Marshal Dughan has too few guards to spare. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and political gridlock in the capital has left local forces stretched thin protecting farms and towns from bandits and gnolls, so Dughan relies on civilian scouts.",al={"why send adventurers","why no stormwind guard","where are the guards"},it="why_me"},{q="Why are kobolds taking over Elwynn's mines?",a="Kobolds tunnel toward mineral veins and damp caves. As Stormwind's military presence thinned, they grew bolder and pushed into human mines like Fargodeep and Jasperlode to claim gold, ore, and territory.",al={"why kobolds in jasperlode","what do kobolds want","kobold infestation reason"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after scouting the Jasperlode Mine?",a="After you report Jasperlode's fall, Marshal Dughan faces the loss of mines in the east and threats on several fronts. He turns his attention to western Elwynn, where Riverpaw gnolls are putting heavy pressure on the Westbrook Garrison.",al={"what next after jasperlode","jasperlode follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the loss of Jasperlode Mine significant to Stormwind?",a="Elwynn's mines supply the ore and stone Stormwind needs for its economy and to forge weapons and armor. Losing Fargodeep and Jasperlode halts mineral extraction and weakens the kingdom's recovery.",al={"why jasperlode matters","jasperlode importance"},it="ruin"},{q="Who owns the Tower of Azora nearby?",a="The Tower of Azora is a small mage tower along Elwynn Forest's eastern road. Theocritus, the Archmage of Azora, presides there, and Azora's servants run the tower. Travelers use it as a landmark on the way to the eastern foothills.",al={"what is tower of azora","who lives in azora tower"}},{q="Why does Marshal Dughan want Jasperlode Mine scouted?",a="Having already confirmed that kobolds have overrun the Fargodeep Mine, Marshal Dughan fears the infestation is not an isolated incident. He needs to know whether the threat has spread east to Jasperlode Mine as well. Securing Elwynn's resource supply and understanding the full scale of the encroaching danger are vital to defending the township of Goldshire and protecting Stormwind's vital trade routes.",al={"dughan motive jasperlode","why scout jasperlode","why does dughan need jasperlode investigated"},it="motive",add="a973508b"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you see valuable deposits in Jasperlode's tunnels, but territorial kobolds stand between you and the ore.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how fragile Stormwind's home territories have become without centralized royal support, with both Fargodeep and Jasperlode lost.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you witness Elwynn's rural infrastructure faltering as frontier resources fall close to the capital."},kw={"azora","dughan","elwynn","fargodeep","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","mine","scout"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","quest:62","subzone:fargodeep-mine","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:tower-of-azora","quest:239","subzone:goldshire","topic:kobold"},m={start="Marshal Dughan",faction="Alliance",id=76},src={"The Jasperlode Mine"}}
E["quest:783"] = {t="quest",n="A Threat Within",z="elwynn",s="Volunteers are answering Stormwind's call in Northshire Valley, where local defenses need help. At Northshire Abbey, Marshal McBride explains that the kingdom's forces are spread thin abroad, leaving garrisons short-handed against trouble at home.",h="Volunteers are answering Stormwind's call in Northshire Valley, where local defenses need help.",sec={{t="A Kingdom Stretched Thin",b="Northshire Valley once offered quiet for prayer, farming, and monastic study. Now it is Elwynn Forest's first line of defense against unrest at home. Stormwind's regular forces serve on distant fronts, leaving the heartlands short of soldiers. With few guards nearby, the Stormwind Guard must call on every willing volunteer who reaches the abbey.",sp=0},{t="The Marshal's Call",b="Marshal McBride directs Northshire Valley's defenses from Northshire Abbey as pressures grow. Distant dangers threaten the Alliance, while bandits, vermin, and pests from below ground take advantage of the shortage of soldiers close to home. You answer the call to serve in the valley, starting with the ground around the abbey as threats spread across Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Marshal McBride is calling new arrivals to Northshire Valley to join its defense. You go inside Northshire Abbey and report to him.",al={"threat within quest","what is this quest","northshire intro quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the senior Stormwind Guard officer at Northshire Abbey. He directs the valley's defense and assigns recruits to address threats in the nearby countryside.",al={"marshal mcbride","who is mcbride","abbey commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Stormwind recruiting volunteers instead of sending regular soldiers?",a="Stormwind's regular forces are serving abroad to protect the Alliance. With heartland garrisons short of soldiers, local commanders rely on volunteers to defend their homes.",al={"why volunteers","where are the guards","why is stormwind understaffed"},it="why_me"},{q="What threats are currently plaguing Northshire Valley?",a="Kobolds infest the nearby mines and hills, while diseased or predatory pests trouble the vineyards. Brigands and outlaws also take advantage of the valley's depleted garrison.",al={"valley threats","what is attacking northshire","northshire problems"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this assignment lead next?",a="After you report to Marshal McBride, you are sent to clear kobolds from the hills, help local farmers and workers, and look into the growing presence of organized bandits.",al={"next quest","what comes after threat within","mcbride follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Northshire Abbey being used as a military command post?",a="Northshire Abbey is a holy place of study and faith, but its stone walls and central position make it the valley's practical base. With local authority under strain, the Stormwind Guard has set up its command within the abbey.",al={"why military in abbey","northshire church military","holy abbey soldiers"},it="place"},{q="Why does Deputy Willem send you to Marshal McBride?",a="Deputy Willem is stationed outside Northshire Abbey to vet able-bodied arrivals as quickly as possible. With the kingdom's military stretched thin and multiple crises closing in on Northshire's borders, he needs every capable volunteer properly mustered into service. Rather than assigning missions himself, Willem directs you straight to his commanding officer, Marshal McBride, so you can be formally briefed and deployed wherever the valley's defenses are faltering most.",al={"why talk to mcbride","willem motive","why speak with mcbride"},it="motive",add="2039075b"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human defender from Northshire, answering Marshal McBride's call is your first official pledge to protect your homeland and the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how commitments across distant lands leave even its heartlands exposed to trouble within."},kw={"a threat within","abbey","elwynn forest","marshal mcbride","northshire","recruitment","stormwind guard","volunteers"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={level="1",faction="Alliance",id=783},src={"A Threat Within"}}
E["quest:83"] = {t="quest",n="Red Linen Goods",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain needs cloth for her tailoring. She asks passing adventurers to hunt Defias bandits and take their linen bandanas, then uses the cloth to make goods for travelers.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Sara Timberlain needs cloth for her tailoring.",sec={{t="Bandits and Burlap",b="Defias bandits across Elwynn wear red linen bandanas. Their less organized kin in Northshire Valley make do with cheap burlap masks. For local craftsmen short on materials, the bandanas offer cloth they can use.",sp=0},{t="Salvage at the Camp",b="Sara Timberlain works as a seamstress at Eastvale Logging Camp, near Elwynn's eastern border. She needs workable textiles for her trade, so she asks adventurers to thin the Defias camps scattered through the woods. The cloth keeps her tailoring supplied while the bandits' encroachment on the area is checked.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the Red Linen Goods quest?",a="Sara Timberlain, a seamstress at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, offers the work.",al={"who gives red linen goods","red linen goods questgiver","sara timberlain quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What items are needed for Red Linen Goods?",a="You need six Red Linen Bandanas from Defias gang members scattered throughout Elwynn Forest.",al={"what do i collect for red linen goods","items for red linen goods","bandanas needed"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Defias bandits in Elwynn Forest?",a="Defias outlaws camp across Elwynn Forest, including around Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Stonefield Farm, and the woods around Jerod's Landing.",al={"defias locations elwynn","where are defias camps","where to get red bandanas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Elwynn Defias wear linen instead of burlap?",a="Low-ranking Defias in Northshire wear burlap masks, while better-equipped members across Elwynn wear red linen. The bandanas mark the Brotherhood's higher level of organization and supply.",al={"why red linen","burlap vs linen defias","defias mask material"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain want bandit bandanas?",a="Sara Timberlain needs fabric for her tailoring. She reuses linen from the Defias masks to sew practical goods for woodsmen and travelers at the logging camp.",al={"why collect bandanas","what does sara do with masks"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp located?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp lies in far eastern Elwynn Forest, just north of the main road toward the bridge into Redridge Mountains.",al={"eastvale location","where is eastvale","how to find sara timberlain"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Red Linen Bandana used for?",a="The red linen bandanas are worn as masks by Defias Brotherhood bandits prowling throughout Elwynn Forest. While the scoundrels in Northshire make do with rough burlap, the thieves in the broader forest carry better-grade cloth. Sara Timberlain unravels and reweaves these captured masks to craft serviceable linen garments.",al={"what is red linen bandana for","red linen bandana use","why red linen bandana"},it="item",add="18a4a024"},{q="Why are Defias bandits in Elwynn Forest?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has established camps scattered across Elwynn Forest to harass travellers, rob supply lines, and undermine Stormwind's authority. Their growing presence threatens local settlements like the Eastvale Logging Camp, taking advantage of the kingdom's stretched guard forces to expand their outlaw operations right outside the capital.",al={"defias in elwynn","why are defias here","defias brotherhood elwynn forest"},it="target",add="8ac6c8ef"},{q="Why does Sara Timberlain need you instead of the guards?",a="Sara Timberlain is a tailor at the Eastvale Logging Camp, not a soldier, and she lacks the means to fight outlaws herself. Stormwind's guards and the local garrison are already overburdened trying to contain widespread Defias incursions and gnoll raids, leaving humble artisans to rely on passing adventurers for materials and protection.",al={"why ask me sara","why not elwynn guards","why timberlain need help"},it="why_me",add="fea06053"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you see how scarce fabric can lead a seamstress to salvage cloth from bandits' clothing.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can weaken the Defias Brotherhood in Elwynn while bringing useful cloth to Eastvale."},kw={"burlap","defias brotherhood","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","red linen bandana","red linen goods","sara timberlain","tailoring"},rel={"npc:sara-timberlain","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Sara Timberlain",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=83,ri={"Red Linen Bandana"}},src={"Red Linen Goods"}}
E["quest:84"] = {t="quest",n="Back to Billy",z="elwynn",s="You carry Bernice Stonefield's freshly baked pie across the road to Billy Maclure, who has information about her missing necklace. The delivery continues the feud between the Stonefield and Maclure families in central Elwynn Forest.",h="You carry Bernice Stonefield's freshly baked pie across the road to Billy Maclure, who has information about...",sec={{t="A Bitter Pie",b="The old feud between the Stonefields and Maclures leaves little room for kindness. Auntie Bernice Stonefield baked a pork belly pie because Billy Maclure would not share what he knew about her family heirloom without it. She hands you the pie with plain irritation and hopes Billy chokes on every bite.",sp=0},{t="A Boy's Bribe",b="At the Maclure Vineyards, across the road, Billy Maclure waits hungry and unable to remember what happened to the necklace. The rivalry between the two homesteads reaches even their children, who barter gossip and stolen trinkets for farm treats. With the pie delivered, Billy's memory returns, and the search for the necklace's true location can begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this delivery?",a="Billy Maclure says he knows where Auntie Bernice Stonefield's lost necklace is, but he will not talk until you bring him a home-cooked pork belly pie. Delivering the pie meets his demand so he will reveal where the heirloom went.",al={"why deliver pie","what does billy want","back to billy goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Auntie Bernice so upset with Billy?",a="The Stonefield and Maclure families have been locked in a bitter rural feud for years. Bernice resents cooking a treat for a troublesome Maclure child to recover an heirloom that went missing on their borders.",al={"why does bernice hate billy","stonefield maclure fight","why tell him to choke"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Billy say the necklace actually is?",a="After eating the pie, Billy reveals that he did not keep the necklace. It fell into the hands of Goldtooth, a notorious kobold in the Fargodeep Mine.",al={"where is the necklace","who took the necklace","goldtooth connection"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Billy Maclure located?",a="Billy Maclure is at the Maclure Vineyards, just south of the road in central Elwynn Forest, opposite the Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who baked the Pork Belly Pie?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield baked the pie at the Stonefield Farm after you gathered fresh chunks of boar meat from the nearby wilderness.",al={"who made the pie","pie cook"},it="origin"},{q="Does this quest resolve the feud between the families?",a="No. Delivering the pie satisfies Billy's personal bribe, while the deep animosity between the adult Stonefields and Maclures remains.",al={"does the feud end","stonefield maclure peace"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice send an outsider to deal with Billy?",a="The bitter feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures makes direct contact between the families nearly impossible. Auntie Bernice cannot bear to step foot on Maclure land herself—let alone cater in person to an obnoxious child demanding food in exchange for stolen property. A passing traveler offers a neutral courier who can walk across the road, deliver the pie, and pry the truth out of young Billy without sparking an outright brawl between the neighboring clans.",al={"why send me back to billy","why not bernice herself","why does auntie bernice need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="6d42dc77"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find that even peaceful Elwynn Forest has disputes between human farmsteads. Helping local folk often means dealing with these quarrels.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know pork belly pie as a comforting Elwynn farmhouse dish made from meat of the forest's roaming wild boars."},kw={"back to billy","bernice stonefield","billy maclure","elwynn forest","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield farm","stonefield necklace"},rel={"npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","quest:86","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},m={start="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",["end"]="Billy Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=84},src={"Back to Billy"}}
E["quest:85"] = {t="quest",n="Lost Necklace",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn, Bernice Stonefield searches for her missing necklace. She suspects Billy Maclure, the young son of the neighboring family, and asks you to find him across the road.",h="In southern Elwynn, Bernice Stonefield searches for her missing necklace.",sec={{t="A Neighborly Accusation",b="The Stonefield and Maclure families live on adjoining land in southern Elwynn Forest, but they share little goodwill. When \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield discovers her cherished necklace is gone, she blames the youngest Maclure. Certain that Billy Maclure slipped onto her farm and took it, the bitter widow asks you to cross the road to the vineyards, find the boy, and demand its return.",sp=0},{t="A Boy with an Appetite",b="At the neighboring vineyard, Billy Maclure denies taking the necklace and insists he is no thief. With a knowing grin, he hints that he may know what became of it. First, he wants someone to satisfy his hunger with a fresh pork pie.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield?",a="Auntie Bernice Stonefield is an elderly widow who lives on Stonefield Farm in southern Elwynn Forest. She distrusts the neighboring Maclure family, especially their troublemaking young son, Billy.",al={"who is auntie bernice","bernice stonefield","who gives lost necklace"},it="identity"},{q="Did Billy Maclure actually steal the necklace?",a="Billy Maclure adamantly denies stealing the necklace. He hints that he knows who took it, but won't share what he knows until someone feeds him.",al={"is billy a thief","did billy steal it","did billy take the necklace"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Where can I find Billy Maclure?",a="You can find Billy Maclure among the grapevines at Maclure Vineyards, just east across the road from Stonefield Farm.",al={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy maclure"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Stonefields and Maclures dislike each other?",a="The neighboring Stonefield and Maclure families have been caught in a bitter rural feud for years. Property, pride, and old personal grudges keep tensions high, so each side suspects the worst of the other.",al={"family feud","stonefield maclure feud","why do they hate each other"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after talking to Billy Maclure?",a="Billy says he is too hungry to remember where the necklace went. He sends you back to Auntie Bernice to bake him a pork pie in exchange for the information.",al={"what next","after lost necklace","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel through southern Elwynn Forest between Stonefield Farm and the adjacent Maclure Vineyards.",al={"quest zone","where is lost necklace"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice want her necklace back?",a="Auntie Bernice is an elderly widow, and the necklace is a deeply cherished personal possession. Losing it distresses her, and she immediately suspects the rival family next door—specifically young Billy Maclure—of snatching it. Recovering the heirloom would bring peace of mind and warm an old widow's heart.",al={"why does bernice want the necklace","bernice necklace motive","stonefield necklace importance"},it="motive",add="b7900c48"},{q="Why doesn't Auntie Bernice confront Billy Maclure herself?",a="The bitter feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures makes it nearly impossible for either side to speak civilly without igniting a brawl. Bernice cannot simply walk over to the Maclure Vineyards herself, and Stormwind's guards are far too stretched dealing with gnolls and Defias bandits to arbitrate petty squabbles between neighboring farmers. A passing adventurer offers a neutral party who can question the boy directly.",al={"why does bernice need me","why send an adventurer to billy","why not ask stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="27b02d6f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance novice in Elwynn Forest, you get a taste of local frontier life by settling a petty dispute between the squabbling Stonefield and Maclure families.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see that strife in the Kingdom of Stormwind comes not only from Defias outlaws and gnoll warbands. Old quarrels between rural neighbors run deep, too."},kw={"bernice","billy","elwynn","farm","maclure","necklace","stonefield","vineyards"},rel={"npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","npc:billy-maclure","quest:86","subzone:maclure-vineyards","zone:elwynn"},m={start="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",["end"]="Billy Maclure",faction="Alliance",id=85},src={"Lost Necklace"}}
E["quest:86"] = {t="quest",n="Pie for Billy",z="elwynn",s="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace has left Billy Maclure bargaining for a pork belly pie. The Stonefield and Maclure families have feuded for generations, and Billy will say who has the necklace only after he gets his pie.",h="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace has left Billy Maclure bargaining for a pork belly pie.",sec={{t="A Boy's Bribe",b="Billy Maclure gives no apology when asked about Auntie Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace. He will not return it or say who has it until he gets a freshly baked pork belly pie. He knows Bernice is the finest cook in the valley, and he means to enjoy the bargain.",sp=0},{t="Baking Through Bad Blood",b="The Maclures and Stonefields have traded insults, brawls, and accusations across their pumpkin patches for generations. Bernice is furious at the thought of feeding the boy she believes stole her family's jewelry, yet she agrees to bake. You gather tender meat from the wild boars roaming the nearby pastures, and she sets aside her pride to get her prized necklace back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Billy want a pie before talking?",a="Billy Maclure knows where Auntie Bernice's necklace is and uses that knowledge to bargain for food. He will not say who has it until he gets one of Bernice's pork belly pies.",al={"why billy wants pie","billy bribe pie","billy pork belly pie"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Auntie Bernice agree to bake for a thief?",a="Auntie Bernice is furious at the boy she believes stole her necklace, but she sees no other way to recover it. She agrees to bake once you bring her boar meat, putting the return of her property ahead of her pride.",al={"why does bernice bake","bernice stonefield pie reason","stonefield baking for maclure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the meat for the pie come from?",a="The meat comes from wild boars foraging in the meadows and along the edges of the Stonefield and Maclure farms in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where to get meat","tender boar meat source"},it="item"},{q="What is the history between the Stonefields and Maclures?",a="The Stonefield and Maclure families are neighboring farmers with a bitter rivalry that has lasted for years. They suspect each other of theft, vandalism, and bad-faith squabbling across their property lines.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","farm rivalry","maclure vs stonefield"},it="conflict"},{q="Did Billy actually steal the necklace?",a="Auntie Bernice accuses Billy directly. He avoids a straight confession, but clearly knows where the necklace ended up and uses that knowledge to bargain for food.",al={"did billy steal necklace","who took necklace","billy necklace thief"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Bernice gets the meat?",a="When you bring her the tender boar meat, Auntie Bernice bakes a pork belly pie for you to take to Billy. She hopes he will then reveal who has her necklace.",al={"next step after pie","what follows pie for billy"},it="next_step"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Auntie Bernice says wild boar meat can be tough and bland, but proper spices and a slow simmer make it exceptional savory pie filling.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the stubborn, insular rivalries of Elwynn's rural homesteaders, just south of Stormwind's gates."},kw={"bernice stonefield","billy maclure","elwynn forest","lost necklace","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield farm","tender boar meat"},rel={"quest:85","quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Billy Maclure",["end"]="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=86,ri={"Tender Boar Meat"}},src={"Pie for Billy"}}
E["quest:8649"] = {t="quest",n="Stormbrow the Elder",z="elwynn",s="Near Goldshire, Stormbrow the Elder waits beside the water during the Lunar Festival. Travelers honor ancient traditions and the olden races of Azeroth, and receive a token of remembrance in return.",h="Near Goldshire, Stormbrow the Elder waits beside the water during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Goldshire",b="A quiet pond lies just behind the smithy in Goldshire, where Stormbrow the Elder appears. Guards, tradesfolk, and weary travelers pass through town on their way into the forest. Beneath Elwynn Forest's canopy, the honored spirit welcomes anyone who comes to honor the realm's long history.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of great ancestors return to walk among the living. Stormbrow the Elder commends travelers who remember those who came before. For honoring the wisdom and legacy of the elder peoples, he grants a blessing and a commemorative coin for the season.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Stormbrow?",a="You can find Stormbrow the Elder beside the pond just behind the blacksmith's forge in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"stormbrow location","where is elder stormbrow","goldshire elder"}},{q="Who is Elder Stormbrow?",a="Stormbrow the Elder is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival and represents the revered elders of Azeroth's olden races.",al={"who is stormbrow","stormbrow lore","elder stormbrow identity"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Stormbrow?",a="Travelers visit Stormbrow the Elder to honor ancient ancestors during the festival. He offers greetings and a token of appreciation in return.",al={"why visit stormbrow","elder stormbrow quest","stormbrow the elder purpose"}},{q="Can Horde players speak to Elder Stormbrow?",a="The Lunar Festival elders honor all who seek them in peace, but Goldshire is heavily guarded Alliance territory, making a visit perilous for Horde travelers.",al={"horde stormbrow","can horde visit stormbrow"}},{q="What token does the Elder offer?",a="Stormbrow the Elder offers a Coin of Ancestry, a traditional token of respect and remembrance shared by elders throughout the festival.",al={"stormbrow reward","what token","lunar coin stormbrow"}},{q="Why does Stormbrow mention the 'olden races'?",a="Stormbrow commends travelers for remembering that present civilizations walk lands shaped by ancient peoples and enduring customs, long before the modern kingdoms arose.",al={"olden races meaning","why olden races","stormbrow dialogue"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human living in Elwynn, you can look to Stormbrow the Elder as a reminder of ancient history beyond Stormwind's walls and its recent wars.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler passing through Goldshire, you can find Stormbrow the Elder in the heart of Elwynn Forest, among the most accessible ancestral spirits for young adventurers."},kw={"ancestor","elder stormbrow","elwynn forest","forge","goldshire","lunar festival","token"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Elder Stormbrow",id=8649},src={"Stormbrow the Elder"}}
E["quest:87"] = {t="quest",n="Goldtooth",z="elwynn",s="Near Fargodeep Mine, Auntie Bernice Stonefield's necklace is missing, and the Stonefield and Maclure families blame each other. Billy Maclure admits he lost it while playing nearby, and you follow the trail to the kobold Goldtooth.",h="Near Fargodeep Mine, Auntie Bernice Stonefield's necklace is missing, and the Stonefield and Maclure families...",sec={{t="A Boy's Mischief",b="Auntie Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace has stirred up trouble between the Stonefield and Maclure families. Bernice suspects her rivals, but Billy Maclure lost the trinket while playing near Fargodeep Mine. He tries to hide his guilt, saying he only found the necklace before a creature snatched it away.",sp=0},{t="The Den Above the Mine",b="Billy says a large kobold with gleaming fangs took the shiny necklace and ran to a den above Fargodeep Mine. Goldtooth actually lurks on the mine's lower level. Slaying the kobold brings Bernice's necklace back, settles the families' dispute, and earns you an old campaign keepsake left by Bernice's late husband.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who stole Auntie Bernice's necklace?",a="Billy Maclure most likely took Auntie Bernice's necklace. He lets slip that he lost it while playing near Fargodeep Mine, then says he only found it there. Before he could retrieve it, Goldtooth the kobold grabbed the shiny trinket.",al={"who stole necklace","who took the necklace","did maclures steal necklace"},sp=1},{q="Where can Goldtooth be found?",a="Goldtooth lurks on the lower level inside Fargodeep Mine, though Billy says the kobold's den is above the mine.",al={"goldtooth location","where is goldtooth","find goldtooth"},gp=true},{q="What kind of creature is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is an oversized kobold with a gleaming golden fang. Like other kobolds, he is drawn to bright, shiny trinkets.",al={"what is goldtooth","is goldtooth a kobold"},it="target"},{q="How does this quest tie into the Maclure and Stonefield feud?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures are bitter rivals who blame each other for petty thefts and misfortunes. Auntie Bernice suspects the Maclures took her necklace out of spite, but the search reveals Billy lost it through carelessness.",al={"stonefield maclure drama","why does bernice blame billy"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What is the reward from Auntie Bernice?",a="Auntie Bernice gives you an old keepsake that belonged to her late husband. She says it was lucky, but he forgot to take it on his final military campaign.",al={"bernice reward","what do you get"},gp=true},{q="What quest leads directly into Goldtooth?",a="Back to Billy leads directly into Goldtooth. You bribe Billy Maclure with pork, and he finally confesses what happened to the necklace.",al={"goldtooth prereq","quest before goldtooth"},gp=true},{q="Why does Billy Maclure want Bernice's necklace back?",a="Billy accidentally dropped Auntie Bernice's necklace while playing near the Fargodeep Mine, though he is desperate to deny stealing it. He knows he is in serious trouble if it remains lost, especially given the fierce feud between the Maclures and the Stonefields. Having you recover it from the kobold lets him set things right without directly facing Bernice's wrath.",al={"billy maclure motive","why does billy want the necklace","why help billy maclure"},it="motive",add="36c74007"},{q="What is Bernice's Necklace?",a="Bernice's Necklace is a cherished family heirloom belonging to \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield. After going missing amidst the bitter rivalry between the Stonefield and Maclure families, it ended up snatched away by a greedy kobold. Its value is largely sentimental to Bernice, who desperately wants it returned home to the Stonefield Farm.",al={"bernices necklace","what is auntie bernices necklace","bernice necklace use"},it="item",add="b7400482"},{q="Why does Billy ask you instead of the guards?",a="Billy is just a frightened child hiding his guilt, and calling upon the Stormwind guards would expose that he took or mishandled Bernice Stonefield's jewelry in the first place. Furthermore, the local guards are already stretched thin dealing with Defias bandits and gnolls throughout Elwynn Forest, making them unlikely to hunt down an aggressive kobold over an old lady's lost necklace.",al={"why me billy","why not stormwind guards","why does billy need help"},it="why_me",add="4539d353"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you help ease friction between two of Elwynn's oldest farming families and face the kobolds that plague the realm."},kw={"bernice","billy","fargodeep","goldtooth","kobold","maclure","necklace","stonefield"},rel={"quest:84","npc:billy-maclure","npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:stonefield-farm","topic:kobold","quest:62","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Billy Maclure",["end"]="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",faction="Alliance",id=87,ri={"Bernice's Necklace"}},src={"Goldtooth (quest)"}}
E["quest:88"] = {t="quest",n="Princess Must Die!",z="elwynn",s="At Stonefield Farm, Ma Stonefield wants Princess Must Die! before Princess ruins the harvest. The enormous prize-winning sow from Brackwell Pumpkin Patch keeps raiding the Stonefields’ vegetables, and Ma wants the family to gather their crops in peace.",h="At Stonefield Farm, Ma Stonefield wants Princess Must Die!",sec={{t="A Menace to the Harvest",b="Princess has put the Stonefield harvest at risk. The prize-winning sow belongs to the Brackwells, but she has grown enormous by crossing onto the Stonefield plots and devouring their vegetables. Ma Stonefield has had enough of the sow eating the crops she worked to grow. She wants Princess put down before the pig ruins the season’s yield.",sp=0},{t="The Porcine Entourage",b="Princess does not roam alone. At Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, east beyond the Maclure homestead, protective boars surround her. To prove the sow will trouble the Stonefield fields no more, you need to get past her guards and bring back the distinctive brass collar from her neck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Princess?",a="Princess is an enormous, prize-winning sow belonging to the Brackwell family. She grew so large by sneaking onto Stonefield Farm and gorging on Ma Stonefield’s vegetables.",al={"what is princess","princess elwynn","who is the pig princess"},it="target"},{q="Why does Ma Stonefield want Princess killed?",a="Princess keeps wandering into Ma Stonefield’s fields and devouring the vegetables. Ma fears the sow will eat the family’s entire harvest, so she hires travelers to slay Princess and bring back her brass collar as proof.",al={"why kill princess","ma stonefield pig quest","why does princess must die"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Princess be found?",a="Princess can be found at Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest, east beyond the Maclure Vineyards. She roams among the ruined pumpkins with boars guarding her.",al={"princess location","where is princess","princess spawn"},gp=true},{q="Who owns the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The Brackwell family owns Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Bandits and wild beasts have brought hard times to the local farmers and their lands in southern Elwynn Forest. Though the family has neglected the patch, Princess stayed behind to gorge on what remained.",al={"who are the brackwells","brackwell farm lore","brackwell owners"}},{q="How do you prove Princess is dead?",a="To prove Princess is dead, bring the Brass Collar from around her neck to Ma Stonefield at Stonefield Farm.",al={"princess proof","what item for princess","brass collar"},gp=true},{q="Does Princess fight alone?",a="No. Defensive boars called the Porcine Entourage accompany Princess and attack anyone who tries to slay the prize sow.",al={"princess adds","princess entourage","princess guards"},gp=true},{q="What is the Brass Collar for?",a="Princess is a prized domestic sow, marked by the brass collar fastened around her thick neck. Ma Stonefield asks you to tear it off her carcass and bring it back as undeniable proof that the gluttonous beast has been put down before she can ravage the Stonefield vegetable patches again.",al={"brass collar purpose","why take princess collar","princess collar"},it="item",add="f51dd6ea"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Princess’s great size has become a tale among local cooks. Elwynn’s oversized boars yield plenty of hearty meat for roasting over an open fire.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help farmers like Ma Stonefield keep rogue beasts from threatening Stormwind’s southern breadbasket, even while the kingdom’s formal army is absent."},kw={"boar","brackwell pumpkin patch","brass collar","elwynn","ma stonefield","princess","sow","stonefield farm"},rel={"npc:ma-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Ma Stonefield",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=88,ri={"Brass Collar"}},src={"Princess Must Die! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:92124"] = {t="quest",n="Book Inventory",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton is frustrated by misplaced and missing tomes. He asks young adventurers to find Daniel, his daydreaming assistant, and take stock of the library archives, but Daniel's thoughts keep wandering to local tradeskills, making a straight answer hard to get.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton is frustrated by misplaced and missing tomes.",sec={{t="A Librarian's Frustration",b="Northshire Abbey preserves old scholarly works, spiritual writings, and historical records that survived the First War in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Brother Paxton, a meticulous monk, takes great pride in the collection. Lately, books have gone missing from the shelves, and Paxton needs a clear inventory to learn how widespread the loss is. He has little patience to chase after his daydreaming helper.",sp=0},{t="Daniel's Straying Interests",b="Daniel works as Brother Paxton's assistant in the abbey library, but his thoughts rarely stay with parchment and catalog numbers. He is fascinated by the practical trades of Elwynn Forest: smithing, leatherworking, tailoring, and herbal craft. Paxton grows exasperated as inventory work leads Daniel to ramble about local crafters instead of locating lost scriptures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a monk of Northshire Abbey who tends its extensive collection of books, scriptures, and historical scrolls. He takes pride in the collection and is quick to lose his temper when books go missing or helpers shirk their duties.",al={"brother paxton","who gives book inventory","paxton elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Daniel?",a="Daniel is Brother Paxton's young assistant in the Northshire Abbey library. He is tasked with organizing books and conducting inventories, though his thoughts often turn to tradeskills and professions across Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is daniel","paxton assistant","daniel northshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why are books missing from Northshire Abbey?",a="Brother Paxton says books have gone missing but does not explain why. He asks Daniel to inventory the collection and determine how much has been lost.",al={"why are books missing","missing books northshire","lost books abbey"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can Daniel be found?",a="Daniel is inside Northshire Abbey, among the shelves and desks of the abbey library.",al={"where is daniel","daniel location","find daniel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Paxton call Daniel useless?",a="Paxton considers Daniel useless because he neglects his archival duties. Instead of cataloging and shelving books, Daniel spends his hours daydreaming and talking about practical tradeskills.",al={"why does paxton hate daniel","daniel useless"},it="ties"},{q="What tradeskills is Daniel interested in?",a="Daniel is fascinated by crafts practiced throughout Elwynn Forest, such as blacksmithing, leatherworking, and tailoring. He prefers hands-on labor to dusty tomes.",al={"daniel tradeskills","what professions does daniel like"}},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want a book inventory done?",a="Northshire Abbey has noticed books disappearing from its shelves, and Brother Paxton needs to determine the full scale of the loss before the abbey's collection suffers further. His assistant, Daniel, is supposed to keep the library in order, but his constant daydreaming about local trades has left Paxton frustrated and completely in the dark about how many volumes have actually gone missing.",al={"why book inventory","why does paxton want an inventory","paxton motive"},it="motive",add="deb80ab5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a young human beginning service at Northshire Abbey, you may know the struggle to balance monastic study with practical village life.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest studying Northshire's sacred archives, you rely on order in the library to preserve holy scriptures and Church traditions."},kw={"book inventory","brother paxton","daniel","elwynn forest","library","northshire abbey","professions","tradeskills"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:344"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Daniel",level="2",id=92124},src={"Book Inventory"},fv=true}
E["quest:94"] = {t="quest",n="A Watchful Eye",z="elwynn",s="Theocritus watches Morganth from the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. He sends travelers east into Redridge Mountains to place an enchanted glyph at an old lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar.",h="Theocritus watches Morganth from the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Rivalry Across the Border",b="Theocritus watches the hills from his tower in eastern Elwynn Forest. His rival, Morganth, is a powerful sorcerer who has claimed the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge Mountains. Theocritus fears Morganth's dark magic may cross the border, so he made the Eye of Azora to watch the rogue wizard from afar.",sp=0},{t="The Lion's Vigil",b="Theocritus needs more than a distant view to learn what Morganth plans. He gives travelers the Glyph of Azora and sends them to the Old Lion Statue near the Tower of Ilgalar. The statue has kept watch there for decades. Set the glyph into the worn hollow at its base, and an arcane link reaches back to Azora, letting Theocritus look into his rival's mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Theocritus is an Alliance wizard who lives in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He studies magic to guard the region from rogue spellcasters, especially Morganth.",al={"theocritus","tower of azora mage","who gives a watchful eye"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Morganth?",a="Morganth is a rogue human wizard who has made the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge Mountains his stronghold. He is Theocritus's bitter rival, and Theocritus fears the schemes he is making against the surrounding lands.",al={"morganth","who is morganth","rival mage"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Old Lion Statue located?",a="The Old Lion Statue stands on the ridges overlooking the Tower of Ilgalar in the eastern hills of Redridge Mountains. A shallow hollow at its base can hold the Glyph of Azora.",al={"lion statue location","where is the statue","where to put glyph of azora"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the Glyph of Azora do?",a="The Glyph of Azora is an enchanted stone made by Theocritus. Set in the lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar, it carries his arcane listening spell and lets him study Morganth's thoughts.",al={"glyph of azora","what is the glyph"},it="item"},{q="What is the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is an isolated stone tower high in the crags of eastern Redridge Mountains. Morganth and his servants occupy and defend it.",al={"tower of ilgalar","ilgalar"},it="threat"},{q="What comes after placing the glyph?",a="After the Glyph of Azora is set in the statue, Theocritus speaks through the stone and offers Looking Further. He begins to uncover Morganth's plans.",al={"next quest","what after a watchful eye"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Theocritus want this done?",a="Morganth is a ruthless mage of formidable power holed up in the Tower of Ilgalar. While Theocritus can view his rival using the scrying magic of the Eye of Azora, seeing him is no longer enough. By affixing the Glyph of Azora to the nearby lion statue, Theocritus hopes to penetrate Morganth's mind and discover what the dark wizard is plotting before he unleashes it upon the region.",al={"theocritus motive","why place the glyph of azora","why spy on morganth"},it="motive",add="0c307b8a"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see how arcane divination can reach across a great distance. Theocritus uses methods from Elwynn, while Morganth practices rogue sorcery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help guard the border between Elwynn Forest and the embattled settlements of Redridge Mountains from rogue human spellcasters like Morganth."},kw={"elwynn","glyph of azora","morganth","old lion statue","redridge","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"quest:178","quest:248","quest:249","npc:theocritus","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Theocritus",["end"]="Old Lion Statue",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=94},src={"A Watchful Eye"}}
E["quest:96607"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="elwynn",s="You learn how rest and preparation help you survive beyond city walls. Travelers across Azeroth teach new wanderers to rest by a campfire and prepare for the wilds.",h="You learn how rest and preparation help you survive beyond city walls.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Trail",b="Even a sharp blade or potent magic cannot protect you from the wilds if you neglect the basics of survival. Seasoned wanderers near roadside clearings share this lesson with travelers leaving their home valleys. Resting by a campfire eases sore boots, settles the mind, and readies you for the road ahead. Regular rest and preparation give you a better chance of surviving long enough to find fortune and glory.",sp=0},{t="A Home Away from Home",b="Once you understand the value of a fire and proper rest, your instructors point you toward town tradesfolk. A field camp needs more than an ember and a bedroll; survival also calls for practical crafts. You can forge replacement rivets, cook trail rations, or stitch torn gear under the stars. Each profession offers camp fixtures that can help turn a bare hillside into a self-sufficient outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this lesson to new wanderers?",a="Veteran travelers offer the lesson, with the instructor depending on where you are. In Elwynn Forest, Sam Sarsaparilla teaches it; elsewhere, instructors include Eric Brighthammer, Lyreena Duskblade, Brakk, Eleanor Shackleton, Kaga Wildhoof, and Raan Wildwind.",al={"who gives the great outdoors","who starts the great outdoors","quest giver great outdoors"}},{q="What is the purpose of sitting by the campfire?",a="Resting by a campfire lets you catch your breath and gain a Boosted Rest effect. Taking time to rest in the field helps you keep your strength during long journeys through the wilds.",al={"why sit by the fire","what does campfire do","boosted rest buff"}},{q="Where does this training lead next?",a="After you rest by the fire, your mentor sends you to nearby settlements to learn practical tradeskills. You can then learn Camping 101: Cooking and field camping lessons suited to the profession you choose.",al={"what comes after great outdoors","great outdoors next quest","camping quests"}},{q="Can Horde adventurers undertake this lesson as well?",a="Yes. Survival matters to adventurers of either faction. Instructors from the Alliance and the Horde, including Brakk, Eleanor Shackleton, and Kaga Wildhoof, teach the same basic campcraft to their initiates.",al={"is this alliance only","horde great outdoors","can orcs do this quest"}},{q="Why do the instructors tell you to speak with trade trainers?",a="Survival takes more than sitting by the fire; you also need self-reliance. Tradeskill trainers teach you to make camp fixtures for your trade, whether you cook trail rations, mend armor, or brew remedies beneath the open sky.",al={"why learn professions","camp fixtures trade trainers","profession camp connection"}},{q="What prior experience is expected before taking this quest?",a="You typically receive this lesson after 'The Adventurer', once you have shown basic ambition and left your starter enclave for the wider region.",al={"prerequisites for the great outdoors","how do i unlock great outdoors","before great outdoors"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Every wilderness camp begins with fire, so cooking belongs naturally beside outdoor survival. After this lesson, your instructors direct you to cooking lessons along the trail.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Elwynn Forest, human travelers learn survival basics from experienced wayfarers before facing the harsher threats in Westfall and Redridge.",["faction:Horde"]="Across Durotar's arid plains and Mulgore's windswept mesas, Horde survivalists teach young warriors firecraft and discipline in the outdoors."},kw={"adventurer","boosted rest","campfire","camping","eleanor shackleton","elwynn forest","sam sarsaparilla","survival","tradeskill"},rel={"quest:96627","quest:96658","npc:eleanor-shackleton","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Varies",level="6",faction="Both",id=96607},src={"The Great Outdoors (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:96627"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends The Adventurer toward Goldshire to find Sam Sarsaparilla. You have shown your skill defending the abbey, and McBride wants you to look into the newcomer.",h="In Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends The Adventurer toward Goldshire to find Sam Sarsaparilla.",sec={{t="Leaving the Valley",b="As threats from the local Defias and vermin ease, Marshal McBride turns his attention to the road beyond Northshire Valley. Stormwind's regular forces are stretched thin across the kingdom, so the local garrison relies on promising fighters to watch travelers and wanderers in the surrounding woods.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Newcomer",b="Marshal McBride asks you to check on Sam Sarsaparilla, a newcomer spotted near Goldshire. It is an unusual request, not a military order or a bounty hunt, and it leads you from Northshire's secluded valley into the wider wilds of Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this task?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of Stormwind's garrison in Northshire Valley, sends you after you prove your mettle defending the abbey.",al={"quest giver","who gives the adventurer","marshal mcbride quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Sam Sarsaparilla?",a="Sam Sarsaparilla is an adventurer near the road by Goldshire. Marshal McBride hears he is there and asks you to find out what he is doing.",al={"sam sarsaparilla","who is sam","goldshire adventurer"},it="target"},{q="Where do I find Sam Sarsaparilla?",a="Sam Sarsaparilla is along the main road south from Northshire toward Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.",al={"sam sarsaparilla location","where is sam","find sam sarsaparilla"},gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal McBride care about a random adventurer?",a="Northshire remains on alert for bandits and intruders. McBride keeps watch on unfamiliar sellswords and wanderers passing through, and trusts dependable locals to make first contact.",al={"why send me","mcbride motives","why look for sam"},it="motive"},{q="Do I need to leave Northshire Valley to finish this?",a="Yes. You leave Northshire Valley through its southern gates and follow the forest road toward Goldshire.",al={"outside northshire","does this leave northshire","go to goldshire"},gp=true},{q="Is this part of the normal Stormwind military chain of command?",a="Marshal McBride is a Stormwind officer, but he calls this an unusual assignment rather than standard guard duty. He relies on your judgment as an independent protector, outside formal military protocol.",al={"stormwind military","is this standard duty","official business"}},{q="Why does Marshal McBride choose me to investigate Sam?",a="Marshal McBride considers this an unusual task rather than standard garrison duty. Having watched you deal with Northshire's local threats, he views you as a capable protector who can operate discreetly beyond the abbey gates. With his own garrison stretched thin dealing with local troubles, sending a trusted recruit to look into rumors down the road makes far more sense than dispatching regular guards.",al={"why me marshal mcbride","why does mcbride send me","why not send a guard to sam"},it="why_me",add="dd262048"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For new Alliance recruits finishing their service in Northshire, this is the first official step into the wider realm of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human defender leaving Northshire Abbey, you take your first steps toward Goldshire, the heart of Elwynn."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","marshal mcbride","northshire","sam sarsaparilla","the adventurer"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Marshal McBride",["end"]="Sam Sarsaparilla",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=96627},src={"The Adventurer (Elwynn Forest)"},fv=true}
E["quest:96658"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="elwynn",s="At nearby settlements, new adventurers learn to cook and kindle a Basic Campfire for life in the wild. The lesson is offered across Alliance and Horde lands.",h="At nearby settlements, new adventurers learn to cook and kindle a Basic Campfire for life in the wild.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wilderness",b="Every traveler needs to know how to build a fire beyond the safety of fortified walls. A campfire can boil water and roast meat, and it anchors a campsite in unfamiliar country.",sp=0},{t="From Embers to Encampments",b="Apprentice cooks can kindle only modest fires with few surroundings. Greater skill in cooking lets them light larger fires that support more elaborate campsites. Other practical trades also teach ways to make useful furnishings for a camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="New adventurers visit a cooking trainer in a nearby settlement to learn basic cooking and light a campfire that anchors an outdoor campsite.",al={"why do camping 101","camping 101 cooking purpose","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who offers this quest to travelers?",a="Experienced wilderness guides and adventurers offer this training across both factions, including Eleanor Shackleton, Eric Brighthammer, Lyreena Duskblade, Sam Sarsaparilla, Brakk, Kaga Wildhoof, and Raan Wildwind.",al={"who gives camping 101","camping quest giver"}},{q="Where do Alliance players turn this in?",a="Alliance adventurers report to trainers in their home territories, such as Tomas in Goldshire, Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos, or Zarrin in Dolanaar.",al={"where to turn in alliance","alliance cooking trainer"}},{q="Where do Horde players turn this in?",a="Horde adventurers can learn with Cook Torka in Razor Hill, William Pickman in Brill, or Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village.",al={"horde cooking trainer","where to turn in horde"}},{q="Can campsite size be expanded later?",a="Yes. Greater cooking skill teaches you to kindle larger fires that support more camp furnishings in the wild.",al={"bigger campfire","improve camp"}},{q="Can other professions contribute to camping?",a="Yes. Cooking provides the campfire, while other tradeskill trainers offer ways to craft practical furnishings if you have practiced their crafts.",al={"camping professions","campsite furnishings"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking provides food to restore strength and the campfire at the heart of an outdoor camp.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer leaving Northshire, Dun Morogh, or Teldrassil, you are guided toward towns like Goldshire, Kharanos, and Dolanaar to learn self-reliance before braving the wilds.",["faction:Horde"]="As a young Horde fighter in Durotar, Mulgore, or Tirisfal, you are directed toward campfires in Razor Hill, Bloodhoof Village, or Brill."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","cooking","goldshire","shackleton","tomas","wilderness","zarrin"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","subzone:kharanos","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:bloodhoof-village","subzone:brill","subzone:dolanaar","npc:eleanor-shackleton","npc:zarrin"},m={start="Varies",level="6",faction="Both",id=96658},src={"Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97919"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="elwynn",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Michelle Belle shows travelers how to prepare for camp. In Goldshire, you can learn to make a First Aid Kit for the road ahead.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn, Michelle Belle shows travelers how to prepare for camp.",sec={{t="Field Medicine on the Road",b="Travel across Elwynn Forest can leave you wounded, far from a town healer or inn. First Aid lets you tend your own injuries and care for yourself without relying on others. Bandages offer help with bleeding and trauma, without arcane rituals or holy supplication.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Campsite",b="A campsite offers a place to rest amid the dangers of the wild. At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Michelle Belle teaches skilled practitioners to assemble First Aid Kits. Keep medical supplies at camp so a weary party can treat injuries and regain strength before facing the perils ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Adventurers who have learned basic First Aid seek Michelle Belle in Goldshire. She teaches them to make a First Aid Kit and stock a wilderness camp with medical supplies.",al={"camping first aid purpose","what does this quest do","why camping 101 first aid"}},{q="Who do I need to speak with in Goldshire?",a="Speak with Michelle Belle, a First Aid trainer in Goldshire. Once you demonstrate sufficient skill, she teaches you techniques for making camping supplies suited to field medicine.",al={"who is michelle belle","camping trainer goldshire","first aid camp trainer"}},{q="Why is First Aid important for travelers?",a="First Aid helps travelers tend injuries from beasts, bandits, and harsh elements. It lets anyone, whether or not they wield divine or arcane magic, bandage wounds and recover between skirmishes.",al={"why learn first aid","is first aid useful","first aid lore"}},{q="Where is Goldshire located?",a="Goldshire is the primary hamlet in Elwynn Forest, just south of Stormwind City along the main trade road. It is a central hub for supplies and local trainers, with respite at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"where is goldshire","goldshire location","how to find michelle belle"}},{q="Do I need prior training to complete this task?",a="Yes. Michelle Belle asks you to demonstrate proficiency in First Aid before teaching you to make camp kits.",al={"requirements camping 101","first aid skill needed","prerequisites"}},{q="How does a First Aid Kit fit into camping?",a="A wilderness campsite provides a safe perimeter to recuperate. A First Aid Kit keeps bandages and remedies close at hand, supplies necessary to save lives far from town healers.",al={"camp first aid kit use","camping item first aid","why make a first aid kit"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Goldshire is a vital crossroads for Alliance travelers heading from Northshire into Elwynn.",["class:Warrior"]="Without innate healing spells, you as a warrior rely on bandages and field kits to endure long campaigns in the wild.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue operating in the shadows far from support, you depend on field medicine to bandage bleeding gashes before moving on to your next mark."},kw={"bandages","camp kit","camping 101","elwynn forest","first aid","goldshire","michelle belle","survival"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={level="6",id=97919},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97920"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, novice anglers seek ways to make camp life more comfortable. Near Goldshire, fishing expert Lee Brown teaches travelers how angling can add simple comforts to a campsite.",h="In Elwynn Forest, novice anglers seek ways to make camp life more comfortable.",sec={{t="Campcraft for Anglers",b="Fishing gives you food, but camp life asks for more than food and shelter. A fish bowl can bring comfort and lift the spirits of weary travelers between excursions. Sound minds and high spirits help make formidable fighters.",sp=0},{t="Lee Brown's Expertise",b="Lee Brown waits beside the waters outside Goldshire to help novice fishermen broaden their craft. Travelers who show skill with rod and line can learn how simple catches and basic materials become useful additions to a campsite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Lee Brown near Goldshire directs aspiring fishermen. After you show basic skill at fishing, he teaches you to craft camp items such as a fish bowl for roadside campsites.",al={"why do camping fishing","what does camping 101 do","purpose of quest"}},{q="Who is Lee Brown?",a="Lee Brown is a fishing trainer beside Crystal Lake, just outside Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. He teaches angling and how to make campcraft items for fishermen.",al={"where is lee brown","who teaches fishing camping","lee brown"}},{q="What does a Fish Bowl do for a campsite?",a="A fish bowl brings comfort and joy to a campsite. Pleasant surroundings lift morale and help adventurers feel ready and capable when facing the wilderness.",al={"fish bowl effect","what does fish bowl do","why make a fish bowl"}},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="The training takes place in Elwynn Forest, by the waters around Goldshire where local anglers gather.",al={"quest location","where do i go","elwynn camping trainer"}},{q="Do I need prior skill in fishing to complete this?",a="Yes. Lee Brown teaches travelers who have practiced casting and shown basic skill at fishing.",al={"fishing skill requirement","do i need fishing","proficiency requirement"}},{q="Is camping useful for combat?",a="Yes. A well-kept camp offers comfort that improves an adventurer's physical and mental preparedness, resilience, and effectiveness in combat in the field.",al={"does camping help combat","camping buffs","why camp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a human traveler starting out in Elwynn Forest, you can learn wilderness self-sufficiency beside the familiar waters of Goldshire."},kw={"campcraft","camping 101: fishing","crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish bowl","goldshire","lee brown"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={level="6",id=97920},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch"] = {t="subzone",n="Brackwell Pumpkin Patch",z="elwynn",s="Defias brigands have taken over Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest. The farm once belonged to the Brackwell family, but now its cottage and fields serve as a hideout where conspirators meet and stolen mine gold is received.",h="Defias brigands have taken over Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in southeastern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven",b="You find the Brackwell farm southeast of the Stonefield homestead, its fields no longer tended. The Brackwell family has vanished, driven away or worse as crime spread through the area. The Defias Brotherhood now occupies the sturdy cottage and overgrown fields. Brigands regroup here beyond the reach of Goldshire's patrols. Morgan the Collector and other prominent conspirators use the isolated farm to receive illicit gold taken from the forest's mines.",sp=0},{t="Pigs and Dark Magic",b="The Defias share the pumpkin vines with a giant sow named Princess, left behind by the Brackwells. She roams the patch and terrorizes neighboring fields. The farmhouse attic and outbuildings shelter other dangerous dealings. Bandit Erlan Drudgemoor seduced Surena Caledon, a rogue warlock apprentice who fled her master in Stormwind with a stolen bloodstone artifact. Her presence has drawn dark practitioners to the hideout.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the Brackwell family?",a="No one knows the Brackwell family's exact fate. When the Defias Brotherhood spread across southeastern Elwynn Forest, the family either fled or was killed, leaving its pumpkin fields and farmhouse to the bandits.",al={"where are the brackwells","who lived at brackwell farm","brackwell family fate"},it="ruin"},{q="Why is the Defias Brotherhood using this farm?",a="The farm gives the Defias an isolated base near the forest's borders. They store plundered goods and arrange smuggling there, including shipments of stolen mine gold brought by couriers such as Morgan the Collector, away from the Stormwind Guard.",al={"why are defias here","what are bandits doing at the pumpkin patch","defias at brackwell"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Princess?",a="Princess is an enormous, prize-winning sow raised by the Brackwells. Left behind when the farm fell, she grew larger by repeatedly breaking into nearby Stonefield Farm to eat its prized crops.",al={"giant pig","princess pig","why is there a huge boar here"}},{q="Why do warlocks come to the pumpkin patch?",a="Surena Caledon, apprentice to Stormwind warlock trainer Gakin the Darkbinder, stole a powerful bloodstone choker and fled to the farm with her lover, Defias bandit Erlan Drudgemoor. Gakin sends novice warlocks to kill her and recover the relic.",al={"warlock quest brackwell","surena caledon","gakin voidwalker quest"}},{q="What is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The Brackwell Pumpkin Patch is a Stormwindian farmstead nestled in southeastern Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful agrarian homestead cultivating ripe pumpkins and raising livestock, it has recently fallen into chaos and outlaw hands.",al={"brackwell pumpkin patch","what is this farm","brackwell farm"},it="place",add="f38a2be0"},{q="What happened at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="Formerly a productive family farm, the patch was overrun by the Defias Brotherhood when bandits seized the territory. The Brackwells vanished, and the farm quickly became an outpost for Defias activities, including gold drop-offs and illicit hideouts.",al={"brackwell farm history","what happened here","brackwell lore"},it="history",add="0e932b65"},{q="Who lives in or runs the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="The farm's original owners are gone, and Defias bandits currently occupy the grounds. Among them, figures like Erlan Drudgemoor and his runaway lover Surena Caledon hide out here, while Morgan the Collector utilizes the farm to receive gold shipments from local mines.",al={"who runs brackwell patch","who lives at brackwell","brackwell inhabitants"},it="residents",add="ae1356ee"},{q="Is the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch dangerous?",a="Yes, you should tread carefully. Armed Defias cutpurses patrol the pumpkin fields, alongside the notorious and voracious prize-winning pig, Princess, who aggressively protects her foraging grounds with her porcine escorts.",al={"is brackwell safe","brackwell dangers","is this farm dangerous"},it="danger",add="90becbea"},{q="Why is it called the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch?",a="It is named after the Brackwell family, the human farmers who settled the land and cultivated its distinctive pumpkin fields before bandit raids forced them from their home.",al={"brackwell name origin","why brackwell","who were the brackwells"},it="name",add="43009602"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Surena Caledon, a fugitive apprentice, hides in the farm's shack. Her stolen bloodstone choker is needed to bind a voidwalker.",["faction:Alliance"]="The overrun patch is one of the Defias Brotherhood's easternmost bases in Elwynn, threatening nearby farms and trade routes."},kw={"brackwell","defias","elwynn","erlan drudgemoor","morgan the collector","princess","pumpkin patch","surena caledon"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","quest:123","quest:88","quest:1688","subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:gakin-the-darkbinder"},src={"Brackwell Pumpkin Patch"}}
E["subzone:crystal-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Crystal Lake",z="elwynn",s="East of Goldshire, Crystal Lake draws travelers toward a shore claimed by murlocs. Their attacks make the water a danger to villagers and passersby.",h="East of Goldshire, Crystal Lake draws travelers toward a shore claimed by murlocs.",sec={{t="A Troubled Shore",b="Crystal Lake lies east of Goldshire, within walking distance of the Lion's Pride Inn. Freshwater murlocs now claim its shore and shallow shoals, attacking anyone who comes too close. William Pestle, an alchemist at the inn, hires travelers to drive them back and gather the crystal kelp they carry for his experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Crystal Lake located?",a="Crystal Lake lies east of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest, just past the village outskirts.",al={"crystal lake location","where is crystal lake","find crystal lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?",a="Crystal Lake gives freshwater murlocs a place to nest and forage. Their numbers near Goldshire have grown as Stormwind's local guard struggles to protect the area.",al={"why murlocs crystal lake","murloc problem goldshire","crystal lake murlocs"},it="threat"},{q="What do adventurers need from Crystal Lake?",a="William Pestle, an apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, hires travelers to slay murlocs along the shore and gather crystal kelp for an invisibility potion.",al={"william pestle crystal lake","kelp quest crystal lake","invisibility potion elwynn"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Crystal Lake?",a="Crystal Lake is a freshwater lake lying directly east of Goldshire in the heart of Elwynn Forest. While it might once have been a peaceful watering hole, its tranquil waters have lately become a hotbed of trouble for nearby travelers and townsfolk.",al={"what is crystal lake","crystal lake elwynn","crystal lake lore"},it="place",add="18711dcc"},{q="Is Crystal Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, it can prove deadly to an unwary or inexperienced traveler. The lake's shores and shallows are heavily infested with aggressive murlocs that will attack anyone wandering too close to the water's edge.",al={"how dangerous is crystal lake","is crystal lake safe","crystal lake threats"},it="danger",add="c07536f5"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Crystal Kelp grows in the lake's freshwater shallows. Most of it is gathered from the resident murlocs, who harvest it from the lake bed.",["faction:Alliance"]="The murlocs near Goldshire show how stretched the kingdom's military is in protecting its core territories."},kw={"crystal kelp","crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","murloc","william pestle"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","npc:william-pestle","topic:murloc","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Crystal Lake"}}
E["subzone:eastvale-logging-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastvale Logging Camp",z="elwynn",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, timber orders from Stormwind meet the dangers of Elwynn’s eastern woods. Wolves and bears drive lumberjacks from their work, while the camp keeps timber moving toward Stormwind and nearby settlements.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, timber orders from Stormwind meet the dangers of Elwynn’s eastern woods.",sec={{t="A Vital Operation Under Siege",b="Timber buyers across the Kingdom of Stormwind send orders to Eastvale Logging Camp, each with a strict deadline. Wolves and bears prowl the woods around the work sites, driving lumberjacks away and leaving cut timber behind. Supervisor Raelen directs the camp’s work, and travelers help drive off the beasts and recover the abandoned wood before deliveries fall behind schedule.",sp=0},{t="Life on the Eastern Frontier",b="Eastvale Logging Camp has homes and horse stables where travelers can buy fine mounts. On a nearby hill above the work site, retired Marshal Haggard lives in a quiet manor. He once led the Stormwind Guard and left its service to retire far from the politics of the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the main purpose of Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is the primary timber source in eastern Elwynn Forest for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Its lumberjacks work long hours to meet strict deadlines and supply builders and nobles across the realm.",al={"why is eastvale here","what is eastvale","eastvale lumber role"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the logging camp always hiring adventurers?",a="Wolves and bears menace the workers in the dense woods around Eastvale Logging Camp. Their attacks drive lumberjacks away from cut timber and put orders at risk of missing shipment deadlines.",al={"eastvale problems","why do loggers need help","wolves at eastvale"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is the retired former leader of the Stormwind Guard. He stepped down from service a few years ago and now lives in a peaceful estate on the bluffs above Eastvale Logging Camp.",al={"haggard","old man near eastvale","marshal haggard elwynn"},it="identity"},{q="Can you buy mounts at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Yes. Eastvale Logging Camp’s horse stable sells riding horses and offers riding training.",al={"horse vendor eastvale","eastvale horses","buy mount elwynn"},gp=true},{q="What is Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is a sprawling network of lumber mills, stables, and worker dwellings tucked into the eastern reaches of Elwynn Forest. It serves as a vital economic lifeline for the Kingdom of Stormwind, constantly processing timber to meet strict orders and construction deadlines across the realm.",al={"what is eastvale","eastvale lumber camp","about eastvale logging camp"},it="place",add="ba9b781f"},{q="What happened at Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="The camp was developed to harvest Elwynn's thick timberlands. Over time, retired veterans such as former Stormwind Guard commander Marshal Haggard settled here for quiet seclusion. Despite steady operations, the camp has found itself increasingly beleaguered as local wildlife surges out of control, threatening timber shipments and worker safety.",al={"eastvale history","history of eastvale logging camp","past of eastvale"},it="history",add="c2c2b618"},{q="Who lives in or runs Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Day-to-day lumber operations fall under Supervisor Raelen, who manages the workers and strives to keep wood shipments moving on schedule. The camp also houses numerous lumberjacks, local stable hands, and retired figures like Marshal Haggard, who keeps to his manor just beyond the busy sawmills.",al={"who runs eastvale","who leads eastvale logging camp","eastvale overseer"},it="residents",add="85f79eeb"},{q="Is Eastvale Logging Camp dangerous?",a="While the camp itself is guarded, the surrounding woods are rife with predatory wolves and aggressive bears that routinely stalk the lumberjacks. Workers have been driven from their work sites and left abandoned timber scattered in the undergrowth, making venturing past the mill buildings perilous for the unwary.",al={"how dangerous is eastvale","is eastvale safe","threats at eastvale"},it="danger",add="6b46ecbb"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you rely on Eastvale’s timber to rebuild and maintain the kingdom’s settlements.",["faction:Alliance"]="At Eastvale Logging Camp, you can buy dependable Stormwind steeds."},kw={"eastvale","elwynn","haggard","horses","logging camp","lumber","raelen","timber"},rel={"npc:supervisor-raelen","quest:1666","quest:52","quest:5545","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Eastvale Logging Camp"}}
E["subzone:echo-ridge-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Echo Ridge Mine",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Valley's northwestern cliffs, Echo Ridge Mine lies rich in stone and ore, but kobolds have seized it.",h="In Northshire Valley's northwestern cliffs, Echo Ridge Mine lies rich in stone and ore, but kobolds have...",sec={{t="A Foothold for Vermin",b="Echo Ridge Mine was cut into the hills above Northshire Abbey to supply the valley with stone and metal. Kobolds poured through its tunnels and drove out the workers. Marshal McBride sees them as a danger to Northshire's safety and its recruits. He sends new recruits into the mine to thin their numbers and take the site back.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Beneath Northshire",b="Kobolds have been pushing into Elwynn Forest beyond Echo Ridge Mine. From the northwestern ridge, they threaten Northshire's training grounds and the flow of resources to the abbey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are kobolds in Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds burrow into dark tunnels rich in minerals. They found Echo Ridge Mine's defenses weak, overran it, and now dig for treasure while claiming the tunnels as their own.",al={"why kobolds here","echo ridge kobolds","who took the mine"},it="residents"},{q="Who is trying to reclaim Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey leads the effort to clear Echo Ridge Mine. He sends newly arrived adventurers to scout its tunnels and thin the kobold numbers before they spread farther into the valley.",al={"who wants echo ridge back","echo ridge quests","mcbride echo ridge"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Echo Ridge Mine located?",a="Echo Ridge Mine's entrance is in Northshire Valley's northwestern corner, cut into the rocky hillside just north of the abbey vineyards.",al={"echo ridge location","where is echo ridge","find echo ridge mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine is a mining cavern tucked into the northwestern ridges of Northshire Valley. Established to supply stone and ore to the valley and the abbey, the site has recently fallen into disarray after being overrun by scavenging kobolds.",al={"what is echo ridge","echo ridge mine info","tell me about echo ridge mine"},it="place",add="7d0021d3"},{q="What happened at Echo Ridge Mine?",a="The mine was actively worked by local human miners until an infestation of kobolds swarmed the shafts. The intruders drove out the workers and took over the tunnels, forcing Northshire authorities to pull back their workforce and seek martial aid to clear the infestation.",al={"echo ridge history","what happened here","why did the mine shut down"},it="history",add="d8e2171b"},{q="Why is Echo Ridge Mine abandoned?",a="Human operations came to an abrupt halt when the kobolds overwhelmed the workers. Lacking the immediate guard numbers to maintain safety underground, the abbey suspended normal mining duties while relying on newly arrived recruits to drive out the pests.",al={"why is echo ridge abandoned","is echo ridge ruined","why is the mine closed"},it="ruin",add="9fd09044"},{q="Is Echo Ridge Mine dangerous?",a="The tunnels are thick with defensive kobolds digging for resources and guarding their candlelit claims. While individual vermin are relatively weak, an inattentive traveler can quickly get cornered inside the winding, enclosed shafts.",al={"is echo ridge mine dangerous","echo ridge danger","how dangerous is echo ridge"},it="danger",add="df055836"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Echo Ridge Mine's shafts hold mineral deposits, but prospectors must fight through the candle-bearing kobolds to reach the ore.",["race:Human"]="As a human answering Stormwind's call, you help clear Echo Ridge Mine and defend Northshire Abbey."},kw={"echo ridge","echo ridge mine","kobold","marshal mcbride","mine","northshire","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:15","quest:21","topic:kobold","zone:elwynn"},src={"Echo Ridge Mine"}}
E["subzone:fargodeep-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Fargodeep Mine",z="elwynn",s="Kobolds now swarm through Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest. The mine once brought gold to Stormwind, but its tunnels are now a kobold warren.",h="Kobolds now swarm through Fargodeep Mine, south of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Lost Vein",b="Gold once flowed from Fargodeep Mine into Stormwind's treasury. As the Kingdom's military presence in Elwynn dwindled, outlying resources became vulnerable. Kobolds soon filled the mine's dark tunnels and made a warren beneath the hills. Marshal Dughan and Goldshire's authorities fear the lost ore and the danger to nearby farms, including the Stonefield and Maclure holdings.",sp=0},{t="Depths of the Warren",b="Fargodeep Mine runs through several levels, with lower shafts reaching deep beneath the forest floor. Kobold laborers and vermin hurry along wooden scaffolds, guarding the wax and gold dust they have scavenged. Goldtooth, a cunning kobold leader, lurks in a den above the main tunnels. He hoards trinkets stolen from travelers and nearby residents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did Stormwind abandon Fargodeep Mine?",a="Stormwind neglected Fargodeep Mine as its military stretched thin across the southern lands. Town guards focused on Goldshire and the main roads, leaving the underground mine unguarded. Kobolds moved in and fortified its tunnels.",al={"why abandoned","why did humans leave fargodeep","who owned fargodeep mine"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are the kobolds here so dangerous to local farmers?",a="Fargodeep Mine lies between the Stonefield and Maclure family farms. Kobolds come out of its tunnels to steal livestock, tools, and personal belongings, and harass anyone near the entrance.",al={"why are kobolds a problem","kobold threat","stonefield kobolds"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Goldtooth?",a="Goldtooth is a prominent kobold who nests in a den in Fargodeep Mine's upper reaches. He is known for stealing Auntie Bernice Stonefield's prized family necklace.",al={"goldtooth","who is goldtooth","goldtooth location"},it="residents"},{q="Why do people in Goldshire want items from the mine?",a="People in Goldshire see a reason to clear the pests from Fargodeep Mine. Remy 'Two Times' buys salvaged gold dust, the alchemist William Pestle uses kobold candle wax for reagents, and Marshal Dughan needs the infestation monitored to protect Elwynn.",al={"fargodeep quests","why gather candles","gold dust"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Fargodeep Mine?",a="Fargodeep Mine is an abandoned gold mine in central Elwynn Forest, south of Goldshire. Once an active excavation site supplying the Kingdom of Stormwind, it has fallen into disuse and is now completely overrun by subterranean kobolds tunneling through its upper chambers and lower shafts.",al={"what is fargodeep","fargodeep mine overview","about fargodeep mine"},it="place",add="7f063a4c",nx={6}},{q="What happened at Fargodeep Mine?",a="Originally operated by Stormwind miners extracting Elwynn's rich gold veins, the site was eventually abandoned as miners withdrew. In their absence, a clan of aggressive kobolds moved in, carving out tunnels, establishing their warrens, and turning the old shafts into a fortified den that threatens neighboring settlements.",al={"fargodeep history","what happened here","fargodeep lore"},it="history",add="e2f4f077"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Though pests infest Fargodeep Mine, its rocky tunnels still hold accessible copper veins for new miners.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing the vermin from Fargodeep Mine helps secure the supply lines and farmlands around Goldshire."},kw={"candles","elwynn","fargodeep","fargodeep mine","goldshire","goldtooth","kobold","marshal dughan","remy two times"},rel={"zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","quest:62","quest:87","quest:47","quest:60","topic:kobold"},src={"Fargodeep Mine"}}
E["subzone:forest-s-edge"] = {t="subzone",n="Forest's Edge",z="elwynn",s="Riverpaw gnolls under Hogger threaten travelers at Forest's Edge, along Elwynn's southwestern frontier.",h="Riverpaw gnolls under Hogger threaten travelers at Forest's Edge, along Elwynn's southwestern frontier.",sec={{t="A Contested Frontier",b="At Forest's Edge, woodland runs southwest from Stormwind City between Mirror Lake Orchard and the rivers that border Westfall. Westbrook Garrison lies nearby, but Stormwind's thin ranks leave the woods open to wild beasts and raiding parties. Boars roam among the trees and along the banks. Riverpaw gnolls gather here in force, using the woods as a staging ground.",sp=0},{t="Hogger's Stronghold",b="Hogger and his pack hunt through the woods of Forest's Edge. A massive, brutal gnoll chieftain, he leads raids on nearby farms and harasses travelers. The Stormwind Army has placed a bounty on his head. His pack makes the timberland dangerous for anyone who crosses it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Forest's Edge?",a="Forest's Edge lies in southwestern Elwynn Forest, south of Westbrook Garrison. Mirror Lake Orchard and the waterways leading toward Westfall border the area.",al={"forests edge location","where is forests edge","forest edge map"},it="place"},{q="Why is this area so dangerous?",a="Riverpaw gnolls have claimed the woods and threaten travel along Elwynn's southwestern border. Their chieftain, Hogger, is the fiercest threat, prowling the same woods.",al={"why dangerous forests edge","what is at forest edge","forests edge threats"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Hogger?",a="Hogger is a powerful gnoll leader who directs violent attacks along Elwynn's borders. The Stormwind Army has offered a bounty for proof of his death and warns adventurers not to face him alone.",al={"hogger lore","who is hogger","hogger info"},it="leader"},{q="Why hasn't Westbrook Garrison cleared the area?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin across the kingdom. Unrest in Westfall and threats on all sides leave Westbrook Garrison without enough soldiers to clear the gnoll camps, so volunteers are left to confront them.",al={"why westbrook garrison not clearing","why stormwind guards not help","westbrook guards"},it="conflict"},{q="Who lives in Forest's Edge?",a="Forest's Edge has fallen entirely into the hands of aggressive gnolls. Under the brutal dominance of the monstrous gnoll Hogger, these raiders have claimed the woodlands and riverbanks for themselves. The local wildlife, mostly wandering boars, now shares the clearing with these prowling gnoll packs.",al={"who lives here","forests edge residents","who is in forests edge"},it="residents",add="898568c8"},{q="Why is it called Forest's Edge?",a="The area forms the southwestern border of Elwynn Forest, where the dense woodland gives way to the Nazferiti River and the open plains toward Westfall. Tucked beside the riverbanks and orchard, it naturally represents the outer rim of the forest before travelers cross into harsher lands.",al={"why is it called forests edge","forests edge name meaning","why forests edge"},it="name",add="61fe669f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn Forest, clearing Forest's Edge and defeating Hogger is an early trial of your readiness to serve the crown.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Forest's Edge has common woodland herbs along its riverbanks and in its shaded groves. You may have to avoid aggressive gnoll patrols while gathering them."},kw={"elwynn forest","forest's edge","forests edge","gnolls","hogger","nazferiti river","riverpaw","westbrook garrison"},rel={"subzone:westbrook-garrison","topic:gnoll","zone:elwynn","subzone:mirror-lake-orchard","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:stormwind","quest:1861"},src={"Forest's Edge"}}
E["subzone:goldshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Goldshire",z="elwynn",s="Goldshire sits where Elwynn’s roads meet, linking Stormwind City with Westfall, Redridge, and the southern frontier. Rebuilt after the First War, the town now offers travelers the Lion’s Pride Inn, while a hard-pressed Stormwind Guard defends it.",h="Goldshire sits where Elwynn’s roads meet, linking Stormwind City with Westfall, Redridge, and the southern...",sec={{t="A Crossroads Under Strain",b="Goldshire stands where the king’s highways meet, the civic and commercial heart of rural Elwynn. Threats press closer as Stormwind’s forces stretch thin and King Varian Wrynn remains mysteriously absent. Marshal Dughan relies on passing adventurers instead of regular troops to hold the surrounding borders. Riverpaw gnolls push in from the west, while hostile murlocs claim the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. Their attacks have killed royal guards and brought danger close to the town center.",sp=0},{t="Scars of the Great Wars",b="Goldshire and Moonbrook were the last strongholds to fall in the First War. Warchief Blackhand cut King Llane Wrynn I off from his realm before sacking Stormwind Keep, and the Orcish Horde overwhelmed both towns. Goldshire was reduced to ash and lay barren until its rebuilding after the Second War.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is in charge of defending Goldshire?",a="Marshal Dughan of the Stormwind Guard commands Goldshire’s defenses. He coordinates the garrison from the town center, but a lack of reinforcements leaves him hiring freelance adventurers to face border threats and monster bounties.",al={"who leads goldshire","goldshire marshal","who protects goldshire"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats are currently menacing the town?",a="Riverpaw gnolls are raiding east toward Westbrook Garrison, while hostile murlocs infest Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. Local scouts warn that the skirmishes could reach Goldshire’s streets without intervention.",al={"goldshire problems","why is goldshire in danger","enemies near goldshire"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Goldshire during the First War?",a="Goldshire was one of the last two human towns to fall before Stormwind was sacked. Warchief Blackhand destroyed it alongside Moonbrook to sever King Llane’s supply lines, leaving it in ruins until its rebuilding after the Second War.",al={"goldshire first war","did goldshire fall to orcs","goldshire destruction"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Lion's Pride Inn so notable?",a="The Lion’s Pride Inn is one of Azeroth’s most respected and frequented alehouses. At the junction of several regional highways, it is a meeting hall, resting place, and training ground for travelers crossing the kingdom.",al={"lions pride inn","goldshire inn","tavern in goldshire"},it="fame"},{q="What is Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is a bustling human town centrally located in Elwynn Forest, resting at the crossroads between Stormwind City, Northshire Valley, Westfall, and Redridge. Serving as a vital waystation for trade and travelers, it is often the first major settlement visited by fledgling heroes departing the abbey.",al={"what is goldshire","about goldshire","goldshire town"},it="place",add="510017eb"},{q="Who lives in Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is home to human merchants, tradesfolk, and craft trainers catering to local travelers and farmers. Security and governance fall under Marshal Dughan and his Stormwind Guards, who garrison the outpost, maintain order along the crossroads, and direct arriving adventurers to where defense is most needed.",al={"who lives here","who lives in goldshire","goldshire residents"},it="residents",add="c15b14b9"},{q="Is Goldshire dangerous?",a="Within town borders, the Stormwind Guard keeps you relatively safe, but danger creeps dangerously close to the perimeter. Aggressive Riverpaw gnolls prowl the western borderlands, while deadly murlocs have overrun nearby lakes and rivers, threatening to push directly into the village if left unchecked.",al={"is goldshire safe","danger in goldshire","is it dangerous here"},it="danger",add="d3dbe578"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human fresh from Northshire Abbey, you find in Goldshire your first real taste of the kingdom beyond the monastery walls, and a sobering view of Stormwind’s strained borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you pass through Goldshire on the way from the capital to the frontier lands of Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","lion's pride inn","marshal dughan","murloc","riverpaw","stone cairn lake"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","quest:46","quest:11","subzone:crystal-lake","topic:first-war"},src={"Goldshire"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Arms (Northshire)",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Abbey, recruits train with the Stormwind Army in the Hall of Arms, south of the Main Hall.",h="In Northshire Abbey, recruits train with the Stormwind Army in the Hall of Arms, south of the Main Hall.",sec={{t="Groundwork of the Guard",b="The Hall of Arms rings with blunted steel and the measured cadence of instruction. South of Northshire Abbey’s Main Hall, the wing trains human fighters and devout aspirants who take up arms for the Stormwind Army. Veteran battle instructors and paladin mentors teach the postures and disciplines needed to defend Elwynn Forest from kobolds, Defias bandits, and gnoll raiders. Across the courtyard, clerics and scholars study ancient tomes in the Library Wing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Arms?",a="The Hall of Arms trains new soldiers, mercenaries, and paladins in weapons and combat inside Northshire Abbey, before they venture into the wider kingdom.",al={"what is this room","hall of arms purpose","what happens here"},it="purpose"},{q="Who can be found inside this wing?",a="Veteran warrior and paladin trainers instruct Stormwind Army recruits in martial disciplines, shield work, and basic combat maneuvers.",al={"who is in hall of arms","trainers hall of arms","who teaches here"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Hall of Arms located within Northshire Abbey?",a="The Hall of Arms stands on the southern side of Northshire Abbey, directly accessible from the central Main Hall. The Library Wing lies across the abbey courtyard.",al={"hall of arms location","where is hall of arms","abbey layout"},it="place"},{q="Is the Hall of Arms dangerous?",a="Not at all. The Hall of Arms is a secure sanctuary within Northshire Abbey, shielded from the Defias cutpurses and kobolds prowling the valley outside. Inside its quiet stone chambers, experienced paladins and seasoned soldiers watch over the recruits. Unless trouble somehow breaches the abbey gates, you can rest and train here without any threat.",al={"hall of arms danger","is hall of arms safe","enemies in hall of arms"},it="danger",add="1c4cb7f4"},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Arms?",a="The wing earns its name from its role as Northshire Abbey's center of martial discipline. While the opposite wing is devoted to study and holy texts in the library, this hall is dedicated to the profession of arms, housing the weapon instructors, armaments, and martial trainers who ready new warriors and paladins for the Stormwind Army.",al={"why hall of arms","hall of arms name meaning","meaning of hall of arms"},it="name",add="c5e01713"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a human warrior entering service, you receive your first lessons here in stance, weapon handling, and the Stormwind Army’s martial discipline.",["class:Paladin"]="As a fledgling paladin, you learn to wield the Light alongside martial arms, joining holy devotion with martial training."},kw={"elwynn forest","hall of arms","northshire abbey","northshire valley","paladin trainer","stormwind army","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:main-hall-northshire","subzone:library-wing-northshire","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:stormwind-army","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Hall of Arms (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:heroes-vigil"] = {t="subzone",n="Heroes' Vigil",z="elwynn",s="On Stone Cairn Lake’s central island, Heroes' Vigil lies neglected and overrun by renegade wizards. Its Stone of Remembrance honors those who fell in the First War.",h="On Stone Cairn Lake’s central island, Heroes' Vigil lies neglected and overrun by renegade wizards.",sec={{t="A Forgotten Memorial",b="Heroes' Vigil stands on an island in Stone Cairn Lake, centered on the Stone of Remembrance. Erected after the First War, its inscribed stone circle honors the soldiers and citizens slaughtered when the Old Horde sacked Goldshire and the surrounding valleys. Once revered as a sacred place of faith and sacrifice, the vigil has slipped from Stormwind's attention. Its grounds now lie overgrown, with no soldiers sent to tend them.",sp=0},{t="Claimed by Renegades",b="With no kingdom garrison on the island, outcasts have taken the memorial. Rogue wizards control Stone Cairn Lake and the grounds, practicing wild, undisciplined magic beyond the oversight of the Kirin Tor and the Academy of Arcane Sciences. Near the stones lies Henze Faulk's body among other tragic casualties. Travelers can only wonder whether the shrine will ever know peace again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Heroes' Vigil?",a="Heroes' Vigil stands on the island in Stone Cairn Lake in eastern Elwynn Forest. Its stone ring and memorial honor those who fell in the First War.",al={"heroes vigil","what is heroes vigil","island shrine elwynn"},it="place"},{q="What does the Stone of Remembrance commemorate?",a="The Stone of Remembrance honors the citizens and defenders who died when the orcish Horde sacked Goldshire and ravaged eastern Elwynn Forest during the First War.",al={"stone of remembrance","monument meaning","what is the stone of remembrance"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Heroes' Vigil today?",a="Hostile rogue wizards occupy the island and Heroes' Vigil. They operate outside Stormwind's law and the oversight of established magical institutions.",al={"who is at heroes vigil","heroes vigil enemies","wizards on lake"},it="residents"},{q="Why has Stormwind neglected the vigil?",a="Stormwind has left the vigil undefended and largely forgotten because King Varian Wrynn is missing and the realm is stretched thin by internal dissent, brigands, and monster incursions. Remote shrines have been left without protection.",al={"why is it abandoned","why did stormwind forget it","forgotten shrine"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Henze Faulk?",a="Henze Faulk is a dwarf whose body lies near the monument. Defias Brotherhood forces struck him down while he was saving his friend, Gazin Tenorm.",al={"henze faulk body","who is the dead guy on the island"},it="identity"},{q="Is Heroes' Vigil dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so for the unwary. The island in Stone Cairn Lake has fallen entirely under the control of Rogue Wizards and conjurers who practice forbidden arts in exile. They attack anyone who approaches the monument on sight, making what should be a peaceful sanctuary of remembrance into a deadly trap for travelers.",al={"is heroes vigil safe","heroes vigil danger","heroes vigil hostile"},it="danger",add="e301b338"},{q="Why is it called Heroes' Vigil?",a="The site was established as an enduring watch and memorial for the fallen defenders of the First War. At its heart stands the Stone of Remembrance, raised to honor the soldiers and civilians slaughtered when the Old Horde rampaged through Elwynn Forest and sacked Goldshire.",al={"why called heroes vigil","heroes vigil name meaning","who are the heroes honored here"},it="name",add="c198f6a4"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see this sacred stone ring as a bitter reminder of the First War's blood price and the kingdom's failure to protect its heritage.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you find renegade wizards encamped on sacred ground, practicing dangerous arts without the discipline or sanction of the Academy of Arcane Sciences."},kw={"elwynn forest","henze faulk","heroes vigil","heroes' vigil","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},rel={"subzone:stone-cairn-lake","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","topic:first-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Heroes' Vigil"}}
E["subzone:jasperlode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Jasperlode Mine",z="elwynn",s="In north-central Elwynn, Jasperlode Mine lies lost to kobolds and giant spiders. Its shafts once supplied Stormwind City with vital iron and minerals, but the resource-strapped kingdom cannot reclaim them.",h="In north-central Elwynn, Jasperlode Mine lies lost to kobolds and giant spiders.",sec={{t="A Lost Resource in Elwynn",b="Jasperlode Mine once supplied Stormwind with a steady wealth of minerals, alongside nearby Fargodeep. With the kingdom's forces stretched thin by outside threats and unrest, local garrisons cannot protect the shafts. Kobolds seized their chance, drove out the human miners, and hoarded stolen gold and tallow candles.",sp=0},{t="Dangers in the Deep",b="Deep within Jasperlode Mine, mine spiders have taken hold beneath the timber supports. A massive matriarch called Mother Fang leads them. The spiders prey on trespassing kobolds and unwary prospectors, making any attempt to salvage the mine dangerous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Jasperlode Mine overrun?",a="Stormwind's army is spread thin across the realm, leaving rural outposts like Goldshire short on manpower. Kobolds swarmed the dig sites once the human miners lost their guards.",al={"why are there kobolds","who controls jasperlode","why abandoned"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the difference between Jasperlode and Fargodeep?",a="Fargodeep Mine lies south near the Maclure and Stonefield farms. Jasperlode sits north in the foothills near the river. Both are major Elwynn mineral sites lost to kobolds.",al={"jasperlode vs fargodeep","other elwynn mine"}},{q="What lurks in the back of the mine?",a="Predatory mine spiders lurk in the deepest shafts, led by a massive arachnid called Mother Fang. Even the kobolds avoid their webbed caverns.",al={"spiders in jasperlode","mother fang","what is at the bottom"},it="residents"},{q="Why hasn't Marshal Dughan cleared the mine?",a="Marshal Dughan lacks the troops for a prolonged clearing underground. With Defias river patrols, gnoll incursions, and garrison duties to cover, the local militia must rely on traveling adventurers to scout and cull the threats inside.",al={"why no stormwind guard","dughan sending soldiers"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine is one of Elwynn Forest's vital mineral extraction sites, carved into the hills northeast of Goldshire. Alongside Fargodeep Mine, it long served as an essential supplier of precious ores and raw metals needed to sustain Stormwind City and its military campaigns. Today, however, the human miners have been completely displaced, leaving its winding tunnels claimed by subterranean monsters.",al={"what is jasperlode","about jasperlode mine","jasperlode elwynn"},it="place",add="ae82ecd7"},{q="What happened at Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode once operated steadily under the watch of Stormwind, fueling the kingdom's war efforts with fresh ore. When the kingdom's military grew thinly stretched and preoccupied with threats elsewhere, swarms of opportunistic kobolds surged into the tunnels, driving out the workers and seizing the mineral veins for themselves.",al={"jasperlode mine history","what happened to jasperlode","jasperlode backstory"},it="history",add="d5d7dec2"},{q="Is Jasperlode Mine dangerous?",a="Jasperlode Mine is exceptionally perilous for unwary travelers. Not only is it heavily infested with territorial kobolds who will ferociously defend their candles and dig sites, but its deepest caverns harbor a colony of predatory mine spiders led by the vicious broodmother, Mother Fang. Venturing into the dark without a weapon and a sharp eye is an easy way to end up dead.",al={"how dangerous is jasperlode","is jasperlode safe","jasperlode threats"},it="danger",add="6ca2598d"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Jasperlode's mineral veins draw prospectors willing to face kobold pickaxes and spider webs to stake a claim.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind needs Jasperlode's raw metal to maintain its equipment supplies while the kingdom's borders face constant peril."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","marshal dughan","mother fang"},rel={"subzone:fargodeep-mine","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:kobold","quest:76","quest:47","quest:60","zone:stormwind"},src={"Jasperlode Mine"}}
E["subzone:jerod-s-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Jerod's Landing",z="elwynn",s="Defias smugglers hold Jerod's Landing on the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River. The dock gives them a hidden route for illicit shipments across the kingdom's waterways.",h="Defias smugglers hold Jerod's Landing on the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River.",sec={{t="A Smuggler's Waypoint",b="Defias outlaws now control the river dock at Jerod's Landing, where Elwynn Forest meets the waters of the Nazferiti River. Once an ordinary boat dock, it now receives goods plundered from the Redridge Mountains under a Defias dockmaster's watch. The outlaws move the cargo discreetly downstream toward holdings such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Jerod's Landing's place on the river has drawn SI:7, Stormwind's covert intelligence network. Its operatives watch Defias activity there and see the dock as a vital link in the syndicate's supply lines. Resourceful rogues slip inside, steal river shipment ledgers, and work to unravel the wider conspiracy strangling the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Jerod's Landing located?",a="Jerod's Landing lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, on the western bank of the Nazferiti River, which marks the boundary between Elwynn and the Redridge Mountains.",al={"jerods landing location","where is jerod's landing","jerod dock map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls Jerod's Landing?",a="Members of the Defias Brotherhood occupy Jerod's Landing. A Defias dockmaster coordinates shipments with armed bandits guarding the waterside.",al={"who is at jerods landing","defias at jerods landing","jerod landing mobs"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the purpose of this dock for the Defias?",a="The Brotherhood uses Jerod's Landing to smuggle stolen goods and weaponry taken in the Redridge Mountains toward rogue strongholds such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",al={"why do defias use jerods landing","defias river smuggling"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is SI:7 interested in Jerod's Landing?",a="Master Mathias Shaw and his intelligence agents track Defias contraband through Jerod's Landing to expose the network linking Westfall, Elwynn, and Redridge.",al={"si7 jerods landing","rogue quest jerods landing"},it="threat"},{q="What is Jerod's Landing?",a="Jerod's Landing is a modest boat dock situated along the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River. Though once a simple river crossing and wharf, it has fallen under the sway of criminals who use its remote waterside position to stage covert operations away from the gaze of Stormwind's guards.",al={"what is jerods landing","jerod landing elwynn","about jerod landing"},it="place",add="d69927bb"},{q="Who lives in or runs Jerod's Landing?",a="The landing is held by the Defias Brotherhood and overseen on-site by their Dockmaster and his crew. These bandits hold the waterfront, using muscle and watchfulness to secure incoming cargo and keep outsiders away from their river trade.",al={"who runs jerods landing","jerods landing dockmaster","who is at jerods landing"},it="residents",add="096cd4eb"},{q="Is Jerod's Landing dangerous?",a="Yes. The docks are crawling with armed Defias smugglers and thugs who will not hesitate to cut down any traveler or Alliance scout wandering near their smuggling operations. Approaching the shoreline without caution invites immediate violence.",al={"is jerods landing safe","how dangerous is jerods landing","jerod landing enemies"},it="danger",add="51e45e55"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue working for SI:7, you are sent to Jerod's Landing to test your stealth, pickpocket the Defias dockmaster, and recover sensitive trade ledgers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how thoroughly the Defias have compromised the waterways linking Elwynn to Redridge, right beneath Stormwind's nose."},kw={"defias dockmaster","jerod's landing","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","nazferiti river","smuggling","snatch and grab"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:2206","quest:2359","zone:elwynn","zone:redridge","zone:westfall","quest:65"},src={"Jerod's Landing"}}
E["subzone:library-wing-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Library Wing (Northshire)",z="elwynn",s="In Northshire Abbey, the Library Wing gathers scholars and new priests and mages. Its quiet southern rooms offer instruction for those joining Stormwind’s defense.",h="In Northshire Abbey, the Library Wing gathers scholars and new priests and mages.",sec={{t="Haven of Arcane and Divine Study",b="The Library Wing branches south from Northshire Abbey’s Main Hall. Dusty shelves, study lecterns, and quiet alcoves fill its rooms, where aspiring mages and priests learn the Arcane and the Holy Light. Across the abbey, martial recruits drill in the Hall of Arms. Priestess Anetta guides novice priests in faith and healing, while Khelden Bremen teaches budding mages to shape primal elemental energy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library Wing located?",a="The Library Wing occupies the southern part of Northshire Abbey, just off the Main Hall and directly opposite the Hall of Arms.",al={"where is the library wing","how to find northshire library","library location northshire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this wing?",a="The wing is Northshire Abbey’s center for study and spiritual instruction, where recruits prepare to serve Stormwind through magical learning and prayer.",al={"why does northshire abbey have a library","library wing purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Library Wing?",a="The Library Wing is the southern annex of Northshire Abbey, set apart from the martial commotion of the Hall of Arms and the central hall. Dedicated to quiet study, mystical practice, and healing, it provides a sanctuary where novice casters and acolytes can learn the fundamental teachings of the Light and the arcane arts.",al={"what is library wing","library wing northshire","about library wing"},it="place",add="43e724fe"},{q="Who lives in or teaches at the Library Wing?",a="Priestess Anetta and Mage Trainer Khelden Bremen reside here to instruct the newest recruits answering Stormwind's call. Along with their pupils, you will find Wounded Trainees resting among the bookshelves and study alcoves, recovering under the watchful care of the abbey's healers.",al={"who is in library wing","library wing trainers","who teaches in library wing"},it="residents",add="cc13243a"},{q="Is the Library Wing dangerous?",a="The wing itself is completely safe, protected by the stout stone walls and vigilant defenders of Northshire Abbey. However, the presence of recovering wounded serves as a grim reminder that the surrounding valley is not at peace, plagued by aggressive wildlife and encroaching Defias bandits.",al={"is library wing safe","library wing danger","threats in library wing"},it="danger",add="240ac0ef"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can learn from Priestess Anetta, who teaches fledgling priests to channel the Holy Light to heal wounds and smite foes.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can study in these quiet halls with Khelden Bremen, who teaches novice mages the foundations of fire and frost."},kw={"elwynn forest","khelden bremen","library wing","mage trainer","northshire","northshire abbey","priest trainer","priestess anetta"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:main-hall-northshire","subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire","subzone:northshire-valley","npc:priestess-anetta","npc:khelden-bremen","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Library Wing (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:lion-s-pride-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Lion's Pride Inn",z="elwynn",s="Travelers gather at the Lion's Pride Inn, Goldshire's tavern and community center in Elwynn Forest. Innkeeper Farley keeps the inn, a place to rest, meet others, and find work just south of Stormwind City.",h="Travelers gather at the Lion's Pride Inn, Goldshire's tavern and community center in Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="Heart of Goldshire",b="The Lion's Pride Inn anchors Goldshire at the crossroads of Elwynn Forest. Innkeeper Farley keeps it by the old motto, “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.” Inside, warm hearths, strong drinks, and rooms welcome weary travelers from Northshire. Goldshire sits on trade routes between Stormwind, Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood, making the inn an indispensable gathering place. Town marshals, local crafters, and seasoned trainers meet there to share news and hire passing mercenaries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns and runs the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn, welcoming weary travelers with the motto, “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.”",al={"innkeeper","who owns lions pride","who runs goldshire inn"},it="residents"},{q="What services are available inside the inn?",a="The inn offers food, drink, and lodging, along with class trainers, visiting merchants, and locals seeking help with Elwynn Forest's gnoll, kobold, and bandit troubles.",al={"trainers","what is inside","amenities"},gp=true},{q="Why is the inn such a central hub in Elwynn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn is the primary rest stop for travelers between Stormwind, Westfall, and the Redridge Mountains. It stands at Goldshire's crossroads just south of Stormwind, and young travelers from Northshire Valley reach it as their first major hub.",al={"why so popular","goldshire crossroads","importance of lions pride"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the motto of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley gives the Lion's Pride Inn's motto as “Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.”",al={"inn motto","motto"}},{q="What is Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn, also called the Goldshire Inn, is the bustling heart of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary gathering place, tavern, and lodging for locals, town guards, and weary travelers journeying along the high roads of Stormwind.",al={"what is lions pride inn","lions pride inn elwynn","goldshire inn lore"},it="place",add="3778d523"},{q="What is the history of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The inn has long stood as a central refuge in Goldshire. Run by Innkeeper Farley, it keeps an honest, welcoming hearth for those on the road under its motto, 'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.'",al={"lions pride inn history","goldshire inn background","farley family inn history"},it="history",add="4a999086"},{q="Is the Lion's Pride Inn dangerous?",a="The inn itself is entirely safe, guarded closely by the Stormwind garrison stationed in Goldshire. Outside, the road can see rowdy brawls and occasional skirmishes, while the surrounding woods teem with Kobolds, Defias bandits, and gnolls, but within its walls, you will find only rest and refuge.",al={"is lions pride inn safe","danger lions pride inn","is goldshire inn dangerous"},it="danger",add="b8029b33"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans leaving Northshire Abbey, the Lion's Pride Inn is their first glimpse of the kingdom's wider life and troubles beyond the monastery walls.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the main inn outside Stormwind's gates, the Lion's Pride Inn is a waystation where Alliance travelers coordinate patrols and trade across the heartlands."},kw={"elwynn forest","farley","goldshire","goldshire inn","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","lions pride"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","npc:innkeeper-farley","zone:elwynn","topic:llane-wrynn-i","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Lion's Pride Inn"}}
E["subzone:maclure-vineyards"] = {t="subzone",n="Maclure Vineyards",z="elwynn",s="In southern Elwynn, Maclure Vineyards sends grapes and wine to Stormwind. The Maclure family's estate is known as much for its bitter feud with the neighboring Stonefields as for its harvest.",h="In southern Elwynn, Maclure Vineyards sends grapes and wine to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="The Maclure Vineyards should be a peaceful haven of farming and winecraft in southern Elwynn Forest. Instead, the feud with the Stonefields down the road overshadows the family's daily labor. Accusations of theft and old resentment keep tempers high between the households. Hungry boars prowl the land, while kobolds press toward both homesteads.",sp=0},{t="A Forbidden Romance",b="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield have fallen secretly in love despite their families' bitter feud. They meet in hidden groves, away from their parents' suspicious eyes. Travelers through the vineyards are drawn into carrying secret messages, settling petty grievances, and helping the young couple seek a life together beyond their families' grudge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Maclures and Stonefields fighting?",a="The Maclures and Stonefields have a long rural feud rooted in years of mistrust, petty accusations, and stubborn pride. Each family blames the other for lost goods and livestock, though neither has proof of foul play.",al={"maclure stonefield feud","why do they hate each other","family feud"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Maybell Maclure?",a="Maybell is the daughter of the Maclure household. She has secretly fallen in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield, defying her family's hatred of their neighbors and hoping they can find a way to be together.",al={"maybell","maclure daughter"},it="people"},{q="What threats do the vineyards face?",a="The vineyards face family disputes, hungry wild boars that trample crops and vines, and kobolds from nearby gold mines who raid the surrounding fields.",al={"vineyard dangers","boars at maclure"},it="threat"},{q="What do the Maclures produce here?",a="The Maclure family grows grapes for wine and fresh fruit, supplying tavern-keepers and merchants throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City.",al={"what grows here","maclure crops"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Maclure Vineyards?",a="Maclure Vineyards is an agricultural homestead located in southern Elwynn Forest. Cultivated and operated by the Maclure family, the grounds produce grapes and fine wine for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Beyond the grape arbors, the farm features a family homestead and open fields, though it is currently plagued by unruly wild boars and tensions with its neighbors.",al={"what is maclure vineyards","maclure vineyards elwynn","maclure farm"},it="place",add="7abbd722"},{q="Who lives in Maclure Vineyards?",a="The vineyard is owned and worked by the Maclure family. The homestead is home to several generations of Maclures, including Gerard Maclure and young Maybell Maclure. Together, they tend the grapevines, defend their crops against intrusive wildlife, and manage the estate despite ongoing friction with the nearby Stonefield clan.",al={"who lives here","maclure family members","who runs maclure vineyards"},it="residents",add="d4181dc3"},{q="Is Maclure Vineyards dangerous?",a="While the farm itself is a peaceful Alliance homestead, you will find danger lurking in the vines. Aggressive wild boars constantly root through the fields, damaging crops and attacking anyone who strays too close. Additionally, kobolds from nearby mines occasionally wander toward the perimeter, making vigilance necessary for farmhands and travelers alike.",al={"is maclure vineyards safe","dangers at maclure vineyards","threats at maclure farm"},it="danger",add="6b11f938"},{q="Why is it called Maclure Vineyards?",a="The estate takes its name directly from the Maclure family, who cleared the land and planted the sprawling grapevines. For generations, their name has been synonymous with the local harvest and the sweet wines produced right here in Elwynn Forest.",al={"why is it called maclure vineyards","maclure vineyards name origin","name maclure vineyards"},it="name",add="5a643901"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, the feud shows the stubbornness of the countryside. Even in the kingdom's heartland, neighbors quarrel over fences while greater perils loom.",["faction:Alliance"]="The estate supplies food and spirits to nearby Goldshire and Stormwind City."},kw={"boars","elwynn","gerard","maclure","maybell","stonefield","vineyard","wine"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:114","quest:86","quest:85","quest:16","quest:88","topic:kobold"},src={"Maclure Vineyards"}}
E["subzone:main-hall-northshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Main Hall (Northshire)",z="elwynn",s="Newcomers report in the Main Hall at Northshire Abbey in western Elwynn. From there, they reach the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and the abbey tower, then receive their first assignments defending Stormwind.",h="Newcomers report in the Main Hall at Northshire Abbey in western Elwynn.",sec={{t="Heart of the Abbey",b="Trainees and clerics pass through the Main Hall after entering Northshire Abbey. The chamber links the Hall of Arms, where recruits prepare for battle, with the Library Wing and the stairs to the abbey tower. Strife in the valley reaches even this quiet place, and officers rally able newcomers to defend the kingdom's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Main Hall?",a="The Main Hall links the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and Northshire Abbey's upper tower. Recruits, priests, and visitors pass through this central chamber.",al={"what is main hall","northshire main hall use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who directs new recruits here?",a="Stormwind defense officers and clerics stationed in the Main Hall assess incoming adventurers and give them their first orders: clear threats from the abbey grounds.",al={"who gives quests here","abbey commander"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey?",a="The Main Hall is the central entrance chamber of Northshire Abbey, nestled in the sheltered Northshire Valley of Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary thoroughfare linking the abbey's tower, the Library Wing, and the Hall of Arms, making it the heart of activity for newly arrived defenders of the realm.",al={"what is main hall","northshire main hall","what is this hall"},it="place",add="23c998e2"},{q="Is the Main Hall dangerous?",a="The hall is guarded and offers shelter from the valley's dangers. Outside the abbey, aggressive wildlife and Defias bandits threaten the surrounding grounds.",al={"is main hall safe","main hall danger","are there enemies in main hall"},it="danger",add="c47795b4"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you begin your service to Stormwind and the Holy Light in the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey."},kw={"abbey","elwynn","hall of arms","library wing","main hall","northshire","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","subzone:hall-of-arms-northshire","subzone:library-wing-northshire","zone:elwynn"},src={"Main Hall (Northshire)"}}
E["subzone:mirror-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirror Lake",z="elwynn",s="Water spills into Mirror Lake beneath Stormwind's cliffs in northwestern Elwynn Forest, near an orchard. Defias bandits prowl the surrounding orchards, while mages watch for trouble in the forest's arcane currents.",h="Water spills into Mirror Lake beneath Stormwind's cliffs in northwestern Elwynn Forest, near an orchard.",sec={{t="A Troubled Idyl",b="Mirror Lake lies beneath Stormwind City's walls, where fishermen and weary travelers might seek a quiet rest. Defias Brotherhood brigands stalk the surrounding orchards, making a long stay perilous for locals. Mystical disturbances across Azeroth have also begun to warp the forest's natural channels of arcane energy. Mages from the Wizard's Sanctum watch the lake closely. They send practitioners to sample its currents and guard against chaotic arcane runoff poisoning communities downstream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Mirror Lake dangerous?",a="Defias bandits prowl the area around Mirror Lake and prey on travelers and farmers. Recent shifts in regional magic have also raised concern about the lake's water.",al={"is mirror lake safe","mirror lake enemies","defias mirror lake"},it="danger"},{q="Why are mages studying Mirror Lake?",a="Massive magical conflicts across Azeroth have unsettled ley currents throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind. The Wizard's Sanctum sends initiates to sample the lake's water for unstable arcane residue that could affect those who drink from it.",al={"wizard sanctum mirror lake","mirror lake quest","magic in mirror lake"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the waterfall at Mirror Lake come from?",a="The waterfall comes from the high cliffs and waterways around Stormwind City. Its water feeds the lake before winding through the Elwynn river system.",al={"mirror lake waterfall","water source mirror lake"}},{q="What is Mirror Lake?",a="Mirror Lake is a small, scenic body of water nestled in western Elwynn Forest near an orchard. Fed by a rushing waterfall pouring down from the mountains beneath Stormwind, it would otherwise be a quiet haven for fishing and swimming if not for the criminal element currently controlling its shores.",al={"mirror lake elwynn","what is mirror lake","about mirror lake"},it="place",add="80ec8f44"},{q="Who controls Mirror Lake?",a="The lake is currently overrun by the Defias Brotherhood. These outlaws prowl the shoreline and surrounding orchards, driving off local fishermen and travelers while using the remote, sheltered waters as a base of operations right outside Stormwind's walls.",al={"who lives at mirror lake","mirror lake bandits","who runs mirror lake"},it="residents",add="e8bd98e7"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Initiates studying at Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum come here to gather water samples. The work shows how turbulent arcane channels can seep into the natural world.",["faction:Alliance"]="The lake lies close to Stormwind's walls, while the kingdom's guards are stretched thin against Defias outlaws in the surrounding area."},kw={"defias","elwynn forest","mirror lake","stormwind","waterfall","wizards sanctum"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:1861","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Mirror Lake"}}
E["subzone:mirror-lake-orchard"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirror Lake Orchard",z="elwynn",s="Defias bandits now hold Mirror Lake Orchard, on Mirror Lake's southern shore in western Elwynn Forest. The quiet homestead near Thunder Falls has fallen to outlaws while Stormwind's guards are stretched thin.",h="Defias bandits now hold Mirror Lake Orchard, on Mirror Lake's southern shore in western Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Grove Under Seizure",b="Mirror Lake Orchard once fed a peaceful farmstead with the clean waters of Mirror Lake. Now Defias Brotherhood bandits have seized the cottage and grounds near Thunder Falls. With Stormwind's military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn missing, rural homes across Elwynn are easy targets for outlaws seeking shelter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Mirror Lake Orchard right now?",a="Defias bandits occupy Mirror Lake Orchard and its cottage. The honest folk who once tended the trees have been driven away, and the secluded grounds now give the outlaws a base in western Elwynn.",al={"who is at mirror lake orchard","who lives here","orchard enemies"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Mirror Lake Orchard located?",a="Mirror Lake Orchard lies on the southern shore of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest, just east of Thunder Falls and north of the main road toward Westfall.",al={"mirror lake orchard location","where is the orchard","find orchard elwynn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind reclaimed the orchard?",a="Stormwind's standing army is largely absent from rural Elwynn amid political deadlock and the mysterious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. With local garrisons short-handed, distant farms and orchards are often left to face the Defias Brotherhood alone.",al={"why are defias here","where are the guards"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the connection between the orchard and Thunder Falls?",a="Mirror Lake drains into Thunder Falls, and the orchard sits just above the cascade. Its secluded place near the cliffs gives bandits a defensible position.",al={"thunder falls connection","orchard and waterfall"},it="ties"},{q="What is Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="Mirror Lake Orchard is a small, quiet farmstead nestled on the southern shore of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful fruit orchard with an adjoining cottage, it has fallen into lawlessness like much of the surrounding countryside.",al={"what is this place","mirror lake orchard lore","about mirror lake orchard"},it="place",add="9fb3552d"},{q="What happened at Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="The peaceful farmers who once tended these trees were driven out or abandoned their home as unrest spread across Elwynn Forest. Seizing the opportunity, outlaws from the Defias Brotherhood moved in, turning the deserted cottage and orchard into another secluded staging ground for their operations.",al={"mirror lake orchard history","what happened here","orchard background"},it="history",add="fc4dc36b"},{q="Why was Mirror Lake Orchard abandoned?",a="With Stormwind's attention divided and local guards stretched thin, rural homesteads throughout Elwynn became prime targets for rogue brigands. The orchard was abandoned to the encroaching Defias bandits, who claimed the cottage and land for themselves.",al={"why is the orchard abandoned","why did farmers leave","who abandoned the orchard"},it="ruin",add="d58df7ba"},{q="Is Mirror Lake Orchard dangerous?",a="Yes. The area is currently overrun by hostile Defias bandits who patrol the groves and occupy the nearby house. Anyone venturing through the trees without their guard up risks being ambushed on sight.",al={"is it safe here","mirror lake orchard danger","enemies at mirror lake orchard"},it="danger",add="90c4a3ea"},{q="Why is it called Mirror Lake Orchard?",a="The orchard takes its name directly from its location along the southern shore of Mirror Lake, where its fruit trees were planted beside the calm, reflective waters.",al={"why is it named mirror lake orchard","mirror lake orchard name meaning","origin of orchard name"},it="name",add="626e53a6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the occupied orchard is another sign of the Defias Brotherhood's bold advance across the kingdom's heartland.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see the Defias strategy in the orchard: seize overlooked, defensible ground near water and cliffs to watch the roads and evade city patrols."},kw={"defias brotherhood","elwynn forest","mirror lake","mirror lake orchard","stormwind bandits","thunder falls"},rel={"zone:elwynn","quest:1861","subzone:thunder-falls","topic:alliance"},src={"Mirror Lake Orchard"}}
E["subzone:northshire-abbey"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Abbey",z="elwynn",s="Northshire Abbey trains new defenders in Northshire Valley, among Elwynn Forest's northern foothills. Rebuilt after the First War, it is the spiritual heart of the Brotherhood of Northshire and a leading school for those answering Stormwind's call.",h="Northshire Abbey trains new defenders in Northshire Valley, among Elwynn Forest's northern foothills.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Faith and Ruin",b="Clerics from Lordaeron came south centuries ago to spread the Holy Light and founded the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics and their abbey. The monastery soon became part of kingdom life, caring for the sick and tending to the young Guardian Medivh during his years in a coma. In the First War, brigands and the Orcish Horde attacked it repeatedly, and the abbey was destroyed. After the Alliance of Lordaeron liberated the region in the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol helped rebuild the sanctuary and refounded its protectors as the Brotherhood of Northshire.",sp=0},{t="The Training Grounds",b="Northshire Abbey trains volunteers, militia recruits, and novices who hope to defend Stormwind. Its Main Hall, Hall of Arms, and Library Wing house instructors in martial, arcane, and holy arts, while scouts and rogues train in the outer yards. The Knights of the Silver Hand keep watch, but peace remains fragile. Kobolds overrun nearby mines, aggressive wolves prowl the orchards, and Defias Brotherhood agents stalk the valley roads. They steal ancient scrolls and sacred librams from the abbey's archives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brotherhood of Northshire?",a="The Brotherhood of Northshire is a religious order of clerics, priests, and paladins based at Northshire Abbey. Clerics from Lordaeron founded it centuries ago, and Archbishop Alonsus Faol re-established it after the First War to train faithful defenders and preserve sacred scripture.",al={"who runs northshire abbey","northshire clerics","brotherhood of northshire lore"},it="residents"},{q="Why was Northshire Abbey destroyed in the First War?",a="During the First War, the abbey was important to Stormwind's defenses and faith. Orcish forces incited human brigands to attack, and after the half-orc Garona was briefly held captive there, a great Horde assault leveled the holy grounds. The abbey lay in ruins until the Alliance drove out the orcish clans and rebuilt it.",al={"who destroyed northshire abbey","northshire first war","what happened to northshire"},it="history"},{q="Why are there Defias bandits and kobolds outside the abbey?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin protecting distant borders, leaving outlying regions poorly guarded. Kobolds have infested the local gold mines, while the Defias Brotherhood takes advantage of the gaps to rob travelers, harass local vineyards, and raid the abbey's library for arcane tomes and holy relics.",al={"why is northshire under attack","kobolds in northshire","defias outside northshire"},it="threat"},{q="What is the connection between Northshire Abbey and the Deadmines?",a="During the First War, the ogre chieftain Turok stole the sacred Tome of Divinity from Northshire Abbey and retreated into the Deadmines. Sir Anduin Lothar led an expedition into the depths to recover it, became trapped, and was rescued by a royal party that returned the tome to the abbey.",al={"tome of divinity northshire","northshire deadmines lore","anduin lothar deadmines"},it="ties"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a revered holy sanctuary nestled in the quiet foothills of northern Elwynn Forest. Originally founded centuries ago by pious clerics from Lordaeron, it serves as the spiritual seat of the Brotherhood of Northshire. Following its reconstruction after the First War, the abbey functions as a recruitment center and proving ground for new champions defending the Kingdom of Stormwind, housing trainers of sacred magic, the martial arts, and arcane lore within its storied halls.",al={"what is northshire abbey","about northshire abbey","northshire abbey overview"},it="place",add="a3256ecc"},{q="Is Northshire Abbey dangerous?",a="The abbey itself remains well guarded by paladins and town watchmen, but the surrounding valley is growing perilously unsafe. Kobolds have overrun the nearby Echo Ridge Mine, aggressive wolves prowl the orchards and forests, and brigands from the Defias Brotherhood openly lurk around the vineyards. While novice adventurers can easily find their footing within the courtyard, wandering the valley unprepared invites sudden danger.",al={"is northshire safe","danger in northshire abbey","is northshire valley dangerous"},it="danger",add="d8226933"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, Northshire Abbey is where your journey begins, and where the kingdom's resilience and devotion welcome every recruit who takes up arms.",["class:Paladin"]="For a paladin, Northshire carries the legacy of Archbishop Alonsus Faol and the early clerics whose sacrifices laid the foundation for the Knights of the Silver Hand."},kw={"abbey","brotherhood","clerics","defias","elwynn","faol","northshire","valley"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","quest:1598","quest:2997","npc:drusilla-la-salle"},src={"Northshire Abbey"}}
E["subzone:northshire-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Valley",z="elwynn",s="Northshire Valley shelters Stormwind's newest defenders in northern Elwynn Forest. Natural barriers guard the peaceful valley, where ancient Northshire Abbey, fertile vineyards, and the rich Echo Ridge Mine sustain a pocket of the kingdom. Bandits, kobolds, and displaced predators now trouble its quiet pastures.",h="Northshire Valley shelters Stormwind's newest defenders in northern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Secluded Sanctuary",b="Northshire Valley lies behind mountain ridges, with one road south through a fortified gatehouse toward Goldshire and the rest of Elwynn Forest. A clear river crosses the pastures and flows into Crystal Lake. At the valley's heart, ancient Northshire Abbey teaches the Holy Light and trains recruits under the Knights of the Silver Hand and seasoned veterans. Beyond its walls, the fertile Northshire Vineyards and Echo Ridge Mine make this a self-sustaining pocket of Stormwind territory, far from the wars beyond its ridges.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching Troubles",b="Stormwind's overextended defenses have strained even this sheltered valley. Marshal McBride and his detachment of the Stormwind Guard struggle to maintain order across it. Wolves driven north from blighted Duskwood prowl the woods, while kobolds have overrun Echo Ridge Mine's tunnels. Masked thugs aligned with the Defias Brotherhood harass the vineyards and threaten the abbey grounds, so local commanders recruit every able-bodied civilian who arrives at the gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Northshire Valley so heavily guarded?",a="Northshire Valley guards Northshire Abbey, a spiritual center and training ground for Stormwind's forces, as well as the vineyards and Echo Ridge Mine. With Stormwind's forces stretched thin, Marshal McBride holds the southern pass behind a guarded gate to keep threats from passing between the valley and greater Elwynn Forest.",al={"why guards northshire","gate in northshire","who protects northshire"},it="danger"},{q="Where did all the wolves in the valley come from?",a="Deputy Willem says wolves have recently crossed the river after fleeing Duskwood's darkened forests to the south. The spreading darkness there has driven wild beasts into the valley's tranquil pastures.",al={"why so many wolves","wolf infestation","wolves from duskwood"},it="threat"},{q="Why are kobolds attacking Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Kobolds are opportunistic burrowers drawn to underground mineral veins. As kingdom patrols thinned, a clan took advantage of the lack of protection to claim Echo Ridge Mine for its gold and candles, forcing the human miners out of the tunnels.",al={"echo ridge kobolds","why kobolds in northshire","kobold problem"},it="threat",nx={18}},{q="Who are the bandits harassing the vineyards?",a="The thieves near Milly Osworth's vineyard are agents of the Defias Brotherhood. They prey on the valley's outskirts to disrupt supplies, harass local farmers, and test the abbey's defenses.",al={"vineyard bandits","defias in northshire","red mask thugs"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Northshire during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Northshire Abbey fell into enemy hands and briefly served as a headquarters for Cho'gall's Twilight's Hammer clan. The Alliance later reclaimed and restored the valley.",al={"northshire second war","twilight hammer northshire","chogall northshire"},it="history"},{q="How do you leave Northshire Valley?",a="The only passable exit on foot is the southern road through the guarded gatehouse. It leads into central Elwynn Forest and points travelers toward Goldshire.",al={"exit northshire","path to goldshire","how to leave"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Valley is a secluded, mountainous valley nestled in northern Elwynn Forest. It is best known as the home of Northshire Abbey and its surrounding vineyards. Bordered by sheer mountains and accessed only by a fortified southern gateway, it serves as the primary training and recruitment ground for fledgling defenders of the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where is northshire valley","tell me about northshire valley","where am i northshire"},it="place",add="9b50c77b",nx={8,9}},{q="Is Northshire Valley part of Stormwind?",a="Yes. Northshire Valley sits squarely within Elwynn Forest, the heartland of the kingdom of Stormwind. The garrison here flies Stormwind's banners, enforces its laws, and reports directly up the kingdom's military hierarchy.",al={"is northshire in stormwind","does stormwind own northshire"},it="place",add="3a470446"},{q="Why do all new recruits train in Northshire Valley?",a="The valley offers a protected, self-contained haven surrounded by high cliffs, making it an ideal staging area. With seasoned marshals, class mentors, and the spiritual presence of the Brotherhood of Northshire all centered at the Abbey, it provides everything necessary to prepare new recruits before they face the wider forest.",al={"why train here","why do recruits come to northshire"},it="place",add="52057ec0"},{q="Why am I here in Northshire Valley as a new recruit?",a="You arrived in response to the kingdom's urgent need for defenders. With Stormwind's regular army stretched thin across contested borders, the authorities opened Northshire Abbey to train any brave soul willing to swear service and keep the realm safe.",al={"why am i here","new recruit why here","what brought me here"},it="arrival",add="0f9fef82"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is a venerable holy site and the historical seat of the Brotherhood of Northshire, an order of clerics founded centuries ago by missionaries of the Church of the Holy Light. Beyond its religious duties, it contains a library, a hall of arms, and quarters for training newly sworn champions of the Alliance.",al={"tell me about northshire abbey","what is the abbey"},it="place",add="0fbb181a",nx={12,13}},{q="Who runs Northshire Abbey?",a="While the clerics attend to the Abbey's spiritual upkeep, Marshal Douglas McBride commands the garrison on site and governs the defense of the entire valley on behalf of the Stormwind Army.",al={"who leads the abbey","abbey leader"},it="in_charge",add="385ef21f"},{q="Why is there an army garrison camped outside a church?",a="Recent troubles have forced martial forces directly into the Abbey's grounds. Bandits have overrun the adjacent vineyards and kobolds have burrowed into nearby mines, leaving the clerics unable to protect the holy grounds without direct military intervention.",al={"why soldiers at the abbey","why garrison at church"},it="place",add="ac0d723b"},{q="Who's in charge around Northshire Valley?",a="Marshal Douglas McBride oversees the defense of Northshire Valley. Stationed inside the Abbey, he directs the garrison, enlists arriving recruits, and coordinates efforts to repel the threats encroaching on the valley.",al={"who is in charge here","northshire commander","who runs northshire"},it="in_charge",add="2babcb98",nx={15}},{q="Who does Marshal McBride answer to?",a="Marshal McBride is an officer of the Stormwind Army serving the crown. His Northshire garrison is part of Elwynn Forest's defense, alongside the forces stationed in Goldshire.",al={"mcbride superior","who is mcbrides boss"},it="in_charge",add="5231335a"},{q="What is 'A Threat Within' about?",a="The phrase refers to the alarming breakdown of security inside the kingdom's own borders. Rather than an army attacking from beyond, Stormwind faces subversion, rogue thieves, and vermin taking root right in its sacred backyard.",al={"a threat within meaning","what threat within quest","what is the threat inside"},it="threat",add="0040026b"},{q="What are kobolds?",a="Kobolds are subterranean rat-like humanoids known for their obsessive tunneling and cowardice in small numbers. They scavenge minerals and dark corners of the realm, fiercely defending their underground warrens from any outsiders.",al={"kobolds lore","what is a kobold","who are kobolds"},it="threat",add="3e58992c"},{q="What is Echo Ridge Mine, was it ours first?",a="Echo Ridge Mine was a productive excavation worked by the kingdom until recently. Kobolds swarmed into the tunnels from the surrounding hills, driving out the human miners and claiming the site as an armed colony.",al={"who owned echo ridge mine","is echo ridge ours","what is echo ridge"},it="threat",add="1071f0ff"},{q="Why do I have to kill so many kobolds, what did they even do?",a="By overrunning Echo Ridge Mine, the kobolds cut off valuable resources and created a hazardous vermin nest adjacent to the Abbey. If left unchecked, their digging threatens to undermine the valley's stability and overwhelm nearby roads.",al={"why kill kobolds","why exterminate kobolds"},it="purpose",add="ffddbb43"},{q="Who are the guys with the red bandanas?",a="Those are agents of the Defias Brotherhood, led locally by Garrick Padfoot. Once skilled craftsmen and laborers from the Stonemasons Guild who rebuilt Stormwind, they turned to banditry and revolt against the crown after a bitter pay dispute.",al={"red bandana bandits","who wears red bandanas","red masks northshire"},it="threat",add="c35515fc"},{q="Why are Defias bandits attacking this close to Stormwind?",a="With royal troops deployed abroad and domestic garrisons starved of resources, the Defias have grown bold enough to seize farms and orchards throughout Elwynn. Northshire's vineyards offer them food, wine, and a staging ground right under the crown's nose.",al={"why bandits near stormwind","why defias in northshire"},it="history",add="c05e8af1"},{q="Why does the Abbey have a warlock trainer at all?",a="Drusilla La Salle trains warlocks in Northshire's cemetery, away from the Abbey's clerics and paladins. Her secluded position reflects the unease surrounding fel magic among those devoted to the Holy Light.",al={"warlock at abbey why","why is there a warlock trainer here"},it="other",add="660e62c8"},{q="Why is everyone asking me, a total beginner, to do all this?",a="The Stormwind Guard is stretched past its breaking point. With soldiers guarding major frontiers and royal forces away, the local garrison simply does not have the manpower to clear every mine or guard every vineyard, leaving recruits like you as their best available line of defense.",al={"why me a beginner","why do i do all the work","why ask recruits"},it="why_me",add="808e49f9"},{q="How did I end up in Northshire Valley?",a="You came seeking Northshire Abbey, the primary recruitment and training grounds for those willing to take up arms for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Surrounded by high mountains and guarded by a fortified pass, this peaceful valley serves as the first assembly point for new defenders. Whether you arrived by foot through Elwynn Forest or answered the crown's call for fresh recruits, Marshal McBride and the abbey's masters were expecting eager souls like you to report for duty.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","why did i arrive in northshire"},it="arrival",add="99bf7d8e"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Northshire Valley?",a="You are here to hone your martial or magical skills under the abbey's trainers while aiding the local garrison. Marshal Douglas McBride and the Stormwind Guard are short-handed and urgently require recruits to deal with nearby threats. You need to cull the predatory wolves encroaching from the timberline, reclaim the Echo Ridge Mine from invasive kobolds, and protect Milly Osworth's vineyards from the Defias Brotherhood bandits lurking nearby before marching south into Elwynn Forest.",al={"what should i be doing here","what is my goal here","what do i do in northshire"},it="purpose",add="bb6d78ec"},{q="Why does a new Human start here, in Northshire Valley?",a="Northshire Abbey has stood for centuries as a foundational pillar of human resilience in the kingdom, home to the Brotherhood of Northshire and a gathering place for the Knights of the Silver Hand. With Stormwind's regular military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing, young humans eager to defend their homeland are directed to this sheltered sanctuary to begin their formal training, receive their letters of introduction, and prove their loyalty to the crown.",al={"why do humans start here","why do human characters begin in northshire","why is northshire the human start"},it="arrival",rc="Human",add="11801d7a"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, your journey begins in Northshire Valley, where you enter the abbey grounds to answer the kingdom's call for help.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find a vital place for recruitment and recovery in Northshire. The valley trains new defenders to stabilize the kingdom's heart."},kw={"abbey","defias","echo ridge","elwynn","kobolds","mcbride","northshire","vineyards","willem"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:northshire-vineyards","subzone:echo-ridge-mine","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Northshire Valley"}}
E["subzone:northshire-vineyards"] = {t="subzone",n="Northshire Vineyards",z="elwynn",s="At Northshire Vineyards, Defias brigands have seized the fields east of Northshire Abbey. The grapes once supplied wine to the clerics, but now the thieves plunder the harvest and threaten local farmers.",h="At Northshire Vineyards, Defias brigands have seized the fields east of Northshire Abbey.",sec={{t="A Plundered Harvest",b="Northshire Vineyards lie east across the stream from Northshire Abbey, where workers such as Milly Osworth once tended the fields. Defias Brotherhood brigands now hold the acreage, led by Garrick Padfoot. The thieves plunder the harvest and strip local farmers of their livelihood. Their occupation gives new Brotherhood recruits a foothold close to the abbey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Northshire Vineyards right now?",a="Defias Brotherhood thieves and cutthroats occupy Northshire Vineyards. Garrick Padfoot leads them, directing the crop looting and terrorizing local workers.",al={"who is at the vineyards","who took over northshire vineyards","who is garrick padfoot"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the abbey letting bandits run rampant in the fields?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin while King Varian Wrynn is missing. Abbey guards protect the abbey and watch the valley roads, leaving local farmers to depend on newly arrived adventurers to recover their stolen goods.",al={"why no stormwind guards","why isn't the abbey defending the vineyards"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Milly Osworth?",a="Milly Osworth is a local farmer who worked the vineyards. The Defias bandits drove her away when they seized the grape harvest, and she now asks travelers to recover her stolen crates.",al={"milly osworth","who is milly"},it="people"},{q="What is Northshire Vineyards?",a="The Northshire Vineyards are agricultural fields located directly east of Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. Under ordinary circumstances, the fields provide grapes and harvest produce for the local settlement, but they have recently fallen into disarray due to criminal activity.",al={"what are northshire vineyards","northshire vineyards overview","about northshire vineyards"},it="place",add="d5ec287a"},{q="What happened at Northshire Vineyards?",a="Agents of the Defias Brotherhood swept in and seized control of the vineyards. Led by the bandit Garrick Padfoot, they pushed out the local workers, stole the harvest belonging to residents like Milly Osworth, and established an armed presence right at the abbey's doorstep.",al={"northshire vineyards history","what happened here","vineyards story"},it="history",add="1ba8e301"},{q="Is Northshire Vineyards dangerous?",a="Yes. The vineyard fields are crawling with hostile Defias bandits and thugs under Garrick Padfoot's command. Anyone wandering among the grapevines without a weapon risks being attacked on sight by cutpurses and brigands who have claimed the land for themselves.",al={"is it safe here","danger northshire vineyards","vineyards safe"},it="danger",add="af15433a"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For many young humans venturing into the world, the occupied vineyards offer a first encounter with the Defias Brotherhood's reach and the bitterness it brings.",["faction:Alliance"]="Unrest in these quiet grape fields shows how far lawlessness has spread, even into the most protected corners of the kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"defias","elwynn","garrick padfoot","grapes","milly osworth","northshire valley","northshire vineyards"},rel={"subzone:northshire-valley","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:3903","zone:elwynn"},src={"Northshire Vineyards"}}
E["subzone:ridgepoint-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Ridgepoint Tower",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind guards watch the eastern frontier from Ridgepoint Tower. They keep vigil over the perilous corridors, valleys, and roads leading into neighboring wilderness.",h="Stormwind guards watch the eastern frontier from Ridgepoint Tower.",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Eastern Border",b="At Ridgepoint Tower, the garrison watches the valleys and roads of eastern Elwynn. The tower stands on high ground, where Stormwind's authority reaches its eastern border and the wilds begin. Its guards keep watch over the routes before threats can reach the farms and settlements nearer Northshire and Goldshire.",sp=0},{t="Threats on Every Horizon",b="Ridgepoint Tower faces threats from several directions. East lie the Redridge Mountains, where aggressive gnoll packs and blackrock orc raiders test human defenses. Across the southern river, undead horrors prowl the timberline of Duskwood. Rogue Defias Brotherhood bandits also haunt nearby wilderness camps, looking for gaps in the guard's defenses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ridgepoint Tower?",a="Ridgepoint Tower is a fortified scout tower in eastern Elwynn Forest, where the Stormwind Guard watches for hostile incursions and works to protect the kingdom.",al={"ridgepoint tower elwynn","what is this guard tower","east elwynn tower"},it="place"},{q="Who controls and mans the tower?",a="Guardsmen and scouts loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind hold and garrison the tower. They operate under the command of the Stormwind Guard.",al={"who is at ridgepoint tower","who owns ridgepoint tower"},it="residents"},{q="What threats does the garrison watch out for?",a="The garrison watches for aggressive gnoll packs and blackrock orc raiders from the Redridge Mountains, undead horrors from Duskwood, and Defias Brotherhood bandits in nearby wilderness camps.",al={"enemies near ridgepoint","what is attacking ridgepoint","why is the tower here"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Ridgepoint Tower located?",a="Ridgepoint Tower stands on high ground in eastern Elwynn Forest, near the borders of the Redridge Mountains and Duskwood.",al={"ridgepoint tower location","where is ridgepoint"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Ridgepoint Tower dangerous?",a="The tower itself is secure and held firmly by the Stormwind Guard, but the surrounding land is fraught with danger. Sitting at a strategic border, the watchpost is constantly under threat from gnolls and orcs descending from Redridge Mountains, restless undead wandering north out of Duskwood, and Defias bandits lurking in nearby camps.",al={"ridgepoint tower dangerous","is it safe at ridgepoint tower","ridgepoint tower threats"},it="danger",add="eff326af"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can take Ridgepoint Tower as a reassuring beacon of safety and order before crossing into the perilous passes of Redridge or the haunted roads of Duskwood.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can respect the stoic resolve of the guardsmen holding this exposed border outpost against surrounding hostiles."},kw={"defias","duskwood","elwynn forest","gnolls","redridge","ridgepoint tower","stormwind guard","watchtower"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","zone:redridge","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:gnoll"},src={"Ridgepoint Tower"}}
E["subzone:stone-cairn-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Stone Cairn Lake",z="elwynn",s="At Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn, hostile murlocs hold the southern shore and renegade wizards camp on the island. Heroes' Vigil honors those lost in the First War.",h="At Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn, hostile murlocs hold the southern shore and renegade wizards camp...",sec={{t="A Monument Besieged",b="Families and pilgrims once crossed the calm waters to honor the dead at Heroes' Vigil. The stone memorial was raised on the lake's central island to mark the heavy loss of human life in the First War against the Orcish Horde. Now renegade wizards have made camp beside the monument, and the island has become a hostile place.",sp=0},{t="Shores of the Lake",b="Aggressive murlocs have claimed the southern banks of Stone Cairn Lake. Their crude huts line the water, and they harass anyone who comes near. The hills and rocky outcrops around the lake hold rich mineral veins, drawing prospectors and miners despite the dangers along the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Stone Cairn Lake takes its name from Heroes' Vigil, a stone cairn on the central island honoring Stormwind's soldiers and civilians who died in the First War.",al={"stone cairn name","why stone cairn","origin of the name"},it="name"},{q="Who is currently occupying the central island?",a="Renegade wizards and other renegades occupy the island, driving away pilgrims and building a fortified camp around the memorial.",al={"who is on the island","island wizards","rogue mages on lake"},it="residents"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the water?",a="A local murloc tribe has settled the southern shallows and riverbanks. They build huts along the waterline and claim the plentiful fishing waters as their territory.",al={"murlocs at stone cairn","lake murlocs","south shore huts"},it="threat"},{q="What is the memorial on the island called?",a="The memorial is called Heroes' Vigil. Its stone cairn is also known as the Stone of Remembrance.",al={"island memorial name","monument name","stone cairn shrine"},it="history"},{q="What is Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Stone Cairn Lake is a ring-shaped body of water situated in northeastern Elwynn Forest. At its center lies an island bearing Heroes' Vigil, a solemn memorial honoring those who perished during the First War. Once a tranquil destination for travelers and mourners, the area has since grown wild and perilous.",al={"what is stone cairn lake","stone cairn lake info","tell me about stone cairn lake"},it="place",add="a25fa3d9"},{q="Is Stone Cairn Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, it poses significant danger to wandering travelers. Rogue wizards have seized the island at the center of the lake, aggressively defending their camp with arcane magic. Furthermore, hostile murlocs have overrun the shallows and erected settlements along the southern banks, attacking anyone who draws near.",al={"is stone cairn lake safe","stone cairn lake threats","danger stone cairn lake"},it="danger",add="9a875c99"},{q="Why was Stone Cairn Lake abandoned as a pilgrimage site?",a="Stone Cairn Lake was once a peaceful pilgrimage destination for citizens honoring fallen soldiers from the First War. However, Stormwind's guards could not keep it secure amid mounting unrest, allowing rogue spellcasters to commandeer the monument island and vicious murlocs to claim the shores.",al={"why is stone cairn lake abandoned","why is stone cairn lake ruined","pilgrimage stone cairn lake"},it="ruin",add="92ff0cce"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The hills and bluffs around Stone Cairn Lake hold one of Elwynn Forest's heaviest concentrations of copper deposits, drawing aspiring blacksmiths and engineers.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the island as a memorial to Stormwind's people, honoring those lost when the kingdom fell in the First War."},kw={"copper","elwynn forest","first war","heroes' vigil","murloc","rogue wizards","stone cairn lake","stone of remembrance"},rel={"subzone:heroes-vigil","zone:elwynn","topic:first-war","topic:murloc"},src={"Stone Cairn Lake"}}
E["subzone:stonefield-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonefield Farm",z="elwynn",s="The Stonefield family works the fields in southern Elwynn Forest. Their long feud with the neighboring Maclures keeps the two households at odds.",h="The Stonefield family works the fields in southern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Bitter Homestead",b="Stonefield Farm lies south of Goldshire, where the family grows crops for the realm. For decades, the Stonefields have quarreled with the nearby Maclure Vineyards. The households trade accusations of theft and trespassing, and even small disputes keep tensions high. Gramma Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield make their home here.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures have quarreled for years in southern Elwynn Forest. They accuse each other of trespassing, theft, and other wrongs, and refuse to cooperate even on simple neighborhood matters.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","why are stonefields fighting","stonefield rivals"},it="conflict"},{q="Who lives at Stonefield Farm?",a="Gramma Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield live at the farm, which is managed by the Stonefield clan.",al={"stonefield npcs","who is at stonefield farm"},it="residents"},{q="What is Tommy Joe Stonefield's secret?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield is secretly in love with Maybell Maclure, despite the hostility between their families. The two rely on sympathetic travelers to carry messages and gifts without their families noticing.",al={"tommy joe secret","tommy joe romance","stonefield love"}},{q="What is Stonefield Farm?",a="Stonefield Farm is a quiet homestead nestled in the southern reaches of Elwynn Forest, worked and tended by the Stonefield family. While it looks like an ordinary farmstead producing crops for the region, it is best known across the valley for its long, bitter rivalry with its neighboring homestead, the Maclure Vineyards. Visitors often find themselves caught squarely in the middle of domestic quarrels, missing heirloom squabbles, and the secret romantic pursuits of the younger generation.",al={"what is stonefield farm","stonefield farmstead elwynn","about stonefield farm"},it="place",add="60255a1c"},{q="Is Stonefield Farm dangerous?",a="The farmstead itself is generally safe and maintained by the family, but the surrounding fields are another matter. Like much of southern Elwynn Forest, wild beasts roam the outskirts, and local bandits and encroaching pests frequently threaten the livestock and crops. Travelers should keep their weapons ready when venturing out into the pastures or wandering down toward the nearby riverbanks and orchards.",al={"is stonefield farm dangerous","threats at stonefield farm","stonefield farm enemies"},it="danger",add="45c8f9cb"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human from Northshire, you can see the squabbles between the Stonefields and Maclures as a glimpse of rural life beyond the threat of bandits and gnolls."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure","stonefield","stonefield farm","tommy joe"},rel={"zone:elwynn"},src={"Stonefield Farm"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-city"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind City",z="elwynn",s="Stormwind City leads the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance as their capital and seat of power. Rebuilt after the First War, it is the greatest remaining human stronghold in Azeroth since the northern kingdoms fell.",h="Stormwind City leads the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance as their capital and seat of power.",sec={{t="A Beacon Rebuilt",b="Stormwind City rose over a thousand years ago, founded by Arathi descendants who migrated south. The coastal capital flourished behind stone ramparts, with swift rivermills powering the city. In the First War, the Orcish Horde laid siege, broke through its defenses, and burned Stormwind to the ground. Sir Anduin Lothar led the surviving refugees across the Great Sea to Lordaeron. After the Alliance won the Second War, the Stonemasons' Guild rebuilt the capital with white stone, canals, and towering spires. The fortress now stands north of Elwynn Forest.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Alliance",b="Stormwind City has become mankind's chief refuge and stronghold after the Scourge shattered Lordaeron and the Third War left Dalaran heavily ruined. The disciplined Stormwind City Guard patrols its broad avenues and defensive walls. The Cathedral of Light's spires guide faith across the southern kingdoms. Beneath the orderly districts and ceremonial gates, political troubles linger. King Varian Wrynn has mysteriously vanished, and his young son Anduin sits on the throne under the regency of Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the whispered counsel of royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Stormwind rebuilt after the First War?",a="The Orcish Horde sacked and burned Stormwind during the First War. After the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron defeated the orcs in the Second War, human refugees reclaimed their ancestral kingdom. The royal court commissioned the Stonemasons' Guild to build a grander fortress city on the original ruins.",al={"who rebuilt stormwind","rebuilding of stormwind","why does stormwind look new"}},{q="Who rules Stormwind City right now?",a="Boy-king Anduin Wrynn sits on the throne after his father, King Varian Wrynn, suddenly and without explanation disappeared. Because Anduin is young, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as Regent and commands the Kingdom's defenses.",al={"who is king of stormwind","who runs stormwind","current ruler of stormwind"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is Stormwind the main human capital instead of Lordaeron?",a="During the Third War, the undead plague and the Scourge devastated Lordaeron from within. With Lordaeron destroyed and other northern human realms devastated, Stormwind is the wealthiest, most intact, and most populous human kingdom remaining on Azeroth.",al={"what happened to lordaeron","why not capital of lordaeron","is stormwind the last city"}},{q="What military forces protect the city?",a="The Stormwind City Guard enforces peace in the wards and along the battlement walls. The Kingdom's knights, soldiers garrisoned at Stormwind Keep, and paladins affiliated with the Church of the Light maintain broader territorial defense and royal protection.",al={"who guards stormwind","stormwind army","city guards"}},{q="What is Stormwind City?",a="Stormwind City is the capital of the kingdom of Stormwind and the greatest human bastion left on Azeroth. Nestled north of Elwynn Forest along the western coast, it stands as the beating heart of the Alliance. Behind its towering white stone ramparts and deep canals lie thriving merchant districts, the seat of the Crown, and the Cathedral of Light, a beacon of faith for all who revere the Holy Light.",al={"what is stormwind","stormwind city overview","about stormwind city"},it="place",add="209accb7"},{q="What happened at Stormwind City?",a="Founded over a millennium ago by Arathi descendants, Stormwind weathered gnoll wars and troll assaults before facing utter devastation in the First War. The Orcish Horde besieged the capital, breached its defenses, and razed it to the ground, forcing survivors to flee north across the sea. After the Alliance triumphed in the Second War, the Stonemasons' Guild painstakingly rebuilt the city into the majestic stronghold standing today.",al={"stormwind history","what happened to stormwind","fall of stormwind"},it="history",add="38604972"},{q="Is Stormwind City dangerous?",a="Within its walls, Stormwind is one of the most secure settlements in the realm, patrolled constantly by the vigilant Stormwind City Guard. However, peace is not absolute. Shadows lurk in darker corners like the alleys of Old Town, political intrigue stirs in the royal court, and the kingdom's surrounding territories remain threatened by outlaws and encroaching monsters.",al={"is stormwind safe","is stormwind city dangerous","threats in stormwind"},it="danger",add="7f858f77"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans across Azeroth, Stormwind's white walls speak of endurance, survival, and mankind's glory after the northern kingdoms were lost.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stormwind is the chief military, naval, and spiritual rallying point in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. It welcomes dwarves, gnomes, and night elven envoys alike."},kw={"alliance","anduin","bolvar","elwynn","first war","stonemasons","stormwind","stormwind city","wrynn"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:stormwind-keep","subzone:cathedral-of-light","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:first-war","topic:alliance"},src={"Stormwind City"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind Gate",z="elwynn",s="At Stormwind Gate, sentries watch the road between Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City. The passage opens onto the Valley of Heroes, where the city’s stone monuments rise beyond the arch.",h="At Stormwind Gate, sentries watch the road between Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Kingdom",b="Stormwind Gate guards the southern road from Elwynn Forest into the capital. The Stormwind City Guard watches from the stone portal, while patrols move between the outer arch and the Valley of Heroes. Unrest lingers in Elwynn, yet the massive iron and stone gates stay open. Travelers, merchants, and returning defenders pass through into the heart of the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Stormwind Gate lead?",a="From Elwynn Forest, the gate opens directly onto the Valley of Heroes, Stormwind City’s grand entryway, lined with towering monuments to the Second War.",al={"where does stormwind gate go","what is past the gate","stormwind entrance"},it="place"},{q="Why is the gate left open if Elwynn Forest is dangerous?",a="Stormwind keeps the passage open for trade and travel from Goldshire and across the Alliance. Guards watch for bandits and Defias activity in the woods while citizens and commerce continue through the gate.",al={"why are the gates open","is stormwind gate closed","why open"}},{q="Who guards the gates?",a="The Stormwind City Guard garrisons the entryway. Two sentries watch just outside in Elwynn Forest, two more guard the inner passage, and armed footmen patrol the bridge through the Valley of Heroes.",al={"stormwind gate guards","who defends the gate"},it="in_charge"},{q="Are there special events held at the gate?",a="Yes. The open ground around Stormwind Gate often hosts major citywide holidays and seasonal gatherings for the Alliance. It gives the city a place to assemble beyond its crowded districts.",al={"holidays at stormwind gate","events at gate"}},{q="Is Stormwind Gate dangerous?",a="Not for members of the Alliance. The gate is heavily secured by Stormwind City Guards patrolling both sides of the threshold and the adjacent Valley of Heroes. However, hostile infiltrators or Horde travelers will find it nearly impossible to breach, as the stationed sentries will instantly attack any declared enemy of the crown on sight.",al={"is the gate safe","stormwind gate danger","stormwind gate safe"},it="danger",add="c23a16f5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the gate is a sign of safety and endurance. Traveling soldiers and young adventurers first glimpse the Grand Alliance’s majesty here.",["race:Human"]="For the people of Stormwind, passing back through these stone arches means coming home to safety after long journeys through Elwynn and beyond."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","stormwind city guard","stormwind gate","valley of heroes"},rel={"zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn","subzone:valley-of-heroes","subzone:goldshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Stormwind Gate"}}
E["subzone:thunder-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Falls",z="elwynn",s="Thunder Falls lies in Elwynn Forest’s northwestern heights, where bandits have taken a riverside cottage.",h="Thunder Falls lies in Elwynn Forest’s northwestern heights, where bandits have taken a riverside cottage.",sec={{t="A Hidden Mountain Hollow",b="Thunder Falls cuts through the ridges above Mirror Lake, where a mountain stream rushes between steep cliffs. It enters over an unreachable cascade in the north, then spills away in waterfalls on both sides. One fall empties into Mirror Lake; the stream’s downstream course runs west toward Westfall’s rugged border. A cottage, dock, and outdoor forge sit beside the water. Bandits now claim the clearing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach Thunder Falls?",a="Reach Thunder Falls from the northern side of Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest. A steep, narrow trail climbs into the hills beside the waterfall’s right side and leads into the ravine.",al={"how to get to thunder falls","thunder falls location","where is thunder falls"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who lives in the cottage at Thunder Falls?",a="The cottage at Thunder Falls appears to have belonged to a solitary fisherman or frontiersman, with a dock, rowing boat, and outdoor anvil nearby. Bandits operating in Elwynn Forest now use it as a remote hideout.",al={"who is at the cottage","thunder falls house","cottage bandits"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the river at Thunder Falls flow?",a="The stream runs through the narrow mountain gap from an upper cascade. It passes the cottage, then plunges down a steep waterfall near Westfall’s eastern boundary.",al={"where does the water go","thunder falls river"},it="place"},{q="What is Thunder Falls?",a="Thunder Falls is a secluded mountain ravine tucked away in the northwestern heights of Elwynn Forest. Fed by an inaccessible cascade dropping from the high northern bluffs, the river carves through a narrow gorge between double waterfalls, emptying down toward Mirror Lake on one side and cascading west toward the border of Westfall on the other. It is a quiet, hidden retreat featuring a solitary rural cottage, a small pier, and cold mountain waters.",al={"what is thunder falls","thunder falls lore","tell me about thunder falls"},it="place",add="1050bd39"},{q="Is Thunder Falls dangerous?",a="Despite its tranquil setting, you must tread carefully. Outlaws and Defias-affiliated bandits have made camp around the isolated cottage, taking advantage of its hidden, defensible location above the falls. In addition to hostile brigands, navigating the steep cliffs and roaring waterfalls requires caution, as one misplaced step can send you tumbling into the rapids below.",al={"is thunder falls safe","thunder falls bandits","threats at thunder falls"},it="danger",add="db2700a0"}},kw={"bandits","cottage","elwynn forest","mirror lake","thunder falls","waterfall"},rel={"quest:1861","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall"},src={"Thunder Falls"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-azora"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Azora",z="elwynn",s="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus leads a scholarly outpost in eastern Elwynn Forest. The slender spire stands north of the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, where its human master keeps watch over a silent magical feud with a hostile tower in the Redridge Mountains.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus leads a scholarly outpost in eastern Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="A Spire of Arcane Vigilance",b="The Tower of Azora stands beside the eastern road to the Redridge Mountains, staffed almost entirely by gnome spellcasters. Archmage Theocritus guides their studies of strange curiosities and teaches wandering spellweavers. A wild magical aura surrounds the spire and sometimes warps nearby wildlife. Within the tower, gnome servants contend with enchanted household items and mutated insects that creep past the doorway.",sp=0},{t="The Feud with Ilgalar",b="The Tower of Azora wages a quiet war of scrying and sabotage. Eastward, atop the crags of the Redridge Mountains, the sinister Tower of Ilgalar is ruled by the renegade sorcerer Morganth. Theocritus and Morganth spy on one another through arcane means. They enlist daring adventurers to plant scrying relics such as the Eye of Azora, piercing Ilgalar's wards to watch Morganth's dark machinations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Tower of Azora?",a="Archmage Theocritus, an accomplished human wizard, presides over the Tower of Azora. He directs its servants and coordinates the tower's magical defenses against rival sorcerers.",al={"who leads the tower of azora","who is in charge here","tower of azora boss"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are there so many gnomes here?",a="Most servants at the Tower of Azora are gnome researchers and acolytes. They help Archmage Theocritus with his studies, arcane experiments, and housekeeping when magic goes awry.",al={"why gnomes in elwynn tower","servants of azora"},it="residents"},{q="Who is the tower fighting against?",a="The Tower of Azora is locked in a magical rivalry with the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains, home to the evil sorcerer Morganth. Both towers spy on each other with scrying artifacts and contest each other's influence.",al={"azora enemy","tower feud","who is azora spying on"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Eye of Azora on the top floor?",a="The Eye of Azora is an enchanted scrying focus on a table in the upper sanctum. Touching it lets an observer gaze across magical distance and watch the outskirts of the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"orb on top floor","eye of azora","crystal ball azora"},it="power"},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is a prominent wizard's tower situated in central Elwynn Forest, east of Goldshire. Led by Theocritus, the Archmage of Azora, it serves as a magical sanctuary and study for arcane practitioners, staffed predominantly by gnomish servants and enchanters.",al={"tower of azora","what is this tower","about tower of azora"},it="place",add="e823b8a2"},{q="Is the Tower of Azora dangerous?",a="The tower is a safe refuge for Alliance travelers, offering shelter and training in enchanting. However, the potent magical aura radiating from the spire has been known to warp everyday objects and wildlife straying too close, forcing the servants within to deal with bizarre oddities like animated buckets and mutant butterflies.",al={"is tower of azora dangerous","danger at tower of azora","tower of azora threats"},it="danger",add="7c8bc76d"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage traveling beyond Stormwind, you can find a secluded place to study, arcane trainers, and a close view of the dangerous arts of remote divination at the tower.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can take pride in seeing an arcane spire in human lands staffed by gnomes under Archmage Theocritus, a showcase of your people's mastery of the mystic arts."},kw={"azora","elwynn","enchanting","ilgalar","morganth","scrying","spire","theocritus"},rel={"zone:elwynn","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:94","zone:redridge","subzone:brackwell-pumpkin-patch","subzone:goldshire","topic:gnome"},src={"Tower of Azora"}}
E["subzone:westbrook-garrison"] = {t="subzone",n="Westbrook Garrison",z="elwynn",s="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer's few guards hold Elwynn's western road against gnolls and bandits. The outpost is short on soldiers and supplies, with danger rising near the Westfall border.",h="At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer's few guards hold Elwynn's western road against gnolls and bandits.",sec={{t="A Beleaguered Border Post",b="Westbrook Garrison watches the road where Elwynn Forest thins toward Westfall. Deputy Rainer and a handful of guards patrol the western roads with too few soldiers to cover them. Much of the Stormwind Army serves abroad, while political indecision in the capital leaves the outpost without needed support. Thieves grow bolder, and Riverpaw gnolls have overrun the southern woods. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire has not sent formal reinforcements, so the guards depend on travelers to help secure the highway.",sp=0},{t="The Menace of Forest's Edge",b="Riverpaw gnolls gather south of Forest's Edge, where their raids threaten supply lines and homesteads. The packs follow Hogger, a fearsome chieftain whose forces outnumber the garrison and overwhelm its guards with brute strength. A high bounty is posted across the outpost, seeking fighters willing to enter the hills and bring down Hogger before the gnolls press farther east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Westbrook Garrison so understaffed?",a="Most of the Stormwind Army serves abroad, while indecision among the House of Nobles in the capital has left regional garrisons short of soldiers and supplies. Westbrook's commanders depend on wandering adventurers to help fill the gap.",al={"why so few guards","westbrook reinforcements","deputy rainer lacking troops"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is in command at the garrison?",a="Deputy Rainer oversees Westbrook Garrison and answers to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. His requests for more soldiers have largely gone unanswered.",al={"who leads westbrook garrison","deputy rainer role","westbrook commander"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats does the garrison face?",a="Westbrook faces bandits from Westfall and Riverpaw gnolls camping in the surrounding woods. The gnolls follow their chieftain, Hogger.",al={"threats to westbrook","gnolls westbrook","who attacks westbrook garrison"},it="threat"},{q="What is the relation between Westbrook and Westfall?",a="Westbrook Garrison is Elwynn's last outpost on the western road before the bridge into Westfall. Its guards watch the border as lawlessness rises from the west.",al={"is westbrook in westfall","border to westfall"},it="ties"},{q="What is Westbrook Garrison?",a="Westbrook Garrison is a Stormwind Guard barracks standing near Forest's Edge on the western border of Elwynn Forest. Situated just across the river from Westfall, this military outpost guards the primary road linking the capital's heartland with the western plains. Though fortified with a sturdy guard tower and barracks, it currently serves as the final, struggling line of defense protecting local homesteads from outlaws and feral gnolls.",al={"what is westbrook","westbrook garrison elwynn","about westbrook garrison"},it="place",add="2e1647ed"},{q="Is Westbrook Garrison dangerous?",a="The garrison itself remains a secure refuge held by the Stormwind Guard, but the surrounding wilderness is perilous. The woods directly to the south teem with the vicious Riverpaw gnoll pack, led by the monstrous chieftain Hogger. In addition, Defias bandits spill across the border from Westfall to prey upon travelers, making any unescorted journey off the garrison's immediate grounds hazardous.",al={"is westbrook dangerous","danger at westbrook","is westbrook garrison safe"},it="danger",add="9e78a278"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Warrior, you can help Westbrook's overstretched guards hold back wilderness predators and fight the gnoll war bands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion traveling from Elwynn toward Westfall, you can help secure Westbrook's perimeter and claim the bounty on Hogger to guard the kingdom's western border."},kw={"deputy rainer","elwynn forest","forest's edge","hogger","marshal dughan","riverpaw","westbrook garrison","westfall"},rel={"npc:deputy-rainer","quest:176","quest:11","subzone:forest-s-edge","subzone:goldshire","npc:marshal-dughan","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall"},src={"Westbrook Garrison"}}
E["zone:elwynn"] = {t="zone",n="Elwynn Forest",z="elwynn",s="In Elwynn Forest, Stormwind draws timber, gold, fish, and crops from the land. Northshire Abbey sends human recruits into the woods, where vermin, displaced wildlife, and brigands threaten the peace.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Stormwind draws timber, gold, fish, and crops from the land.",sec={{t="The Breadbasket of the Realm",b="Elwynn Forest stretches south from Stormwind’s gates to the Nazferiti River. Rain feeds its fertile fields, while dense hardwood forests supply the capital. Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp send grain, livestock, lumber, and raw copper to Stormwind. Elwynn also breeds sturdy Evendale horses, prized by travelers and knights across the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Peace",b="Trouble presses in from every side. The Stormwind Army is stretched thin by duties far away, leaving local marshals and deputies to depend on untested recruits. Kobolds have overrun the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines. Riverpaw gnolls prowl the southwestern borders, while murlocs hold the shores of Stone Cairn Lake and Crystal Lake. Wolves fleeing corruption across the river in Duskwood have crossed into Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="The Red Bandana Threat",b="The Defias Brotherhood has spread through Elwynn as an organized band of outlaws. Its members came from Edwin VanCleef’s Stonemasons Guild after bitter disputes over pay with the House of Nobles. They have taken the Northshire Vineyards, the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, Jerod’s Landing, and Mirror Lake Orchard. Rumors say their agents are guiding nearby gnolls and kobolds to unsettle the realm. Guards Rolf and Malakai went to investigate murlocs near Stone Cairn Lake; both were killed and left on its banks.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="Why is the Stormwind Guard barely policing the forest?",a="Stormwind’s armed forces are stretched thin. The kingdom sent large forces south into Stranglethorn Vale, piling up debt and draining local manpower. Westbrook Garrison and Goldshire now rely on small crews and volunteer recruits to face bandits, gnolls, and murlocs.",al={"where are the guards","why no stormwind army","why is elwynn undefended"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there kobolds inside all the mines?",a="Guards are scarce, and kobolds have swarmed into Fargodeep Mine, Jasperlode Mine, and Echo Ridge Mine for gold and minerals. They drove out the human prospectors and miners, then defended their claims with candles, crude picks, and scavenged tools.",al={"why are kobolds in the mines","elwynn kobolds","fargodeep infested"},it="threat"},{q="Who are the bandits wearing red masks?",a="The red-masked bandits are the Defias Brotherhood, outlaws who have seized farms and mines across Elwynn and Westfall. The People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall is still trying to learn who leads them and why.",al={"red masks","red bandana bandits","who are the defias in elwynn"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the road south lead?",a="The road south crosses the Nazferiti River into Duskwood. Once peaceful, the territory has fallen into unnatural darkness and is infested with undead, monstrous spiders, and ravenous beasts.",al={"what is across the river","where does duskwood bridge go","bridge across the nazferiti"},it="place"},{q="What is the feud between the Maclures and Stonefields?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures are neighboring farming families in southern Elwynn, locked in a bitter, longstanding grudge. Their younger kin, Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield, have secretly fallen in love, making the rivalry more fraught.",al={"maclure vs stonefield","elwynn farm rivalry","stonefield maclure feud"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane spire beside the road between Goldshire and the Eastvale Logging Camp. Secluded mages live there, including Theocritus, who studies the region’s leylines and conducts magical research beyond the direct oversight of Stormwind’s Wizard’s Sanctum.",al={"tower on the road to eastvale","wizard tower elwynn","who lives in the tower of azora"},it="place"},{q="What is Elwynn Forest?",a="Elwynn Forest is the verdant heartland of the Kingdom of Stormwind. Nestled below the foothills of the Burning Steppes, these ancient woods of stately hardwoods, rolling hills, and rushing rivers supply the kingdom with lumber, fish, crops, and ore. Its majestic canopy shelters small farmsteads, winding country roads, and towns like Goldshire, while the capital city of Stormwind watches over the realm from the northwestern ridge.",al={"what is elwynn","where am i","elwynn forest lore"},it="place",add="23586590"},{q="What happened to Elwynn Forest in the past?",a="Founded centuries ago by human migrants of the Arathi bloodline, Elwynn flourished into a thriving realm. During the First War, however, the Orcish Horde swept through the forest, burning its woodland glades and encircling Stormwind City before razing Goldshire and the capital. After the Second War, Supreme Commander Turalyon helped oversee the repatriation of its people and the forest was rebuilt anew, leaving only scattered, rotting catapults as reminders of the invasion.",al={"history of elwynn forest","elwynn forest past","elwynn first war"},it="history",add="4e6f8475"},{q="Is Elwynn Forest dangerous?",a="Though Elwynn appears idyllic, its peaceful exterior hides rising turmoil. Kobolds have overrun the realm's crucial gold mines, while hostile Riverpaw gnolls raid from the western border. Vicious murlocs have established camps around Crystal Lake and Stone Cairn Lake, ambushing guards and travelers alike. Worse, the red-masked Defias Brotherhood works from the shadows, occupying orchards and farmsteads while Stormwind's forces struggle to maintain control.",al={"is elwynn safe","elwynn forest threats","threats in elwynn"},it="danger",add="2f8050d9"},{q="Is this part of Stormwind?",a="Yes, Elwynn Forest is the core territory of the Kingdom of Stormwind. The forest directly borders the capital city's gates and feeds its markets with lumber from Eastvale, crops from rural farmsteads, and ore from regional mines. The Stormwind Guard maintains outposts throughout the woods, including Westbrook Garrison and Northshire Valley, though royal resources are currently stretched thin across the realm.",al={"is elwynn stormwind","stormwind kingdom territory","elwynn allegiance"},it="place",add="41d1722e"},{q="Why is it so peaceful here compared to everywhere else?",a="Elwynn sits in the sheltered center of the kingdom, right beneath the protective walls of Stormwind City. Unlike Duskwood to the south, which fell to a creeping magical curse, or Westfall to the west, which was abandoned to drought and banditry, Elwynn saw extensive rebuilding after the Second War. Its close proximity to the throne keeps it shielded from the worst horrors lurking in neighboring lands.",al={"why is elwynn peaceful","elwynn vs duskwood","why is elwynn not ruined"},it="history",add="36c6d40e"},{q="What is Goldshire?",a="Goldshire is the central crossroads village of Elwynn Forest, located just south of Northshire and southeast of Stormwind City. Founded centuries ago, it serves as the vital hub linking trade roads to Westfall, the Redridge Mountains, and Duskwood. It hosts busy crafters, local trainers, and the famous Lion's Pride Inn, offering hospitality to travelers passing through the heart of the kingdom.",al={"goldshire","tell me about goldshire","goldshire lore"},it="place",add="7bf05012"},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan and why does everyone send me to him?",a="Marshal Dughan is the municipal commander and chief law enforcer for Goldshire and the surrounding forest. Stationed in town, he oversees local security, coordinates regional patrols, and attempts to protect travelers and supply lines. Because the Stormwind military is overextended elsewhere, Dughan relies heavily on capable adventurers to investigate threats and restore order across Elwynn.",al={"marshal dughan","who is dughan","dughan goldshire"},it="in_charge",add="2eb13bb0"},{q="Does Marshal Dughan answer to Stormwind?",a="Yes, Marshal Dughan is an officer of the Stormwind Guard and answers directly to the kingdom's high command in Stormwind City. He enforces the crown's laws and attempts to uphold royal authority throughout the central forest, though he must constantly petition the capital for troops and supplies that rarely arrive.",al={"dughan stormwind","who does dughan report to","is dughan stormwind guard"},it="ties",add="68a6801b"},{q="Why did I start at Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Valley is a sheltered, fortified haven designed to train and enlist promising new recruits for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Guarded behind stone walls and natural cliffs, the valley houses Northshire Abbey, where novice warriors, priests, paladins, and other aspirants hone their craft and assist local commanders before marching out into the wider world.",al={"why northshire","northshire start","starting in northshire"},it="arrival",add="6c2b38d9"},{q="What is Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey is the historic seat of the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics, an order of the Holy Light that aided Stormwind through its darkest eras. Comprising the Main Hall, Hall of Arms, and Library Wing, it once sheltered the Guardian Medivh during his coma and preserved sacred tomes like the Tome of Divinity. Rebuilt after the Second War, it now trains recruits and champions of the Light.",al={"northshire abbey lore","what is northshire","the abbey in northshire"},it="place",add="f22f39d1"},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the municipal law enforcer and military commander in charge of Northshire Valley. Based at Northshire Abbey, he oversees local defenses, monitors threats from the infested Echo Ridge Mine and encroaching Defias brigands, and recruits capable new citizens into service for the defense of the realm.",al={"marshal mcbride","mcbride northshire","who is mcbride"},it="in_charge",add="c283ebda"},{q="What is the Fargodeep Mine?",a="The Fargodeep Mine is an abandoned gold and copper mine located south of Goldshire. Once an essential source of revenue and metal for Stormwind's treasury, the mine fell into chaos when a clan of kobolds invaded its tunnels. Now overrun, it remains a contested hazard right near local farmsteads, prompting Marshal Dughan to send adventurers into its depths to scout and clear out the infestation.",al={"fargodeep mine","fargodeep","fargodeep lore"},it="place",add="16daccd8"},{q="Who are the Riverpaw gnolls and why are they attacking us?",a="The Riverpaw pack is a savage clan of hyena-like gnolls entrenched along the western border of Elwynn near Westbrook Garrison. Aggressive and predatory, they have long contested human expansion and raided farms and unwary travelers. They have set up encampments along the Forest's Edge and Stone Cairn Lake, pushing aggressively into human lands.",al={"riverpaw gnolls","why do riverpaw attack","riverpaw pack"},it="threat",add="e239f261"},{q="Are the Riverpaw gnolls working for someone?",a="While gnolls usually act out of raw ferocity and greed, rumors across the forest suggest they may be in league with the Defias Brotherhood. Strange ties and bounties, including dealings with shady collectors near Ridgepoint Tower, hint that the bandits may be arming or coordinating with the gnolls to destabilize Elwynn's western frontier.",al={"who leads riverpaw","are gnolls with defias","riverpaw defias connection"},sp=1,it="ties",add="da4445a3"},{q="Why is everyone so worried about murlocs by the river?",a="Murlocs have moved in force into the waterways of Elwynn, infesting Crystal Lake and Stone Cairn Lake. These primitive amphibious creatures are fiercely territorial, ambushing local fishermen, travelers, and town patrols. Guard Thomas fears that if their expanding shoreline settlements are left unchecked, they will overrun local roads and push their skirmishes right into Goldshire itself.",al={"murloc threat elwynn","why worry about murlocs","murloc problem"},it="threat",add="29c0080a"},{q="What happened to Rolf and Malakai?",a="Guards Rolf and Malakai were Stormwind sentries dispatched to investigate growing murloc activity near the eastern waterways and Stone Cairn Lake. They have not reported back, and Guard Thomas asks travelers to investigate.",al={"rolf and malakai","lost guards elwynn","what happened to guards hartford and stone"},sp=1,it="history",add="f8d7f725"},{q="What is going on at the Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp is the heart of Elwynn's bustling timber industry, nestled in the eastern woods along the border with the Redridge Mountains. Its loggers fell the forest's massive hardwoods to provide lumber for construction, wagons, and fortifications throughout Stormwind's realm, though hostile wolves and bears frequently threaten its work crews.",al={"eastvale logging camp","eastvale lumber","what is eastvale"},it="place",add="0c4f3fe8"},{q="Where does all this lead after Elwynn?",a="Once you finish assisting Marshal Dughan, the roads from Goldshire branch out toward harsher frontiers. The western bridge across the river Nazferiti leads to the dust and wind of Westfall, where the Defias hold sway. To the east lies the elevated frontier of the Redridge Mountains, while crossing the southern bridges takes you into the cursed, haunted gloom of Duskwood.",al={"where to after elwynn","next zone after elwynn","after elwynn forest"},it="next_step",add="9effb187"},{q="What is Westfall like?",a="Westfall is an arid, windswept agricultural territory southwest of Elwynn. Once the breadbasket of the kingdom, its rolling pastures now lie fallow and dry, infested by rogue mechanical harvest watchers, ravenous carrion birds, and bandits. The Defias Brotherhood holds almost complete control over the region, leaving only a desperate local militia at Sentinel Hill to resist them.",al={"what is westfall","about westfall","westfall overview"},it="place",add="cd54a445"},{q="How did I end up in Elwynn Forest?",a="If you are human, Elwynn Forest is the heartland of your people. You likely took your first steps in the sheltered valley of Northshire Abbey, answering the call of the realm to train your abilities and aid the local authorities. Once you dealt with the early troubles in the valley, Marshal McBride directed you south along the road to Goldshire. Travelers of other races usually journey here from the Deeprun Tram into Stormwind City, stepping through the capital's grand gates directly out into the forest.",al={"how did i get here","why am i in elwynn forest","how did i get to elwynn","how did i end up here"},it="arrival",add="4080ef4d"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Elwynn Forest?",a="With Stormwind's army stretched thin across the realm, Elwynn's defense has fallen to local deputies and able-bodied recruits like you. Marshal Dughan in Goldshire needs help clearing out kobolds infesting the gold mines, repelling Riverpaw gnolls along the western border, and fighting off vicious murlocs around the lakes. At the same time, red-masked Defias bandits have overrun local farms and orchards, while squabbling landowners like the Maclures and Stonefields need their disputes resolved. Once you help restore order here, the road leads west into Westfall or east toward the Redridge Mountains.",al={"what should i do in elwynn","what am i doing here","what is my mission in elwynn forest","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="f92572cc"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin in the ancestral heart of the kingdom. You train at Northshire Abbey before setting out to defend your homeland from bandits, beasts, and political ruin.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find Elwynn crossed by the Defias Brotherhood’s shadow, with thievery, smuggled goods, and underground rebel signals.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you find copper veins in Echo Ridge, Fargodeep, and Jasperlode. Kobolds infest these mines, but they remain an important early proving ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect the Alliance’s primary human kingdom. Stormwind City depends on Elwynn’s lumber, ore, and grain routes."},kw={"defias","eastvale","elwynn","elwynn forest","fargodeep","goldshire","hogger","jasperlode","nazferiti","northshire","northshire abbey","vancleef"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:goldshire","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:westfall","zone:duskwood","zone:redridge","subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:65"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Elwynn Forest (Classic)","Elwynn Forest"}}
